COPY public."Tour" (id, title, slug, gallery, duration, "bestTime", destination, grade, "maxAltitude", "startPoint", "endPoint", meals, overview, highlights, itinerary, inclusions, exclusions, price, "order", "createdAt", "updatedAt", activity, description, "discountedPrice", "focusKeyphrase", "groupSize", "heroImage", "isAllInclusive", "isBestSeller", "mapUrl", "metaDescription", "originalPrice", "packingList", "priceRange", "primaryDestination", regions, "seoTitle", transport, "videoType", "videoUrl", "mapImage", "routeMap", published, "altitudeData", rate, rating) FROM stdin;
098b9921-2f90-4dd4-bf82-ce4ee7f70701	Bhaktapur  Day Tour– 4 hours	bhaktapur-day-tour	{}	4 Hours	March – May	Nepal	Moderate		Kathmandu	Kathmandu	B.B.	Bhaktapur Bhadgaon, also known as Bhaktapur, stood the capital of Nepal Valley once during the olden days. And today it is a treasure home of medieval arts and architectures. According to a legend this city was founded in 889 A.D. by late King Anand Deb who belonged to the famous Lichhabi dynasty. The whole city takes the relevant shape of a 'Khat-Kon' or David's Star. Bhaktapur signifies the "City of Devotees", with the sole majority of Hindus. The urban sector covers an area of 4 square miles. Pottery plus weaving form its traditional industries. They make the best yogurt of the kingdom; so it is known as 'juju dhou' or 'king curd.' Nowadays numerous cottage factories produce masks and wooden handicrafts as well. Bhaktapur is 13 kilometers direct east of Kathmandu and is accessible by public taxi vehicles including the bus, mini-bus, trolley-bus, cab and auto-rickshaw.\n\n<strong>Tour starts at - </strong>9 am\n<strong>Tour Ends at</strong> - 3 pm\n<strong>Trip Duration - </strong>6 hours\n<h2>What to see in Bhaktapur</h2>\n<h4>Bhaktapur Durbar Square</h4>\nBhaktapur, literally the city of Devotees', is renowned for its elegant art, fabulous culture, colorful festivals, traditional dances and the typical Newar life style. Tourists visiting Nepal feel their visit incomplete unless they get a mesmerizing glimpse of this ancient city of culture. Old dances and festival are still observed by the locals with the same fervor and enthusiasm as their ancestors did in the past. King Yarsh Mall (15th century) heavily fortified this city. The Hindus and the Buddhists have coexisted in harmony and drawn inspirations from each other through the ages. Bhaktapur is predominantly comprised of the peasantry, painting, carving, masonry, bronze casting, jewelry; pottery, etc are other traditional enterprises still existing. Monuments and artistic carvings on wood, stone and metals are strewn all over the historical core of the city. Alleys and narrow and zigzagged lanes lead you to see the Environment of Newar medieval settlements.\n<h4>Datta - Traya Square</h4>\nFurther to the north-east of Toumadhi Square is another interesting locality called Datta-Traya Square. In fact this is the second important urban spot of Bhadgaon. The Datta-Traya Temple also built by late King Vupatindra Malla in the 17th century is a famous pagoda carrying an amusing history. This is a wooden temple facing west; it is believed that the timber used for its relevant construction was sawed out of a single tree. So you can imagine how big the tree must have been. The square has been nomenclatures from the name of the Deity itself. The three-storied temple is dedicated to the three-headed Deity of the orthodox Hindus. It symbolizes the divine triad, a mere combination of Brahma (the Creator), Bishnu (the Preserver) and Maheshwor (the Destroyer). The square as a whole can be regarded as a marvelous gallery of intricate wood carvings. One can smell environments of medieval period around the square. In the periphery of the temple, you can also see monasteries, Vimsen Temple and a platform. There are a couple of handicraft quarters around where watching the skills of the carvers is a sheer joy. The Pujari-Math Temple has the renowned Peacock Window in the lane side facing the cardinal direction of east. It is a pure wooden structure, a master-piece indeed. Apart from these, there exist two special museums-the Metal Craft Museum and the Wood Craft Museum.\n<h4>Changu Narayan</h4>\nIt is Listed in the world cultural heritage, it is also a scenic spot situated at the altitude of about 1700, 4 km to the north of Bhaktapur. The temple is believed to be the oldest of all the temples of Nepal. It is said to have built by king Hari Datta Verma in 323 A.D. And most Authentic inscription locates in the precinct of changu Narayan is dated 464 AD. And it is accredited to the King Lichavi King Mandeva.		[]			200	0	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	\N	Bhaktapur Bhadgaon, also known as Bhaktapur, stood the capital of Nepal Valley once during the olden days. And today it is a treasure home of medieval	\N	\N	\N	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Bhaktapur-day-toursd.jpg	f	f	\N	\N	\N		\N	\N	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
0be6f957-bf9d-40b7-a3b5-174866affd89	Chandra Giri Cable Car - 3 hours	chandra-giri-cable-car-day-tour	{}	3 Hours		Nepal	Moderate		Kathmandu	Kathmandu	B.B.	Trip Duration – One day (4 hours)\nTour Starts at – 9 am\nTour Ends at – 1 am\nHighlight – Soaring peaks and breath taking views of whole Kathmandu Valley and Himalayan range\n\nChandragiri Hill, 7 km from Thankot, lies on the South-West of Kathmandu Valley and is 2551 meters from sea level. Soaring peaks and breath taking views of whole Kathmandu Valley covered with lush green blanket of flora makes Chandragiri truly a great bountiful and pristine landscape. The panoramic views of Kathmandu Valley &amp; Himalayan ranges from Annapurna to Everest makes any one feel like seeing whole Nepal from this hill.\n<h4>The Cost – 90 US$ per person</h4>		[]			350	0	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	\N	Trip Duration – One day (4 hours)\nTour Starts at – 9 am\nTour Ends at – 1 am\nHighlight – Soaring peaks and breath taking views of whole Kathmandu Valle	\N	\N	\N	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/chandragiri-cable-car.jpg	f	f	\N	\N	\N		\N	\N	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
6a967248-6205-4b28-84f7-005d34fa9982	Helicopter Sightseeing	helicopter-sightseeing	{}	14 Days	October	Nepal	Moderate		Kathmandu	Kathmandu	B.B.	Sightseeing by Helicopter around the Himalayas is one of the most pleasurable space journey for every visitors to get a closest, almost touching distance to the high Himalayan ranges. Helicopter tour over the Nepal Himalayas is truly awesome adventure for a lifetime filled with breathtaking scenery and glistering snow peak. Ever Peak Adventure customize Helicopter day tour as per the preferences of individual, family or friends. We have been running the Heli tour over the Himalayas covering the visit of all 8000 meter peaks.\n\nOur most popular Heli Package in the Himalayas\nEverest Helicopter Tour\n\nTour Duration                   :     3 hours 30 minutes including ground time in Everest View Hotel and Lukla\nMinimum Group Size      :     1 (Five-seated helicopter)\nBest time                           :     September – December and January and June\n\nEverest helicopter Sightseeing tour is one of the most popular Helicopter tour in the Nepal Himalayas. Our flight takes off at 7 am from Kathmandu airport. The helicopter take you over the Himalayas giving you a wonderful feeling of being close to the mountains. You will be stopping at Lukla to refuel on the way up and continue your space journey enjoying the views of the highest mountain on earth. You will land in Pheriche to get Oxygen cylinder before flying to Kalapather and Everest Base Camp. While flying you will be able to see the Mt. Everest in a closest point , spectacular mountains like Pumari, Lhotse, Nuptse, Ama Dablam, Thamaserku, Kongde, Gaurishanker, Number and many others places like Gokyo Lake, Chukung valley… On the way back you will be stopping at Everest View Hotel (highest located star hotel) for a cup of tea or breakfast/ lunch. The total flight hour will be about three hours. You will be given extra time for breakfast, photography, viewing mountain etc.\n\nItinerary:\n\n7:15 am       -     Fly from Pokhara airport to Annapurna Base Camp\n8:10 am       -     Land at Lukla for fuel\n8:30 am       -     Continue to over Himalayas\n9:00 am       -     Land in Pheriche for oxygen cylinder\n9:15 am       -     Continue toward EBC, Kalapathar\n10:00 am     -     Land in Everest view Hotel for cup of tea/ breakfast\n10:40 am     -     Fly to Kathmandu\n11:40 am     -     Land in Kathmandu\n\nCost:\n\nUS$ 5000 in group of 04 pax per helicopter\n\nCost inclusion:\nHelicopter tour\nAirport transfer by car\nAirport Tax\nPrice Excludes:\nNational park fee US$ 32 per person\nBreakfast/coffee at Syangboche\nAnnapurna Base Camp Helicopter Tour\n\nTour Duration                    :     1 hour including ground time in Annapurna Base Camp\nMinimum Group Size       :     1 (Four-seated helicopter)\nBest time                            :     September – December and January and June\n\nEver Peak Adventure one hour Heli tour from Pokhara to Annapurna Base Camp (ABC) commences from a great scenic flight towards South of Sarangkot via Fewa Lake or North of Sarangkot and Deurali towards stunning views of world’s top Himalayan ranges such as Machhapuchhre at 6,993 meters which dominates the beautiful valley. Also you can enjoy the beauty of Annapurna South, Patal Hiunchuli, Bharha Chuli, Annapurna I, II, III &amp; IV, Khangsar Kang, Tare Kang and Gangapurna and finally landing on the vast field at Annapurna base camp at 4,095 meters high. From there you can overlook striking views of Annapurna I, A III, A South and Huinchuli, Gangapurna, including the great North West Face of Mt. Machhapuchhre after an enjoyable stop with refreshment heading back to Pokhara.\nHimalayana Nomad Trek has been operating Heli tour regularly from Pokhara – Annapurna Base Camp (ABC) – Pokhara. (Normally we off the flight in monsoon time from May to September)\n\nABC Flight accommodates maximum 5 – 6 persons depending on the weight. The total bearable weight for the ABC flight from Pokhara is max. 470/480 kgs.\n\nWe also provide the flight on individual (per person) basis.\nThe two way flight timing for ABC from Pokhara is max. 30-35 minutes and the ground time at ABC is max. 30 minutes.\n\nItinerary:\n\n8:30 am      -     Fly from Pokhara airport to Annapurna Base Camp\n\n9:00 am      -     Land at Annapurna Base Camp\n\n9:30 am      -     Fly to Pokhara\n\n9:15 am      -     Pokhara Land\n\nCost:\n\nUS$ 2400 in group of 4/5 pax per helicopter\n\nCost inclusion:\nHelicopter tour\nAirport transfer by car\nAirport Tax\nPrice Exclusion:\nNational park fee US$ 32 per person\nBreakfast/coffee at Syangboche\nLangtang Valley Helicopter Tour\n\nTour Duration                  :     1 hour including ground time in Kyangjing Gompa\nMinimum Group Size     :     1 (Four-seated helicopter)\nBest time                          :     September – December and January and June\n\nIn a few minutes of Heli tour toward the northern part of Kathmandu takes you into the high alpine country. Langtang valley is inhabited by the Shepra and Tamang ethnic group. It is completely recovered from the massive avalanche due to earthquake in April 2015. Ever Peak Adventure organize Heli tour for individuals, couples, families and groups. You will be flying above the Gosaikunda Lake and to Kyanging Gompa and surrounding Langtang Himalayan ranges. You will be rewarded by breathtaking beautiful display of Himalayas\n\nItinerary:\n\n8:30 am       -     Fly from Kathmandu airport to Langtang Valley\n\n9:00 am       -     Land at Kyangjing Gompa\n\n10:15 am     -     Fly to Kathmandu\n\n10:45 am     -     Land in Kathmandu\n\nCost:\n\nUS$ 2000 in group of 4/5 pax per helicopter\n\nCost inclusion:\nHelicopter tour\nAirport transfer by car\nAirport Tax\nPrice Exclusion:\nNational park fee US$ 32 per person\nBreakfast/coffee at Kyangjing Gompa\nRara Lake Helicopter Tour (Far Western Nepal)\n\nTour Duration                  :     4 hour including ground time in Rara Lake\nMinimum Group Size     :     1 (Four-seated helicopter)\nBest time                          :     September – December and January and June\n\nA flight to Rara Lake is one of the most incredible and fascinating flight in all the Himalayan range lie northwest of Kathmandu in the remote area of Karnali. If you are looking of wilderness and solitude journey, this flight is an ideal choice. Rara Lake is the largest lake of Nepal located in high altitude. The untouched beauty of the Rara Lake is considered as the virgin blue lake. It is so clear which mirrors the snow capped Himalayas is ringed with blue pine, black juniper forest and Himalayan cypress Lake Rara is a popular serenity pilgrimage for Nepalese.\n\nThe national Park is one of the best places in Nepal to see wildlife: musk deer, leopards, ghorals, tahr, Himalayan black beer, and the rare red panda are all native. The park is also a bird watcher's delight, especially during November and April when many species of birds visit during their seasonal migration.\n\nItinerary:\n\n8:30 am             -     Fly from Kathmandu airport to Rara Lake\n\n10 am                -     Land Rara Lake\n\n10 to 12 pm      -     Spend time around Rara\n\n2:00 pm             -     Land in Kathmandu\n\nCost:\n\nUS$ 7500 in group of 4/5 pax per helicopter\n\nCost inclusion:\nHelicopter tour\nAirport transfer by car\nAirport Tax\nPrice Exclusion:\nRara Naional park fee US$ 32 per person\nBreakfast/coffee at Rara Lake\n\nIn the meanwhile, should you require further information, please revert to us at your convenience. We look forward to provide you best service in the safety and comfort of our helicopter		[]			0	0	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	\N	Sightseeing by Helicopter around the Himalayas is one of the most pleasurable space journey for every visitors to get a closest, almost touching dista	\N	\N	\N	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Helicopter-Sightseeing.jpg	f	f	\N	\N	\N		\N	\N	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
d02f4248-9957-44fb-8e80-82a39bc451ea	Bardia National Park Tour	bardia-national-park-tour	{}	7 Days	March -June , Oct -Dec	Nepal	Moderate		Kathmandu	Kathmandu	B.B.	<p data-start="0" data-end="644">A Kathmandu and Bardia Tour is a perfect combination of Nepal’s rich cultural heritage and unspoiled wilderness adventure. This unique travel experience connects the ancient temples and UNESCO World Heritage Sites of <span><span>Kathmandu</span></span> with the pristine jungle landscapes of <span><span>Bardiya National Park</span></span>, offering travelers an authentic and diverse Nepal holiday. Ideal for culture lovers, wildlife enthusiasts, photographers, and nature seekers, the Kathmandu and Bardia tour provides a balanced itinerary that showcases the spiritual heart of Nepal alongside one of the country’s best wildlife safari destinations.</p>\n<p data-start="646" data-end="1407">The journey typically begins in Kathmandu Valley, where visitors explore centuries-old temples, royal palaces, and sacred pilgrimage sites. Highlights include the holy <span><span>Pashupatinath Temple</span></span>, one of the most important Hindu temples dedicated to Lord Shiva, and the magnificent <span><span>Boudhanath Stupa</span></span>, a spiritual center for Tibetan Buddhism. Travelers also visit the hilltop shrine of <span><span>Swayambhunath</span></span>, which offers panoramic views of the Kathmandu Valley, and the historic <span><span>Kathmandu Durbar Square</span></span>, known for its ancient palaces and intricate wood carvings. These cultural landmarks provide deep insight into Nepal’s Hindu and Buddhist traditions, vibrant festivals, and architectural brilliance.</p>\n<p data-start="1409" data-end="2223">After exploring Kathmandu’s cultural treasures, the tour continues to Bardiya National Park in western Nepal. Less crowded and more remote than other wildlife reserves, Bardiya offers a truly wild and authentic jungle safari experience. Spanning vast areas of subtropical forest, grasslands, and river systems, Bardiya National Park is home to rare and endangered species, including the Bengal tiger, one-horned rhinoceros, wild elephants, swamp deer, and Gangetic dolphins. Jeep safaris, guided jungle walks, canoe rides along the Karnali River, and bird-watching tours allow visitors to experience Nepal’s incredible biodiversity up close. Because Bardiya is less commercialized, wildlife sightings are often more intimate and rewarding, making it a top choice for serious wildlife enthusiasts and photographers.</p>\n<p data-start="2225" data-end="2590">In addition to wildlife activities, the Kathmandu and Bardiya Tour also offers cultural encounters with the indigenous Tharu community. Visitors can explore traditional Tharu villages, learn about their unique customs and lifestyle, and enjoy local cultural dance performances. This cultural interaction adds depth and authenticity to the overall travel experience.</p>\n<p data-start="2592" data-end="2882">The best time to enjoy the Kathmandu and Bardiya Tour is during autumn (September to November) and spring (March to May), when the weather is clear and ideal for sightseeing and jungle activities. Winter months also provide good wildlife viewing opportunities, especially for bird watchers.</p>\n<p data-start="2884" data-end="3214" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Overall, the Kathmandu and Bardiya Tour is a perfect Nepal travel package that combines ancient heritage, spiritual exploration, and thrilling wildlife adventure. From the sacred temples of Kathmandu to the untamed jungles of Bardiya, this tour offers an unforgettable journey into the heart of Nepal’s culture and natural beauty.</p>	<h4 data-start="426" data-end="466">🏛️ Kathmandu Cultural Highlights</h4>\n<ul data-start="467" data-end="976">\n<li data-start="467" data-end="580">\n<p data-start="469" data-end="580">Explore the historic city of <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Kathmandu</span></span>, the cultural and spiritual heart of Nepal</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="581" data-end="708">\n<p data-start="583" data-end="708">Visit UNESCO World Heritage Sites including <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Pashupatinath Temple</span></span> and <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Boudhanath Stupa</span></span></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="709" data-end="803">\n<p data-start="711" data-end="803">Discover panoramic valley views from <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Swayambhunath</span></span> (Monkey Temple)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="804" data-end="887">\n<p data-start="806" data-end="887">Explore ancient palaces and courtyards at <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Kathmandu Durbar Square</span></span></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="888" data-end="976">\n<p data-start="890" data-end="976">Experience vibrant local markets, traditional art, architecture, and living heritage</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="978" data-end="1022">🐅 Bardiya Wildlife Safari Highlights</h4>\n<ul data-start="1023" data-end="1417">\n<li data-start="1023" data-end="1105">\n<p data-start="1025" data-end="1105">Adventure in the untouched wilderness of <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Bardiya National Park</span></span></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1106" data-end="1171">\n<p data-start="1108" data-end="1171">Jeep safari and guided jungle walks for Bengal tiger tracking</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1172" data-end="1260">\n<p data-start="1174" data-end="1260">Spot rare one-horned rhinoceros, wild elephants, swamp deer, and exotic bird species</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1261" data-end="1339">\n<p data-start="1263" data-end="1339">Canoe ride along the Karnali River to see crocodiles and Gangetic dolphins</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1340" data-end="1417">\n<p data-start="1342" data-end="1417">Less crowded and more authentic safari experience compared to other parks</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="1419" data-end="1457">🌿 Cultural &amp; Nature Experience</h4>\n<ul data-start="1458" data-end="1670">\n<li data-start="1458" data-end="1532">\n<p data-start="1460" data-end="1532">Visit traditional Tharu villages and enjoy cultural dance performances</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1533" data-end="1603">\n<p data-start="1535" data-end="1603">Ideal for wildlife photographers, bird watchers, and nature lovers</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1604" data-end="1670">\n<p data-start="1606" data-end="1670">Perfect balance of heritage tour and jungle adventure in Nepal</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="1672" data-end="1700">📅 Best Time to Visit</h4>\n<ul data-start="1701" data-end="1924">\n<li data-start="1701" data-end="1774">\n<p data-start="1703" data-end="1774">Autumn (September–November) – Clear skies and ideal safari conditions</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1775" data-end="1849">\n<p data-start="1777" data-end="1849">Spring (March–May) – Pleasant weather and excellent wildlife sightings</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1850" data-end="1924">\n<p data-start="1852" data-end="1924">Winter (December–February) – Best for bird watching and tiger tracking</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 data-start="1926" data-end="1970">Why Choose Kathmandu and Bardiya Tour?</h3>\n<ul data-start="1971" data-end="2251">\n<li data-start="1971" data-end="2053">\n<p data-start="1973" data-end="2053">Combination of cultural tour in Kathmandu and wildlife safari in western Nepal</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2054" data-end="2110">\n<p data-start="2056" data-end="2110">Ideal for families, couples, and adventure travelers</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="211