e flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn">\n<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow">\n<div class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" dir="auto" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="890b6d69-fff6-4ce1-9f28-71fd722c034c" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden">\n<div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling">\n<h4 data-start="30" data-end="42">🎒 Bags</h4>\n<p data-start="43" data-end="105">• Daypack (20–30L)<br data-start="61" data-end="64" />• Duffel bag or suitcase<br data-start="88" data-end="91" />• Rain cover</p>\n<h4 data-start="107" data-end="123">👕 Clothing</h4>\n<p data-start="124" data-end="231">• T-shirts and trekking pants<br data-start="153" data-end="156" />• Warm fleece or jacket<br data-start="179" data-end="182" />• Waterproof jacket<br data-start="201" data-end="204" />• Socks and undergarments</p>\n<h4 data-start="233" data-end="249">👟 Footwear</h4>\n<p data-start="250" data-end="306">• Comfortable hiking shoes<br data-start="276" data-end="279" />• Sandals or casual shoes</p>\n<h4 data-start="308" data-end="326">☀️ Essentials</h4>\n<p data-start="327" data-end="413">• Sun hat or cap<br data-start="343" data-end="346" />• Sunglasses<br data-start="358" data-end="361" />• Sunscreen and lip balm<br data-start="385" data-end="388" />• Reusable water bottle</p>\n<h4 data-start="415" data-end="434">📱 Electronics</h4>\n<p data-start="435" data-end="498">• Mobile phone &amp; charger<br data-start="459" data-end="462" />• Power bank<br data-start="474" data-end="477" />• Camera (optional)</p>\n<h4 data-start="500" data-end="524">🥾 For Dhampus Hike</h4>\n<p data-start="525" data-end="599">• Small daypack<br data-start="540" data-end="543" />• Trekking poles (optional)<br data-start="570" data-end="573" />• Headlamp or flashlight</p>\n<h4 data-start="601" data-end="623">🩹 Personal Items</h4>\n<p data-start="624" data-end="694" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">• Toiletries<br data-start="636" data-end="639" />• Personal medications<br data-start="661" data-end="664" />• Hand sanitizer and wet wipes</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"></div>\n<div class="mt-3 w-full empty:hidden">\n<div class="text-center"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="pointer-events-none -mt-px h-px translate-y-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom)-14*var(--spacing))]" aria-hidden="true"></div>\n	\N	\N	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
e55d67b8-73fc-4205-abb6-8c284c6469d4	Bhutan Cultural & Scenic Tour	bhutan-culture-tour	{}	7 Days / 6 Nights	March-Jun / Oct-Jan	Nepal	Moderate		Kathmandu	Kathmandu	B.B.	<p>Experience the beauty, culture and peaceful Himalayan atmosphere of Bhutan on this carefully designed 7-day tour from Nepal. With six nights in Bhutan, this journey combines the country’s most important cultural landmarks with beautiful mountain scenery, traditional villages and the unforgettable Tiger’s Nest Monastery.</p>\n<p>The adventure begins with a scenic flight from Kathmandu to Paro, where Bhutan’s spectacular Himalayan landscape welcomes you. After meeting your local guide, drive through the beautiful Paro Valley toward Thimphu, Bhutan’s capital. The journey itself is part of the experience, with green hills, traditional houses, prayer flags and dramatic mountain scenery along the road.</p>\n<p>Spend two nights in Thimphu exploring the capital and experiencing Bhutanese culture. Visit the impressive Buddha Dordenma Statue, National Memorial Chorten, Tashichho Dzong and local handicraft areas. You will also have time to walk around the town and experience the relaxed lifestyle of the Bhutanese people.</p>\n<p>The journey then continues to Punakha through the spectacular Dochula Pass. On clear days, the pass provides beautiful views of the snow-covered Himalayan peaks. In Punakha, visit the magnificent Punakha Dzong, one of Bhutan’s most beautiful and historically important fortresses, dramatically situated between two rivers.</p>\n<p>From Punakha, continue to the peaceful Gangtey Valley. Surrounded by forests and wide open landscapes, Gangtey provides a wonderful opportunity to experience Bhutan away from busy tourist areas. Visit Gangtey Monastery and enjoy a gentle walk through the valley and surrounding villages.</p>\n<p>The final part of the journey takes you back to Paro, where you will spend two nights. The highlight is a hike to the world-famous Taktsang Monastery, better known as Tiger’s Nest. Built dramatically on a cliffside above Paro Valley, this sacred monastery is one of Bhutan’s most iconic destinations. The hike takes several hours and rewards you with beautiful mountain views and an unforgettable cultural experience.</p>\n<p>Your final evening in Paro is relaxed, giving you time to explore the town, shop for traditional handicrafts or enjoy the peaceful surroundings before your flight back to Kathmandu the following day.</p>\nThis 6-night, 7-day Bhutan tour is an excellent choice for travelers who want to experience Bhutan’s culture, Buddhist heritage, Himalayan scenery and traditional way of life in a comfortable and well-balanced itinerary.	<div class="" data-turn-id-container="e944cc97-36e2-42a8-88a6-96301403cf22" data-is-intersecting="true">\n<div class="qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot">\n<div class="" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:958d0081-1395-45e0-8dea-90c3d866500a-7" data-is-intersecting="true">\n<section class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:958d0081-1395-45e0-8dea-90c3d866500a-7" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:958d0081-1395-45e0-8dea-90c3d866500a-7" data-testid="conversation-turn-16" data-turn="assistant">\n<div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-8 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)">\n<div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-wi