ce00caec-316c-4558-beb5-9a1e07d45c7c	Bhutan Spiritual & Meditation Tour	bhutan-spiritual-meditation-tour	{}	7 Days	March–May &amp; September–November	Nepal	Moderate		Kathmandu	Kathmandu	B.B.	<p data-start="219" data-end="595">The <strong data-start="223" data-end="261">Bhutan Spiritual &amp; Meditation Tour</strong> is a transformative journey designed for travelers seeking inner peace, mindfulness, and spiritual awakening in the serene Himalayan kingdom of <span><span>Bhutan</span></span>. Known as the last Buddhist kingdom, Bhutan offers a deeply spiritual environment filled with monasteries, temples, prayer flags, and meditation caves.</p>\n<p data-start="597" data-end="972">This tour takes you through sacred destinations like Paro, Thimphu, and Punakha, where you will meditate in ancient monasteries, interact with monks, and experience Bhutan’s rich Buddhist philosophy. Meditation sessions in peaceful natural settings and holy sites provide a unique opportunity for self-reflection and mental relaxation.</p>	<ul data-start="995" data-end="1417">\n<li data-section-id="19ihfaf" data-start="995" data-end="1050">Meditation sessions in monasteries and sacred caves</li>\n<li data-section-id="1dz5ubp" data-start="1051" data-end="1105">Visit iconic <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Tiger’s Nest Monastery</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="1c4xwej" data-start="1106" data-end="1165">Spiritual teachings and interaction with Buddhist monks</li>\n<li data-section-id="cs5ezz" data-start="1166" data-end="1229">Visit <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Dochula Pass</span></span> with 108 stupas</li>\n<li data-section-id="1p4gkm3" data-start="1230" data-end="1273">Explore peaceful valleys like Phobjikha</li>\n<li data-section-id="1dztsci" data-start="1274" data-end="1330">Experience Bhutanese spiritual lifestyle and rituals</li>\n<li data-section-id="1tn71jq" data-start="1331" data-end="1380">Yoga, mindfulness &amp; self-reflection practices</li>\n<li data-section-id="s4mz1x" data-start="1381" data-end="1417">Visit ancient temples and dzongs</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Arrive at Paro International Airport and transfer to your hotel. Meet your guide and receive a briefing about your spiritual journey. Spend the day relaxing and acclimatizing to Bhutan’s peaceful environment. In the evening, enjoy a gentle meditation session or short walk through Paro town to begin your mindfulness experience.\\";", "elev": 2200, "title": "Day 01: Arrival in Paro (2,200 m)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Visit sacred temples and monasteries in Paro valley. Participate in guided meditation sessions and explore spiritual sites associated with Guru Rinpoche. Experience peaceful surroundings and begin deeper mindfulness practices.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 02: Paro Spiritual Exploration &amp; Meditation"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Hike to the legendary Tiger’s Nest Monastery, perched dramatically on a cliff. This sacred site is believed to be where Guru Rinpoche meditated. Enjoy meditation moments and breathtaking views of Paro valley.\\";", "elev": 3120, "title": "Day 03: Hike to Tiger’s Nest Monastery (3,120 m)\\";"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Drive to Thimphu and visit spiritual landmarks such as monasteries, memorial chortens, and Buddha statues. Participate in meditation sessions guided by monks and learn about Bhutanese Buddhist philosophy.", "elev": 2320, "title": "Day 04: Drive Paro to Thimphu (2,320 m)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Drive via Dochula Pass, offering stunning Himalayan views and meditation spots. Continue to Punakha and visit sacred monasteries for peaceful reflection and spiritual learning. Meditation at tranquil sites enhances inner peace.", "elev": 3100, "title": "Day 05: Thimphu to Punakha via Dochula Pass (3,100 m)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Spend a full day in meditation retreat guided by monks or spiritual practitioners. Practice mindfulness, breathing techniques, and reflection sessions in peaceful surroundings such as monasteries or nature sites.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 06: Full Day Meditation &amp; Retreat Experience"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Return to Paro with scenic views and transfer to the airport for departure. Reflect on your spiritual journey and experiences gained throughout the tour.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 07: Return to Paro &amp; Departure"}]	<ul data-start="1722" data-end="2050">\n<li data-section-id="14iwjbm" data-start="1722" data-end="1751">Airport pickup &amp; drop-off</li>\n<li data-section-id="1fjk3" data-start="1752" data-end="1777">Bhutan visa &amp; permits</li>\n<li data-section-id="a1w3c1" data-start="1778" data-end="1813">Hotel / monastery accommodation</li>\n<li data-section-id="8jb9l3" data-start="1814" data-end="1854">All meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1r4es0z" data-start="1855" data-end="1893">Private transportation (SUV/coach)</li>\n<li data-section-id="v5ene" data-start="1894" data-end="1933">Professional English-speaking guide</li>\n<li data-section-id="1bdydmn" data-start="1934" data-end="1968">Meditation sessions with monks</li>\n<li data-section-id="1dnahta" data-start="1969" data-end="2007">Entrance fees &amp; government royalty</li>\n<li data-section-id="v4jim5" data-start="2008" data-end="2050">Cultural programs &amp; spiritual sessions</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul data-start="2079" data-end="2289">\n<li data-section-id="sckugo" data-start="2079" data-end="2104">International airfare</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gecbsa" data-start="2105" data-end="2125">Travel insurance</li>\n<li data-section-id="i12pz7" data-start="2126" data-end="2166">Personal expenses (shopping, drinks)</li>\n<li data-section-id="50jr5y" data-start="2167" data-end="2192">Tips for guide/driver</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mvmhoi" data-start="2193" data-end="2235">Additional private meditation retreats</li>\n<li data-section-id="1h0ui8f" data-start="2236" data-end="2289">Expenses due to delays (weather, road conditions)</li>\n</ul>\n	0	0	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	\N	<p data-start="219" data-end="595">The <strong data-start="223" data-end="261">Bhutan Spiritual &amp; Meditation Tour</strong> is a transformative jou	\N	\N	\N	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/bhutan-spiritual.jpg	f	f	\N	\N	\N	<ul data-start="2332" data-end="2589">\n<li data-section-id="175dv0s" data-start="2332" data-end="2381">Comfortable clothing (modest for monasteries)</li>\n<li data-section-id="thiij6" data-start="2382" data-end="2412">Light jacket / warm layers</li>\n<li data-section-id="40v7fj" data-start="2413" data-end="2442">Comfortable walking shoes</li>\n<li data-section-id="13sff5b" data-start="2443" data-end="2481">Meditation shawl or mat (optional)</li>\n<li data-section-id="6jdbki" data-start="2482" data-end="2505">Personal toiletries</li>\n<li data-section-id="v5wqrd" data-start="2506" data-end="2522">Water bottle</li>\n<li data-section-id="5paajv" data-start="2523" data-end="2565">Notebook (for reflection &amp; journaling)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mb52x7" data-start="2566" data-end="2589">Personal medication</li>\n</ul>\n	\N	\N	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
6c40e725-cf3d-4888-9b90-6ea8a429b73b	Bhutan Honeymoon Tour	bhutan-honeymoon-tour	{}	6 Days	Spring &amp; Autumn	Nepal	Moderate		Kathmandu	Kathmandu	B.B.	<p data-start="190" data-end="508">The Bhutan Honeymoon Tour is a romantic and peaceful getaway designed for couples seeking privacy, natural beauty, and cultural charm in the Himalayan kingdom of Bhutan. Known for its serene landscapes, spiritual ambiance, and warm hospitality, Bhutan offers a perfect setting for unforgettable honeymoon memories.</p>\n<p data-start="510" data-end="915">This tour covers the scenic valleys of <span><span>Paro</span></span>, the vibrant capital <span><span>Thimphu</span></span>, and the picturesque Punakha valley. Couples can enjoy romantic walks, monastery visits, luxury stays, and breathtaking views of the Himalayas. The highlight includes a hike to the iconic <span><span>Tiger’s Nest Monastery</span></span>, symbolizing spiritual connection and love.</p>	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="1pw810d" data-start="938" data-end="991">Romantic getaway in peaceful Himalayan landscapes</li>\n<li data-section-id="egiaat" data-start="992" data-end="1046">Visit iconic <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Tiger’s Nest Monastery</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="1io4kwq" data-start="1047" data-end="1138">Explore <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Thimphu</span></span> and <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Punakha</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="gf20ly" data-start="1139" data-end="1197">Scenic drive via <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Dochula Pass</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="t46icc" data-start="1198" data-end="1243">Candlelight dinner &amp; romantic hotel stays</li>\n<li data-section-id="ply75q" data-start="1244" data-end="1289">Traditional Bhutanese cultural experience</li>\n<li data-section-id="t0bs2j" data-start="1290" data-end="1337">Stunning mountain views &amp; photography spots</li>\n<li data-section-id="7o4n40" data-start="1338" data-end="1384">Private and peaceful honeymoon environment</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Arrive at Paro International Airport where you will be warmly welcomed and transferred to your hotel. After check-in, relax and enjoy the peaceful atmosphere of Bhutan. Couples can take a romantic walk around the valley and enjoy their first evening together with a special welcome dinner arranged at the hotel.", "elev": 2200, "title": "Day 01: Arrival in Paro (2,200 m)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Explore Paro valley including monasteries, temples, and cultural sites. Enjoy peaceful surroundings, romantic views, and private moments together. Visit local markets and enjoy a relaxed evening.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 02: Paro Sightseeing &amp; Romantic Experiences"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Hike to the iconic Tiger’s Nest Monastery, perched dramatically on a cliff. This is one of Bhutan’s most sacred sites and a highlight of your honeymoon journey. Enjoy stunning views, peaceful surroundings, and unforgettable shared moments.\\";s:", "elev": 3120, "title": "Day 03: Hike to Tiger’s Nest Monastery (3,120 m)\\";"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Drive to Thimphu, Bhutan’s capital city. Visit landmarks such as Buddha Dordenma, monasteries, and markets. Enjoy a romantic evening exploring the city or relaxing at your hotel.\\";", "elev": 2320, "title": "Day 04: Drive Paro to Thimphu (2,320 m)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Drive through Dochula Pass offering panoramic Himalayan views. Continue to Punakha and visit beautiful monasteries and valleys. Enjoy a romantic riverside environment and peaceful surroundings.", "elev": 3100, "title": "Day 05: Thimphu to Punakha via Dochula Pass (3,100 m)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Drive back to Paro with scenic views along the way. Transfer to the airport for your departure, carrying unforgettable memories of your romantic Bhutan honeymoon.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 06: Return to Paro &amp; Departure"}]	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="14iwjbm" data-start="1690" data-end="1719">Airport pickup &amp; drop-off</li>\n<li data-section-id="1fjk3" data-start="1720" data-end="1745">Bhutan visa &amp; permits</li>\n<li data-section-id="b8k8hb" data-start="1746" data-end="1795">Hotel / resort accommodation (romantic setup)</li>\n<li data-section-id="8jb9l3" data-start="1796" data-end="1836">All meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner)</li>\n<li data-section-id="uh0kbs" data-start="1837" data-end="1870">Private vehicle for all tours</li>\n<li data-section-id="v5ene" data-start="1871" data-end="1910">Professional English-speaking guide</li>\n<li data-section-id="14edd5e" data-start="1911" data-end="1965">Honeymoon special arrangements (cake / decoration)</li>\n<li data-section-id="2pscnx" data-start="1966" data-end="1994">Sightseeing &amp; entry fees</li>\n<li data-section-id="1i6e45g" data-start="1995" data-end="2025">Government taxes &amp; royalty</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="sckugo" data-start="2054" data-end="2079">International airfare</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gecbsa" data-start="2080" data-end="2100">Travel insurance</li>\n<li data-section-id="i12pz7" data-start="2101" data-end="2141">Personal expenses (shopping, drinks)</li>\n<li data-section-id="50jr5y" data-start="2142" data-end="2167">Tips for guide/driver</li>\n<li data-section-id="bkjnx" data-start="2168" data-end="2198">Additional luxury upgrades</li>\n<li data-section-id="1eyauw2" data-start="2199" data-end="2225">Expenses due to delays</li>\n</ul>\n	0	0	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	\N	<p data-start="190" data-end="508">The Bhutan Honeymoon Tour is a romantic and peaceful getaway designed for couples seeking privacy, natural beauty, 	\N	\N	\N	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/bhutanhoneymoon1.webp	f	f	\N	\N	\N	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="8kg8r4" data-start="2268" data-end="2292">Comfortable clothing</li>\n<li data-section-id="14xt608" data-start="2293" data-end="2324">Light jacket / warm clothes</li>\n<li data-section-id="bkzkkb" data-start="2325" data-end="2342">Walking shoes</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mp49jy" data-start="2343" data-end="2369">Sunglasses &amp; sunscreen</li>\n<li data-section-id="ks61g1" data-start="2370" data-end="2380">Camera</li>\n<li data-section-id="6jdbki" data-start="2381" data-end="2404">Personal toiletries</li>\n<li data-section-id="1euyxpo" data-start="2405" data-end="2425">Travel documents</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mb52x7" data-start="2426" data-end="2449">Personal medication</li>\n</ul>\n	\N	\N	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
234c8495-ddf7-4992-8482-3b22b60be6bd	Bhutan Adventure Tour	bhutan-adventure-tour	{}	6 Days	March–May &amp; September–November	Nepal	Moderate		Kathmandu	Kathmandu	B.B.	<p data-start="191" data-end="501">The <strong data-start="195" data-end="220">Bhutan Adventure Tour</strong> is an exciting blend of hiking, nature exploration, and cultural discovery in the pristine Himalayan kingdom of Bhutan. This tour is perfect for travelers who want light adventure without extreme trekking, combining scenic hikes, mountain views, and visits to ancient monasteries.</p>\n<p data-start="503" data-end="857">You will explore the valleys of <span><span>Paro</span></span>, the capital <span><span>Thimphu</span></span>, and the peaceful Punakha region. The journey includes adventurous hikes to iconic sites like <span><span>Tiger’s Nest Monastery</span></span>, nature walks, and exploration of hidden trails, offering a perfect balance of adventure and culture.</p>	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="2dn8g1" data-start="880" data-end="929">Hike to <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Tiger’s Nest Monastery</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="1k7sm8r" data-start="930" data-end="973">Scenic trekking trails and nature walks</li>\n<li data-section-id="1io4kwq" data-start="974" data-end="1065">Explore <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Thimphu</span></span> and <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Punakha</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="6u5ipz" data-start="1066" data-end="1117">Drive via <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Dochula Pass</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="1nml0jo" data-start="1118" data-end="1158">River valley views and forest trails</li>\n<li data-section-id="qh5vdj" data-start="1159" data-end="1204">Cultural visits to monasteries and dzongs</li>\n<li data-section-id="896v8x" data-start="1205" data-end="1252">Bird watching and photography opportunities</li>\n<li data-section-id="vse3gj" data-start="1253" data-end="1296">Peaceful Himalayan adventure experience</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Arrive in Paro and enjoy a scenic drive to Thimphu, Bhutan’s capital. Along the way, experience the beautiful landscapes, rivers, and traditional villages. After hotel check-in, visit local markets and cultural sites. This day allows you to acclimate and get introduced to Bhutanese culture and lifestyle in a peaceful environment.\\";", "elev": 2200, "title": "Day 01: Arrival in Paro (2,200 m) &amp; Transfer to Thimphu (2,334 m)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Explore major attractions in Thimphu including Buddha Dordenma, Memorial Chorten, and local handicraft markets. Learn about Bhutanese traditions, culture, and government systems while visiting monasteries and cultural institutions.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 02: Thimphu Sightseeing Tour"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Drive back to Paro and explore local attractions such as Paro Dzong and the National Museum. Enjoy scenic views of valleys and traditional Bhutanese architecture.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 03: Drive Thimphu to Paro &amp; Sightseeing"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Embark on a rewarding hike to the iconic Tiger’s Nest Monastery. The trail passes through pine forests and offers breathtaking views. This spiritual site is one of Bhutan’s most sacred landmarks and a highlight of the trip.\\";s:", "elev": 3120, "title": "Day 04: Hike to Tiger’s Nest Monastery (3,120 m)\\";"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Enjoy a leisure day exploring Paro valley, local villages, and traditional Bhutanese life. You may visit farmhouses, interact with locals, or relax in nature.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 05: Excursion &amp; Cultural Experience in Paro"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Transfer to the airport for your departure. Your Bhutan adventure concludes with unforgettable memories of culture, nature, and spiritual experiences.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 06: Departure from Paro"}]	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="14iwjbm" data-start="1598" data-end="1627">Airport pickup &amp; drop-off</li>\n<li data-section-id="1fjk3" data-start="1628" data-end="1653">Bhutan visa &amp; permits</li>\n<li data-section-id="1o1sl40" data-start="1654" data-end="1685">Hotel / lodge accommodation</li>\n<li data-section-id="8jb9l3" data-start="1686" data-end="1726">All meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1jl2m7s" data-start="1727" data-end="1765">Private vehicle for transportation</li>\n<li data-section-id="ml04yh" data-start="1766" data-end="1788">Professional guide</li>\n<li data-section-id="1tvk7ct" data-start="1789" data-end="1824">Sightseeing &amp; hiking activities</li>\n<li data-section-id="2da8e6" data-start="1825" data-end="1860">Entry fees &amp; government royalty</li>\n<li data-section-id="1ot7a29" data-start="1861" data-end="1882">First aid support</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="sckugo" data-start="1911" data-end="1936">International airfare</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gecbsa" data-start="1937" data-end="1957">Travel insurance</li>\n<li data-section-id="f3p6kj" data-start="1958" data-end="1998">Personal expenses (drinks, shopping)</li>\n<li data-section-id="50jr5y" data-start="1999" data-end="2024">Tips for guide/driver</li>\n<li data-section-id="1tdr8ft" data-start="2025" data-end="2069">Extra adventure activities not mentioned</li>\n<li data-section-id="1eyauw2" data-start="2070" data-end="2096">Expenses due to delays</li>\n</ul>\n	0	0	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	\N	<p data-start="191" data-end="501">The <strong data-start="195" data-end="220">Bhutan Adventure Tour</strong> is an exciting blend of hiking, nature e	\N	\N	\N	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/bhutan-1.jpg	f	f	\N	\N	\N	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="k1vozo" data-start="2223" data-end="2251">Comfortable hiking shoes</li>\n<li data-section-id="15500da" data-start="2252" data-end="2279">Warm clothing (layered)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mp49jy" data-start="2280" data-end="2306">Sunglasses &amp; sunscreen</li>\n<li data-section-id="11p2dfp" data-start="2307" data-end="2325">Small backpack</li>\n<li data-section-id="1ov3723" data-start="2326" data-end="2349">Camera / smartphone</li>\n<li data-section-id="6dl1ug" data-start="2350" data-end="2374">Personal medications</li>\n<li data-section-id="v5wqrd" data-start="2375" data-end="2391">Water bottle</li>\n</ul>\n	\N	\N	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
ff8f3778-6e9e-4e74-b974-1c0585119288	Lhasa Cultural & Heritage Tour – 4/5 Days	lhasa-cultural-heritage-tour-4-5-days	{}	4 Days	April–June &amp; September–November	Nepal	Moderate		Kathmandu	Kathmandu	B.B.	<p data-start="258" data-end="599">The <strong data-start="262" data-end="296">Lhasa Cultural &amp; Heritage Tour</strong> is a short yet deeply enriching journey into the spiritual and cultural heart of <span><span>Tibet</span></span>. Centered in the historic city of <span><span>Lhasa</span></span>, this tour introduces travelers to Tibetan Buddhism, ancient architecture, and traditional Himalayan lifestyle.</p>\n<p data-start="601" data-end="871">You will explore UNESCO-listed landmarks like the magnificent <span><span>Potala Palace</span></span>, sacred monasteries, and vibrant local markets. This tour is ideal for those seeking cultural immersion, spiritual insight, and a short yet meaningful Tibetan experience.</p>	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="r4m858" data-start="897" data-end="955">Visit the iconic <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Potala Palace</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="1d7etjg" data-start="956" data-end="1005">Explore <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Jokhang Temple</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="pwaimk" data-start="1006" data-end="1063">Walk around Barkhor Street (local pilgrimage circuit)</li>\n<li data-section-id="ncr7c6" data-start="1064" data-end="1129">Witness monk debates at <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Sera Monastery</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="126454j" data-start="1130" data-end="1183">Experience Tibetan culture, religion &amp; daily life</li>\n<li data-section-id="hlctpb" data-start="1184" data-end="1234">Visit traditional monasteries &amp; heritage sites</li>\n<li data-section-id="qvxgxg" data-start="1235" data-end="1281">Short and easy high-altitude cultural tour</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Arrive in Lhasa and transfer to your hotel. Spend the rest of the day resting and acclimatizing to the high altitude. Avoid heavy activities and stay hydrated. In the evening, your guide will brief you about the tour, culture, and safety precautions. This day is essential for adjusting to Tibet’s altitude before starting sightseeing.\\";", "elev": 3650, "title": "Day 01: Arrival in Lhasa (3,650 m)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Visit the world-famous Potala Palace, once the residence of the Dalai Lama. Continue to Jokhang Temple, the most revered religious site in Tibet. Walk around Barkhor Street and experience local culture, markets, and pilgrims performing traditional rituals.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 02: Lhasa Sightseeing – Potala Palace &amp; Jokhang Temple\\";"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Explore Drepung Monastery, one of the largest monasteries in Tibet, followed by Sera Monastery. Witness the famous monk debate sessions, a unique tradition of Tibetan Buddhist education. This day offers deep insight into monastic life, philosophy, and spiritual practices.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 03: Lhasa Sightseeing – Sera &amp; Drepung Monasteries\\";"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Transfer to the airport for your departure. Your Lhasa Cultural Tour concludes with unforgettable memories of Tibetan culture, spirituality, and heritage.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 04: Departure from Lhasa"}]	<ul data-start="1578" data-end="1820">\n<li data-section-id="zjc9ah" data-start="1578" data-end="1601">Tibet Travel Permit</li>\n<li data-section-id="14iwjbm" data-start="1602" data-end="1631">Airport pickup &amp; drop-off</li>\n<li data-section-id="1pazwe9" data-start="1632" data-end="1666">Hotel accommodation (BB basis)</li>\n<li data-section-id="58c038" data-start="1667" data-end="1702">Private vehicle for sightseeing</li>\n<li data-section-id="11oanq0" data-start="1703" data-end="1733">Professional Tibetan guide</li>\n<li data-section-id="1o6urhh" data-start="1734" data-end="1781">All entrance fees (monuments &amp; monasteries)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1b55flg" data-start="1782" data-end="1820">Government taxes &amp; service charges</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="sckugo" data-start="1852" data-end="1877">International airfare</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gvqe0e" data-start="1878" data-end="1896">China visa fee</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gecbsa" data-start="1897" data-end="1917">Travel insurance</li>\n<li data-section-id="1be9l0o" data-start="1918" data-end="1936">Lunch &amp; dinner</li>\n<li data-section-id="i12pz7" data-start="1937" data-end="1977">Personal expenses (shopping, drinks)</li>\n<li data-section-id="50jr5y" data-start="1978" data-end="2003">Tips for guide/driver</li>\n<li data-section-id="eep6w7" data-start="2004" data-end="2026">Extra hotel nights</li>\n</ul>\n	0	0	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	2026-08-23 02:08:08.019	\N	<p data-start="258" data-end="599">The <strong data-start="262" data-end="296">Lhasa Cultural &amp; Heritage Tour</strong> is a short yet deeply enric	\N	\N	\N		f	f	\N	\N	\N	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="1uwp67e" data-start="2072" data-end="2110">Warm clothing (temperature varies)</li>\n<li data-section-id="40v7fj" data-start="2111" data-end="2140">Comfortable walking shoes</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mp49jy" data-start="2141" data-end="2167">Sunglasses &amp; sunscreen</li>\n<li data-section-id="1spx0mq" data-start="2168" data-end="2207">Personal medications (for altitude)</li>\n<li data-section-id="v5wqrd" data-start="2208" data-end="2224">Water bottle</li>\n<li data-section-id="1ov3723" data-start="2225" data-end="2248">Camera / smartphone</li>\n</ul>\n	\N	\N	{}	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	\N	\N
e665fcc1-bacd-4d4b-bb7d-2e42720e2d87	Tibet Overland Tour (Lhasa to Kathmandu) – 7/8 Days	tibet-overland-tour-lhasa-to-kathmandu-7-8-days	{}	7–8 Days	April–June &amp; September–November	Nepal	Moderate		Kathmandu	Kathmandu	B.B.	<p data-start="270" data-end="631">The <strong data-start="274" data-end="321">Tibet Overland Tour from Lhasa to Kathmandu</strong> is one of the most scenic cross-border journeys in the Himalayas. This adventure takes you from the spiritual city of <span><span>Lhasa</span></span> across the vast Tibetan Plateau, through high mountain passes, pristine lakes, and traditional villages, ending in <span><span>Kathmandu</span></span>.</p>\n<p data-start="633" data-end="969">Travel along the legendary Friendship Highway, visiting iconic sites such as <span><span>Yamdrok Lake</span></span> and the north face of <span><span>Mount Everest</span></span> near <span><span>Rongbuk Monastery</span></span>. This tour combines culture, adventure, and breathtaking landscapes, making it one of the most popular Tibet journeys.</p>	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="36l9ox" data-start="995" data-end="1104">Scenic overland drive from <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Lhasa</span></span> to <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Kathmandu</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="dm5q73" data-start="1105" data-end="1192">Visit <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Potala Palace</span></span> &amp; <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Jokhang Temple</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="1w21300" data-start="1193" data-end="1254">Stunning views of <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Yamdrok Lake</span></span></li>\n<li data-section-id="1ez0uhw" data-start="1255" data-end="1296">Explore Everest north face at Rongbuk</li>\n<li data-section-id="10cmvn2" data-start="1297" data-end="1346">Drive through high Himalayan passes (5,000m+)</li>\n<li data-section-id="6dn88d" data-start="1347" data-end="1388">Unique Tibetan culture and landscapes</li>\n<li data-section-id="1jtdybr" data-start="1389" data-end="1428">Cross Tibet–Nepal border at Gyirong</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Arrive in Lhasa and transfer to your hotel. Spend the day resting and acclimatizing to the high altitude. Avoid physical exertion and stay hydrated. In the evening, attend a short briefing about the overland journey, safety precautions, and itinerary details. This day is crucial for adjusting to the altitude before starting exploration.", "elev": 3650, "title": "Day 01: Arrival in Lhasa (3,650 m)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Visit Potala Palace and Jokhang Temple. Explore Barkhor Street and experience Tibetan culture, pilgrims, and local markets.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 02: Lhasa Sightseeing Tour"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Drive through high passes and visit Yamdrok Lake. Continue via Gyantse to Shigatse, enjoying panoramic Himalayan scenery and traditional villages.", "elev": 3900, "title": "Day 03: Lhasa to Gyantse to Shigatse (3,900 m)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Drive across the Tibetan plateau towards Tingri with distant views of the Himalayas. The landscape becomes more rugged and remote.", "elev": 4300, "title": "Day 04: Shigatse to Tingri (4,300 m)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Drive to Everest Base Camp (Tibet side) and visit Rongbuk Monastery. Enjoy breathtaking views of Everest’s north face.\\";", "elev": 5200, "title": "Day 05: Tingri to Everest Base Camp (5,200 m)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Descend from Everest region to Gyirong near the Nepal border. The landscape gradually changes to green valleys.", "elev": 2700, "title": "Day 06: EBC to Gyirong (2,700 m)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Cross the Tibet–Nepal border and drive to Kathmandu. Enjoy changing landscapes from Tibet plateau to Nepal hills.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 07: Gyirong to Kathmandu"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "Free day in Kathmandu or transfer to the airport for departure.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 08: Departure / Rest Day in Kathmandu (Optional)"}]	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="y4ejn1" data-start="1759" data-end="1806">Tibet Travel Permit &amp; all necessary permits</li>\n<li data-section-id="115e19r" data-start="1807" data-end="1834">Airport pickup in Lhasa</li>\n<li data-section-id="1tuh4hc" data-start="1835" data-end="1880">Hotel accommodation (Lhasa &amp; major towns)</li>\n<li data-section-id="uqp48" data-start="1881" data-end="1914">Guesthouse/lodge near Everest</li>\n<li data-section-id="15smeij" data-start="1915" data-end="1950">Private vehicle for entire tour</li>\n<li data-section-id="11oanq0" data-start="1951" data-end="1981">Professional Tibetan guide</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gnejw8" data-start="1982" data-end="2003">All entrance fees</li>\n<li data-section-id="11x91m7" data-start="2004" data-end="2025">Breakfast (daily)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1hsoxc6" data-start="2026" data-end="2046">Government taxes</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="sckugo" data-start="2078" data-end="2103">International airfare</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gvqe0e" data-start="2104" data-end="2122">China visa fee</li>\n<li data-section-id="116xcid" data-start="2123" data-end="2141">Nepal visa fee</li>\n<li data-section-id="1be9l0o" data-start="2142" data-end="2160">Lunch &amp; dinner</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gecbsa" data-start="2161" data-end="2181">Travel insurance</li>\n<li data-section-id="1fc0b8z" data-start="2182" data-end="2203">Personal expenses</li>\n<li data-section-id="50jr5y" data-start="2204" data-end="2229">Tips for guide/driver</li>\n<li data-section-id="1k9qu5z" data-start="2230" data-end="2249">Kathmandu hotel</li>\n</ul>\n	0	0	2026-08-23 02: