cmt563w1u0005kbrluwlppss0	nagarkot-dhulikhel-namobuddha-hike	Nagarkot-Dhulikhel-Namobuddha hike	<h2 data-section-id="rzkdgm" data-start="229" data-end="240">Overview</h2>\n<p data-start="242" data-end="590">The <strong data-start="246" data-end="2	<h2 data-section-id="rzkdgm" data-start="229" data-end="240">Overview</h2>\n<p data-start="242" data-end="590">The <strong data-start="246" data-end="284"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=3d80f3da76bac683&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnvBG-zZCILjmzwghZpL1IKkwGtlxQ:1783140438685&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832U1CFDVh7aOiOPRjGOuZsttGjVtm3SQ8YygAFFH6bpyGlf4c5PR0UmHncQtj0N3hy6ucswm9SgR1T1FYCn8f_OfZCKzHYL5PQuYxbLC1sKJr_IIkTQdXdgjKK7NZHtyPuRbbz7vL4oeeC7x1tW31_lwhvmb2OVByEyVTUBNw1lqcs4F4yQ&amp;q=nagarkot+hotels&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwiJuLrjm7iVAxWxyjgGHYXyIwMQtKgLegQIExAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Nagarkot</a> Dhulikhel Namobuddha Hike</strong> is one of the best short hiking adventures near Kathmandu. It combines beautiful Himalayan views, peaceful hill trails, traditional villages, and important cultural sites. Therefore, it is an excellent choice for travelers who want to experience nature and local culture without trekking at high altitude.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="1s69itg" data-start="592" data-end="632">Scenic Trail and Cultural Experience</h3>\n<p data-start="634" data-end="1071">The journey begins with a drive to Nagarkot, a famous hill station known for its spectacular sunrise over the Himalayas. From there, the trail follows forest paths and quiet ridges to Dhulikhel, offering panoramic views of the Langtang, Ganesh, Everest, and Gaurishankar ranges. Along the way, you pass charming villages, green farmland, and terraced hills. In addition, you can meet local people and experience authentic Newari culture.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="14vsj6n" data-start="1073" data-end="1104">Visit the Sacred Namobuddha</h3>\n<p data-start="1106" data-end="1486">The highlight of the hike is Namobuddha, one of Nepal's most important Buddhist pilgrimage sites. Here, you can visit the peaceful monastery, observe monks during daily prayers, and enjoy the calm surroundings. Moreover, the spiritual atmosphere makes this destination truly memorable. Afterward, the trip continues to the historic city of Bhaktapur before returning to Kathmandu.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="1wfgthn" data-start="1488" data-end="1513">Why Choose This Hike?</h3>\n<p data-start="1515" data-end="1891">The <strong data-start="1519" data-end="1557">Nagarkot Dhulikhel Namobuddha Hike</strong> is suitable for beginners, families, and anyone looking for a relaxing outdoor adventure. Because the trails are easy to moderate, no previous trekking experience is required. Furthermore, the hike is enjoyable throughout the year, especially during spring and autumn when the weather is clear and the mountain views are outstanding.</p>\n<p data-start="1893" data-end="2136">Overall, the <strong data-start="1906" data-end="1944">Nagarkot Dhulikhel Namobuddha Hike</strong> offers the perfect mix of mountain scenery, cultural heritage, and spiritual discovery. As a result, it remains one of the most rewarding short hikes in Nepal for travelers with limited time.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/ChatGPT-Image-Jun-4-2026-12_13_57-PM.png	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	4 Days	599	Nepal	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Feb	Hotel	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{}	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="6gos8w" data-start="117" data-end="181">🌅 Stunning Himalayan sunrise views from Nagarkot viewpoint</li>\n<li data-section-id="1es1bxn" data-start="182" data-end="254">🥾 Scenic ridge trek through forests, hills, and terraced farmlands</li>\n<li data-section-id="uqyohm" data-start="255" data-end="335">🏛️ Visit to the ancient UNESCO World Heritage Site – Changu Narayan Temple</li>\n<li data-section-id="1rvj59o" data-start="336" data-end="401">🏞️ Peaceful hiking trails connecting Nagarkot and Dhulikhel</li>\n<li data-section-id="1krguv4" data-start="402" data-end="472">🏡 Authentic experience of traditional Newari and Tamang villages</li>\n<li data-section-id="nsm8ko" data-start="473" data-end="541">🕊️ Spiritual journey to the sacred Buddhist site of Namobuddha</li>\n<li data-section-id="1rzalmh" data-start="542" data-end="616">🏯 Exploration of historic Bhaktapur Durbar Square and old city charm</li>\n<li data-section-id="1epoa4d" data-start="617" data-end="686">🌿 Combination of nature, culture, and spirituality in one route</li>\n<li data-section-id="eedgaw" data-start="687" data-end="782">📸 Panoramic views of Himalayan ranges including Langtang and Everest (weather permitting)</li>\n<li data-section-id="2wails" data-start="783" data-end="864">🚶 Perfect short trek near Kathmandu ideal for beginners and culture lovers</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="g2zpp8" data-start="100" data-end="143">🚖 Hotel pickup and drop from Kathmandu</li>\n<li data-section-id="p0m9a0" data-start="144" data-end="195">🥾 Guided hiking tours throughout the itinerary</li>\n<li data-section-id="1ym7tvk" data-start="196" data-end="241">🏛️ Entrance fee to Changu Narayan Temple</li>\n<li data-section-id="zsr3ik" data-start="242" data-end="321">🏨 Accommodation in Nagarkot, Dhulikhel, and Namobuddha (standard category)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1xdkpid" data-start="322" data-end="361">🍽️ Daily breakfast during the trip</li>\n<li data-section-id="10znzm5" data-start="362" data-end="415">🧑‍🏫 Experienced English-speaking trekking guide</li>\n<li data-section-id="up6ya5" data-start="416" data-end="475">🚗 All necessary ground transportation as per itinerary</li>\n<li data-section-id="1m3hd5j" data-start="476" data-end="541">🕊️ Visit to Namobuddha Monastery and Bhaktapur Durbar Square</li>\n<li data-section-id="1rlpnwd" data-start="542" data-end="588">🩺 Basic first aid support during the trek</li>\n<li data-section-id="1irfm7v" data-start="589" data-end="643">📸 Assistance for photography spots and viewpoints</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="9hfjak" data-start="677" data-end="717">✈️ International or domestic airfare</li>\n<li data-section-id="10y9g1z" data-start="718" data-end="757">🍛 Lunch and dinner during the trip</li>\n<li data-section-id="1uq8gen" data-start="758" data-end="817">🛍️ Personal expenses (snacks, drinks, souvenirs, etc.)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1w5cpie" data-start="818" data-end="870">🎟️ Monument entry fees (except where mentioned)</li>\n<li data-section-id="xya7yg" data-start="871" data-end="915">🧳 Travel insurance (highly recommended)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1h8gi63" data-start="916" data-end="951">👨‍💼 Tips for guide and driver</li>\n<li data-section-id="ut41zt" data-start="952" data-end="1018">🏨 Extra night accommodation due to delays or personal reasons</li>\n<li data-section-id="1cycyjg" data-start="1019" data-end="1075">🚑 Emergency evacuation or medical costs if required</li>\n</ul>\n	<h3 data-section-id="sbghua" data-start="104" data-end="119">👕 Clothing</h3>\n<ul data-start="120" data-end="384">\n<li data-section-id="py0bsa" data-start="120" data-end="162">🧥 Light windproof jacket / warm layer</li>\n<li data-section-id="jw23ky" data-start="163" data-end="213">👕 Breathable t-shirts (quick dry recommended)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1l7rm2k" data-start="214" data-end="247">👖 Comfortable trekking pants</li>\n<li data-section-id="htvcr4" data-start="248" data-end="295">🧦 Extra pairs of socks (wool or quick dry)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1x4ywvu" data-start="296" data-end="333">🧣 Buff / scarf for dust and wind</li>\n<li data-section-id="1hgitg2" data-start="334" data-end="384">🧤 Light gloves (for winter or early mornings)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="386" data-end="389" />\n<h3 data-section-id="t3hd6f" data-start="391" data-end="406">👟 Footwear</h3>\n<ul data-start="407" data-end="501">\n<li data-section-id="i71o23" data-start="407" data-end="457">🥾 Comfortable trekking shoes (well broken-in)</li>\n<li data-section-id="9c7tid" data-start="458" data-end="501">🩴 Light sandals/slippers for hotel use</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="503" data-end="506" />\n<h3 data-section-id="12pb6s7" data-start="508" data-end="534">🎒 Backpack Essentials</h3>\n<ul data-start="535" data-end="735">\n<li data-section-id="17xko94" data-start="535" data-end="569">🎒 Small day backpack (20–30L)</li>\n<li data-section-id="ub1knx" data-start="570" data-end="607">💧 Water bottle or hydration pack</li>\n<li data-section-id="wn4sz5" data-start="608" data-end="652">🍫 Energy snacks (chocolate, nuts, bars)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1cs1wq" data-start="653" data-end="679">🧴 Sunscreen (SPF 30+)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1u4ycuw" data-start="680" data-end="698">🕶️ Sunglasses</li>\n<li data-section-id="k0c71y" data-start="699" data-end="735">🧢 Cap or hat for sun protection</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="737" data-end="740" />\n<h3 data-section-id="oaszyu" data-start="742" data-end="763">🧰 Personal Items</h3>\n<ul data-start="764" data-end="971">\n<li data-section-id="12oe9wz" data-start="764" data-end="789">🪪 Passport / ID copy</li>\n<li data-section-id="1fx92ki" data-start="790" data-end="838">💰 Cash (Nepali currency for small expenses)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1fun6jr" data-start="839" data-end="871">📱 Mobile phone &amp; power bank</li>\n<li data-section-id="1eyditp" data-start="872" data-end="912">📸 Camera (optional but recommended)</li>\n<li data-section-id="wld47" data-start="913" data-end="944">🧻 Tissue paper / wet wipes</li>\n<li data-section-id="1uhqgqg" data-start="945" data-end="971">🧴 Personal toiletries</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="973" data-end="976" />\n<h3 data-section-id="c2yx67" data-start="978" data-end="1005">🏔️ Trekking Essentials</h3>\n<ul data-start="1006" data-end="1143">\n<li data-section-id="1xv9eq5" data-start="1006" data-end="1041">🩹 Basic personal first aid kit</li>\n<li data-section-id="ea9uzb" data-start="1042" data-end="1078">💊 Personal medications (if any)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1hs81or" data-start="1079" data-end="1109">🔦 Small torch or headlamp</li>\n<li data-section-id="1nmrxl5" data-start="1110" data-end="1143">🗺️ Offline map (recommended)</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Begin your journey with a hotel pickup, explore the ancient Changu Narayan Temple, and enjoy a scenic hike to Nagarkot through beautiful village trails.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Hotel Pickup in Kathmandu, Visit Changu Narayan &amp; Hike to Nagarkot"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Enjoy a breathtaking sunrise over the Himalayas from Nagarkot and trek through scenic ridge trails, forests, and villages to reach Dhulikhel.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Nagarkot Sunrise &amp; Scenic Trek to Dhulikhel"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Trek from Dhulikhel to the sacred Buddhist site of Namobuddha through peaceful forests, hills, and traditional villages.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Dhulikhel to Namobuddha Spiritual Trek"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Descend from Namobuddha and explore the ancient city of Bhaktapur before returning to Kathmandu, experiencing rich culture and heritage.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Namobuddha to Bhaktapur Heritage Tour &amp; Drive to Kathmandu"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u0002kbrl82y705fu	classic-everest-trek-from-jiri	Classic Everest Trek (Jiri -EBC)	<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=XDS5z_4h/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-com	<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=XDS5z_4h/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Classic Everest Trek from Jiri – The Pioneer Route<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIFxAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">The <strong data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Classic Everest Trek from Jiri<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></strong> is a historic journey to Everest Base Camp. This legendary route is the original trail followed by the first Everest pioneers before the airport in Lukla was built. Because it features uncommercialized pathways, deep valleys, and slow altitude gains, this multi-day walking expedition remains an absolute favorite for travelers looking for an authentic, deep immersion into the Solukhumbu region.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=XDS5z_4q/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">What to Expect on Your Historical Journey<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIGBAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Your mountain adventure begins with a scenic drive from Kathmandu to the trailhead town of Jiri. From there, the footpaths wind gracefully through lush sub-tropical forests, green terraced fields, and over beautiful river suspension bridges. Along the way, staying in quiet local teahouses allows you to experience warm Nepalese hospitality firsthand while building excellent physical stamina for the higher altitude segments ahead.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=XDS5z_4y/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Walk Through Authentic Villages to Everest Base Camp<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIGRAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">One of the greatest highlights of the <strong data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Classic Everest Trek from Jiri<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></strong> is walking through traditional ethnic settlements like Bhandar, Sete, and Junbesi that are completely bypassed by modern flights. You will cross the challenging Lamjura La Pass at 3,530 meters before entering the main Khumbu valley at Phakding. This gradual foot journey allows for proper acclimatization, drastically reducing the risks of altitude sickness while exposing you to ancient Buddhist monasteries.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=XDS5z_57/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Why Choose This Legendary Wilderness Holiday?<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIGhAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" aria-owns="action-menu-parent-container" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Opting for the <strong data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Classic Everest Trek from Jiri<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></strong> offers the perfect mix of dramatic high-mountain landscapes, deep cultural discovery, and raw historical adventure. It serves as an ideal choice for hikers who want a classic Himalayan holiday away from the standard crowded modern routes. Ultimately, this unforgettable journey delivers incredible photography opportunities, profound peace, and memories that will last a lifetime.</div>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/11111.jpeg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	21 Days	2399	everest	Moderate		Spring (March–May) &amp; Autumn (September–November)	Hotel in Kathmandu &amp; Teahouses During Trek	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{everest-region}	<p><strong>The Trail Conditions</strong></p>\n<p>Straight, Uphill, Downhill, Jig Jag with small rocky, pebbles, somewhere flat man made stone steps, through the rhododendron, moss covered forests, suspensions metal bridges</p>\n<p><strong>Medication</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bandage for sprains</li>\n<li>Plasters/Band-aids</li>\n<li>Iodine or water filter (optional)</li>\n<li>Moleskin/Second skin – for blisters</li>\n<li>Antiseptic ointment for cuts</li>\n<li>Anti-bacterial throat lozenges (with antiseptic)</li>\n<li>Aspirin/paracetamol – general painkiller</li>\n<li>Oral dehydration salts</li>\n<li>Broad-spectrum antibiotic (norfloxacin or ciprofloxin)</li>\n<li>Anti-diarrhea medication (antibiotic)</li>\n<li>Diarrhea stopper (Imodium – optional)</li>\n<li>Antibiotic for Giardia or similar microbe or bacteria</li>\n<li>Diamox (altitude sickness – can be bought in Kathmandu)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Clothing / Equipment List</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pair trekking boots and waterproofing agent</li>\n<li>Pair lightweight trekking sandals</li>\n<li>Pairs thin walking socks</li>\n<li>Pairs lightweight wind – water proof pants</li>\n<li>T-shirts</li>\n<li>Fleece Jacket</li>\n<li>Set lightweight thermals</li>\n<li>North Face down Jacket (Preferably)</li>\n<li>Small thin towel (sports towel best)</li>\n<li>Soap</li>\n<li>Shampoo</li>\n<li>Sunscreen</li>\n<li>Extra lightweight shirt for daypacks – for stops along the way</li>\n<li>Hat</li>\n<li>Cotton or silk bag liner – optional</li>\n<li>Neck warmer</li>\n<li>Pairs ‘thinners’ gloves</li>\n<li>Rucksack</li>\n<li>Pack tissues</li>\n<li>Pair sunglasses</li>\n<li>Water filter / Iodine (you could buy boiled water in hotels/ lodges which is safe to drink.</li>\n<li>Camera and films</li>\n<li>Head torch and spare batteries</li>\n<li>Sleeping bag (rated -15(above) deg C during our trek)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Above things are required for Annapurna Circuit Trek. However if you do not have clothing you can either buy or rent in Nepal. In this case we have equipment cheaper than your country.</p>\n	<ul>\n<li>Airport pick-up and drop-off services in Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Kathmandu–Jiri transportation by tourist vehicle</li>\n<li>Lukla–Kathmandu domestic flight ticket</li>\n<li>Three nights hotel accommodation in Kathmandu with breakfast</li>\n<li>Sagarmatha National Park Entry Permit</li>\n<li>Khumbu Pasang Lhamu Rural Municipality Permit</li>\n<li>TIMS Card (if required by current regulations)</li>\n<li>Experienced government-licensed English-speaking trekking guide</li>\n<li>Porter service (one porter for every two trekkers)</li>\n<li>All guide and porter expenses including salary, meals, accommodation, insurance, and transportation</li>\n<li>Teahouse accommodation throughout the trek</li>\n<li>Three meals per day during the trek (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner)</li>\n<li>Seasonal fresh fruits during the trek</li>\n<li>Comprehensive first aid medical kit</li>\n<li>Trek completion certificate</li>\n<li>Government taxes and service charges</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>International airfare to and from Nepal</li>\n<li>Nepal entry visa fees</li>\n<li>Travel and rescue insurance</li>\n<li>Personal trekking equipment and clothing</li>\n<li>Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Additional accommodation in Kathmandu due to early arrival, late departure, or flight delays</li>\n<li>Personal expenses such as hot showers, internet, battery charging, laundry, and telephone calls</li>\n<li>Bottled water, soft drinks, alcoholic beverages, and snacks</li>\n<li>Tips for guides, porters, and support staff</li>\n<li>Emergency evacuation and rescue costs</li>\n<li>Costs caused by weather delays, flight cancellations, natural disasters, political situations, or other unforeseen circumstances</li>\n<li>Any services not specifically mentioned in the Package Includes section</li>\n</ul>\n	<div class="qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot">\n<div class="" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:09004f46-8f67-45b2-ae2a-fe3ef4911786-3" data-is-intersecting="true">\n<section class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:09004f46-8f67-45b2-ae2a-fe3ef4911786-3" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:09004