 data-section-id="ht9c86" data-start="254" data-end="275">Thermal base layers</li>\n<li data-section-id="4ccdyu" data-start="276" data-end="291">Fleece jacket</li>\n<li data-section-id="108ul6w" data-start="292" data-end="305">Down jacket</li>\n<li data-section-id="x46bqt" data-start="306" data-end="333">Waterproof jacket &amp; pants</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gmos76" data-start="334" data-end="356">Warm hat and sun hat</li>\n<li data-section-id="1xfofe4" data-start="357" data-end="365">Gloves</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="367" data-end="383">👞 Footwear</h4>\n<ul data-start="384" data-end="479">\n<li data-section-id="1lca0sf" data-start="384" data-end="411">Waterproof trekking boots</li>\n<li data-section-id="1jhchx8" data-start="412" data-end="432">Camp shoes/sandals</li>\n<li data-section-id="1r9e18k" data-start="433" data-end="461">Trekking socks (5–6 pairs)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mfsepp" data-start="462" data-end="479">Warm wool socks</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="481" data-end="507">🥾 Trekking Equipment</h4>\n<ul data-start="508" data-end="633">\n<li data-section-id="jx4r1" data-start="508" data-end="542">Sleeping bag (-15°C recommended)</li>\n<li data-section-id="jpijbi" data-start="543" data-end="559">Trekking poles</li>\n<li data-section-id="1s6undc" data-start="560" data-end="570">Headlamp</li>\n<li data-section-id="5c7vo5" data-start="571" data-end="607">Water bottles or hydration bladder</li>\n<li data-section-id="11rfapo" data-start="608" data-end="620">Sunglasses</li>\n<li data-section-id="dluokx" data-start="621" data-end="633">Power bank</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="635" data-end="657">🧴 Personal Items</h4>\n<ul data-start="658" data-end="769">\n<li data-section-id="10pl9xo" data-start="658" data-end="669">Sunscreen</li>\n<li data-section-id="1voh31b" data-start="670" data-end="680">Lip balm</li>\n<li data-section-id="l5061k" data-start="681" data-end="703">Personal medications</li>\n<li data-section-id="1h5dihr" data-start="704" data-end="725">Basic first-aid kit</li>\n<li data-section-id="8yarze" data-start="726" data-end="738">Toiletries</li>\n<li data-section-id="k8zdnf" data-start="739" data-end="769">Wet wipes and hand sanitizer</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start="771" data-end="1000" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node=""><strong data-start="771" data-end="783">❄️ Note:</strong> This 21-day trek involves longer walking days and a wider range of climates, from the lower hills of Jiri to the high-altitude Everest region. Warm layers, comfortable boots, and a quality sleeping bag are essential.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"></div>\n<div class="mt-3 w-full empty:hidden">\n<div class="text-center"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="pointer-events-none -mt-px h-px translate-y-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom)-14*var(--spacing))]" aria-hidden="true"></div>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Drive from Kathmandu to Jiri (1905m / 6250 ft)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Trek from Jiri to Bhandar (2190m / 7185 ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Trek from Bhandar to Sete (2520m / 8268 ft)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Trek from Sete to Junbesi (2700m / 8858 ft)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Trek from Junbesi to Nunthala (2220m / 7283 ft)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Trek from Nunthala to Bupsa (2360m / 7743 ft)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Trek from Bupsa to Phakding (2610m / 8563 ft)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Trek from Phakding to Namche Bazaar (3440m / 11286 ft)"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Acclimatization Day in Namche Bazaar"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Trek from Namche Bazaar to Tengboche (3860m / 12664 ft)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Trek from Tengboche to Dingboche (4410m / 14469 ft)"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Acclimatization Day in Dingboche"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Trek from Dingboche to Lobuche (4910m / 16109 ft)"}, {"day": "15", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 15: Trek from Lobuche to Gorakshep and Everest Base Camp (5364m / 17598 ft)"}, {"day": "16", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 16: Hike to Kala Patthar and Trek to Pheriche (4371m / 14340 ft)"}, {"day": "17", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 17: Trek from Pheriche to Namche Bazaar (3440m / 11286 ft)"}, {"day": "18", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 18: Trek from Namche Bazaar to Lukla (2860m / 9383 ft)"}, {"day": "19", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 19: Fly from Lukla to Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}, {"day": "20", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 20: Free Day in Kathmandu"}, {"day": "21", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 21: Final Departure from Kathmandu"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.779	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u0000kbrlcp5u5n5q	chisapani-nagarkot-hike	Chisapani / Nagarkot Hike	<div>\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:21aa552f-0b65-4959-9426-e16258066912-2" data-is-intersecting="true"><section dir="auto" data-turn-id="r	<div>\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:21aa552f-0b65-4959-9426-e16258066912-2" data-is-intersecting="true"><section dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:21aa552f-0b65-4959-9426-e16258066912-2" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:21aa552f-0b65-4959-9426-e16258066912-2" data-testid="conversation-turn-6" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant">\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div dir="auto" tabindex="0" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="7033d722-3c33-467d-845f-d447a8f26c13" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div>\n<div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<h2 data-section-id="rzkdgm" data-start="209" data-end="220">Overview</h2>\n<p data-start="222" data-end="687">The <a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=3d80f3da76bac683&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnvnnglYYK1MQHgbex5vB8EnMPYcIQ:1783140946678&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832cK-OlyrFp0q_lDSVqWSWpDEzO_-mUx3hdbQlSvWRAm3a3D3y0P_3kyEtVBac4Ukym0-lzOIDTsceJ8zFU6F7ZK1n2TUdjizsEBJzl8cfqW01lEWpKFRTdDWqjo6TfoAnqtLpqiB7rw-JhlMl9YWKw660ET9Eop1xz445_rBzP2levswlw&amp;q=chisapani&amp;sa=X&amp;sqi=2&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjg99fVnbiVAxV0R2cHHeNmCAUQtKgLegQIFRAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25"><strong data-start="226" data-end="253">Chisapani Nagarkot Hike</strong></a> is one of the most popular short trekking adventures near Kathmandu. It offers an excellent combination of Himalayan scenery, peaceful forests, traditional villages, and rich cultural experiences. Therefore, it is an ideal choice for travelers who want to enjoy Nepal's natural beauty without trekking to extreme altitudes. Moreover, the trail is suitable for beginners, families, and anyone looking for a relaxing outdoor adventure.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="1qjvcyc" data-start="689" data-end="733">Highlights of the Chisapani Nagarkot Hike</h2>\n<p data-start="735" data-end="1105">The <strong data-start="739" data-end="766">Chisapani Nagarkot Hike</strong> begins with a scenic drive to Sundarijal before entering the beautiful Shivapuri Nagarjun National Park. Along the way, you walk through dense forests, cross small streams, and pass charming villages surrounded by green hills and terraced farmland. In addition, the peaceful environment allows you to enjoy nature away from the busy city.</p>\n<p data-start="1107" data-end="1439">After reaching Chisapani, the trail follows scenic ridges toward Nagarkot, one of Nepal's most famous hill stations. Furthermore, Nagarkot is well known for its spectacular sunrise and panoramic Himalayan views. On clear days, you can admire Langtang, Ganesh Himal, Gaurishankar, Dorje Lakpa, and even Mount Everest in the distance.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="88chp6" data-start="1441" data-end="1483">Why Choose the Chisapani Nagarkot Hike?</h2>\n<p data-start="1485" data-end="1937">The <strong data-start="1489" data-end="1516">Chisapani Nagarkot Hike</strong> offers more than beautiful landscapes. During the journey, you experience authentic village life, meet friendly local people, and enjoy traditional Nepali hospitality. Afterwards, many travelers continue to the historic city of Bhaktapur, where they can explore ancient temples, courtyards, and impressive Newari architecture. As a result, the trip combines trekking, culture, and sightseeing in one rewarding itinerary.</p>\n<p data-start="1939" data-end="2241">Because the trail is easy to moderate, it is suitable for most fitness levels. Additionally, comfortable local lodges provide cozy accommodation and traditional meals along the route. Spring and autumn are the best seasons because the weather is pleasant and the mountain views are exceptionally clear.</p>\n<p data-start="2243" data-end="2545">Overall, the <strong data-start="2256" data-end="2283">Chisapani Nagarkot Hike</strong> is the perfect short escape from Kathmandu. Whether you are visiting Nepal for the first time or looking for a peaceful nature walk, this memorable hike offers stunning Himalayan panoramas, cultural discovery, and unforgettable experiences close to the capital.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section></div>\n</div>\n<div aria-hidden="true"></div>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/ChatGPT-Image-Jun-4-2026-11_26_05-AM.png	{/uploads/images/d9269b49-8527-4d45-9b3d-2f1ed4aba15a.jpg,/uploads/images/e50d196f-da15-49bb-bdec-62832b381fd3.jpg,https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/Restricted-Area-Trekking.jpeg,https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/upper-Mustang-trek-1.jpg,https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/Tours-In-Nepal.jpg,https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/Nepal-A-Country-Where-Peace-Thrives.jpeg}	\N	749	US$ 399 - US$ 599	f	6	399	Nepal	Moderate	2,175 M	March-Jun / Oct-Jan	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.	2 - 10 Pax		Trekking	{"All Trekking Packages"}					[{"day": "1", "desc": "Arrive in Kathmandu and enjoy a warm Nepali welcome as you prepare for your Chisapani & Nagarkot hiking adventure.", "elev": 1400, "note": "Explore the cultural and historical treasures of Kathmandu Valley, home to ancient temples, palaces, and UNESCO World Heritage Sites.Explore the cultural and historical treasures of Kathmandu Valley, home to ancient temples, palaces, and UNESCO World Heritage Sites.Explore the cultural and historical treasures of Kathmandu Valley, home to ancient temples, palaces, and UNESCO World Heritage Sites.", "hours": "40 minutes", "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1,400m)", "distance": "Approx 8 KM", "endPoint": "Phadking", "startPoint": "Kathmandu"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Explore the cultural and historical treasures of Kathmandu Valley, home to ancient temples, palaces, and UNESCO World Heritage Sites.", "elev": 0, "hours": "6 hrs", "title": "Day 2: Kathmandu Sightseeing Tour", "distance": "appriox 20km", "endPoint": "ABC", "startPoint": "Phadking"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Begin your trek with a scenic hike through forests, waterfalls, and traditional villages to the beautiful hilltop settlement of Chisapani.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Drive to Sundarijal and Hike to Chisapani"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Enjoy a scenic ridge-top hike through traditional villages and countryside landscapes to the famous hill station of Nagarkot.", "elev": 2175, "title": "Day 4: Trek from Chisapani to Nagarkot (2,175m)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Witness a spectacular Himalayan sunrise, hike through scenic countryside to Bhaktapur, and explore one of Nepal’s finest medieval cities.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Sunrise at Nagarkot – Hike to Bhaktapur and Drive to Kathmandu\\";"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Bid farewell to Nepal as your memorable Chisapani and Nagarkot hiking adventure comes to an end.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Departure from Kathmandu"}]		f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-26 14:41:24.739	youtube	\N	\N	{"peaks": [], "routePoints": [], "routeSegments": []}	t	[{"day": 1, "note": "", "place": "", "altitude": ""}]	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u0006kbrl00cojahq	dhaulagiri-trekking-3	Dhaulagiri Trekking	<h1 data-section-id="1jsi2o6" data-start="557" data-end="587"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=23c6f1fa80babc08&amp;sxsrf=APpeQntZpizlYd	<h1 data-section-id="1jsi2o6" data-start="557" data-end="587"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=23c6f1fa80babc08&amp;sxsrf=APpeQntZpizlYd2Ma4T-n1Tnp3vHhTeJTA:1783131159102&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gIHbHEqXWbyThyPdUCKqTmZAKzBcRFb2qe3OBMfh6G5URtuzGpQgwyLjG0HlVfwOhBKT-_MjHW6JAI50fK8ctSDBzYN4QFmM5h2f-J2LGaBBmSbliULKp1HwnGA8zByXKCw81aKc7LO2xjbgBVfvicOu9VOvA&amp;q=dhaulagiri&amp;sa=X&amp;sqi=2&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjvz82a-beVAxXQjWMGHezgAL4QtKgLegQIHRAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Dhaulagiri</a> Trekking Overview</h1>\n<p data-start="589" data-end="936"><strong data-start="589" data-end="612">Dhaulagiri Trekking</strong> is one of Nepal's most challenging and rewarding trekking adventures. It takes you around <strong data-start="703" data-end="733">Mount Dhaulagiri (8,167 m)</strong>, the world's seventh-highest mountain. Unlike many popular trekking routes, this trail remains quiet and remote. Therefore, it is perfect for experienced trekkers looking for a true Himalayan adventure.</p>\n<p data-start="938" data-end="1317">The journey begins through traditional villages, terraced fields, and beautiful forests. Soon, the trail enters rugged alpine landscapes filled with glaciers and rocky valleys. Moreover, every day brings spectacular views of Dhaulagiri, Tukuche Peak, Nilgiri, Annapurna I, and other snow-covered mountains. As a result, the scenery changes constantly and keeps the trek exciting.</p>\n<p data-start="1319" data-end="1613">Furthermore, the route follows peaceful trails with very few trekkers. Consequently, you can enjoy nature without large crowds. In addition, the remote campsites provide a genuine wilderness experience. Although the trek is demanding, every step rewards you with unforgettable mountain scenery.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="1kpr5wr" data-start="1615" data-end="1654">Cross High Passes and Hidden Valleys</h2>\n<p data-start="1656" data-end="2006">One of the biggest highlights of <strong data-start="1689" data-end="1712">Dhaulagiri Trekking</strong> is crossing the famous French Pass (5,360 m). Afterwards, you continue through the beautiful Hidden Valley before reaching Dhampus Pass (5,240 m). From both passes, you enjoy breathtaking panoramic views of the Himalayas. Meanwhile, massive glaciers and dramatic ice fields surround the trail.</p>\n<p data-start="2008" data-end="2262">Moreover, the trek passes rivers, forests, alpine meadows, and rocky landscapes. Because the environment changes every day, the journey never feels repetitive. Likewise, wildlife lovers may spot blue sheep, Himalayan griffons, and other mountain animals.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="b4jex4" data-start="2264" data-end="2300">Best Time for Dhaulagiri Trekking</h2>\n<p data-start="2302" data-end="2705">Spring (March to May) and autumn (September to November) are the best seasons for <strong data-start="2384" data-end="2407">Dhaulagiri Trekking</strong>. During these months, the weather is usually stable, and the skies stay clear. Therefore, mountain views are outstanding. However, the route reaches high elevations, so proper acclimatization is essential. In addition, good physical fitness and previous trekking experience are highly recommended.</p>\n<p data-start="2707" data-end="3051">Finally, <strong data-start="2716" data-end="2739">Dhaulagiri Trekking</strong> offers an unforgettable journey through one of Nepal's wildest mountain regions. Overall, it combines remote trails, towering peaks, high mountain passes, and stunning glacier scenery. Whether you want adventure, solitude, or spectacular Himalayan landscapes, this trek delivers a once-in-a-lifetime experience.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Dhaulagiri-Trekking-2.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	24 Days	1850	Nepal	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Feb		B.B.		\N	Trekking	{}	<p><strong>The Trail Conditions: </strong></p>\n<p>Straight, Uphill, Downhill, Jig Jag with small rocky, pebbles, somewhere flat man made stone steps, through the rhododendron, moss covered forests, suspensions metal bridges</p>\n<p><strong>Medication </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bandage for sprains</li>\n<li>Plasters/Band-aids</li>\n<li>Iodine or water filter (optional)</li>\n<li>Moleskin/Second skin - for blisters</li>\n<li>Antiseptic ointment for cuts</li>\n<li>Anti-bacterial throat lozenges (with antiseptic)</li>\n<li>Aspirin/paracetamol - general painkiller</li>\n<li>Oral dehydration salts</li>\n<li>Broad-spectrum antibiotic (norfloxacin or ciprofloxin)</li>\n<li>Anti-diarrhea medication (antibiotic)</li>\n<li>Diarrhea stopper (Imodium - optional)</li>\n<li>Antibiotic for Giardia or similar microbe or bacteria</li>\n<li>Diamox (altitude sickness - can be bought in Kathmandu)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong> </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Clothing / Equipment List </strong></p>\n<p><em>Kindly bring the following list of clothing / equipment for our trek to Dhaulagiri Trek </em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pair trekking boots and waterproofing agent</li>\n<li>Pair lightweight trekking sandals</li>\n<li>Pairs thin walking socks</li>\n<li>Pairs lightweight wind – water proof pants</li>\n<li>T-shirts</li>\n<li>Fleece Jacket</li>\n<li>Set lightweight thermals</li>\n<li>North Face down Jacket (Preferably)</li>\n<li>Small thin towel (sports towel best)</li>\n<li>Soap</li>\n<li>Shampoo</li>\n<li>Sunscreen</li>\n<li>Extra lightweight shirt for daypacks - for stops along the way</li>\n<li>Hat</li>\n<li>Cotton or silk bag liner – optional</li>\n<li>Neck warmer</li>\n<li>Pairs 'thinners' gloves</li>\n<li>Rucksack</li>\n<li>Pack tissues</li>\n<li>Pair sunglasses</li>\n<li>Water filter / Iodine (you could buy boiled water in hotels/ lodges which is safe to drink.</li>\n<li>Camera and films</li>\n<li>Head torch and spare batteries</li>\n<li>Sleeping bag (rated -15(above) deg C during our trek)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Above things are required for Dhaulagiri Trek. However if you do not have clothing you can either buy or rent in Nepal. In this case we have equipment cheaper than your country.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n				[]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u0008kbrlxpz2dksw	rara-lake-trekking	Rara Lake Trekking	<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=LJeLqf_43/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-co	<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=LJeLqf_43/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><span data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><span data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><span data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="c" data-ved="2ahUKEwjv-tXQ0rSWAxXLjOEIHXDsPDsQ0fERegYIAAgUEAA" data-complete="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Rara Lake Trekking<!--TgQPHd|||[]--><!--TgQPHd|||[false,&quot;&quot;,false,{&quot;u&quot;:0}]--></span><!--TgQPHd|||[]--><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></span> – A Remote Himalayan Journey<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></span><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIFRAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">The <strong data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Rara Lake Trekking<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></strong> experience stands out as one of Nepal's most beautiful, remote, and peaceful wilderness adventures. Tucked away in the hidden Karnali region of western Nepal, this scenic pathway leads to the country's largest and deepest freshwater lake. Because it is far removed from the busier, highly commercialized routes, this serene high-altitude expedition remains an absolute favorite for travelers seeking deep tranquility and untouched natural landscapes.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=LJeLqf_4h/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">What to Expect on Your Wilderness Trail<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIFhAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Your mountain journey begins with an exciting flight from Nepalgunj to the remote airstrip in Talcha. From there, the walking trails wind through pristine coniferous woods filled with blue pine, spruce, and rhododendron trees. As you ascend toward the water's edge, you explore traditional villages that reveal a unique local lifestyle and traditional culture unchanged by modern times. Along the way, staying in quiet teahouses allows you to experience authentic Nepalese hospitality.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=LJeLqf_4p/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Discover the Magnificent Blue Gem of Karnali<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIFxAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Arriving at your final destination provides an unparalleled view of the magnificent water body, which sits beautifully inside Rara National Park at an elevation of 2,990 meters. The lake is famous for its changing colors, shifting from deep blue to brilliant emerald throughout the day. Additionally, the surrounding protected conservation area serves as a safe sanctuary for rare wildlife, including the musk deer, Himalayan black bear, and numerous migratory bird species.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=LJeLqf_4x/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Why Choose This Remote Wilderness Holiday?<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIGBAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" aria-owns="action-menu-parent-container" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Opting for <strong data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><span data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><span data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><span data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="c" data-ved="2ahUKEwjv-tXQ0rSWAxXLjOEIHXDsPDsQ0fERegYIAAgYEAE" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Rara Lake Trekking<!--TgQPHd|||[]--><!--TgQPHd|||[false,&quot;&quot;,false,{&quot;u&quot;:0}]--></span><!--TgQPHd|||[]--><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></span><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></span><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></strong> offers the perfect blend of dramatic alpine landscapes, rich cultural discovery, and peaceful trails. Not only do you walk through diverse ecological zones, but you also experience an off-the-beaten-path holiday that very few tourists ever witness. Ultimately, this unforgettable Himalayan journey delivers incredible photography opportunities, profound isolation, and a deep appreciation for the natural world.</div>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Rara-Lake-Trekking-2.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	13 Days	0	Nepal	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Jan		B.B.		\N	Trekking	{}	<p><strong>The Trail Conditions: </strong></p>\n<p>Straight, Uphill, Downhill, Jig Jag with small rocky, pebbles, somewhere flat man made stone steps, through the rhododendron, moss covered forests, suspensions metal bridges</p>\n<p><strong>Medication </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bandage for sprains</li>\n<li>Plasters/Band-aids</li>\n<li>Iodine or water filter (optional)</li>\n<li>Moleskin/Second skin - for blisters</li>\n<li>Antiseptic ointment for cuts</li>\n<li>Anti-bacterial throat lozenges (with antiseptic)</li>\n<li>Aspirin/paracetamol - general painkiller</li>\n<li>Oral dehydration salts</li>\n<li>Broad-spectrum antibiotic (norfloxacin or ciprofloxin)</li>\n<li>Anti-diarrhea medication (antibiotic)</li>\n<li>Diarrhea stopper (Imodium - optional)</li>\n<li>Antibiotic for Giardia or similar microbe or bacteria</li>\n<li>Diamox (altitude sickness - can be bought in Kathmandu)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong> </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Clothing / Equipment List </strong></p>\n<p><em>Kindly bring the following list of clothing / equipment for our trek to Rara Lake<br />\n</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pair trekking boots and waterproofing agent</li>\n<li>Pair lightweight trekking sandals</li>\n<li>Pairs thin walking socks</li>\n<li>Pairs lightweight wind – water proof pants</li>\n<li>T-shirts</li>\n<li>Fleece Jacket</li>\n<li>Set lightweight thermals</li>\n<li>North Face down Jacket (Preferably)</li>\n<li>Small thin towel (sports towel best)</li>\n<li>Soap</li>\n<li>Shampoo</li>\n<li>Sunscreen</li>\n<li>Extra lightweight shirt for daypacks - for stops along the way</li>\n<li>Hat</li>\n<li>Cotton or silk bag liner – optional</li>\n<li>Neck warmer</li>\n<li>Pairs 'thinners' gloves</li>\n<li>Rucksack</li>\n<li>Pack tissues</li>\n<li>Pair sunglasses</li>\n<li>Water filter / Iodine (you could buy boiled water in hotels/ lodges which is safe to drink.</li>\n<li>Camera and films</li>\n<li>Head torch and spare batteries</li>\n<li>Sleeping bag (rated -15(above) deg C during our trek)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Above things are required for Rara Lake Trek. However if you do not have clothing you can either buy or rent in Nepal. In this case we have equipment cheaper than your country.</p>\n				[]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u0009kbrlr550mu1h	nar-phu-valley-trek-thorong-la-pass	Nar Phu Valley & Thorong La Pass Expedition Trek	<h3 data-section-id="swacyn" data-start="579" data-end="615">Discover the Nar Phu Valley Trek</h3>\n<p data-start="617" data-end="1099">The <strong dat	<h3 data-section-id="swacyn" data-start="579" data-end="615">Discover the Nar Phu Valley Trek</h3>\n<p data-start="617" data-end="1099">The <strong data-start="621" data-end="644">Nar Phu Valley Trek</strong> is one of Nepal's most remote and rewarding Himalayan adventures. This remarkable journey combines the untouched landscapes of Nar and Phu with the dramatic crossing of Thorong La Pass. Along the way, trekkers experience ancient villages, traditional Tibetan-influenced culture, historic monasteries, and spectacular mountain scenery. The route is ideal for experienced hikers who want to explore a quieter and less-traveled part of the Annapurna region.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="emd4kv" data-start="1101" data-end="1143">Explore the Hidden Nar and Phu Valleys</h3>\n<p data-start="1145" data-end="1433">The adventure begins with a scenic drive from Kathmandu before joining the Annapurna trail toward Koto. From there, the route enters the restricted Nar Phu region, where narrow valleys, dramatic cliffs, stone-built villages, and peaceful forests create an unforgettable Himalayan setting.</p>\n<p data-start="1435" data-end="1779">The trail passes through traditional settlements such as Meta, Phu, and Nar. Trekkers can observe local lifestyles, visit ancient monasteries, and enjoy impressive views of Annapurna II, Himlung Himal, Kang Guru, Pisang Peak, and Chulu East. The remote location and welcoming local communities give the journey an authentic cultural experience.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="qamhl2" data-start="1781" data-end="1820">Experience Remote Himalayan Culture</h3>\n<p data-start="1822" data-end="2187">One of the most rewarding aspects of the journey is the opportunity to experience the traditional way of life in the high Himalayas. The villages of Nar and Phu have preserved their distinctive customs, architecture, and Buddhist heritage. Exploring these communities provides a deeper understanding of mountain life while adding cultural richness to the adventure.</p>\n<p data-start="2189" data-end="2336">After leaving the Nar Phu region, the trail continues toward the Annapurna Circuit and prepares trekkers for the challenging high-altitude section.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="lljev7" data-start="2338" data-end="2363">Cross Thorong La Pass</h3>\n<p data-start="2365" data-end="2614">A major highlight is the ascent to <strong data-start="2400" data-end="2435">Thorong La Pass at 5,416 meters</strong>. Proper acclimatization is essential before attempting the pass. The demanding climb is rewarded with spectacular panoramic views of the Annapurna and Dhaulagiri mountain ranges. After crossing the pass, the trail descends toward <strong data-start="2667" data-end="2680">Muktinath</strong>, an important pilgrimage destination known for its religious significance and dramatic mountain surroundings. From here, the journey continues through the beautiful Kali Gandaki region toward Pokhara.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="jc4v4s" data-start="2883" data-end="2923">Why Choose This Himalayan Adventure?</h3>\n<p data-start="2925" data-end="3259">The <strong data-start="2929" data-end="2952">Nar Phu Valley Trek</strong> is an excellent choice for experienced trekkers seeking remote landscapes, cultural discovery, and challenging Himalayan trails. The combination of restricted valleys, traditional villages, high mountain passes, and spectacular scenery makes this route different from more crowded trekking trails in Nepal.</p>\n<p data-start="3261" data-end="3479">For more information about related trekking routes, you can internally link to your <strong data-start="3345" data-end="3373">[Annapurna Circuit Trek]</strong> page. You can also add a trustworthy external reference to the <strong data-start="3437" data-end="3460">Nepal Tourism Board</strong> where appropriate.</p>\n<p data-start="3481" data-end="3742">This adventure is best suited to trekkers with good fitness and previous high-altitude experience. With proper preparation, gradual acclimatization, and an experienced guide, the journey offers an unforgettable exploration of Nepal's remote mountain landscapes.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ChatGPT-Image-Jun-4-2026-01_12_59-PM.png	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	16 Days	1599	annapurna	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Dec	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{annapurna-region}	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="bqszg8" data-start="132" data-end="228">🏔️ Explore the remote and restricted Nar Phu Valley, one of Nepal’s most untouched regions</li>\n<li data-section-id="1et6qcu" data-start="229" data-end="324">🏘️ Experience ancient Tibetan-influenced villages like Phu and Nar with preserved culture</li>\n<li data-section-id="ny9q01" data-start="325" data-end="419">🥾 Scenic trekking through deep gorges, alpine valleys, and dramatic Himalayan landscapes</li>\n<li data-section-id="17umpgn" data-start="420" data-end="504">🕉️ Visit sacred monasteries, chortens, and prayer-flag-filled spiritual trails</li>\n<li data-section-id="7boeq0" data-start="505" data-end="593">🌿 Cross diverse terrain from lush river valleys to high-altitude barren landscapes</li>\n<li data-section-id="rsz94x" data-start="594" data-end="669">🧭 Acclimatization experience in Manang with panoramic Himalayan views</li>\n<li data-section-id="1bayl7d" data-start="670" data-end="773">🏔️ Cross the legendary Thorong La Pass (5,416m) – one of the highest trekking passes in the world</li>\n<li data-section-id="1pabpg7" data-start="774" data-end="868">🙏 Visit the sacred pilgrimage site of Muktinath, important for both Hindus and Buddhists</li>\n<li data-section-id="1sj3azq" data-start="869" data-end="949">🚗 Scenic descent through Mustang region and Kali Gandaki valley to Pokhara</li>\n<li data-section-id="1ff5xhf" data-start="950" data-end="1048">🌏 A complete Himalayan expedition combining wilderness, culture, and adventure in one route</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="5tipfv" data-start="169" data-end="233">🚖 Airport pickup and drop (Kathmandu International Airport)</li>\n<li data-section-id="8s34w1" data-start="234" data-end="304">🏨 2 nights hotel accommodation in Kathmandu (arrival &amp; departure)</li>\n<li data-section-id="yam812" data-start="305" data-end="372">🥾 Full guided trekking service with experienced licensed guide</li>\n<li data-section-id="43qexa" data-start="373" data-end="442">🧑‍🤝‍🧑 Required number of porters (2 trekkers : 1 porter basis)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1tvsfbo" data-start="443" data-end="497">🎟️ Restricted Area Permit (Nar Phu Valley Permit)</li>\n<li data-section-id="rcmsq0" data-start="498" data-end="547">🏔️ Annapurna Conservation Area Permit (ACAP)</li>\n<li data-section-id="dg1jo7" data-start="548" data-end="601">🚗 Kathmandu → Koto private/public transportation</li>\n<li data-section-id="qfq3mb" data-start="602" data-end="643">🚙 Muktinath → Pokhara transportation</li>\n<li data-section-id="fz1nz1" data-start="644" data-end="691">🚌 Pokhara → Kathmandu tourist bus transfer</li>\n<li data-section-id="1r4ngn6" data-start="692" data-end="746">🏡 Basic tea house/lodge accommodation during trek</li>\n<li data-section-id="nvtql9" data-start="747" data-end="817">🍽️ Three meals per day during trekking (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner)</li>\n<li data-section-id="10ikf02" data-start="818" data-end="881">🩺 First aid kit and basic medical support carried by guide</li>\n<li data-section-id="wbq8bb" data-start="882" data-end="921">🗺️ Trekking map and route briefing</li>\n<li data-section-id="18gfsy5" data-start="922" data-end="972">🧑‍🏫 All government taxes and service charges</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="2ldx0r" data-start="1006" data-end="1048">✈️ International airfare to/from Nepal</li>\n<li data-section-id="1bi62n2" data-start="1049" data-end="1076">🛂 Nepal entry visa fee</li>\n<li data-section-id="1yxg010" data-start="1077" data-end="1140">🍛 Meals in Kathmandu, Pokhara (except breakfast if stated)</li>\n<li data-section-id="8j1tf8" data-start="1141" data-end="1212">🛍️ Personal expenses (snacks, drinks, hot showers, charging, etc.)</li>\n<li data-section-id="11y5iq8" data-start="1213" data-end="1284">🏨 Extra hotel nights due to early arrival/late departure or delays</li>\n<li data-section-id="f2k6wr" data-start="1285" data-end="1337">🧗 Travel insurance (mandatory but not included)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1734aej" data-start="1338" data-end="1384">💰 Tips for guide and porter (recommended)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1boxp7o" data-start="1385" data-end="1451">🚁 Emergency evacuation or helicopter rescue costs (if needed)</li>\n<li data-section-id="radgcm" data-start="1452" data-end="1495">📸 Personal trekking equipment and gear</li>\n<li data-section-id="1y3nwra" data-start="1496" data-end="1545">🎫 Entry fees for monuments during city tours</li>\n</ul>\n	<h3 data-section-id="oql6ph" data-start="163" data-end="197"><span role="text">👕 <strong data-start="170" data-end="197">Clothing (Layer System)</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start="198" data-end="587">\n<li data-section-id="1knx2qa" data-start="198" data-end="242">🧥 Down jacket (high altitude essential)</li>\n<li data-section-id="hlmotr" data-start="243" data-end="277">🧥 Waterproof/windproof jacket</li>\n<li data-section-id="14apr0u" data-start="278" data-end="322">👕 Quick-dry trekking t-shirts (2–4 pcs)</li>\n<li data-section-id="15w7g36" data-start="323" data-end="354">👖 Trekking pants (2 pairs)</li>\n<li data-section-id="lyze3o" data-start="355" data-end="404">🧦 Woolen socks + quick-dry socks (5–6 pairs)</li>\n<li data-section-id="10m3u8d" data-start="405" data-end="446">🧣 Buff / neck gaiter for dust &amp; cold</li>\n<li data-section-id="j5ycjk" data-start="447" data-end="493">🧤 Warm gloves (inner + outer if possible)</li>\n<li data-section-id="iqj23f" data-start="494" data-end="541">🧢 Sun hat + woolen cap (for cold mornings)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1i68ddp" data-start="542" data-end="587">🩳 Light clothes for lower altitude areas</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="589" data-end="592" />\n<h3 data-section-id="17i7fg7" data-start="594" data-end="613"><span role="text">👟 <strong data-start="601" data-end="613">Footwear</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start="614" data-end="719">\n<li data-section-id="ukt42y" data-start="614" data-end="670">🥾 Strong waterproof trekking boots (well broken-in)</li>\n<li data-section-id="d6rai3" data-start="671" data-end="719">🩴 Lightweight sandals/slippers (for lodges)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="721" data-end="724" />\n<h3 data-section-id="cuhko5" data-start="726" data-end="755"><span role="text">🎒 <strong data-start="733" data-end="755">Backpack &amp; Storage</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start="756" data-end="879">\n<li data-section-id="kaim0g" data-start="756" data-end="797">🎒 30–50L trekking backpack (day use)</li>\n<li data-section-id="4ahom7" data-start="798" data-end="848">🎒 Duffel bag (carried by porter, if included)</li>\n<li data-section-id="op8gb9" data-start="849" data-end="879">🧳 Rain cover for backpack</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="881" data-end="884" />\n<h3 data-section-id="1emmpjv" data-start="886" data-end="916"><span role="text">🧭 <strong data-start="893" data-end="916">Trekking Essentials</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start="917" data-end="1129">\n<li data-section-id="a0z03r" data-start="917" data-end="966">💧 Reusable water bottle or hydration bladder</li>\n<li data-section-id="auc9y0" data-start="967" data-end="1003">🔦 Headlamp with extra batteries</li>\n<li data-section-id="my479z" data-start="1004" data-end="1032">🧴 Sunscreen (SPF 30–50)</li>\n<li data-section-id="3204m0" data-start="1033" data-end="1065">🕶️ UV protection sunglasses</li>\n<li data-section-id="j3py0c" data-start="1066" data-end="1097">🧻 Wet wipes &amp; toilet paper</li>\n<li data-section-id="135x7o8" data-start="1098" data-end="1129">🍫 Energy bars / dry snacks</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="1131" data-end="1134" />\n<h3 data-section-id="18x1rwk" data-start="1136" data-end="1162"><span role="text">🩺 <strong data-start="1143" data-end="1162">Health &amp; Safety</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start="1163" data-end="1294">\n<li data-section-id="1t3bob3" data-start="1163" data-end="1190">💊 Personal medications</li>\n<li data-section-id="wyyb11" data-start="1191" data-end="1217">🩹 Basic first aid kit</li>\n<li data-section-id="1cgc372" data-start="1218" data-end="1268">💊 Altitude sickness medicine (consult doctor)</li>\n<li data-section-id="pebrus" data-start="1269" data-end="1294">🧂 ORS / electrolytes</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="1296" data-end="1299" />\n<h3 data-section-id="3uod23" data-start="1301" data-end="1323"><span role="text">📱 <strong data-start="1308" data-end="1323">Electronics</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start="1324" data-end="1457">\n<li data-section-id="11xwhoq" data-start="1324" data-end="1356">📱 Mobile phone + power bank</li>\n<li data-section-id="50f9a3" data-start="1357" data-end="1381">📸 Camera (optional)</li>\n<li data-section-id="iswa4j" data-start="1382" data-end="1406">🔌 Universal adapter</li>\n<li data-section-id="tjxx82" data-start="1407" data-end="1457">🔋 Extra batteries (cold reduces battery life)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="1459" data-end="1462" />\n<h3 data-section-id="1fyl3so" data-start="1464" data-end="1492"><span role="text">🪪 <strong data-start="1471" data-end="1492">Documents &amp; Money</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start="1493" data-end="1614">\n<li data-section-id="yp0c6u" data-start="1493" data-end="1520">🪪 Passport + photocopy</li>\n<li data-section-id="1m2m535" data-start="1521" data-end="1556">🎫 Permits (provided by agency)</li>\n<li data-section-id="vulof6" data-start="1557" data-end="1614">💵 Cash (Nepali rupees for tea houses &amp; personal use)</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="1616" data-end="1619" />\n<h3 data-section-id="16krzy6" data-start="1621" data-end="1651"><span role="text">🧗 <strong data-start="1628" data-end="1651">Optional but Useful</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start="1652" data-end="1783">\n<li data-section-id="50ajgs" data-start="1652" data-end="1709">🥢 Trekking poles (highly recommended for Thorong La)</li>\n<li data-section-id="12tegie" data-start="1710" data-end="1749">🛏️ Sleeping bag (for cold seasons)</li>\n<li data-section-id="hxgq4m" data-start="1750" data-end="1783">🧤 Hand warmers (winter trek)</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Arrive in Kathmandu and receive a warm welcome before beginning your adventurous Nar Phu Valley and Thorong La Pass trekking journey.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "A scenic long drive from Kathmandu to Koto passing through beautiful river valleys, hills, and mountain landscapes.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Drive from Kathmandu to Koto"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Begin trekking into the restricted Nar Phu Valley region as you enter remote landscapes, deep gorges, and peaceful Himalayan wilderness.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Trek from Koto to Meta"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "A gradual ascent into higher Himalayan terrain as you trek from Meta to the remote settlement of Kyang in the Nar Phu Valley.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Trek from Meta to Kyang"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "A dramatic trek deeper into the remote Nar Phu Valley leading to the ancient Tibetan-style village of Phu.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Trek from Kyang to Phu Village"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Spend a rest and exploration day in the remote Phu Village, visiting ancient monasteries, traditional homes, and surrounding Himalayan landscapes.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Acclimatization &amp; Exploration in Phu Village"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Descend from the remote Phu Village and trek through dramatic landscapes to reach Nar Phedi Monastery, a peaceful spiritual retreat.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Trek from Phu Village to Nar Phedi"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "A short but steady ascent from Nar Phedi Monastery to the culturally rich and historic Nar Village.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Trek from Nar Phedi to Nar Village"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "A challenging high-altitude crossing from Nar Valley toward Ngawal, entering the Annapurna region with dramatic mountain views.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Trek from Nar Village to Ngawal"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "A scenic descent into the Manang valley with stunning views of Annapurna range and traditional Himalayan villages.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Trek from Ngawal to Manang"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "A gradual ascent from Manang to Yak Kharka as you enter higher alpine terrain with stunning mountain views.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Trek from Manang to Yak Kharka"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "A steady ascent through alpine terrain as you approach Thorong Phedi, the base for crossing Thorong La Pass.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Trek from Yak Kharka to Thorong Phedi"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "The most challenging and rewarding day of the trek as you cross Thorong La Pass and descend to the sacred site of Muktinath.", "elev": 5416, "title": "Day 13: Cross Thorong La Pass (5416m) and Trek to Muktinath"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "A scenic long drive descending from the Mustang region to the beautiful lakeside city of Pokhara.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Drive from Muktinath to Pokhara"}, {"day": "15", "desc": "A scenic drive back to Kathmandu from Pokhara, passing rivers, hills, and traditional villages along the highway.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 15: Drive from Pokhara to Kathmandu"}, {"day": "16", "desc": "Final departure from Kathmandu after completing the unforgettable Nar Phu Valley and Thorong La Pass trekking adventure.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 16: Departure from Kathmandu"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.805	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
