t: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<span data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></span><!--TgQPHd|||[]-->\n\n</div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<!--TgQPHd|||[]-->\n\n</div>\n<div data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">\n<div data-container-id="rhs-col" data-sfc-root="ep" data-ved="2ahUKEwjR5_jPyLSWAxXwWnADHVTBLPYQ3aYQegYIAAgJEAI" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: -58px 0px 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"></div>\n</div>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Upper-Dolpo-Trekkingsss.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	25 Days	3500	Nepal	Moderate		March – May	Heritage Hotels	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{}	<p><strong>The Trail Conditions: </strong></p>\n<p>Straight, Uphill, Downhill, Jig Jag with small rocky, pebbles, somewhere flat man made stone steps, through the rhododendron, moss covered forests, suspensions metal bridges</p>\n<p><strong>Medication </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bandage for sprains</li>\n<li>Plasters/Band-aids</li>\n<li>Iodine or water filter (optional)</li>\n<li>Moleskin/Second skin - for blisters</li>\n<li>Antiseptic ointment for cuts</li>\n<li>Anti-bacterial throat lozenges (with antiseptic)</li>\n<li>Aspirin/paracetamol - general painkiller</li>\n<li>Oral dehydration salts</li>\n<li>Broad-spectrum antibiotic (norfloxacin or ciprofloxin)</li>\n<li>Anti-diarrhea medication (antibiotic)</li>\n<li>Diarrhea stopper (Imodium - optional)</li>\n<li>Antibiotic for Giardia or similar microbe or bacteria</li>\n<li>Diamox (altitude sickness - can be bought in Kathmandu)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Clothing / Equipment List </strong></p>\n<p><em>Kindly bring the following list of clothing / equipment for our trek to Upper Dolpo Trek </em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pair trekking boots and waterproofing agent</li>\n<li>Pair lightweight trekking sandals</li>\n<li>Pairs thin walking socks</li>\n<li>Pairs lightweight wind – water proof pants</li>\n<li>T-shirts</li>\n<li>Fleece Jacket</li>\n<li>Set lightweight thermals</li>\n<li>North Face down Jacket (Preferably)</li>\n<li>Small thin towel (sports towel best)</li>\n<li>Soap</li>\n<li>Shampoo</li>\n<li>Sunscreen</li>\n<li>Extra lightweight shirt for daypacks - for stops along the way</li>\n<li>Hat</li>\n<li>Cotton or silk bag liner – optional</li>\n<li>Neck warmer</li>\n<li>Pairs 'thinners' gloves</li>\n<li>Rucksack</li>\n<li>Pack tissues</li>\n<li>Pair sunglasses</li>\n<li>Water filter / Iodine (you could buy boiled water in hotels/ lodges which is safe to drink.</li>\n<li>Camera and films</li>\n<li>Head torch and spare batteries</li>\n<li>Sleeping bag (rated -15(above) deg C during our trek)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Above things are required for Upper Dolpo trek. However if you do not have clothing you can either buy or rent in Nepal. In this case we have equipment cheaper than your country.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n	<ul data-start="134" data-end="1171">\n<li data-start="134" data-end="228">\n<p data-start="136" data-end="228">Airport Transfers: Pick-up and drop-off from Tribhuvan International Airport in Kathmandu.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="229" data-end="339">\n<p data-start="231" data-end="339">Accommodation in Kathmandu &amp; Nepalgunj: 3-star hotel accommodation on a twin-sharing basis with breakfast.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="340" data-end="422">\n<p data-start="342" data-end="422">Domestic Flights: Kathmandu–Nepalgunj and Nepalgunj–Jumla round-trip airfares.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="423" data-end="535">\n<p data-start="425" data-end="535">Trekking Permits: Upper Dolpo Restricted Area Permit, Shey Phoksundo National Park entry fee, and TIMS card.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="536" data-end="616">\n<p data-start="538" data-end="616">Trekking Accommodation: Tented or basic lodge accommodation during the trek.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="617" data-end="708">\n<p data-start="619" data-end="708">Meals During Trek: All meals (breakfast, lunch, and dinner) during the trekking period.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="709" data-end="822">\n<p data-start="711" data-end="822">Guide and Porters: Experienced licensed trekking guide and necessary porters (1 porter for every 2 trekkers).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="823" data-end="898">\n<p data-start="825" data-end="898">Staff Insurance: Insurance and proper equipment for all trekking staff.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="899" data-end="959">\n<p data-start="901" data-end="959">First Aid Kit: Basic first aid kit carried by the guide.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="960" data-end="1051">\n<p data-start="962" data-end="1051">Camping Equipment: Tents, mattresses, cooking utensils, and all necessary camping gear.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1052" data-end="1130">\n<p data-start="1054" data-end="1130">All Ground Transportation: As per itinerary by private or public vehicles.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1131" data-end="1171">\n<p data-start="1133" data-end="1171">Government Taxes and Service Charges</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-start="1203" data-end="1248">\n<p data-start="1205" data-end="1248">International Airfare: To and from Nepal.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1249" data-end="1325">\n<p data-start="1251" data-end="1325">Nepal Entry Visa: Visa fees and processing (can be obtained on arrival).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1326" data-end="1417">\n<p data-start="1328" data-end="1417">Lunch and Dinner in Kathmandu/Nepalgunj: Meals in cities not included except breakfast.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1418" data-end="1498">\n<p data-start="1420" data-end="1498">Personal Expenses: Bar bills, laundry, phone calls, extra snacks, or drinks.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1499" data-end="1600">\n<p data-start="1501" data-end="1600">Travel Insurance: Mandatory personal travel and medical insurance including emergency evacuation.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1601" data-end="1696">\n<p data-start="1603" data-end="1696">Tips and Gratitude: For guide, porter, and other trekking staff (optional but recommended).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1697" data-end="1801">\n<p data-start="1699" data-end="1801">Additional Costs: Due to unforeseen events like flight delays, weather issues, or natural disasters.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1802" data-end="1883">\n<p data-start="1804" data-end="1883">Extra Accommodation: If the trek is delayed or extended beyond the itinerary.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1884" data-end="1953">\n<p data-start="1886" data-end="1953">Any Other Costs: Not mentioned in the "Package Includes" section.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n		[]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000ekbrlytqiwa32	everest-three-pass-trek	Everest Three Pass Trek	<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=w2iAV_49/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-com	<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=w2iAV_49/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Everest Three Pass Trek – The Ultimate Himalayan Challenge<!--TgQPHd|||[]--><strong data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"> Three Pass Trek<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></strong> is the ultimate trekking adventure in Nepal's Khumbu region. It is designed for experienced hikers who want to experience the complete variety of terrains in the Everest sanctuary. Because it loops through high mountain passes and glacier valleys, this challenging multi-day expedition remains an absolute favorite for elite travelers seeking deep solitude and raw alpine wilderness.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=w2iAV_4i/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Conquer the Three Giant Mountain Passes<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIFRAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Your mountain journey begins with a scenic flight from Kathmandu to Lukla before following the trails into Sagarmatha National Park. Unlike standard base camp routes, this challenging circuit takes you over three massive high-altitude passes: Kongma La (5,535m), Cho La (5,420m), and Renjo La (5,360m). Along the way, staying in cozy local teahouses allows you to experience authentic Sherpa hospitality firsthand while resting after demanding trekking days.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=w2iAV_4q/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Discover Pristine Glaciers and Sacred Lakes<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIFhAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Arriving at the high points of the <strong data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Everest Three Pass Trek<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></strong> provides unparalleled close-up views of giant peaks, including Mount Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, and Makalu. Additionally, the route navigates through the dramatic Ngozumpa Glacier and passes along the beautiful, emerald-blue Gokyo Lakes. The challenging alpine paths allow for a thorough exploration of the entire region, making it a highly rewarding expedition for passionate high-altitude hikers.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=w2iAV_4z/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Why Choose This Legendary Wilderness Circuit?<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIFxAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" aria-owns="action-menu-parent-container" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Opting for the <strong data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Everest Three Pass Trek<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></strong> offers the perfect mix of dramatic high-mountain landscapes, deep cultural discovery, and raw physical challenge. It serves as an ideal choice for hikers who want a complete Himalayan holiday away from the standard crowded trails. Ultimately, this unforgettable journey delivers incredible photography opportunities, profound isolation, and a deep appreciation for the world's highest mountains.</div>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Everest-Kangsung-Face-Trek.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	20 Days	2499	Nepal	Moderate		March -June , Oct -Dec	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{}	<p><strong>The Trail Conditions </strong></p>\n<p>Straight, Up hill, Down hill, Jig Jag with small rocky, pebbles, muddy, some where dusty, man made stone steps, through the moss covered forests, Rocky glacier or If snows, snowy path crossing suspensions metal bridges and wooden bridges over the rivers</p>\n<p><strong>High Altitude Sickness: </strong></p>\n<p>Often times treks that ascends beyond 3500 m would require more days for acclimatization to ensure that trekkers do not suffer from high altitude sickness. The thinner air affects you in many ways and if you go high too fast there is a high chance to get effect.</p>\n<p><strong>Insurances of Guide and Porters</strong></p>\n<p>We do our Trekking insurance for the duration of 10 or 15 years from reputed insurance company in Kathmandu, Nepal which covers our insurance for the duration of our trek as well. On the other hand we (Himalayana Nomad Trek are member of TAAN (Trekking Agent Association of Nepal) TAAN takes fully responsible for the staffs of its members while we are on the trek. You are highly recommended to be insured for this trek from your country.</p>\n<p>We, Nepalese eat a meal of Dhal Bhaat (rice with lentil soup, curry and  pickles) twice daily. The ingredients vary according to local and seasonal availability, but vegetarian options are the norm. Another cheap popular local dish is the ubiquitous instant noodle soup, enhanced by local vegetables, or meat or egg, depending on availability.. Eating Nepali-style will provide you with a truly local experience, guarantees fresh ingredients everywhere, and rules out disappointments.</p>\n<p>Also, in all lodges tourists will be served their meals in the lodge dining room before the Nepali staff gets their meals in the kitchen or another place where guides and porters relax. And staff members' quarters are separate from the tourist rooms. This seemingly two-class system may be a difficult concept for some tourists, but it can also be seen as "time off" for the staff members. Nepalese eat mostly with their hands, a custom that is considered offensive by some tourists another reason why the staff members may actually prefer to eat separately.</p>\n<p><strong>Medication  </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bandage for sprains</li>\n<li>Plasters/Band-aids</li>\n<li>Iodine or water filter (optional)</li>\n<li>Moleskin/Second skin - for blisters</li>\n<li>Antiseptic ointment for cuts</li>\n<li>Anti-bacterial throat lozenges (with antiseptic)</li>\n<li>Aspirin/paracetamol - general painkiller</li>\n<li>Oral dehydration salts</li>\n<li>Broad-spectrum antibiotic (norfloxacin or ciprofloxin)</li>\n<li>Anti-diarrhea medication (antibiotic)</li>\n<li>Diarrhea stopper (Imodium - optional)</li>\n<li>Antibiotic for Giardia or similar microbe or bacteria</li>\n<li>Diamox (altitude sickness - can be bought in Kathmandu)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Clothing / Equipment List </strong></p>\n<p>Kindly bring the following list of clothing / equipment for our trek to Everest 3 pass Trek</p>\n<p>-Pair trekking boots and waterproofing agent</p>\n<p>-Pair lightweight trekking sandals</p>\n<p>-Pairs thin walking socks</p>\n<p>-Pairs lightweight wind – water proof pants</p>\n<p>-T-shirts</p>\n<p>-Fleece Jacket</p>\n<p>-Set lightweight thermals</p>\n<p>-North Face down Jacket (Preferably)</p>\n<p>-Small thin towel (sports towel best)<br />\n-Soap<br />\n-Shampoo<br />\n-Sunscreen<br />\n-Extra lightweight shirt for daypacks - for stops along the way<br />\n-Hat<br />\n-Cotton or silk bag liner - optional<br />\n-Neck warmer</p>\n<p>-Pairs 'thinners' gloves</p>\n<p>-Rucksack</p>\n<p>-Pack tissues</p>\n<p>-Pair sunglasses</p>\n<p>-Water filter / Iodine (you could buy boiled water in hotels/ lodges which is safe to drink.</p>\n<p>-Camera and films</p>\n<p>-Head torch and spare batteries</p>\n<p>-Sleeping bag (rated -15(above) D C during our trek )</p>\n<p>Above things are required for Everest 3 pass trek. However if you do not have clothing you can either buy or rent in Nepal. In this case we have equipment cheaper than your country.</p>\n				[]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000ckbrli4pl465z	trekking-langtang-gosaikunda-trek	Langtang - Gosainkunda Trek	<h2 data-section-id="1bcblte" data-start="276" data-end="320">Discover the Langtang and Gosaikunda Trek</h2>\n<p data-start="322" data-end="784">The <s	<h2 data-section-id="1bcblte" data-start="276" data-end="320">Discover the Langtang and Gosaikunda Trek</h2>\n<p data-start="322" data-end="784">The <strong data-start="326" data-end="354">Langtang Gosaikunda Trek</strong> is a rewarding Himalayan adventure that combines the natural beauty of Langtang Valley with the spiritual importance of the sacred Gosaikunda Lakes. This diverse journey takes you through peaceful forests, traditional Tamang villages, alpine landscapes, and dramatic mountain terrain. It is an excellent choice for trekkers who want to experience Nepal's scenery and culture beyond the more crowded Everest and Annapurna regions.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="oyxpxf" data-start="786" data-end="831">Explore Langtang Valley and Kyanjin Gompa</h3>\n<p data-start="833" data-end="1185">The adventure begins with a scenic drive from Kathmandu to Syabrubesi, the gateway to Langtang National Park. From there, the trail follows beautiful river valleys through dense forests filled with rhododendron, bamboo, and oak trees. Along the way, you will pass traditional Tamang settlements and experience the warm hospitality of local communities.</p>\n<p data-start="1187" data-end="1519">As the trail climbs higher, the landscape becomes increasingly spectacular. The journey leads to Kyanjin Gompa, an important cultural and spiritual center surrounded by impressive Himalayan peaks. From here, trekkers can enjoy panoramic views of Langtang Lirung, Dorje Lakpa, Yala Peak, Gangchempo, and other snow-covered mountains.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="tt0yky" data-start="1521" data-end="1566">Cross Lauribina Pass and Visit Gosaikunda</h3>\n<p data-start="1568" data-end="1794">One of the most exciting sections of the journey is the crossing of Lauribina Pass at approximately 4,610 meters. The challenging ascent rewards trekkers with expansive mountain views and a remarkable high-altitude experience.</p>\n<p data-start="1796" data-end="2140">Beyond the pass lies Gosaikunda, a sacred alpine lake surrounded by rugged Himalayan landscapes. The lake holds great religious significance for Hindu and Buddhist pilgrims and creates a peaceful setting for trekkers. The combination of natural beauty and cultural importance makes this section one of the most memorable parts of the adventure.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="jc4v4s" data-start="2142" data-end="2182">Why Choose This Himalayan Adventure?</h3>\n<p data-start="2184" data-end="2494">This trek is ideal for travelers looking for a combination of mountain scenery, cultural discovery, and challenging high-altitude trails. The route offers opportunities to explore traditional villages, interact with local communities, visit monasteries, and experience the changing landscapes of the Himalayas.</p>\n<p data-start="2496" data-end="2804">With comfortable teahouses, welcoming locals, and spectacular mountain views throughout the route, the <strong data-start="2599" data-end="2627">Langtang Gosaikunda Trek</strong> provides an unforgettable experience for adventurous travelers. It is a perfect choice for those seeking a diverse Himalayan journey filled with nature, culture, and adventure.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Langtang-Gosainkunda-Trek-2.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	11 Days	1199	langtang	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Jan	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{langtang-region}	<p><strong>The Trail Conditions: </strong></p>\n<p>Straight, Uphill, Downhill, Jig Jag with small rocky, pebbles, somewhere flat man made stone steps, through the rhododendron, moss covered forests, suspensions metal bridges</p>\n<p><strong>Medication </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bandage for sprains</li>\n<li>Plasters/Band-aids</li>\n<li>Iodine or water filter (optional)</li>\n<li>Moleskin/Second skin - for blisters</li>\n<li>Antiseptic ointment for cuts</li>\n<li>Anti-bacterial throat lozenges (with antiseptic)</li>\n<li>Aspirin/paracetamol - general painkiller</li>\n<li>Oral dehydration salts</li>\n<li>Broad-spectrum antibiotic (norfloxacin or ciprofloxin)</li>\n<li>Anti-diarrhea medication (antibiotic)</li>\n<li>Diarrhea stopper (Imodium - optional)</li>\n<li>Antibiotic for Giardia or similar microbe or bacteria</li>\n<li>Diamox (altitude sickness - can be bought in Kathmandu)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Clothing / Equipment List </strong></p>\n<p><em>Kindly bring the following list of clothing / equipment for our trek to Langtang / Gosaikunda Trek </em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pair trekking boots and waterproofing agent</li>\n<li>Pair lightweight trekking sandals</li>\n<li>Pairs thin walking socks</li>\n<li>Pairs lightweight wind – water proof pants</li>\n<li>T-shirts</li>\n<li>Fleece Jacket</li>\n<li>Set lightweight thermals</li>\n<li>North Face down Jacket (Preferably)</li>\n<li>Small thin towel (sports towel best)</li>\n<li>Soap</li>\n<li>Shampoo</li>\n<li>Sunscreen</li>\n<li>Extra lightweight shirt for daypacks - for stops along the way</li>\n<li>Hat</li>\n<li>Cotton or silk bag liner – optional</li>\n<li>Neck warmer</li>\n<li>Pairs 'thinners' gloves</li>\n<li>Rucksack</li>\n<li>Pack tissues</li>\n<li>Pair sunglasses</li>\n<li>Water filter / Iodine (you could buy boiled water in hotels/ lodges which is safe to drink.</li>\n<li>Camera and films</li>\n<li>Head torch and spare batteries</li>\n<li>Sleeping bag (rated -15(above) deg C during our trek)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Above things are required for Langtang / Gosaikunda Trek. However if you do not have clothing you can either buy or rent in Nepal. In this case we have equipment cheaper than your country.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n				[{"day": "1", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day1: Arrived in Kathmandu(1350m/4412ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "", "elev": 1750, "title": "Day 2: Kathmandu to Syabrubesi to Pairo (1,750m)(6 hrs drive, 2 hrs trek)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Pahiro to Ghoda Tabela (2,900m/9,514 ft)(6 hrs trek)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Ghoda Tabela to Kyanjin Gompa (3,870m/12,696 ft)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Kyanjin Gomba - explore"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Kyanjing to lama hotel"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Lama Hotel To Thulo sybru"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Thulo Sybru To lauribena"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9 : Lauribina To Gosaikunda Back Down To Singgompa"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: SingGompa To Dhunche Drive to Kathmandu"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11:Depature"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.813	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000dkbrletahwfet	ama-dablam-base-camp-trek	Amadablam Base Camp Trek	<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div data-scroll-root="">\n<div>\n<div role="presentation">\n<div>\n<div><article dir="auto" tabindex="-1" data-turn-id="request-W	<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div data-scroll-root="">\n<div>\n<div role="presentation">\n<div>\n<div><article dir="auto" tabindex="-1" data-turn-id="request-WEB:9fc28dc3-ea80-4f23-b62c-7f31632a2031-2" data-testid="conversation-turn-6" data-scroll-anchor="true" data-turn="assistant">\n<div>\n<div tabindex="-1">\n<div>\n<div dir="auto" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="158554ce-678c-473e-99da-d022957952fb" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-2">\n<div>\n<div>\n<h2 data-section-id="wjdbgu" data-start="349" data-end="386"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=23c6f1fa80babc08&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnv-xzMyjPDNa6rJZRwaCqPt8oyKOA:1783130572678&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gLZhoVnym8adqD7lVa5VazpkNnF17El65JJ9iJzoDhtOZ3c4eC69nGSxkgTuqjcXKqNMgXgZjsdxeXP2par2EF0hx65r7sbke9WNSWJsu8AnUiCaeGp0TMwyP00adf9kVcjGfczsBmcGvalsWdO1Mzy6wFVZw&amp;q=Amadabalam&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjfkP2C97eVAxWpcGwGHd-HEN8QtKgLegQILhAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Ama Dablam</a> Base Camp Trek Overview</h2>\n<p data-start="388" data-end="804">The Ama Dablam Base Camp Trek is one of Nepal's most scenic and rewarding trekking adventures. It takes you to the foot of the stunning Ama Dablam (6,812 m), one of the most beautiful mountains in the Himalayas. Although it is close to the Everest region, this trail is quieter than the Everest Base Camp Trek. Therefore, it is perfect for trekkers who want breathtaking mountain views and a peaceful experience.</p>\n<p data-start="806" data-end="1226">The journey begins with a scenic flight to Lukla. From there, you follow traditional Sherpa trails through beautiful villages such as Phakding, Namche Bazaar, Tengboche, and Pangboche. Along the way, you cross suspension bridges, walk through rhododendron forests, and pass colorful prayer flags. Moreover, the route lies inside Sagarmatha National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site rich in wildlife and natural beauty.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="bjmnsv" data-start="1228" data-end="1276">A Perfect Blend of Nature and Sherpa Culture</h3>\n<p data-start="1278" data-end="1571">Besides spectacular scenery, the trek offers a unique cultural experience. You can visit ancient Buddhist monasteries, meet friendly Sherpa families, and learn about their traditions. In addition, comfortable tea houses provide warm hospitality and delicious local meals after each day's walk.</p>\n<p data-start="1573" data-end="1908">As you gain altitude, the views become even more impressive. You will enjoy panoramic sights of Mount Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Thamserku, Kangtega, and many other Himalayan peaks. Finally, reaching Ama Dablam Base Camp at 4,570 meters is the highlight of the trek. Standing beneath the towering mountain is an unforgettable experience.</p>\n<p data-start="1910" data-end="2258">The best seasons for the Ama Dablam Base Camp Trek are spring (March to May) and autumn (September to November). During these months, the weather is usually stable, the skies are clear, and the mountain views are outstanding. However, good physical fitness is still important because the trail involves several days of walking at higher elevations.</p>\n<p data-start="2260" data-end="2578">Overall, the Ama Dablam Base Camp Trek is an excellent choice for travelers seeking incredible mountain scenery, rich Sherpa culture, and a less crowded Himalayan adventure. Whether you are an experienced trekker or an active beginner, this journey promises lasting memories and an authentic Everest region experience.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</article></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n&nbsp;\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div></div>\n</div>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/IMG_20260220_223042.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	12 Days	1499	everest	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Dec	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{everest-region}	<h4><strong>The Trail Conditions </strong></h4>\n<p>Straight, Up hill, Down hill, Jig Jag with small rocky, pebbles, muddy, some where dusty, man made stone steps, through the moss covered forests, Rocky glacier or If snows, snowy path crossing suspensions metal bridges and wooden bridges over the rivers</p>\n<h4><strong>High Altitude Sickness: </strong></h4>\n<p>Often times treks that ascend beyond 3500 m would require more days for acclimatization to ensure that trekkers do not suffer from high altitude sickness. The thinner air affects you in many ways and if you go high too fast there is a high chance to get affected.</p>\n<h4><strong>Insurances of Guide and Porters</strong></h4>\n<p>We do our Trekking insurance for the duration of 10 or 15 years from reputed insurance company in Kathmandu, Nepal which covers our insurance for the duration of our trek as well. On the other hand we (Hike Nepal) are a member of TAAN (Trekking Agent Association of Nepal) TAAN takes fully responsible for the staff of its members while we are on the trek. You are highly recommended to be insured for this trek from your country.</p>\n<p>We, Nepalese eat a meal of Dhal Bhaat (rice with lentil soup, curry, and pickles) twice daily. The ingredients vary according to local and seasonal availability, but vegetarian options are the norm. Another cheap popular local dish is the ubiquitous instant noodle soup, enhanced by local vegetables, or meat or egg, depending on availability. Eating Nepali-style will provide you with truly local experience, guarantees fresh ingredients everywhere, and rules out disappointments.</p>\n<p>Also, in all lodges tourists will be served their meals in the lodge dining room before the Nepali staff gets their meals in the kitchen or another place where guides and porters relax. And staff members' quarters are separate from the tourist rooms. This seemingly two-class system may be a difficult concept for some tourists, but it can also be seen as "time off" for the staff members. Nepalese eat mostly with their hands, a custom that is considered offensive by some tourists another reason why the staff members may actually prefer to eat separately.</p>\n<h4><strong>Medication  </strong></h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Bandage for sprains</li>\n<li>Plasters/Band-aids</li>\n<li>Iodine or water filter (optional)</li>\n<li>Moleskin/Second skin - for blisters</li>\n<li>Antiseptic ointment for cuts</li>\n<li>Anti-bacterial throat lozenges (with antiseptic)</li>\n<li>Aspirin/paracetamol - general painkiller</li>\n<li>Oral rehydration salts</li>\n<li>Broad-spectrum antibiotic (norfloxacin or ciprofloxacin)</li>\n<li>Anti-diarrhea medication (antibiotic)</li>\n<li>Diarrhea stopper (Imodium - optional)</li>\n<li>Antibiotic for Giardia or similar microbe or bacteria</li>\n<li>Diamox (altitude sickness - can be bought in Kathmandu)</li>\n</ul>\n<h4><strong>Clothing / Equipment List </strong></h4>\n<p>Kindly bring the following list of clothing/equipment for our trek to Everest Base Camp Trek</p>\n<p>-Pair trekking boots and waterproofing agent</p>\n<p>-Pair lightweight trekking sandals</p>\n<p>-Pairs thin walking socks</p>\n<p>-Pairs lightweight wind – water proof pants</p>\n<p>-T-shirts</p>\n<p>-Fleece Jacket</p>\n<p>-Set lightweight thermals</p>\n<p>-North Face down Jacket (Preferably)</p>\n<p>-Small thin towel (sports towel best)<br />\n-Soap<br />\n-Shampoo<br />\n-Sunscreen<br />\n-Extra lightweight shirt for daypacks - for stops along the way<br />\n-Hat<br />\n-Cotton or silk bag liner - optional<br />\n-Neck warmer</p>\n<p>-Pairs 'thinners' gloves</p>\n<p>-Rucksack</p>\n<p>-Pack tissues</p>\n<p>-Pair sunglasses</p>\n<p>-Water filter / Iodine (you could buy boiled water in hotels/ lodges which is safe to drink.</p>\n<p>-Camera and films</p>\n<p>-Head torch and spare batteries</p>\n<p>-Sleeping bag (rated -15(above) DC during our trek )</p>\n<p>The above things are required for Everest Base Camp. However, if you do not have clothing you can either buy or rent in Nepal. In this case we have equipment cheaper than your country.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n				[{"day": "1", "desc": "", "elev": 1350, "title": "Day 1 : Arrive in Kathm​andu (1350M)\\";"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Your adventure begins with an early morning mountain flight to Tenzing-Hillary Airport. The short flight itself is unforgettable, with dramatic views of snow-covered peaks stretching across the horizon. After landing, you meet your Everpeak Adventure guide and crew, who will assist with final preparations before starting the trek.\\n\\nThe walk to Phakding is gentle and relaxing, following the Dudh Koshi River through small villages, prayer wheels, and colorful suspension bridges. This first day is designed to help you ease into the trekking rhythm without pushing your body too hard.\\";", "elev": 2860, "title": "Day 2: Fly to Lukla (2,860 m) – Trek to Phakding (2,610 m)\\";"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Today is a more active day, taking around 6–7 hours. You officially enter Sagarmatha National Park, where forests, rivers, and mountain scenery surround you. The trail crosses several long suspension bridges, including the famous Hillary Bridge, hanging high above the river gorge.\\n\\nThe final climb to Namche Bazaar is steady and challenging, but your guide keeps a slow and comfortable pace. If the weather is clear, you may catch your first glimpse of Mount Everest along the way. Arriving in Namche feels exciting—this lively Sherpa town is full of energy, bakeries, small shops, and stunning mountain views.\\";s:23", "elev": 3440, "title": "Day 3: Phakding to Namche Bazaar (3,440 m)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": " This rest day is very important for adjusting to the altitude. Instead of staying completely inactive, Everpeak Adventure follows the “climb high, sleep low” rule. You hike up to Everest View Hotel or nearby viewpoints for panoramic views of Everest, Lhotse, and the breathtaking Ama Dablam. Seeing Ama Dablam standing tall in the distance builds excitement for the days ahead.\\n\\nAfter returning to Namche, you can relax at a café, explore the Sherpa museum, or simply enjoy the peaceful mountain atmosphere.\\";s:23:", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Acclimatization Day in Namche"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "", "elev": 3930, "title": "Day 5 : Tyangboche - Pangboche (3930m)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "", "elev": 4600, "title": "Day 6 : Pangboche - Amadablam Base camp- Pangboche (4600m)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "-Extra lightweight shirt for daypacks - for stops along the way\\n-Hat\\n-Cotton or silk bag liner - optional\\";", "elev": 3860, "title": "Day 7 : Pangboche- Phortse   (3860m)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "", "elev": 3440, "title": "Day 8 : Phortse- Namche Bazaar  (3440m)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "", "elev": 2840, "title": "Day 9 : Namche Bazaar- Lukla (2840m)"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.816	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000fkbrld1x0pg35	annapurna-panorama-trek	Annapurna Panorama Trek	<h1 data-section-id="78xg62" data-start="626" data-end="660"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=9d8d6ffe3c6fa5d1&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnsRrcO6kWk	<h1 data-section-id="78xg62" data-start="626" data-end="660"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=9d8d6ffe3c6fa5d1&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnsRrcO6kWkW6B1gKPs96XLWEvAbgw:1783135291486&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gKq1sgc0zFmtILFJcehpQnp8EvsgtsNoHlk8yRnPtPFZTFppidpMf3acGusE4WvlMaqVeJ_G7aj1Gz_ymywOPYPTIOv3WGYQHHgc5nVcfWPA2jyTEUSd8triSJAXyyatewLdgwLM3BOpfnoNdQL2VYGJg25xA&amp;q=Annapurna+Base+Camp+Trek&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwiKqorNiLiVAxVJxDgGHRiLAlQQtKgLegQIGBAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Annapurna</a> Panorama Trek Overview</h1>\n<p data-start="662" data-end="1094"><strong data-start="662" data-end="689"><a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/6-day-annapurna-base-camp-treking/">Annapurna</a> Panorama Trek</strong> is one of the most rewarding short trekking adventures in Nepal. It combines spectacular Himalayan scenery, traditional mountain villages, and rich local culture in the famous Annapurna region. Moreover, the trail is suitable for beginners, families, and experienced trekkers. Therefore, it is an excellent choice for anyone who wants an authentic Himalayan experience without reaching extreme altitudes.</p>\n<p data-start="1096" data-end="1508">The journey begins with a scenic drive from Pokhara before following well-maintained trails through rhododendron forests, terraced fields, and charming Gurung and Magar villages. Along the way, you cross suspension bridges, enjoy peaceful surroundings, and stay in comfortable tea houses. In addition, friendly local people warmly welcome visitors and share their traditions, making the trek even more memorable.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="1owba7a" data-start="1510" data-end="1538">Highlights of the Journey</h2>\n<p data-start="1540" data-end="1935">The biggest highlight is the early morning hike to the famous Poon Hill viewpoint. From the top, you can watch a breathtaking sunrise over Annapurna I, Annapurna South, Machhapuchhre (Fishtail), Dhaulagiri, Nilgiri, and Hiunchuli. Furthermore, the golden light on the snow-covered peaks creates unforgettable views. As a result, this viewpoint is one of the most photographed locations in Nepal.</p>\n<p data-start="1937" data-end="2277">Meanwhile, the trail continues through beautiful villages where you can experience local culture, taste traditional Nepali food, and learn about everyday mountain life. Likewise, the peaceful forests and colorful landscapes make every day enjoyable. Although the trek is relatively easy, it offers impressive scenery throughout the journey.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="bp5oa" data-start="2279" data-end="2300">Best Time to Visit</h2>\n<p data-start="2302" data-end="2617">Spring (March to May) and autumn (September to November) are the best seasons for the <strong data-start="2388" data-end="2415">Annapurna Panorama Trek</strong>. During these months, the weather is usually clear, and the mountain views are outstanding. However, winter also offers peaceful trails and beautiful snow-covered landscapes for well-prepared trekkers.</p>\n<p data-start="2619" data-end="2934">Overall, this trek is perfect for travelers looking for breathtaking mountain views, authentic village life, and a memorable Himalayan adventure. Whether you are visiting Nepal for the first time or returning to explore more of the Annapurna region, <strong data-start="2869" data-end="2896">Annapurna Panorama Trek</strong> promises an unforgettable experience.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Annapurna-Panoramasdfg.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	12 Days	1200	annapurna	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Feb		B.B.		\N	Trekking	{annapurna-region}					[]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.819	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000hkbrlmkuigcld	ghorepani-ghandruk-trek	Ghorepani Ghandruk trek	<h1 data-section-id="1a5y5no" data-start="249" data-end="283"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=23c6f1fa80babc08&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnutuY_XbK	<h1 data-section-id="1a5y5no" data-start="249" data-end="283"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=23c6f1fa80babc08&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnutuY_XbKpPm-7OLtItq_0WKc3CbA:1783131415827&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832cK-OlyrFp0q_lDSVqWSWpDEzO_-mUx3hdbQlSvWRAm3a3D3y0P_3kyEtVBac4Ukyhuw8w7LpgH4P8gabJmURZOPQ4a3gZGUodu7xwLfDZxZfAGRVNeHZa4rjqOzxW8vGjvSV0TkFaCxKU3opgvz93ZBmZmPf2FlC1JNr8eE-UUKshOmBQ&amp;q=ghandruk&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwid54KV-reVAxW9zDgGHdVfCdQQtKgLegQIFhAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Ghorepani Ghandruk</a> Trek Overview</h1>\n<p data-start="285" data-end="664">The <strong data-start="289" data-end="316"><a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/ghandruk-trekking/">Ghorepani Ghandruk</a> Trek</strong> is one of the most popular short treks in Nepal. It offers spectacular mountain views, charming Gurung and Magar villages, and beautiful rhododendron forests. Moreover, the trek is suitable for beginners, families, and experienced trekkers. Therefore, it is an excellent choice for anyone who wants to explore the Annapurna region in a short time.</p>\n<p data-start="666" data-end="1016">The journey begins with a scenic drive from Pokhara to Nayapul or Ulleri. From there, the trail passes through peaceful forests, stone staircases, rivers, and traditional mountain villages. Along the way, you enjoy warm local hospitality and comfortable tea houses. In addition, every day offers breathtaking views of the surrounding Himalayan peaks.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="fb82io" data-start="1018" data-end="1059">Sunrise at Poon Hill and Local Culture</h2>\n<p data-start="1061" data-end="1491">One of the biggest highlights of the <strong data-start="1098" data-end="1125">Ghorepani Ghandruk Trek</strong> is the early morning hike to <strong data-start="1155" data-end="1178">Poon Hill (3,210 m)</strong>. From the viewpoint, you can watch a spectacular sunrise over the Annapurna and Dhaulagiri mountain ranges. Furthermore, you enjoy panoramic views of Annapurna South, Machhapuchhre (Fishtail), Hiunchuli, Nilgiri, and many other snow-covered peaks. As a result, Poon Hill is one of Nepal's most famous viewpoints.</p>\n<p data-start="1493" data-end="1815">After visiting Poon Hill, the trail continues to the beautiful village of Ghandruk. Meanwhile, you can explore traditional stone houses, ancient monasteries, and the local Gurung Museum. Moreover, you have the opportunity to learn about Gurung culture, customs, and daily life while enjoying genuine Himalayan hospitality.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="bedqnn" data-start="1817" data-end="1861">Best Time for the Ghorepani Ghandruk Trek</h2>\n<p data-start="1863" data-end="2201">Spring (March to May) and autumn (September to November) are the best seasons for the <strong data-start="1949" data-end="1976">Ghorepani Ghandruk Trek</strong>. During spring, colorful rhododendron forests bloom across the hills. Likewise, autumn offers clear skies and excellent mountain views. However, this trek is also enjoyable during winter because the trails remain accessible.</p>\n<p data-start="2203" data-end="2513">Overall, the <strong data-start="2216" data-end="2243">Ghorepani Ghandruk Trek</strong> combines stunning Himalayan scenery, rich local culture, peaceful forests, and unforgettable sunrise views. Whether you are trekking in Nepal for the first time or returning for another adventure, this journey offers an unforgettable experience in the Annapurna region.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Ghorepani-Poonhill-Trekkingasdfgh.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	9 Days	999	annapurna	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Feb	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{annapurna-region}	<p><strong>The Trail Conditions: </strong></p>\n<p>Straight, Uphill, Downhill, Jig Jag with small rocky, pebbles, somewhere flat man made stone steps, through the rhododendron, moss covered forests, suspensions metal bridges</p>\n<p><strong>Medication </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bandage for sprains</li>\n<li>Plasters/Band-aids</li>\n<li>Iodine or water filter (optional)</li>\n<li>Moleskin/Second skin - for blisters</li>\n<li>Antiseptic ointment for cuts</li>\n<li>Anti-bacterial throat lozenges (with antiseptic)</li>\n<li>Aspirin/paracetamol - general painkiller</li>\n<li>Oral dehydration salts</li>\n<li>Broad-spectrum antibiotic (norfloxacin or ciprofloxin)</li>\n<li>Anti-diarrhea medication (antibiotic)</li>\n<li>Diarrhea stopper (Imodium - optional)</li>\n<li>Antibiotic for Giardia or similar microbe or bacteria</li>\n<li>Diamox (altitude sickness - can be bought in Kathmandu)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong> </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Clothing / Equipment List </strong></p>\n<p><em>Kindly bring the following list of clothing / equipment for our trek to Ghorepani ( Poon Hill Trek<br />\n</em></p>\n<p><strong> </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pair trekking boots and waterproofing agent</li>\n<li>Pair lightweight trekking sandals</li>\n<li>Pairs thin walking socks</li>\n<li>Pairs lightweight wind – water proof pants</li>\n<li>T-shirts</li>\n<li>Fleece Jacket</li>\n<li>Set lightweight thermals</li>\n<li>North Face down Jacket (Preferably)</li>\n<li>Small thin towel (sports towel best)</li>\n<li>Soap</li>\n<li>Shampoo</li>\n<li>Sunscreen</li>\n<li>Extra lightweight shirt for daypacks - for stops along the way</li>\n<li>Hat</li>\n<li>Cotton or silk bag liner – optional</li>\n<li>Neck warmer</li>\n<li>Pairs 'thinners' gloves</li>\n<li>Rucksack</li>\n<li>Pack tissues</li>\n<li>Pair sunglasses</li>\n<li>Water filter / Iodine (you could buy boiled water in hotels/ lodges which is safe to drink.</li>\n<li>Camera and films</li>\n<li>Head torch and spare batteries</li>\n<li>Sleeping bag (rated -15(above) deg C during our trek)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Above things are required for Ghorepani ( Poon Hill ) Trek. However if you do not have clothing you can either buy or rent in Nepal. In this case we have equipment cheaper than your country.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n				[{"day": "1", "desc": "We will meet you outside of Tribhuvan International Airport (TIA), waiting with a warm greeting and take you towards your hotel. In the evening, our team will explain overall pre - tour plan in brief. We will take you around thamel if you needed. Over Night hotel.   ", "elev": 0, "title": "Day - 1: Arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport (TIA) Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "After breakfast in the morning, we take a short 20-30 minutes flight from Kathmandu to Pokhara. Soon after takeoff from TIA in Kathmandu, the snowcapped giants of the Himalaya begin to appear. Arriving in Pokhara, the contrast is striking. The journey from Pokhara to Ulleri begins with a scenic drive along winding mountain roads, passing through terraced fields, rivers, and charming hillside villages. The road gradually climbs higher, offering glimpses of Annapurna peaks before reaching the Gurung village of Ulleri. Overnight at tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": " Day – 2: Fly to Pokhara / Drive to Ulleri (2050m/6750ft ) 30 min flight/ 3 hrs drive\\";"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "The trek from Ulleri to Ghorepani is a refreshing walk through enchanting section of Annapurna region. The trail winds gently uphill, shaded by dense rhododendron and oak trees. The path allows you to soak in the natural beauty and serenity of the forest. After few hours of trekking, the traditional houses of Ghorepani covered with Magar community can be seen. From the cozy tea houses of Ghorepani, we can see stunning views of Mt. Annapurna, Mt. Dhaulagiri and Mt. Nilgiri. Overnight at tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 3: Trek from Ulleri to Ghorepani (2780m / 9121ft) 4 hrs hike\\";"}, {"day": "4", "desc": " Early in the morning, we hike up to Poon Hill (3210m) observing the breathtaking sunrise over the Mt. Annapurna and Mt. Dhaulagiri ranges, where golden rays light up the snowcapped peaks in an unforgettable panorama. After returning to hotel for breakfast, we continue our hike towards another beautiful hilltop Tadapani through enchanting forests having fresh mountain air. Then the path leads to a peaceful, small village Tadapani, surrounded by forest. From here, we can enjoy the closer, dramatic views of the Himalayas such as Annapurna South, himchuli, and Mt. Fishtail in a serene setting.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 4: Trek form Ghorepani/Poon Hill to Tadapani (2680m/8727ft) 5 hrs hike\\";"}, {"day": "5", "desc": " The trek from Tadapani to Ghandruk is one of the most scenic and rewarding short sections of the Ghorepani Ghandruk section. Lasting around 3-4 hours, the trail descends through dense rhododendron and oak forests, where sunlight filters through the trees and the sound of birdsong fills the air. As the trail continues downhill, glimpses of terraced farmlands and traditional stone house begin to appear, signaling approach to the Gurung village of Ghandruk. By lunch time, we’ll be in Ghandruk, one of the most beautiful villages in Nepal,offering warm hospitality. From here, we can enjoy the breathtaking views of Himalayas. After a short explore around Ghandruk, we take a jeep or car to Pokhara. Within 3 hours the journey ends in Pokhara, the peaceful lakeside city. Overnight at hotel.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 5: Trek from Tadapani to Ghandruk / Drive to Pokhara (820m/2697ft) 4 hrs hike/ 3 hrs drive\\";"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "After completing our unforgettable journey, today we will take a flight back to Kathmandu.it will take around 30 minutes, finally we reach Kathmandu.Once we are in Kathmandu we take you a few historical places including Pashupathinath temple,Bouddhanath stupa and old Kathmandu royal place,which are must tourist attraction in Kathmandu.pashupatinath temple the holiest hindu temple dedicated to lord shiva, with a complex of shrines and cremation ghats.Boudhanath stupa one of largest spherical stupas in the worlds and a spiritual center for Tibetan Buddhism.Kathmandu durbar square once the royal palace,it is knows for its palaces,temples, and the famous kasthamandap structure from which Kathmandu gets its name.after visiting all the places we will take you to your hotel. overnight at hotel.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 6: Fly back to Kathmandu\\";"}, {"day": "7", "desc": " Today after breakfast we walk around tourist hub of thamel for last hour shopping. a quality souvenir for yourself and familys. After a wonderful trip as per your flight schedule,we will take you to the airport for your final departure namaste.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day ­– 7: Departure\\";s"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.825	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000jkbrlcx0iwzd9	everest-panorama-trek-2	Everest Ponarama trek	<h2 data-section-id="b96atx" data-start="443" data-end="506"><span role="text"><strong data-start="446" data-end="506"><a href="https://www.google.com	<h2 data-section-id="b96atx" data-start="443" data-end="506"><span role="text"><strong data-start="446" data-end="506"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=11b7b2325caaf8c6&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnuzRo8qvax5wmIUIvH99XU-8BwQww:1782911332830&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gIHbHEqXWbyThyPdUCKqTmZAKzBcRFb2qe3OBMfh6G5URtuzGpQgwyLjG0HlVfwOhBKT-_MjHW6JAI50fK8ctSDBzYN4QFmM5h2f-J2LGaBBmSbliULKp1HwnGA8zByXKCw81aKc7LO2xjbgBVfvicOu9VOvA&amp;q=everest&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjk56KlxrGVAxUaV3ADHYKfELAQtKgLegQIEhAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Everest Panorama</a> Trek – The Perfect Himalayan Experience</strong></span></h2>\n<p data-start="508" data-end="948">The <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking-types/everest-region/"><strong data-start="512" data-end="537">Everest Panorama Trek</strong> </a>is the perfect choice for travelers who want to experience the beauty of the Everest region without trekking to Everest Base Camp. <strong data-start="669" data-end="679">Unlike</strong> longer high-altitude expeditions, this journey combines breathtaking mountain scenery, authentic Sherpa culture, and comfortable trekking days. <strong data-start="824" data-end="839">As a result</strong>, it is ideal for families, beginners, and anyone with limited time who still dreams of seeing Mount Everest.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="upkd51" data-start="950" data-end="998"><span role="text"><strong data-start="953" data-end="998">Explore Sherpa Villages and Scenic Trails</strong></span></h2>\n<p data-start="1000" data-end="1528">The <strong data-start="1004" data-end="1029">Everest Panorama Trek</strong> begins with a spectacular mountain flight from Kathmandu to Lukla before following scenic trails through Sagarmatha National Park. <strong data-start="1161" data-end="1178">Along the way</strong>, you cross suspension bridges, walk through rhododendron and pine forests, and visit traditional Sherpa villages such as Phakding and Namche Bazaar. <strong data-start="1328" data-end="1343">Furthermore</strong>, friendly local hospitality and centuries-old monasteries provide a fascinating cultural experience. <strong data-start="1445" data-end="1460">In addition</strong>, every day offers incredible views of snow-covered Himalayan peaks.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="1c5l7v8" data-start="1530" data-end="1576"><span role="text"><strong data-start="1533" data-end="1576">Enjoy Incredible Everest Mountain Views</strong></span></h2>\n<p data-start="1578" data-end="2069">One of the highlights of the <strong data-start="1607" data-end="1632">Everest Panorama Trek</strong> is the hike to the famous Everest View Hotel, one of the world's highest hotels. <strong data-start="1714" data-end="1727">From here</strong>, trekkers enjoy unforgettable panoramic views of Mount Everest, Ama Dablam, Lhotse, Thamserku, and many other Himalayan giants. <strong data-start="1856" data-end="1869">Meanwhile</strong>, the gradual ascent allows proper acclimatization, making the trek safer and more enjoyable. <strong data-start="1963" data-end="1979">Consequently</strong>, you can appreciate the spectacular scenery while reducing the risk of altitude sickness.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="1wfzkpl" data-start="2071" data-end="2115"><span role="text"><strong data-start="2074" data-end="2115">Why Choose the Everest Panorama Trek?</strong></span></h2>\n<p data-start="2117" data-end="2629">The <strong data-start="2121" data-end="2146">Everest Panorama Trek</strong> offers the perfect balance of adventure, culture, and natural beauty. <strong data-start="2217" data-end="2229">Not only</strong> does it showcase some of the world's most famous mountains, <strong data-start="2290" data-end="2305">but it also</strong> introduces you to the unique traditions of the Sherpa people. <strong data-start="2368" data-end="2384">Additionally</strong>, the shorter itinerary makes it suitable for travelers with limited holiday time. <strong data-start="2467" data-end="2481">Ultimately</strong>, the <strong data-start="2487" data-end="2512">Everest Panorama Trek</strong> delivers an unforgettable Himalayan experience filled with stunning landscapes, rich culture, and lifelong memories.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/IMG20251130114737-scaled.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	9 Days	1300	everest	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Feb	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{everest-region}	<h3>Key Highlights of the Everest Panorama Trek</h3>\n<div class="flex flex-col text-sm pb-25">\n<article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:60184696-d07d-45f3-8cae-0858a15f062e-7" data-testid="conversation-turn-16" data-scroll-anchor="true" data-turn="assistant">\n<div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)">\n<div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn">\n<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow">\n<div class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" dir="auto" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="cd612c76-f6e8-470a-af82-bbb0b343b02d" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-2">\n<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]">\n<div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling">\n<ul data-start="50" data-end="1033" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">\n<li data-start="50" data-end="194">\n<p data-start="52" data-end="194">Scenic mountain flight from <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Kathmandu</span></span> to <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Lukla</span></span> with spectacular Himalayan views.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="196" data-end="331">\n<p data-start="198" data-end="331">Trek through the pristine landscapes of <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Sagarmatha National Park</span></span>, a UNESCO World Heritage Site rich in natural beauty.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="333" data-end="450">\n<p data-start="335" data-end="450">Explore <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Namche Bazaar</span></span>, the vibrant Sherpa capital and cultural hub of the Everest region.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="452" data-end="531">\n<p data-start="454" data-end="531">Panoramic viewpoints from the famous <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Everest View Hotel</span></span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="533" data-end="708">\n<p data-start="535" data-end="708">Stunning views of iconic Himalayan peaks including <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Mount Everest</span></span>, <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Ama Dablam</span></span>, and <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Lhotse</span></span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="710" data-end="821">\n<p data-start="712" data-end="821">Immersive Sherpa culture with monasteries, prayer flags, mani stones, and traditional teahouse hospitality.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="823" data-end="934">\n<p data-start="825" data-end="934">Moderate altitude (around 3,880 meters) with lower risk of altitude sickness compared to Everest Base Camp.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="936" data-end="1033" data-is-last-node="">\n<p data-start="938" data-end="1033" data-is-last-node="">Ideal short trek (7–10 days) suitable for beginners, families, and travelers with limited time.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</article>\n</div>\n<div class="pointer-events-none h-px w-px absolute bottom-0" aria-hidden="true" data-edge="true"></div>\n	<div class="tour-page time-table-price">\n<ul class="tour-page time-table-price-include">\n<li> Government local taxes, Permit and TIMs</li>\n<li><i class="ti-check"></i> A comprehensive medical kit</li>\n<li><i class="ti-check"></i> Company's t-shirt and trekking map</li>\n<li><i class="ti-check"></i> Airport Pick up and drop off</li>\n<li><i class="ti-check"></i> An English speaking guide and porters</li>\n<li><i class="ti-check"></i> Domestic land and air transportation</li>\n<li><i class="ti-check"></i> Food and Accommodation on Trek</li>\n<li><i class="ti-check"></i> 1 main course meals 3 times a day while on trekking with a cup of tea or coffee.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n	<div class="tour-page time-table-price">\n<ul class="tour-page time-table-price-exclude">\n<li data-start="1176" data-end="1240">\n<p data-start="1179" data-end="1206"><strong data-start="1179" data-end="1204">International Flights</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="1210" data-end="1240">\n<li data-start="1210" data-end="1240">Airfare to and from Nepal.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1242" data-end="1300">\n<p data-start="1245" data-end="1261"><strong data-start="1245" data-end="1259">Nepal Visa</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="1265" data-end="1300">\n<li data-start="1265" data-end="1300">Visa fees for entry into Nepal.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1302" data-end="1469">\n<p data-start="1305" data-end="1328"><strong data-start="1305" data-end="1326">Personal Expenses</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="1332" data-end="1469">\n<li data-start="1332" data-end="1410">Snacks, bottled drinks, extra meals in Kathmandu, and alcoholic beverages.</li>\n<li data-start="1414" data-end="1469">Hot showers, WiFi, and charging fees in tea houses.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1471" data-end="1581">\n<p data-start="1474" data-end="1496"><strong data-start="1474" data-end="1494">Travel Insurance</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="1500" data-end="1581">\n<li data-start="1500" data-end="1581">Mandatory insurance covering high-altitude trekking and emergency evacuation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1583" data-end="1681">\n<p data-start="1586" data-end="1610"><strong data-start="1586" data-end="1608">Trekking Equipment</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="1614" data-end="1681">\n<li data-start="1614" data-end="1681">Personal gear like trekking boots, jackets, poles, gloves, etc.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1683" data-end="1755">\n<p data-start="1686" data-end="1709"><strong data-start="1686" data-end="1707">Tips &amp; Gratuities</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="1713" data-end="1755">\n<li data-start="1713" data-end="1755">Tips for guides, porters, and drivers.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1757" data-end="1885">\n<p data-start="1760" data-end="1782"><strong data-start="1760" data-end="1780">Additional Costs</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="1786" data-end="1885">\n<li data-start="1786" data-end="1885">Extra night stays in Kathmandu due to early arrival, late departure, or bad weather conditions.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n		[{"day": "1", "desc": "Upon arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport in Kathmandu, our team will welcome you and transfer you to your hotel. After check-in, you can rest and recover from your journey. Kathmandu is a historic city rich in culture, temples, and traditional architecture. Later in the evening, your guide will provide a short trekking briefing, review the itinerary, and check essential trekking equipment before the adventure begins.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrive in Kathmandu (1350m / 4412ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "The adventure begins with a scenic mountain flight from Kathmandu to Lukla, offering incredible views of the Himalayan range. After landing at the famous Lukla airstrip, the trek begins through beautiful Sherpa villages, forests, and suspension bridges crossing the Dudh Koshi River. The trail is relatively gentle and allows your body to gradually adjust to the altitude before reaching the village of Phakding.", "elev": 2840, "title": "Day 2: Fly to Lukla (2840m) and Trek to Phakding (2610m)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Today’s trek follows the Dudh Koshi River valley and crosses several suspension bridges decorated with colorful prayer flags. After entering Sagarmatha National Park, the trail gradually climbs through forests of pine and rhododendron. The final ascent to Namche Bazaar is steep but rewarding, offering your first views of the surrounding Himalayan peaks. Namche Bazaar is the vibrant Sherpa capital of the Everest region.\\";", "elev": 3440, "title": "Day 3: Trek from Phakding to Namche Bazaar (3440m)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "This day is planned for acclimatization while enjoying spectacular mountain views. The trail climbs above Namche Bazaar to the famous Hotel Everest View, one of the highest hotels in the world. From here, trekkers enjoy breathtaking views of Mount Everest, Lhotse, and Ama Dablam. After spending time admiring the scenery, the trail continues to the traditional Sherpa village of Khumjung.", "elev": 3780, "title": "Day 4: Hike to Khumjung (3780m) via Hotel Everest View (3880m)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Today’s trek begins with a descent through beautiful forest trails before gradually climbing again toward Tengboche. Along the way, trekkers enjoy panoramic views of Everest, Ama Dablam, and other Himalayan peaks. Tengboche is famous for its historic monastery, one of the most important spiritual centers in the Everest region, surrounded by stunning mountain scenery.\\";", "elev": 3860, "title": "Day 5: Trek from Khumjung to Tengboche (3860m)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Leaving Tengboche, the trail descends through forests and small Sherpa settlements. You will pass through Namche Bazaar again before continuing further down the valley toward Monjo. As the altitude decreases, the landscape becomes greener and warmer. The route follows scenic river trails and suspension bridges, providing a relaxing yet rewarding day of trekking.", "elev": 2835, "title": "Day 6: Trek from Tengboche to Monjo (2835m)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "This is the final day of trekking in the Everest region. The trail follows the Dudh Koshi River and passes through several villages and forest trails you crossed earlier in the trek. Gradual climbs and descents lead back to Lukla, where the trekking journey concludes. In the evening, many trekkers celebrate the successful completion of their adventure with their guides and porters.", "elev": 2840, "title": "Day 7: Trek from Monjo to Lukla (2840m)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "An early morning flight takes you back to Kathmandu. The short but spectacular mountain flight offers one last view of the Himalayan peaks. After landing, you will be transferred to your hotel. The rest of the day is free to relax, explore local markets, or enjoy a comfortable meal after your successful trekking adventure.", "elev": 1350, "title": "Day 8: Fly from Lukla to Kathmandu (1350m)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "After breakfast, our team will transfer you to Tribhuvan International Airport for your international departure flight. This marks the end of your unforgettable trekking journey in Nepal. As you leave, you carry memories of spectacular mountain landscapes, Sherpa culture, and one of the world’s most famous trekking regions.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Depart from Kathmandu"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.83	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000kkbrls1yzwue2	6-day-annapurna-base-camp-treking	6-Day Annapurna Base Camp Trek	<h2 data-section-id="nf4i51" data-start="292" data-end="332">Discover the <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/annapurna-circuit-trek-via-	<h2 data-section-id="nf4i51" data-start="292" data-end="332">Discover the <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/annapurna-circuit-trek-via-tilicho-lake/">Annapurna</a> Base Camp Trek</h2>\n<p data-start="334" data-end="770">The <strong data-start="338" data-end="372">6-Day<a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=372d971a2d5e8d1e&amp;sxsrf=APpeQntU9q_UT-SuWKm7EOeV6Un425sVEg:1787390721705&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832QGGMdFXpDyzkQgEdtB8w9w-GD6PIjvNPpUnrx3WoOVI8IYRvRcHwOLNlkriIFPSnydpf9SoR6qrdb-NEaWJhlnMBK09v6fKwixdqyeLtOCLT1baDZVJgIJF_Ns2zsvTxtofK1dzpPxmGB4HH06aID26zFzsx_jYaoZ_lP5esYSWimXG1A&amp;q=annapurna&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwj21Kqo9bOWAxUhmeEIHYK4KgAQtKgLegQIGBAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25"> Annapurna Base Camp</a> Trek</strong> is an ideal Himalayan adventure for travelers who want to experience the beauty of Nepal in a limited amount of time. This short journey combines spectacular mountain scenery, traditional villages, peaceful forests, and unforgettable trekking experiences. Despite its compact itinerary, the route takes you deep into the Annapurna Sanctuary and close to some of the region’s most impressive peaks.</p>\n<p data-start="772" data-end="1163">The adventure begins with a scenic drive from Pokhara to Jhinu Danda, where the walking journey starts. From there, the trail passes through charming Gurung and Magar villages, lush rhododendron forests, terraced fields, and rushing mountain streams. Along the way, welcoming teahouses provide comfortable accommodation, traditional meals, and an opportunity to experience local hospitality.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="wa884v" data-start="1165" data-end="1199">Scenic Trails and Local Culture</h2>\n<p data-start="1201" data-end="1562">As the trail gains elevation, the landscape gradually changes from green valleys and forests to dramatic alpine terrain. The surrounding mountains become increasingly impressive, creating beautiful views throughout the journey. The peaceful villages and traditional lifestyles along the route also provide a genuine glimpse into life in the Himalayan foothills.</p>\n<p data-start="1564" data-end="1779">The trail eventually enters the Annapurna Sanctuary, a spectacular natural amphitheater surrounded by towering peaks. Fresh mountain air, quiet trails, and panoramic scenery make this section particularly rewarding.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="a8wdbe" data-start="1781" data-end="1809">Reach Annapurna Base Camp</h2>\n<p data-start="1811" data-end="2022">The ultimate destination is <strong data-start="1839" data-end="1878">Annapurna Base Camp at 4,130 meters</strong>. From the base camp, trekkers can enjoy magnificent views of Annapurna I, Machhapuchhre (Fishtail), Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, and Gangapurna.</p>\n<p data-start="2024" data-end="2244">Early morning is one of the most memorable times to be there, as the first sunlight illuminates the surrounding snow-covered peaks. Standing beneath these enormous mountains creates an unforgettable Himalayan experience.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="16lbvu7" data-start="2246" data-end="2270">Why Choose This Trek?</h2>\n<p data-start="2272" data-end="2576">This short Himalayan adventure is suitable for travelers with a reasonable level of fitness who want to explore the mountains without spending several weeks on the trail. Established paths, teahouse accommodation, beautiful scenery, and cultural encounters make the journey both convenient and rewarding.</p>\n<p data-start="2578" data-end="2759">For travelers looking for a <strong data-start="2606" data-end="2645">short Annapurna trekking experience</strong>, this route offers an excellent combination of mountain views, local culture, and adventure within just six days.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/IMG_20260220_221909.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	6 Days	649	annapurna	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Jan	Tea House	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{annapurna-region}	<ul data-start="160" data-end="1128">\n<li data-start="160" data-end="254">\n<p data-start="162" data-end="254">Scenic drive from Pokhara to Jhinu, followed by a beautiful trek into the Annapurna region</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="255" data-end="338">\n<p data-start="257" data-end="338">Reach Annapurna Base Camp (4,130 meters) surrounded by stunning Himalayan peaks</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="339" data-end="432">\n<p data-start="341" data-end="432">Enjoy close views of Annapurna I, Machapuchhre (Fishtail), Hiunchuli, and Annapurna South</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="433" data-end="525">\n<p data-start="435" data-end="525">Experience traditional Gurung and Magar villages, including the famous Chhomrong village</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="526" data-end="610">\n<p data-start="528" data-end="610">Walk through lush forests filled with bamboo, waterfalls, and rhododendron trees</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="611" data-end="687">\n<p data-start="613" data-end="687">Explore the peaceful and breathtaking Annapurna Sanctuary glacial valley</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="688" data-end="766">\n<p data-start="690" data-end="766">Witness unforgettable sunrise and sunset views over snow-covered mountains</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="767" data-end="842">\n<p data-start="769" data-end="842">Stay in traditional mountain teahouses and experience local hospitality</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="843" data-end="933">\n<p data-start="845" data-end="933">Opportunity to see wildlife such as langur monkeys, Himalayan thar, and colorful birds</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="934" data-end="1027">\n<p data-start="936" data-end="1027">Short and rewarding trek suitable for trekkers with limited time but big Himalayan dreams</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1028" data-end="1128">\n<p data-start="1030" data-end="1128">Experience a complete journey from green hills to high alpine mountain landscapes in just six days</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Authorized English-speaking/local Expert Trekking Guide x1 during trek</li>\n<li>Hotel pickup and drop-off</li>\n<li>Road permits, all necessary paperwork, ACAP, and Trekkers' Information Management System fee(s)</li>\n<li>All applicable government tax</li>\n<li>Accommodation x4 nights during the trek</li>\n<li>All meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) during the trek</li>\n<li>Private Transportation by 4 wheel drive jeep from Pokhara to Samrung and Jhinu Hot Spring to Pokhara as<br />\nper the itinerary.</li>\n<li>All expenses for the guide/porter; meals, accommodation, salary, equipment, insurance, and<br />\ntransportation.</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Soft and hard drinks</li>\n<li>Travel and rescue insurance</li>\n<li>International flights; Nepalese visa fee</li>\n<li>Tips for guide(s), porter(s) and driver(s)</li>\n<li>Personal expenses (phone calls, laundry, bar bills, battery recharge, extra porters, bottle or boiled water,<br />\nshower, etc.)</li>\n<li>Extra night accommodation in Pokhara because of early arrival, late departure, or early return from the<br />\ntrip due to any reason other than the scheduled itinerary</li>\n</ul>\n		[{"day": "1", "desc": "Your Annapurna Base Camp trek begins with a scenic journey from Pokhara (822m) to Chhomrong (2,150m), a beautiful Gurung village and the gateway to the sanctuary. After a comfortable drive from Pokhara, the trek starts through lush green hills, terraced farmlands, and traditional settlements. The trail includes gradual ascents and offers stunning views of Annapurna South and the iconic Machhapuchhre (Fishtail) mountain. The peaceful environment and fresh mountain air make the walk enjoyable and refreshing. Chhomrong is a culturally rich village with warm hospitality and breathtaking scenery. You will spend your first night here in a cozy teahouse, preparing for the higher elevations ahead.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day1:- Pokhara – Chomrong\\";"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "After breakfast in Chhomrong, the trek begins with a steep descent on stone steps to the Chhomrong Khola. After crossing a suspension bridge, you will climb uphill to reach Sinuwa, where you can enjoy beautiful forest and mountain views. From Sinuwa, the trail continues through dense bamboo and rhododendron forests, offering a peaceful walking experience. The path is mostly gradual with some short ascents and descents. You will reach Bamboo, a quiet forest settlement, where you will stay overnight in a teahouse surrounded by nature.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day2:- Chomrong - bamboo"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Today’s trek continues through peaceful bamboo and rhododendron forests as you gradually gain altitude. The trail passes through small settlements like Dovan and Himalaya, where you can stop for rest and enjoy the fresh mountain air. As you move higher, the forest becomes thinner and the landscape starts to open up. You will walk alongside the Modi Khola and see beautiful waterfalls and rocky cliffs. After a steady climb, you will reach Deurali, a quiet mountain stop surrounded by impressive Himalayan scenery.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day3:- Bamboo – Deurali\\";"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Today is the highlight of your Annapurna Base Camp trek as you journey from Deurali to Annapurna Base Camp (4,130m). The trail gradually ascends through alpine landscapes and brings you to Machhapuchhre Base Camp, where the views become more dramatic and close. Continuing onward, you enter the Annapurna Sanctuary, surrounded by towering snow-covered peaks. The final destination, Annapurna Base Camp, offers breathtaking 360-degree panoramic views of Annapurna I, Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, and Machhapuchhre. The feeling of standing in the heart of the Himalayas is unforgettable. Overnight stay at a teahouse in Annapurna Base Camp.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Deurali – Annapurna Base Camp\\";"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "After spending a remarkable night at Annapurna Base Camp, you begin your descent toward Bamboo. The day starts with breathtaking morning views of the surrounding peaks before retracing the trail through Machhapuchhre Base Camp and Deurali. As you continue downward, the rugged alpine environment slowly gives way to greener surroundings filled with rhododendron and bamboo forests. The trail is long but mostly downhill, making it easier to walk while still requiring good endurance. Bamboo offers a peaceful resting place beside the forest, providing a comfortable setting to relax after one of the most rewarding sections of the trek.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Annapurna Base Camp – Bamboo\\";"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Your final day begins with a pleasant descent from Bamboo, passing through beautiful forests and familiar villages along the Modi River valley. The trail continues toward the road access point, marking the end of your trekking journey. From here, you will take a scenic drive back to Pokhara, where comfortable hotels, restaurants, and lakeside views await. Returning to Pokhara brings a sense of achievement after completing one of Nepal’s most iconic treks. The rest of the day is free to relax, enjoy the peaceful atmosphere by the lake, and reflect on the unforgettable experience in the Annapurna region.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Bamboo to Pokhara"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.832	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000lkbrleeggiull	annapurna-circuit-trek	Annapurna Circuit Trek	<h2 data-section-id="si30zp" data-start="321" data-end="355"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=372d971a2d5e8d1e&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnuYngcB2DR	<h2 data-section-id="si30zp" data-start="321" data-end="355"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=372d971a2d5e8d1e&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnuYngcB2DRR9sUevhHjXj6WZq4DwQ:1787390407236&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832QGGMdFXpDyzkQgEdtB8w9w-GD6PIjvNPpUnrx3WoOVI8IYRvRcHwOLNlkriIFPSnydpf9SoR6qrdb-NEaWJhlnMBK09v6fKwixdqyeLtOCLT1baDZVJgIJF_Ns2zsvTxtofK1dzpPxmGB4HH06aID26zFzsx_jYaoZ_lP5esYSWimXG1A&amp;q=annapurna&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjmh7GS9LOWAxWYxzgGHcrxOUwQtKgLegQIFRAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Annapurna</a> Circuit Trek Overview</h2>\n<p data-start="357" data-end="674">The <strong data-start="361" data-end="387">Annapurna Circuit Trek</strong> is one of Nepal’s most diverse Himalayan adventures, taking travelers through lush forests, peaceful mountain villages, alpine valleys, and dramatic high-altitude landscapes. The route offers an incredible combination of natural beauty, local culture, and exciting mountain experiences.</p>\n<p data-start="676" data-end="1034">From the lower valleys to the high Himalayan passes, the scenery changes throughout the journey. Trekkers can enjoy terraced fields, rhododendron forests, traditional settlements, rocky landscapes, and spectacular views of snow-covered peaks. The gradual change in altitude also allows time to experience different environments and communities along the way.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="19t8c52" data-start="1036" data-end="1073">Highlights of the <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/annapurna-circuit-trek-via-tilicho-lake/">Annapurna</a> Region</h2>\n<p data-start="1075" data-end="1383">The trail passes through communities influenced by Gurung, Manang, and Thakali cultures. Travelers can experience traditional village life, local food, mountain hospitality, and historic religious sites. These cultural encounters add depth to the adventure and provide a closer look at life in the Himalayas.</p>\n<p data-start="1385" data-end="1606">The route also offers impressive views of <strong data-start="1427" data-end="1514">Annapurna II, Annapurna III, Gangapurna, Tilicho Peak, Chulu Peaks, and Pisang Peak</strong>. Each section of the journey provides a different perspective of the surrounding mountains.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="uze1xc" data-start="1608" data-end="1635">Crossing Thorong La Pass</h2>\n<p data-start="1637" data-end="1926">One of the most memorable parts of the journey is crossing <strong data-start="1696" data-end="1731">Thorong La Pass at 5,416 meters</strong>. The climb requires proper preparation and acclimatization, particularly around Manang. Reaching the pass is a rewarding achievement, with panoramic Himalayan views making the effort worthwhile.</p>\n<p data-start="1928" data-end="2113">After crossing the pass, the trail descends toward Muktinath and continues through the dramatic Kali Gandaki region. The changing terrain makes the route exciting from beginning to end.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="r0jqf3" data-start="2115" data-end="2154">Why Choose This Himalayan Adventure?</h2>\n<p data-start="2156" data-end="2413">This trek is an excellent choice for travelers looking for a combination of mountain scenery, cultural discovery, and outdoor adventure. Comfortable teahouses, welcoming local communities, and experienced trekking support make the experience more enjoyable.</p>\n<p data-start="2415" data-end="2607">Whether you are an experienced trekker or planning your first major Himalayan journey, the <strong data-start="2506" data-end="2527">Annapurna Circuit</strong> offers an unforgettable way to explore Nepal’s spectacular mountain landscapes.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/everpeak-adventures-e1773406653298.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	13 days	1399	annapurna	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Dec	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{annapurna-region}	<p data-start="40" data-end="123">• Cross Thorong La Pass (5,416m), one of the highest trekking passes in the world</p>\n<p data-start="125" data-end="205">• Experience dramatic landscape changes from green hills to high alpine desert</p>\n<p data-start="207" data-end="287">• Enjoy breathtaking views of Annapurna, Dhaulagiri, Manaslu, and Tilicho Peak</p>\n<p data-start="289" data-end="359">• Explore beautiful mountain villages like Chame, Pisang, and Manang</p>\n<p data-start="361" data-end="442">• Visit the sacred temple of Muktinath, important for both Hindus and Buddhists</p>\n<p data-start="444" data-end="515">• Walk through the Kali Gandaki Gorge, the deepest gorge in the world</p>\n<p data-start="517" data-end="591">• Discover unique culture influenced by Tibetan and Himalayan traditions</p>\n<p data-start="593" data-end="677">• Visit Manang village, one of the most scenic and important acclimatization stops</p>\n<p data-start="679" data-end="723">• Relax in natural hot springs at Tatopani</p>\n<p data-start="725" data-end="810">• Experience peaceful monasteries, prayer flags, and traditional mountain lifestyle</p>\n<p data-start="812" data-end="875">• Walk through diverse forests of pine, oak, and rhododendron</p>\n<p data-start="877" data-end="953">• Suitable for trekkers seeking a complete and diverse Himalayan adventure</p>\n	<div dir="auto">\n<p data-start="45" data-end="96">• Airport pick-up and drop-off by private vehicle</p>\n<p data-start="98" data-end="177">• Standard hotel accommodation in Kathmandu with breakfast (as per itinerary)</p>\n<p data-start="179" data-end="323">• Tourist bus or private vehicle transportation (Kathmandu to trek starting point and trek ending point to Kathmandu/Pokhara as per itinerary)</p>\n<p data-start="325" data-end="404">• Domestic flights if required by itinerary (if applicable, optional upgrade)</p>\n<p data-start="406" data-end="464">• Accommodation in comfortable teahouses during the trek</p>\n<p data-start="466" data-end="534">• Three meals a day during the trek (Breakfast, Lunch, and Dinner)</p>\n<p data-start="536" data-end="598">• Experienced, licensed, and English-speaking trekking guide</p>\n<p data-start="600" data-end="717">• Necessary number of porters (1 porter for 2 trekkers), including their salary, insurance, food, and accommodation</p>\n<p data-start="719" data-end="764">• Annapurna Conservation Area Permit (ACAP)</p>\n<p data-start="766" data-end="821">• Trekkers’ Information Management System (TIMS) card</p>\n<p data-start="823" data-end="876">• All government taxes and official service charges</p>\n<p data-start="878" data-end="916">• First aid kit carried by the guide</p>\n<p data-start="1013" data-end="1107">• Assistance for emergency rescue arrangement (rescue cost covered by your travel insurance)</p>\n</div>\n	<div dir="auto">\n<p data-start="45" data-end="88">• International airfare to and from Nepal</p>\n<p data-start="90" data-end="140">• Nepal entry visa fees and visa extension costs</p>\n<p data-start="142" data-end="234">• Travel insurance (must include high-altitude trekking and emergency evacuation coverage)</p>\n<p data-start="236" data-end="318">• Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu and Pokhara</p>\n<p data-start="320" data-end="399">• Personal trekking equipment and gear (such as boots, jackets, gloves, etc.)</p>\n<p data-start="401" data-end="490">• Personal expenses such as hot shower, Wi-Fi, charging, telephone, laundry, and drinks</p>\n<p data-start="492" data-end="606">• All kinds of beverages including tea, coffee, soft drinks, bottled water, and alcoholic drinks during the trek</p>\n<p data-start="608" data-end="664">• Porter service beyond the standard package allowance</p>\n<p data-start="666" data-end="722">• Tips for guide and porter (expected and appreciated)</p>\n<p data-start="724" data-end="812">• Extra accommodation and meals due to flight delay, early return, or personal reasons</p>\n<p data-start="814" data-end="918">• Costs arising from natural disasters, weather conditions, strikes, or other unforeseen circumstances</p>\n<p data-start="920" data-end="983">• Any expenses not mentioned in the “Package Include” section</p>\n</div>\n	<h3 data-start="31" data-end="43">Clothing</h3>\n<p data-start="45" data-end="409">• Moisture-wicking base layer (top and bottom)<br data-start="91" data-end="94" />• Warm fleece or insulated jacket<br data-start="127" data-end="130" />• Down jacket (for cold and high altitude)<br data-start="172" data-end="175" />• Waterproof and windproof outer jacket<br data-start="214" data-end="217" />• Trekking pants (2–3 pairs)<br data-start="245" data-end="248" />• Thermal innerwear<br data-start="267" data-end="270" />• Warm hat or beanie<br data-start="290" data-end="293" />• Sun hat or cap<br data-start="309" data-end="312" />• Warm gloves and inner gloves<br data-start="342" data-end="345" />• Wool or trekking socks (3–5 pairs)<br data-start="381" data-end="384" />• Comfortable underwear</p>\n<hr data-start="411" data-end="414" />\n<h3 data-start="416" data-end="428">Footwear</h3>\n<p data-start="430" data-end="573">• Good quality waterproof trekking boots<br data-start="470" data-end="473" />• Lightweight shoes or sandals (for teahouse use)<br data-start="522" data-end="525" />• Gaiters (optional, useful for snow and dust)</p>\n<hr data-start="575" data-end="578" />\n<h3 data-start="580" data-end="588">Bags</h3>\n<p data-start="590" data-end="728">• Daypack (20–30 liters)<br data-start="614" data-end="617" />• Duffel bag (carried by porter)<br data-start="649" data-end="652" />• Rain cover for backpack<br data-start="677" data-end="680" />• Dry bags or plastic bags (to keep items dry)</p>\n<hr data-start="730" data-end="733" />\n<h3 data-start="735" data-end="752">Sleeping Gear</h3>\n<p data-start="754" data-end="851">• Sleeping bag (rated for cold temperatures)<br data-start="798" data-end="801" />• Sleeping bag liner (optional for extra warmth)</p>\n<hr data-start="853" data-end="856" />\n<h3 data-start="858" data-end="880">Trekking Equipment</h3>\n<p data-start="882" data-end="1062">• Trekking poles<br data-start="898" data-end="901" />• Sunglasses with UV protection<br data-start="932" data-end="935" />• Headlamp or flashlight with extra batteries<br data-start="980" data-end="983" />• Water bottles or hydration bladder<br data-start="1019" data-end="1022" />• Water purification tablets or filter</p>\n<hr data-start="1064" data-end="1067" />\n<h3 data-start="1069" data-end="1087">Personal Items</h3>\n<p data-start="1089" data-end="1237">• Sunscreen (SPF 30 or higher)<br data-start="1119" data-end="1122" />• Lip balm with SPF<br data-start="1141" data-end="1144" />• Personal toiletries<br data-start="1165" data-end="1168" />• Quick-dry towel<br data-start="1185" data-end="1188" />• Hand sanitizer<br data-start="1204" data-end="1207" />• Wet wipes and tissue paper</p>\n<hr data-start="1239" data-end="1242" />\n<h3 data-start="1244" data-end="1269">Medical and First Aid</h3>\n<p data-start="1271" data-end="1422">• Personal medications<br data-start="1293" data-end="1296" />• Basic first aid kit<br data-start="1317" data-end="1320" />• Blister treatment<br data-start="1339" data-end="1342" />• Pain relief tablets<br data-start="1363" data-end="1366" />• Altitude sickness prevention medicine (consult doctor)</p>\n<hr data-start="1424" data-end="1427" />\n<h3 data-start="1429" data-end="1460">Documents and Miscellaneous</h3>\n<p data-start="1462" data-end="1576">• Passport and permits<br data-start="1484" data-end="1487" />• Travel insurance copy<br data-start="1510" data-end="1513" />• Cash (local currency)<br data-start="1536" data-end="1539" />• Camera and charger<br data-start="1559" data-end="1562" />• Power bank</p>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Welcome to Kathmandu, the capital city of Nepal and the starting point of your Annapurna Circuit Trek. Upon your arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport, our representative will greet you and transfer you to your hotel. After check-in, you can relax and recover from your journey. Depending on your arrival time, you may explore the nearby streets, local markets, and experience the vibrant atmosphere of the city. In the evening, there will be a trek briefing where your guide will explain the trek and check your preparation. Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival In Kathmandu"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "After breakfast, you will begin your journey from Kathmandu toward Dharapani via Besisahar. The drive follows scenic highways, rivers, and beautiful countryside with views of hills, terraced farms, and traditional villages. After reaching Besisahar, the road becomes more adventurous as you continue along a mountain trail toward Dharapani. This village marks the official starting point of the Annapurna Circuit Trek and offers your first experience of the mountain environment. Upon arrival, you can relax and enjoy the peaceful surroundings. Overnight stay at teahouse in Dharapani.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2:Kathmandu - Besisahar - Dharapani(1800m/5,905 ft) (8/9 hrs drive)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "From Dharapani, your trek officially begins as you follow the Annapurna trail deeper into the mountains toward Chame. The trail winds through pine and fir forests, traditional villages, and alongside the Marsyangdi River, with beautiful views of the surrounding Himalayan peaks gradually unfolding. This scenic and steady ascent marks the true beginning of your high-altitude adventure. Upon reaching Chame, the district headquarters of Manang, you will stay overnight at a comfortable teahouse, where you can relax and prepare for the days ahead.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Dharapani to Chame (2,670m / 8,760ft) – 6 hrs trek\\";"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "After leaving Chame, you’ll trek through pine and fir forests, passing small traditional villages along the way, such as Telaku and Bhratang . The trail gradually climbs up to Dhukurpokhari offering stunning views of Annapurna II, Annapurna IV, and Pisang Peak. You’ll reach Upper Pisang, a picturesque hillside village with stone houses, prayer flags, and a monastery, where you can relax, explore, and soak in the breathtaking Himalayan scenery.\\";s:", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Chame to Upper Pisang (3,300m / 10,826ft) – 6 hrs trek\\";"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "The trek from Upper Pisang to Manang is one of the most scenic sections of the Annapurna Circuit. You will follow the higher trail, which offers spectacular panoramic views of Annapurna II, Annapurna III, Gangapurna, and Tilicho Peak. The trail passes through traditional villages such as Ghyaru and Ngawal, where you can experience local culture and lifestyle. As you approach Manang, the landscape becomes more open and dry, reflecting the high Himalayan environment. Manang is a beautiful village and an important acclimatization stop. Overnight stay at teahouse in Manang.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Upper Pisang to Manang (3,540m / 11,614ft) – 6 hrs trek\\";"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Today is a rest and acclimatization day in Manang, allowing your body to adjust to the higher altitude before continuing further. You may take a short hike to nearby viewpoints such as Gangapurna Lake, Ice Lake, or a local monastery for better acclimatization and stunning mountain views. Manang is a beautiful village surrounded by Annapurna III, Gangapurna, and Tilicho Peak. You can also explore the village, visit local bakeries, or learn about the culture and lifestyle of the region. Overnight stay at teahouse in Manang.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Manang (3,540m / 11,614ft) – Acclimatization Day\\";"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Today’s trek from Manang to Yak Kharka is a gradual ascent into a more open and rugged Himalayan landscape. The trail climbs steadily above the tree line, offering wide views of surrounding mountains and valleys. You may see grazing yaks and traditional herding settlements along the way, which gives Yak Kharka its name. The peaceful environment and dramatic scenery make this section unique and memorable. As the altitude increases, the air becomes thinner, so proper pacing is important. Upon arrival, you will rest and prepare for the higher elevation ahead. Overnight stay at teahouse in Yak Kharka.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Manang to Yak Kharka (4,050m / 13,287ft) – 6 hrs trek\\";"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "Today’s trek from Yak Kharka to Thorong Phedi is shorter but very important as it prepares you for crossing Thorong La Pass. The trail gradually ascends through rocky terrain and offers impressive views of surrounding snow-covered peaks. The landscape becomes more barren and dramatic as you approach Thorong Phedi, which lies at the base of the pass. This is the final stop before the most challenging and rewarding day of the trek. After arriving, you will rest, prepare your equipment, and get ready for the early morning climb. Overnight stay at teahouse in Thorong Phedi.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Yak Kharka to Thorong Phedi (4,450m / 14,600ft) – 6 hrs trek\\";"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "Today is the highlight of the Annapurna Circuit as you cross Thorong La Pass, the highest point of the trek at 5,416 meters. The climb is demanding but incredibly rewarding, offering breathtaking panoramic views of the Annapurna and Dhaulagiri ranges. After reaching the top, you will have time to rest and take photos before beginning the long descent toward Muktinath. The trail gradually leads to the sacred village of Muktinath, an important pilgrimage site for both Hindus and Buddhists. This is a truly memorable and fulfilling day of your trekking journey. Overnight stay at teahouse in Muktinath.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Thorong Phedi to Muktinath (3,800m / 12,467ft) via Thorong La Pass (5,416m / 17,769ft) – 12 hrs trek\\";"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "After breakfast, you will begin your scenic drive from Muktinath to Pokhara. The journey passes through the beautiful Kali Gandaki valley, traditional villages, and diverse landscapes ranging from dry mountain terrain to green hills. Along the way, you will enjoy views of rivers, waterfalls, and rural countryside. As you reach Pokhara, you will notice the warmer climate and comfortable environment. Pokhara is a peaceful lakeside city and the perfect place to relax after completing your Annapurna Circuit Trek. Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Muktinath to Pokhara (822m / 2,697ft) – 8 hrs drive\\";"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "Today you will explore the beautiful city of Pokhara, one of Nepal’s most popular tourist destinations. The sightseeing includes visits to famous attractions such as Phewa Lake, where you can enjoy peaceful surroundings and mountain reflections, Tal Barahi Temple located in the middle of the lake, Davis Falls, Gupteshwor Cave, and the World Peace Stupa, which offers stunning panoramic views of Pokhara and the Annapurna range. After completing the city tour, you can relax at your hotel or enjoy the lakeside atmosphere. Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Pokhara City Visit and Relaxation (822m / 2,697ft)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "After breakfast, you will begin your scenic drive from Pokhara to Kathmandu. The journey offers beautiful views of rivers, green hills, terraced farmland, and rural villages along the highway. Following the Trishuli River for much of the route, the drive provides a relaxing opportunity to enjoy Nepal’s countryside. Upon arrival in Kathmandu, you will be transferred to your hotel. The rest of the day is free for you to relax, explore nearby markets, or enjoy your final time in Nepal. Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Drive to Kathmandu (1,350m / 4,412ft) – 6/7 hours\\";"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "Today you will enjoy a short visit to some of Kathmandu’s cultural and historical attractions, depending on your flight time. You may explore famous sites such as Pashupatinath Temple, Boudhanath Stupa, or local markets for last-minute shopping. This is a great opportunity to experience the rich culture and heritage of Nepal’s capital. After the visit, our representative will transfer you to Tribhuvan International Airport for your final departure. Your Annapurna Circuit Trek ends with wonderful memories of the mountains, culture, and adventure. Safe journey and farewell.\\";s:", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Kathmandu Visit and Transfer to Airport (1,350m / 4,412ft)"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.834	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000nkbrl9bjxojfw	pikey-peak-trek-8-days	Pikey Peak Trek – 8 Days	<h3 data-section-id="agfbyt" data-start="233" data-end="265">Discover the Pikey Peak Trek</h3>\n<p data-start="267" data-end="579">The Pikey Peak Trek 	<h3 data-section-id="agfbyt" data-start="233" data-end="265">Discover the Pikey Peak Trek</h3>\n<p data-start="267" data-end="579">The Pikey Peak Trek is a scenic short adventure in Nepal’s lower Everest region, offering spectacular Himalayan views, peaceful trails, and authentic Sherpa culture. Away from the busier routes, this journey provides a wonderful opportunity to experience the natural beauty of the Himalayas in a quieter setting.</p>\n<p data-start="581" data-end="926">The adventure takes you through traditional mountain villages, lush rhododendron forests, alpine meadows, and peaceful hillside trails. Along the way, trekkers can experience the warm hospitality of local communities while discovering the customs and traditions of the Sherpa people. The changing landscapes make every day of the journey unique.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="1xkrzxu" data-start="928" data-end="967">Spectacular Himalayan Sunrise Views</h3>\n<p data-start="969" data-end="1227">One of the main highlights is the early morning ascent to <strong data-start="1027" data-end="1057">Pikey Peak at 4,065 meters</strong>. From the summit, trekkers can enjoy panoramic views of Mount Everest, Makalu, Kanchenjunga, Gaurishankar, Numbur, Annapurna, Dhaulagiri, and many other Himalayan peaks.</p>\n<p data-start="1229" data-end="1462">The sunrise over the snow-covered mountains creates a memorable experience, especially for photographers and nature lovers. The viewpoint offers an impressive perspective of the Himalayan range without requiring a lengthy expedition.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="1pv3021" data-start="1464" data-end="1493">Experience Sherpa Culture</h3>\n<p data-start="1495" data-end="1830">The route also provides opportunities to experience traditional mountain life. Trekkers pass through welcoming Sherpa settlements and learn about local customs, Buddhist traditions, and everyday life in the region. Ancient monasteries, including Thupten Chholing Monastery near Junbesi, add cultural and spiritual value to the journey.</p>\n<p data-start="1832" data-end="1953">Comfortable teahouses along the trail provide accommodation, local meals, and warm hospitality after each day of walking.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="1ilfrsq" data-start="1955" data-end="1996">A Rewarding Short Himalayan Adventure</h3>\n<p data-start="1998" data-end="2251">This journey is suitable for both beginners and experienced hikers with a reasonable level of fitness. The moderate trails and manageable itinerary make it ideal for travelers who have limited time but still want to enjoy a genuine Himalayan experience.</p>\n<p data-start="2253" data-end="2458">With peaceful trails, beautiful forests, traditional villages, rich culture, and panoramic mountain scenery, the <strong data-start="2366" data-end="2385">Pikey Peak Trek</strong> is a rewarding way to explore Nepal’s Everest region in just eight days.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Pikey-Peak-Trek-7.jpeg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	8 Days	999	everest	Moderate		Spring (March–May) &amp; Autumn (September–November)	Hotel in Kathmandu &amp; Local Teahouses During Trek	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{everest-region}	<ul>\n<li>Sunrise hike to Pikey Peak (4,065 m)</li>\n<li>Spectacular panoramic views of Everest, Makalu, Kanchenjunga, Gaurishankar, and other Himalayan peaks</li>\n<li>Experience authentic Sherpa culture and hospitality</li>\n<li>Explore traditional villages of Dhap, Jhapre, and Junbesi</li>\n<li>Visit the historic Thupten Choling Monastery</li>\n<li>Trek through rhododendron forests and alpine landscapes</li>\n<li>Less crowded alternative to Everest region treks</li>\n<li>Scenic drive through rural Nepal</li>\n<li>Beautiful mountain sunsets and peaceful trekking trails</li>\n<li>Ideal short Himalayan trekking adventure</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Airport pick-up and drop-off services in Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Two nights hotel accommodation in Kathmandu with breakfast</li>\n<li>Private jeep transportation Kathmandu–Dhap and Junbesi–Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Local teahouse accommodation during the trek</li>\n<li>Experienced government-licensed English-speaking trekking guide</li>\n<li>Porter service (one porter for every two trekkers)</li>\n<li>All guide and porter expenses including salary, meals, accommodation, insurance, and transportation</li>\n<li>Required trekking permits</li>\n<li>Three meals per day during the trek (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner)</li>\n<li>First aid medical kit carried by the guide</li>\n<li>Trek completion certificate</li>\n<li>Government taxes and service charges</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul data-spread="false">\n<li>International airfare</li>\n<li>Nepal entry visa fees</li>\n<li>Travel and rescue insurance</li>\n<li>Personal trekking equipment and clothing</li>\n<li>Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Personal expenses such as internet, laundry, charging devices, hot showers, drinks, and snacks</li>\n<li>Tips for guide and porter</li>\n<li>Emergency evacuation and rescue expenses</li>\n<li>Additional accommodation due to weather conditions, road delays, or personal reasons</li>\n<li>Any services not specifically mentioned in the Package Includes section</li>\n</ul>\n		[{"day": "1", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Drive from Kathmandu to Dhap"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Trek from Dhap to Jhapre"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Continue trekking through rhododendron forests and open ridges. Reach Pikey Base Camp with stunning Himalayan views.\\n\\nTrek: 5–6 hours\\nOvernight: Teahouse\\";s:2", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Trek from Jhapre to Pikey Base Camp"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Hike to Pikey Peak and Trek to Junbesi"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Explore Junbesi, Monastery and Nearby Area"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Drive from Junbesi to Kathmandu"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Final Departure from Kathmandu"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.84	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000pkbrl0n366wx7	gokyo-lake-cho-la-pass-trek	Gokyo Lake Cholapass+ EBC Trekking	<h2 data-section-id="1oztuv2" data-start="455" data-end="501">Why Choose the <a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=326223ae55b11ae7&amp;sxsrf	<h2 data-section-id="1oztuv2" data-start="455" data-end="501">Why Choose the <a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=326223ae55b11ae7&amp;sxsrf=APpeQntFBztRQERgaO82tX6me0O6PA2Hcw:1787388859826&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gLZhoVnym8adqD7lVa5VazpFlqSqjydmsVpq4dhqK4u6T3kTrhVgNiGNRZboWfWF8BOhAMcmKYcPYZe5HoTIZ8_YVqr8ul767Is49zjLJg80Fx_EC0tHRFJ-7qRBeYYe7cvcggLyz3ZHPmAch3DIVKA4COWmw&amp;q=gokyo+lake+ebc&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjXy8Kw7rOWAxUPjuEIHfoyB_wQtKgLegQIExAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Gokyo Lake Cho La Pass</a> Trek?</h2>\n<p data-start="503" data-end="811">The <strong data-start="507" data-end="538"><a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/gokyo-valley-trek-14-days/">Gokyo Lake Cho La Pass</a> Trek</strong> is an unforgettable Himalayan adventure combining turquoise mountain lakes, dramatic passes, Sherpa culture, and Everest Base Camp. The route offers a rewarding alternative to the classic Everest trail, with diverse landscapes and spectacular views throughout the journey.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="135ytgy" data-start="813" data-end="846">Stunning Himalayan Landscapes</h3>\n<p data-start="848" data-end="1137">The journey takes you through the heart of the Everest region, with impressive views of Everest, Lhotse, Makalu, and Cho Oyu. The trail passes through peaceful valleys, alpine meadows, suspension bridges, and rugged mountain terrain. Each section brings a new perspective of the Himalayas.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="atsubn" data-start="1139" data-end="1166">Explore the Gokyo Lakes</h3>\n<p data-start="1168" data-end="1428">One of the major highlights is the beautiful Gokyo Lakes, surrounded by towering peaks and glaciers. Trekkers can also climb Gokyo Ri for panoramic views across the Everest region. The peaceful lakes and dramatic scenery make this section especially memorable.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="1pv3021" data-start="1430" data-end="1459">Experience Sherpa Culture</h3>\n<p data-start="1461" data-end="1719">The route passes through traditional Sherpa settlements, including Namche Bazaar and Khumjung. Along the way, travelers can visit monasteries, prayer wheels, and other cultural sites while learning more about the region's mountain communities and traditions.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="u0n6bj" data-start="1721" data-end="1758">Cross the Challenging Cho La Pass</h3>\n<p data-start="1760" data-end="2039">Crossing Cho La Pass adds an exciting challenge to the adventure. The high-altitude pass connects the Gokyo Valley with the Everest Base Camp route and requires good fitness and proper acclimatization. In return, trekkers are rewarded with spectacular glacier and mountain views.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="113666p" data-start="2041" data-end="2085">Reach Everest Base Camp and Kala Patthar</h3>\n<p data-start="2087" data-end="2349">The journey continues toward <strong data-start="2116" data-end="2137">Everest Base Camp</strong>, one of Nepal's most iconic trekking destinations. After reaching the base camp, the climb to <strong data-start="2232" data-end="2248">Kala Patthar</strong> provides exceptional views of Everest and surrounding peaks, particularly around sunrise and sunset.</p>\n<p data-start="2351" data-end="2527">This combination of high-altitude landscapes, local culture, turquoise lakes, and iconic Himalayan viewpoints makes the journey a memorable experience for adventurous trekkers.</p>\n\n<div aria-hidden="true"></div>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/gokyo-lake.png	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	16 Days	1999	everest	Moderate		March -June , Oct -Dec	Hotels in Kathmandu and teahouses during the trek	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{everest-region}	<p><strong>Shr‍epa Culture</strong><br />\nThe Gok⁠yo Ri trek takes you through Khu‍mbu, which is the ho​meland of the Sherpa people, a⁠n ethnic gro⁠u‍p of Tibeta‌n descent th‌at is famous​ around the worl‍d for their ski​lls in mounta​ineering, as we​ll as their h‍os​pita‌lity‍ for others‍.</p>\n<p><strong>Buddhism &amp;​ Sacred Sites⁠</strong><br />\n⁠While tr⁠ekking‌, you will pa​ss lots of monasteries (Gompas), c‌ho⁠rte‍n‌s (stupas), p​r⁠ayer f‌lags, and mani stones.Etiquette at Rel‍igious SitesTo be consid‍erate to the Bu⁠ddhi‍st rel​i⁠g⁠ion, Walk​ around st​upas and mani walls in a clockwise direc​tion.Only s⁠pi‌n p‍r⁠ayer wh⁠e​els‌ in a cloc‌kwise direc⁠tion.Take off your sho‍es before en​tering a monastery.Don't speak l​o‌udly, take s‍elfies, or take i‌nappropriate pictures.Although‍ donati⁠ons are appreciated, they are‌ not necessary; d‍on‍ati‌ons⁠ are more⁠ welcome if don‍e qu‍ietly​.</p>\n<p><strong>What we can do</strong><br />\nSay “Na⁠mas‌te” while placing palms together- always respectful an‌d not to mention appreciated.<br />\nAlways‍ ask‌ if you can photograph locals (es​pecially‌ monk​s and older people).<br />\nRes‌pect yak-t⁠r​ain‌s – give way and stand to‌ the mountai⁠n si‌de o‌f a trail. Dress modestly​ (cov‌ered shoulders and n‌o s‌hort shorts).<br />\nShow int‍erest in l​ocal customs – if y⁠ou ask‌ respec‍tfully⁠, w‍e want to he‌lp educ‌ate.</p>\n<p><strong>What we can't do</strong><br />\nDon’⁠t point with a f‍inger – especially don’t point with feet​ (about anything).‍<br />\nDon‌’t to​u‍ch pe‍ople on the he⁠a​d – always considered sa‍cred.<br />\n⁠ Don’t bargain aggressively – pri⁠ces⁠ ar⁠e already f⁠air in the mountains.<br />\nDon't​ show Public Displ⁠ay⁠ of Aff⁠ection – people frown on this in​ rural areas.<br />\nDon't lit‍t​er or throw f‌o‌od i‌n fire​ pits (fire is sacred).</p>\n	<p>Airport pickup and drop-off, as well as all‍ g​r⁠ound tran​sportation while trave​ling.‍<br />\nTwo-star hotel in Kathmand‍u wi​th twin beds and breakfast.‍<br />\nLodge lodgin‍g and full-‍board meals while trekkin⁠g.<br />\nA g‍overnment-trained‌ g‍uide and the‍ required num‍ber‍ of port⁠ers, along with their insurance, pay, a‌nd‌ meals.‍<br />\nAll T‌IMS c​ard and‌ trekking permit fees​ for dome⁠stic flights‍ in acc‌ordance w‌i‌th the i‌tinerar​y.<br />\nsleeping bag,⁠ down jacket, and other gear neede‌d for the hi​ke On⁠e c​ult​ural perform⁠anc​e​ and meal program.</p>\n	<p>Yo‍ur pers​onal e‌xpenses and the ticket for y⁠our internati​onal flight.<br />\nLarge meals in urban areas ar​e co​ld, and alcoholic beverages are c⁠onsumed.<br />\nAdditional s‌hower‌, laundry char⁠g‍e, batte⁠ry recharge, etc‍.<br />\nAdvi‌ce for‌ naviga⁠ting‌, carrying, and⁠ your insu‌rance.</p>\n		[{"day": "1", "desc": "Welcome to Kathmandu! Upon arrival at the airport, you will be warmly greeted by a representative from Ever Peak Adventure and transferred to your hotel. In the evening, we will conduct a short briefing and provide detailed information about the trip program.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1 : Arrive in Kathm​andu (134‌5m‍)\\";s:11"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Lukla is recognized as a Sherpa village and the main gateway to the Everest region. We continue our journey after securing our loads and enjoy a thrilling mountain flight that offers phenomenal aerial views and an unforgettable experience. Upon reaching Lukla, the trek begins along the Dudh Koshi River, also known as the Milk River. The trail passes through green forests with breathtaking views of Mount Kusum Kanguru and other surrounding peaks as we ascend and descend the path. After hours of hiking, we cross monasteries and small Sherpa villages before arriving in Phakding. ", "elev": 2620, "title": "‌Day 2⁠ : Fly to Lu⁠kla and trek to P‌hakd⁠i​ng (2620m)\\";s:11:\\"desc"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Namche Bazaar is the main administrative and commercial center of the Khumbu region. Along the trail, you can observe Himalayan locals engaged in various occupations. The journey passes through beautiful forests of blue pine, fir, juniper, and rhododendron, offering the first glimpse of Mount Everest and building excitement for the adventure ahead. We pass several villages, including Tok Tok, Banker, Monjo, Jorsalle, Thamserku, Kangtega, and Konde, before entering Sagarmatha National Park. Here, we experience the Sherpa way of life, shaped by long-standing traditions and cultural values", "elev": 3440, "title": "Day 3 : Trek t‍o Namche Bazaar (3440m)\\";"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "We ad‍j⁠us​t to the new environment and altitude in Nam‍che Bazaar. We spend t‍he day takin⁠g i⁠n th‌e mounta‍in views and Khumbu⁠ Peak's sunrise and s‌unset. We h‌ike a s‌hort distance to the Sherpa Mu​seum, where we can​ see the d‌istinctive custo‍ms and cu‍ltures of the⁠ Sherp⁠a people.‍ I⁠n a⁠dditi⁠on,‍ y‍ou will either be sh‌own a‍round Khumjung vil​lage‍ or Tham‌e Monastery. We live in Khumjung​ Village, a s‍izab‍le Sherpa community w​here we can observe their distinctive cultura‌l v‌alues and wa‌y of life‍. W‍e take in the expansive mountain views as w‌e acclimate t‍o the lighter air and get read‍y for the‍ next day​'s excursion! In​cluded​ in the‌ m‌e​als are breakf​ast, lunch⁠, and din‌ner, followed by an ove‍rnigh‍t sta​y at a​ tre​kking l‍odge.\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:21:\\"Namche Bazaar (3440m)\\";s:21:\\"day_wise_en", "elev": 3440, "title": "Day 4 : Acclimatizatio‌n/explor⁠ati‌on/⁠rest day at Namche Bazaar (3440m)\\";s:11:\\""}, {"day": "5", "desc": "We begin our journ​ey to Dole this morn‌in‍g af‌te​r ea‌ting breakfast. Fir​s​t, with a view of​ the snow-capped Shana​sa mountains​, we eventually make our way around Na‍mche Bazaar, clim⁠b​ Mongl‌a Hill, des​cend to Pho‌rtse Than​g‍a, a⁠nd t‍h‍en wal⁠k to Dole. There are t​eah⁠ouses in the small⁠ village of Dole in this area. We travel past br​eathtaking vistas of mounta​ins s‍u​ch as Eve‌rest, Kantega, Th⁠amserku‌, Lhotse, Nuptse, and Amada⁠blam. We arrive at M‌ong a​nd beg‍in‌ our descent to the Dudhkoshi bank. We cl​imb the hill once mor‍e, pas‍s through a tiny villag‌e​, and arriv‍e at Do‍le. Included in th‍e meals are breakfast, lu⁠nch, and dinner, followed by‍ an o‌v‌ernight sta⁠y at a trekking lodg​e.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:21:\\"Namche Bazaar (3440m)\\";s:21", "elev": 4110, "title": "D⁠ay 5 : Trek‍ to Do⁠le (4110m)\\";s:11"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "We leave Dole and climb ov​er the pic​turesqu​e ridge. Along the river​, we wil‌l trav‍erse sand spurs⁠ and‌ w​a⁠lk h‍igh ab⁠ove the valley.‍ We have the opportuni‌ty​ t‌o observe the life⁠s​tyles of the locals with varyin​g cu‍ltur⁠al values as we‌ pa‌ss through the‌ villages of Lhabharm​a and Luza. We stroll pas‌t the Dudhkoshi valley afte​r t​aking in the breatht‍aking scener⁠y. Before movi⁠ng on to our next destinati‍o‌n, we‌ will‍ also stop by the H‍imalay‌a Rescue O​peration, which wa‍s⁠ founded to provide basic med⁠i⁠c​al​ care,⁠ and res‍t. Included in the meals are breakfast, lunch, and din⁠ner, foll⁠owed by an overnight stay at a tre‌kking lodge.‌\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:12:\\"Dole (4110m)\\";s:21:\\"da", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6 : Trek to Machher​mo (4‌410m‌)\\";s:11"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "We hike to Gokyo to​d‍ay⁠, which‌ is encircled by b‍reathtaki​ng mountain views‍, while f​o‌llowing the Lama foo​tprints. Af​ter trav‌ersing a path dotted with boulders at the edge of th‌e third la​ke,‍ we reach Goky⁠o after c⁠ross‌ing the second lake, Long‌ponga (469​0m). Ascending th⁠e‌ ri​dge pr​ovides breathtaking v‌iews of the Cho-Oyu, Kantega, C‍holat‌se, and Pan​gk⁠a mountains‍. While traveli‌ng, we stop in P⁠angka, th⁠e site o‍f the 1‌995 ava​l​an‍che disas​ter th‌at claimed the lives of‍ ov⁠er 40 peop‌le. We now‌ desc⁠end to the river and​ a⁠scend steeply to the Ngozumpa moraine. W⁠e pass b‍oth the upper and l‌ower Gokyo L‍akes‌ b‌ef‍ore arriving at⁠ G​o​ky​o aft​er a few⁠ ho​urs of walking. I‍nclu​de‍d in the meals are brea‍kfast, lunc‌h, and dinner, followed by an overnight stay at a trekking lodge.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:17:\\"Machhermo (4410m)\\";s:21:\\"day_wise_ending_point\\";s:13:\\"G", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7 : Trek⁠ to Gokyo (4760m​)\\";s:"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "Gok‍yo Ri ha‍s an altitude of 5483m. And we will⁠ hike i⁠t up‍ steeply in the morning. It is a satisfying place‍ because you can‌ see the spectacular vie​ws of the Gokyo Valley​, the Kh​u‌mbu Him‍alayas, Everest, L‍hotse‌, N‍uptse, Makalu, Cho-Oyu⁠ and Gychun⁠g K​ang. Sunrise and sunset vi‌ews of the Everes‌t peaks also j​ustify tre‍kking to G‌okyo. As‍ we hike dow‍n towards Gokyo Val​ley‍, we will al‌so peek at the vie​ws of K‍usum Kagaru, Kantega, T​hamse‌rku⁠, and others. We travel to Thangnak after spending a few hours st⁠rolling through the verdant fo​rests that e⁠nc‍ircle the glaciers. Included in the meals are breakfast, lunch​, and di​nne​r, follo‍wed by‍ an‌ overn‍ig​ht stay at a trekking lodge.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:13:\\"Gokyo (4760m)", "elev": 0, "title": "Da‌y 8 : Day​ hike to Gokyo Ri and tr⁠ek to Thagnak (4678m⁠)\\";s:11:\\""}, {"day": "9", "desc": "Since we must a‌s‍c​end the steep path to the region's highest point and traver‌se some ext‍rem‍ely icy tra‌cks, today i​s tr‌u​ly the day when na‌tur‍e puts​ our strength to the​ te‍st.⁠ To ge​t to Cho La Pass‌, we⁠ will first clim‌b‍ a steep path t‌h‍at leads to a trail w‌ith sharp d‍rops, and then we will climb once more. This time, w⁠e are accomp‍anied by views of the‍ moun‌tains an⁠d Bu⁠ddhi⁠st p‌raye‌r flags. We have a close-up view⁠ of the m‌agnificent peaks⁠ Cholatse and Tabuch​e because⁠ we are adjacent to them. With st‌unning vie⁠ws of the vall‍ey a​nd⁠ villages from the summ‍it,⁠ we des​cend​ gent‍ly to Dzongla after c⁠rossing the Cho La Pass​. Inclu‌ded in the meals are break‍fa⁠st, l‍unc⁠h, and dinner, follow⁠ed by an overnigh‌t‍ sta‌y at a trekking lodge.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:15:\\"Thagnak (4678m)\\";s:21:\\"day_wise_ending_poin", "elev": 5420, "title": "‍D‍ay 9​ : Trek to Dzonglha via Cho La P‌a‌ss (5420m)\\";s:11:\\"de"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "As⁠ you app‌roach the end of th⁠e moraine of the Khumb‌u Gla‌cier, the h‌ike‍ towards Ev​e​rest Base Camp cont⁠inues across alpine meadows and summer yak pastures.‌ After this⁠, t⁠he trek to the village⁠ of Gora‍k Shep is s‍teep and arduous. Next, you w‍ill⁠ go to Lobuche t⁠o ta⁠ke in Nuptse distant and the stunning sunset. As we walk through the glacial v⁠is‌tas, we had w​onderf‍ul vi‌ews‍ of the mount⁠ains including Nupts​e, Lhotse, Amadabl‍am, and many other towering pea​ks.​ Meals⁠ will include breakfast, lunch, and dinner, followed by‌ an overnight at a tr​ekking l​odge.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\"", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10 : Trek to Lobuche (494‍0m)\\";"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "W‍e hike to‍ Gorak Shep f‍rom Lobuche​. This 5-kil‍ometer hi‍ke gives us a gre⁠at opport⁠unity to see the Cha​ngri glaci‍er and oth‍er mo​untain​s, p‌rimarily Pumori. One of the greatest ti‍mes to trek⁠ to Ever‍est‍ Cho La Pass is du⁠ring the‌ Go‍rakshep trek. We exper‌ience many u‍ps and downs while trekking t‌hro‌ugh the verdant forests.​ We arrive at th‌e base camp after c‌limbing over th⁠e g​lacial route‌. Here, we take pleasure in the magnificent glacial surroundings and the stunning moun‌tain v⁠iews‍. In‍clude‍d i‌n the meals a‍re breakfast,​ lunch, and dinn‍e⁠r⁠, followed by an ove‌rnight stay a​t a‌ trekking lo‍dg‌e.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:15:\\"Lobuche (4940m)\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11 : Trek to G‌orak Shep (5​14⁠7m)\\";s:11"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "Today,​ we⁠ will be hiking to kala‌patthar, whic‍h as the‍ name suggests, is the b‍est place t​o \\"view\\" E​ver⁠es‍t. And, If E⁠BC is the base of Everest, it is also where all climber⁠s‍ are present at tim​es, and we get to take nice photos in fro​n⁠t of Everest duri‌ng the climbing season. But th⁠en,‍ we w⁠ill view lots o‌f peaks including  Nupt​se, Lhotse, Amadablam, Taboche, Cholatse, Pumor‌i, Everest, a‍nd others from ka​lapat‌thar. Then we‌ wi‌l​l hike from G‌o‌rak Shep to Per‌i​che. Th‌e hike t​o Periche will ta‍ke us⁠ d⁠o‌wn thr⁠ough rhodode‌ndron forests and‌ down terrain. The meal‌s included are breakfa⁠st, lunch, and dinner, and we​ wil‍l s‌tay in a‌ trekking lo‍dge. \\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:18:\\"Gorak Shep (5147m)\\";s", "elev": 5365, "title": "D​ay 12 :‍ M⁠orning h‌ike to either Eve​rest Base Camp (5365m)or Kala Patth​ar (5550m) a‍nd trek to Pheri‌che (3950m)\\";s:11:\\"descript"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "W‌e hike d‌ownhill from Peric​he to Tengboc‍he, where we visit an old mon​ast​ery before⁠ returning to N​amc‍he Bazaar. This monastery was j‌ust‍ rebuilt. We get t​o‍ s‍ee t‌he expa​nsive vistas of the mo‌untains Thams‌erk‌u, Kangtega, Khumbi La, and⁠ Kong‌do R​i as we hike just beneath t⁠he breathtaking Himalayas. We inve‌stigate​ the local way of life as we travel thro‌ugh the tiny village of​ Pangboche. A‌fter a while‍ o⁠f walking, th​e trail leads u‌s to Tengboche Nmache, the oldest monastery. In​cluded in the meals a​re brea​k‍fast, lu⁠nch, and di​nner, f⁠ollowed by a​n overnight stay‌ at a trekking lodge.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:16:\\"Pheri", "elev": 3440, "title": "Day 13 : Trek t‌o Namche bazar (3440m)\\";"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "We‍ will be t​rekking back to Lukla today to catch our f‌light to Kathma‍ndu, which will be our final trek. We‍'‌l​l⁠ explore Lukla during the day. We pass the lovely vil‌lages of the K​humbu region‌ as‌ we stro‌l‍l a⁠bove the hill. We follow‍ t‍he Dudhkos⁠hi​ Rive t​rail e‌dge, cros‍sing suspension bridges before arriving at Lukla. Included in the⁠ meals a​re breakfast, lunch, and dinner, followed by an overnight stay at a trekking lodge‌.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_", "elev": 2840, "title": "Da⁠y 14 : Trek to Lukla (2840m)\\";"}, {"day": "15", "desc": "We fly back t‌o Kathm​andu in the morning, where we can‌ once more take in the breatht​aking valleys and landscape⁠s r‌ep⁠lete with breathtaking mountain v​ista‍s. Yo⁠u‍ can part‍ic‍ipate in t⁠he‍ compan​y's‍ e‌vening meal an‍d c​ul‌tural pro‍gr⁠am in the evening.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"d", "elev": 0, "title": "Da‌y⁠ 15 : Fly to Kathman​du (134‌5m‍)\\";s:11:\\"de"}, {"day": "16", "desc": "On the final d​ay, yo​u can eit‌her relax and head home safel⁠y or follow a​lo​ng w⁠ith us at Sunr⁠ise Adven‌ture Treks and​ Tour for⁠ another day of ad‌ve‍nture. Als​o,​ in accord⁠an‍ce with your flight‍ itin‍erar‍y, we‌ will take you to the⁠ a⁠irport abo‌ut three hours e⁠arly to make sure you​ get your next flight.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wi", "elev": 0, "title": "Da‌y 16 : Tr​ip‌ conclu‍de⁠s an⁠d departure\\";s:11:\\"desc"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.846	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000qkbrlkxzcy3yg	annapurna-circuit-trek-via-tilicho-lake	Annapurna Circuit Trek via Tilicho Lake	<p data-start="123" data-end="463">Hidden high in the heart of the Himalayas, Tilicho Lake and the <a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=2abe	<p data-start="123" data-end="463">Hidden high in the heart of the Himalayas, Tilicho Lake and the <a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=2abe5610bf025d75&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnu3q1NLc69B1Z3STmOUi_4R5s_A6A:1781931694365&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gKq1sgc0zFmtILFJcehpQnp8EvsgtsNoHlk8yRnPtPFZTFppidpMf3acGusE4WvlMaqVeJ_G7aj1Gz_ymywOPYPTIOv3WGYQHHgc5nVcfWPA2jyTEUSd8triSJAXyyatewLdgwLM3BOpfnoNdQL2VYGJg25xA&amp;q=annapurna&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwiu6p_thJWVAxVcV2wGHWoDBV0QtKgLegQIGBAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25#sv=CAMSURoyKhBlLVk4LVgxblFBSzBxcVVNMg5ZOC1YMW5RQUswcXFVTToONHNiU3VTcTE3Q2ozNE0gBCoXCgFzEhBlLVk4LVgxblFBSzBxcVVNGAEwARgHIIzvyZwCSggQARgBIAEoAQ">Annapurna</a> Circuit Trek together create one of the most breathtaking adventures in the world. This journey is not just a trek; it is a life-changing experience that combines dramatic mountain landscapes, ancient cultures, remote villages, and one of the highest lakes on Earth.</p>\n\n<h3 data-start="465" data-end="510">Tilicho Lake – The World Above the Clouds</h3>\n<p data-start="512" data-end="871">Situated at an altitude of 4,919 meters, Tilicho Lake is often celebrated as one of the highest lakes in the world. Surrounded by towering peaks of the <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/annapurna-circuit-trek/">Annapurna</a> range, the turquoise waters shimmer against a backdrop of snow-covered giants and rugged cliffs. The trail to Tilicho is both challenging and rewarding, offering raw Himalayan beauty at every step.</p>\n<p data-start="873" data-end="1256">Trekkers pass through remote settlements, glacial valleys, and landslide-prone trails carved into steep mountainsides. The journey demands determination, but the moment you stand before the pristine lake, framed by Tilicho Peak and the Annapurna massif, every step feels worthwhile. The silence, broken only by mountain winds, creates a sense of peace that is rare and unforgettable.</p>\n\n<h3 data-start="1258" data-end="1302">Annapurna Circuit – Nepal’s Classic Trek</h3>\n<p data-start="1304" data-end="1552">The Annapurna Circuit is one of Nepal’s most iconic trekking routes. It circles the Annapurna Massif, offering an incredible variety of landscapes — from lush subtropical forests and terraced rice fields to alpine meadows and high-altitude deserts.</p>\n<p data-start="1554" data-end="1855">The trek traditionally begins in the lower Marsyangdi Valley and gradually ascends through diverse cultural regions inhabited by Gurung, Thakali, and Manangi communities. Along the way, trekkers experience centuries-old monasteries, prayer flags fluttering in the wind, and warm Himalayan hospitality.</p>\n<p data-start="1857" data-end="2128">One of the major highlights of the circuit is crossing the Thorong La Pass (5,416 meters), one of the highest trekking passes in the world. Reaching the top at sunrise, surrounded by panoramic Himalayan views, is a powerful and emotional achievement for many adventurers.</p>\n\n<h3 data-start="2130" data-end="2180">A Perfect Combination of Adventure and Culture</h3>\n<p data-start="2182" data-end="2497">Adding Tilicho Lake to the Annapurna Circuit extends the adventure and offers a deeper exploration of the region. It introduces more dramatic landscapes and a sense of remoteness that feels untouched by time. The blend of physical challenge, spiritual atmosphere, and cultural richness makes this trek truly unique.</p>\n<p data-start="2499" data-end="2822">From rhododendron forests to barren high-altitude landscapes, from warm teahouses to icy mountain winds, every day brings a new perspective. The Annapurna Circuit with Tilicho Lake is not just about reaching a destination — it’s about embracing the journey, connecting with nature, and discovering strength within yourself.</p>\n<p data-start="2824" data-end="2974" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">For trekkers seeking one of the most diverse and rewarding Himalayan experiences, this combination stands as a dream adventure waiting to be explored.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Annapurna-Circut-trek-5.jpeg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	15 Days	1499	annapurna	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Jan	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{annapurna-region}	<h3 data-start="204" data-end="251"></h3>\n<ul data-start="252" data-end="479">\n<li data-start="252" data-end="331">\n<p data-start="254" data-end="331">Visit Tilicho Lake at 4,919 meters, surrounded by dramatic Himalayan peaks.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="332" data-end="411">\n<p data-start="334" data-end="411">Witness the stunning turquoise water reflecting the snow-covered mountains.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="412" data-end="479">\n<p data-start="414" data-end="479">Experience a peaceful and less-crowded high-altitude destination.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="520" data-end="580">\n<p data-start="522" data-end="580">Conquer one of the highest trekking passes in the world.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="581" data-end="659">\n<p data-start="583" data-end="659">Enjoy breathtaking sunrise views over the Annapurna and Dhaulagiri ranges.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="660" data-end="715">\n<p data-start="662" data-end="715">Feel the true achievement of high-altitude adventure.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="757" data-end="815">\n<p data-start="759" data-end="815">Walk through lush green forests and terraced farmland.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="816" data-end="867">\n<p data-start="818" data-end="867">Trek across alpine meadows and glacial valleys.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="868" data-end="933">\n<p data-start="870" data-end="933">Explore the dramatic desert-like terrain of Manang and Mustang.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="980" data-end="1060">\n<p data-start="982" data-end="1060">Experience the warm hospitality of Gurung, Thakali, and Manangi communities.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1061" data-end="1137">\n<p data-start="1063" data-end="1137">Visit ancient monasteries, mani walls, and prayer flags along the trail.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1138" data-end="1206">\n<p data-start="1140" data-end="1206">Discover Tibetan-influenced culture in high Himalayan settlements.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1243" data-end="1323">\n<p data-start="1245" data-end="1323">Enjoy close-up views of Annapurna, Tilicho Peak, Gangapurna, and Dhaulagiri.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1324" data-end="1381">\n<p data-start="1326" data-end="1381">Capture unforgettable panoramas throughout the journey.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1419" data-end="1466">\n<p data-start="1421" data-end="1466">A perfect blend of adventure and endurance.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1467" data-end="1546">\n<p data-start="1469" data-end="1546">Ideal for trekkers seeking both natural beauty and physical accomplishment.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1547" data-end="1610">\n<p data-start="1549" data-end="1610">A rewarding extension to the classic Annapurna Circuit route.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Hotel pickup and drop by private vehicle.</li>\n<li>Authorized English-speaking government licensed Guide</li>\n<li>All necessary paperworks, trekking permits (TIMS ), ACAP and all government and local taxes.</li>\n<li>Tea-house accommodation x10 nights during the trek</li>\n<li>All meals (breakfast, lunch, and dinner) during the trek</li>\n<li>All expenses for staffs: including their salary, insurance, equipment, food, transportation and accommodation.</li>\n<li>All applicable government tax</li>\n<li>Private Transportation as per the itinerary as per the number of pax (Kathmandu –Besisahar - Chame, Muktinath –<br />\nTatopani Hot spring - Pokhara)</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul data-start="188" data-end="1109">\n<li data-start="188" data-end="232">\n<p data-start="190" data-end="232">International airfare to and from Nepal.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="233" data-end="333">\n<p data-start="235" data-end="333">Nepal entry visa fees (obtainable upon arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport in Kathmandu).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="334" data-end="435">\n<p data-start="336" data-end="435">Travel and rescue insurance (mandatory and must cover high-altitude trekking up to 5,500 meters).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="436" data-end="530">\n<p data-start="438" data-end="530">Personal trekking equipment (except sleeping bag and down jacket provided by the company).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="531" data-end="565">\n<p data-start="533" data-end="565">Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu and Pokhara</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="566" data-end="671">\n<p data-start="568" data-end="671">Extra accommodation in Kathmandu due to early arrival, late departure, or early return from the trek.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="672" data-end="799">\n<p data-start="674" data-end="799">Personal expenses such as snacks, soft drinks, bottled water, hot showers, Wi-Fi, battery charging, laundry, and bar bills.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="800" data-end="871">\n<p data-start="802" data-end="871">Tips for guide, porter, and driver (tipping is customary in Nepal).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="872" data-end="1024">\n<p data-start="874" data-end="1024">Costs arising from natural disasters, weather conditions, flight delays, political disturbances, or any unforeseen circumstances beyond our control.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1025" data-end="1109">\n<p data-start="1027" data-end="1109">Any other expenses not specifically mentioned in the “Package Includes” section.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<h3 data-start="344" data-end="358">Upper Body</h3>\n<ul data-start="359" data-end="572">\n<li data-start="359" data-end="403">\n<p data-start="361" data-end="403">Moisture-wicking base layer (thermal tops)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="404" data-end="433">\n<p data-start="406" data-end="433">Trekking shirts (quick-dry)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="434" data-end="462">\n<p data-start="436" data-end="462">Fleece or insulated jacket</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="463" data-end="510">\n<p data-start="465" data-end="510">Down jacket (provided if included in package)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="511" data-end="572">\n<p data-start="513" data-end="572">Waterproof and windproof outer jacket (Gore-Tex or similar)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 data-start="574" data-end="588">Lower Body</h3>\n<ul data-start="589" data-end="737">\n<li data-start="589" data-end="618">\n<p data-start="591" data-end="618">Thermal base layer (bottom)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="619" data-end="657">\n<p data-start="621" data-end="657">Trekking pants (2 pairs recommended)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="658" data-end="695">\n<p data-start="660" data-end="695">Waterproof/windproof trekking pants</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="696" data-end="737">\n<p data-start="698" data-end="737">Comfortable casual pants (for evenings)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 data-start="739" data-end="752">Innerwear</h3>\n<ul data-start="753" data-end="860">\n<li data-start="753" data-end="768">\n<p data-start="755" data-end="768">Undergarments</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="769" data-end="794">\n<p data-start="771" data-end="794">Sports bras (for women)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="795" data-end="819">\n<p data-start="797" data-end="819">Warm socks (3–4 pairs)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="820" data-end="860">\n<p data-start="822" data-end="860">Lightweight trekking socks (2–3 pairs)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-start="867" data-end="881"> Footwear</h2>\n<ul data-start="882" data-end="1014">\n<li data-start="882" data-end="934">\n<p data-start="884" data-end="934">Sturdy, waterproof trekking boots (well broken-in)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="935" data-end="970">\n<p data-start="937" data-end="970">Lightweight sandals or camp shoes</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="971" data-end="1014">\n<p data-start="973" data-end="1014">Gaiters (recommended for snow conditions)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-start="1021" data-end="1043"> Head &amp; Hand Gear</h2>\n<ul data-start="1044" data-end="1188">\n<li data-start="1044" data-end="1069">\n<p data-start="1046" data-end="1069">Warm wool or fleece hat</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1070" data-end="1086">\n<p data-start="1072" data-end="1086">Sun hat or cap</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1087" data-end="1108">\n<p data-start="1089" data-end="1108">Neck gaiter or buff</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1109" data-end="1140">\n<p data-start="1111" data-end="1140">Sunglasses with UV protection</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1141" data-end="1188">\n<p data-start="1143" data-end="1188">Warm gloves (inner + outer waterproof gloves)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-start="1195" data-end="1219"> Trekking Equipment</h2>\n<ul data-start="1220" data-end="1460">\n<li data-start="1220" data-end="1253">\n<p data-start="1222" data-end="1253">Backpack (30–40L for daily use)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1254" data-end="1286">\n<p data-start="1256" data-end="1286">Duffel bag (carried by porter)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1287" data-end="1335">\n<p data-start="1289" data-end="1335">Sleeping bag (provided if included in package)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1336" data-end="1352">\n<p data-start="1338" data-end="1352">Trekking poles</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1353" data-end="1384">\n<p data-start="1355" data-end="1384">Headlamp with extra batteries</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1385" data-end="1421">\n<p data-start="1387" data-end="1421">Water bottles or hydration bladder</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1422" data-end="1460">\n<p data-start="1424" data-end="1460">Water purification tablets or filter</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-start="1467" data-end="1499"> Toiletries &amp; Personal Care</h2>\n<ul data-start="1500" data-end="1655">\n<li data-start="1500" data-end="1525">\n<p data-start="1502" data-end="1525">Toothbrush &amp; toothpaste</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1526" data-end="1539">\n<p data-start="1528" data-end="1539">Small towel</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1540" data-end="1561">\n<p data-start="1542" data-end="1561">Sunscreen (SPF 30+)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1562" data-end="1581">\n<p data-start="1564" data-end="1581">Lip balm with SPF</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1582" data-end="1598">\n<p data-start="1584" data-end="1598">Hand sanitizer</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1599" data-end="1610">\n<p data-start="1601" data-end="1610">Wet wipes</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1611" data-end="1632">\n<p data-start="1613" data-end="1632">Basic first-aid kit</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1633" data-end="1655">\n<p data-start="1635" data-end="1655">Personal medications</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-start="1662" data-end="1679"> Accessories</h2>\n<ul data-start="1680" data-end="1798">\n<li data-start="1680" data-end="1692">\n<p data-start="1682" data-end="1692">Power bank</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1693" data-end="1715">\n<p data-start="1695" data-end="1715">Camera or smartphone</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1716" data-end="1733">\n<p data-start="1718" data-end="1733">Charging cables</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1734" data-end="1773">\n<p data-start="1736" data-end="1773">Travel adapter (Type C/D/M for Nepal)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1774" data-end="1798">\n<p data-start="1776" data-end="1798">Snacks and energy bars</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-start="1805" data-end="1830"> Important Documents</h2>\n<ul data-start="1831" data-end="1987">\n<li data-start="1831" data-end="1847">\n<p data-start="1833" data-end="1847">Valid passport</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1848" data-end="1860">\n<p data-start="1850" data-end="1860">Nepal visa</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1861" data-end="1917">\n<p data-start="1863" data-end="1917">Travel insurance (covering high altitude up to 5,500m)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1918" data-end="1955">\n<p data-start="1920" data-end="1955">Passport-sized photos (for permits)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="1956" data-end="1987">\n<p data-start="1958" data-end="1987">Copies of important documents</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr data-start="1989" data-end="1992" />\n<h2 data-start="1994" data-end="2021">Optional but Recommended</h2>\n<ul data-start="2022" data-end="2136">\n<li data-start="2022" data-end="2067">\n<p data-start="2024" data-end="2067">Microspikes (early spring/late autumn snow)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2068" data-end="2097">\n<p data-start="2070" data-end="2097">Lightweight book or journal</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2098" data-end="2108">\n<p data-start="2100" data-end="2108">Earplugs</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start="2109" data-end="2136">\n<p data-start="2111" data-end="2136">Dry bags or zip-lock bags</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Welcome to Nepal! Upon arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport in Kathmandu, our representative will warmly greet you and transfer you to your hotel. After check-in, you can relax and recover from your journey. If time allows, explore nearby markets, cafés, or cultural streets to experience the lively atmosphere of the city. In the evening, you will meet your trekking guide for a short briefing about the upcoming trek and to check your equipment and preparations. Overnight stay at a comfortable hotel in Kathmandu.\\"", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1,350 m / 4,429 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "After breakfast, we begin a scenic drive from Kathmandu toward Dharapani. The journey passes through rivers, terraced farmland, small towns, and beautiful countryside landscapes. As we move closer to the Annapurna region, the scenery gradually changes into dramatic hills and mountain views. By evening we reach Dharapani, a small village that marks the starting area for many Annapurna treks. Overnight stay at a teahouse.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Drive Kathmandu → Dharapani\\";"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Today the trekking adventure officially begins. After breakfast, we follow the trail through forests and small villages while walking alongside the Marsyangdi River. The trail gradually climbs and offers beautiful natural scenery with occasional views of snow-capped peaks. After several hours of trekking, we arrive at Chame, the administrative center of the Manang district.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Trek Dharapani → Chame\\";"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "After breakfast, we continue trekking through pine forests and scenic mountain valleys. The trail offers impressive views of Annapurna II and other surrounding peaks. Crossing suspension bridges and passing traditional settlements, we gradually climb toward the picturesque village of Upper Pisang.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Trek Chame → Upper Pisang\\";"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Today’s trail offers spectacular panoramic views of the Annapurna mountain range. We walk through traditional Himalayan villages and Buddhist cultural areas before reaching Manang, a beautiful high-altitude village surrounded by dramatic mountain landscapes.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Trek Upper Pisang → Manang\\";"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Today is an important rest day for acclimatization. You can explore Manang village, visit local monasteries, or take a short hike to nearby viewpoints to enjoy panoramic views of the Annapurna range. This rest day helps your body adapt to the altitude before continuing the trek.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Acclimatization Day in Manang"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "After breakfast, we leave Manang and follow a scenic trail toward Shree Kharka. The path climbs gradually through alpine landscapes and rugged mountain terrain while offering incredible views of the surrounding peaks.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Trek Manang → Shree Kharka\\";"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "Today we trek toward Tilicho Base Camp along a scenic mountain trail that passes through steep slopes and rocky sections. The route offers dramatic views of surrounding peaks and valleys before reaching the base camp.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Trek Shree Kharka → Tilicho Base Camp\\";"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "Early in the morning we hike to Tilicho Lake, one of the highest lakes in the world. Surrounded by snow-covered mountains, the lake offers breathtaking views. After spending some time enjoying the scenery, we return to the base camp and trek back to Shree Kharka.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Visit Tilicho Lake → Trek back to Shree Kharka\\";"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "We continue trekking through alpine landscapes as we reconnect with the main Annapurna Circuit trail. The path passes through open areas where yaks are often seen grazing.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Trek Shree Kharka → Yak Kharka\\";"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "After breakfast, we gradually trek toward Thorong Phedi, the base point for crossing Thorong La Pass. The trail passes through rugged high-altitude terrain and offers dramatic mountain scenery.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Trek Yak Kharka → Thorong Phedi\\";"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "Today is the most challenging and rewarding day of the trek. We start early in the morning to cross Thorong La Pass, the highest point of the Annapurna Circuit. From the top, enjoy breathtaking panoramic views of the Himalayan mountains before descending toward the sacred pilgrimage site of Muktinath.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Cross Thorong La Pass and Trek to Muktinath (3760m / 12336 ft)"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "After breakfast, we leave the mountains and drive toward Pokhara. The journey passes through beautiful valleys, rivers, and traditional villages. Gradually the landscape changes from high mountains to lush hills as we descend. By afternoon we arrive in Pokhara.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Drive Muktinath to Pokhara (822m / 2697 ft)"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "Today we return to Kathmandu either by a scenic drive or a short flight. The journey offers beautiful views of hills, rivers, and mountain landscapes. Once back in Kathmandu, you can relax, explore local markets, or enjoy your final evening in Nepal.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Drive or Fly Pokhara to Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}, {"day": "15", "desc": "Your unforgettable Himalayan adventure comes to an end today. Our representative will transfer you from your hotel to Tribhuvan International Airport according to your flight schedule. We hope you had a memorable trekking experience in Nepal.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 15: Final Departure from Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.849	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000rkbrl6s5dh0ho	everest-base-camp-trek	Everest Base Camp	<h2 data-start="38" data-end="527">Why choose Everest Base Camp trek?</h2>\n<p data-start="38" data-end="527">The Everest Base Camp Trek is widely rega	<h2 data-start="38" data-end="527">Why choose Everest Base Camp trek?</h2>\n<p data-start="38" data-end="527">The Everest Base Camp Trek is widely regarded as one of the finest trekking experiences in the world. This classic 15-day journey leads you deep into the Khumbu region to the base of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Everest">Mount Everest</a> (8,848.86 meters), the highest peak on the planet. Along the way, trekkers encounter a powerful mix of dramatic mountain scenery, traditional Sherpa culture, and ever-changing landscapes. It is a journey that offers not only natural beauty, but also a strong sense of purpose and achievement.</p>\n<p data-start="529" data-end="970">The adventure begins with a scenic flight from Kathmandu to Lukla, a mountain airstrip set among steep hills and towering peaks. From here, the trail follows the Dudh Koshi River through a series of traditional villages connected by suspension bridges and forested paths. Early sections of the trek pass through green valleys filled with pine and rhododendron, while higher elevations reveal more rugged terrain and expansive mountain views.</p>\n<p data-start="972" data-end="1484">Namche Bazaar is one of the most significant stops along the route. This vibrant mountain town serves as the main gateway to the<a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=everest&amp;sca_esv=0d642a333c7f7a40&amp;udm=2&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnvwqQ2QG1ZZ9uGOxx7drxvUiKyCQA%3A1781886151779&amp;ei=x2w1aviAL6nB4-EPrrD2-Qg&amp;ved=0ahUKEwi4gO2Y25OVAxWp4DgGHS6YPY8Q4dUDCBM&amp;uact=5&amp;oq=everest&amp;gs_lp=Egtnd3Mtd2l6LWltZyIHZXZlcmVzdDIHECMYyQIYJzIOEAAYgAQYigUYsQMYgwEyCBAAGIAEGLEDMgQQABgDMgUQABiABDIFEAAYgAQyBRAAGIAEMg4QABiABBiKBRixAxiDATIFEAAYgAQyDhAAGIAEGIoFGLEDGIMBSMYaUMsHWL8YcAF4AJABAJgBsQGgAbgIqgEDMC43uAEDyAEA-AEBmAIIoAKECagCA8ICChAjGMkCGOoCGCfCAgoQABiABBiKBRhDwgILEAAYgAQYigUYsQPCAgsQABiABBixAxiDAZgDDpIHAzEuN6AHyyeyBwMwLje4B_YIwgcFMi03LjHIBzeACAE&amp;sclient=gws-wiz-img#sv=CAMSURoyKhBlLUxLS1pjUWtKTlpPSVNNMg5MS0taY1FrSk5aT0lTTToOYTNhanZFeFNfdzk2bE0gBCoXCgFzEhBlLUxLS1pjUWtKTlpPSVNNGAEwARgHIP65nbQMSggQARgBIAEoAQ"> Everest</a> region and provides an important acclimatization break. Trekkers can enjoy clear views of Everest, Ama Dablam, and nearby peaks while exploring local markets, bakeries, and cultural sites. The journey continues to Tengboche, where the region’s most important monastery stands against a backdrop of towering mountains, offering both cultural insight and unforgettable scenery.</p>\n<p data-start="1486" data-end="1959">Beyond Tengboche, the trail climbs steadily through Dingboche and Lobuche, where the environment becomes more remote and alpine in character. These higher settlements play a key role in helping trekkers adjust safely to the altitude. The final approach leads to Gorakshep and then to Everest Base Camp (5,364 meters), the historic starting point for Everest expeditions. Standing here, surrounded by glaciers and immense peaks, is a moment that leaves a lasting impression.</p>\n<p data-start="1961" data-end="2286">A further highlight is the ascent of Kala Patthar (5,545 meters), a viewpoint known for its exceptional panorama of Everest. The early morning climb rewards trekkers with clear, close views of the mountain and a sunrise that illuminates the entire range. For many, this becomes one of the most memorable parts of the journey.</p>\n<p data-start="2288" data-end="2657">Throughout the trek, accommodation is provided in locally operated teahouses, where trekkers experience genuine hospitality and daily life in the mountains. The route also passes through Sagarmatha National Park, a protected area recognized for its natural and cultural importance. Its forests, wildlife, and mountain landscapes add depth and variety to the experience.</p>\n<p data-start="2659" data-end="2998">Although the <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/gokyo-lake-trekking/">Everest</a> Base Camp Trek requires good physical condition and preparation, it does not involve technical climbing. With proper pacing and acclimatization, it is achievable for many trekkers. More than just a physical challenge, it is a journey that offers perspective, connection with nature, and a deep sense of accomplishment.</p>\n<p data-start="3000" data-end="3244" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">For those who have dreamed of walking in the shadow of Everest, this trek represents an extraordinary opportunity. It is not simply about reaching base camp, but about the experience of the journey itself and the memories created along the way.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/ever-peak-everest-base-camp-15-days-trek.png	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	15 Days	1799	everest	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Dec	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{everest-region}	<ul>\n<li>Reach Everest Base Camp (5,364m), the base of the world’s highest mountain</li>\n<li>Enjoy breathtaking sunrise views over Mount Everest from Kala Patthar (5,545m)</li>\n<li>Experience a scenic mountain flight between Kathmandu and Lukla</li>\n<li>Explore Namche Bazaar, the main gateway and cultural center of the Everest region</li>\n<li>Visit Tengboche Monastery, the most important and historic monastery in the area</li>\n<li>Walk through Sagarmatha National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site</li>\n<li>Witness spectacular views of Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Ama Dablam, and other major peaks</li>\n<li>Experience authentic Sherpa culture, traditions, and mountain lifestyle</li>\n<li>Trek through diverse landscapes including forests, rivers, glaciers, and alpine terrain</li>\n<li>Cross suspension bridges over deep mountain valleys and rivers</li>\n<li>Stay in traditional teahouses and enjoy warm local hospitality</li>\n<li>Achieve a personal milestone by completing one of the world’s most iconic treks</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Cost including</li>\n<li>3 night Kathmandu hotel.</li>\n<li>Tea house accommodation during trek with Brekfast/lunch/dinner(3 meals a day)</li>\n<li>All necessary(permit/national park fee)paper work</li>\n<li>Domestic flight to &amp; from lukla</li>\n<li>English speaking experience guide</li>\n<li>porter service (1 porter for 2 trekkers)</li>\n<li>ground transport as per itinerary</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n	<ul>\n<li>Nepal visa feeI</li>\n<li>International airfare to &amp; from Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Extra night accommodation in Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Travel and rescue insurance</li>\n<li>personal expenses (battery charge,internet,laundry,bar bills,bottle water etc.</li>\n<li>Tips for guide porter</li>\n</ul>\n	<p>Proper equipment and trekking gear are essential for a safe and comfortable Everest Base Camp Trek. Since the trek passes through different altitudes and weather conditions, having the right clothing and gear helps you stay warm, dry, and protected throughout the journey.</p>\n<p>Clothing should be layered to adjust easily to changing temperatures. A moisture-wicking base layer, warm fleece or down jacket, and a waterproof outer jacket are highly recommended. Comfortable trekking pants, thermal innerwear, gloves, warm hat, and wool socks are also important, especially at higher elevations where temperatures drop significantly.</p>\n<p>Good quality trekking boots are one of the most important items. They should be well-fitted, waterproof, and already broken in before the trek to avoid blisters. A lightweight daypack is needed to carry daily essentials such as water, snacks, camera, and extra clothing.</p>\n<p>Other essential items include sunglasses with UV protection, sunscreen, lip balm, reusable water bottle, trekking poles, and a sleeping bag suitable for cold temperatures. Personal items such as basic toiletries, medications, and a headlamp are also necessary.</p>\n<p>Choosing the right gear ensures comfort, safety, and confidence, allowing you to fully enjoy the Everest Base Camp trekking experience.</p>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Welcome to Nepal. Upon your arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport in Kathmandu, our representative will warmly greet you and transfer you to your hotel. After check-in, you can take some time to rest and recover from your journey.\\n\\nKathmandu is a vibrant city rich in culture, history, and tradition. Depending on your arrival time, you may explore the nearby streets, local markets, and experience the unique atmosphere of Nepal’s capital. In the evening, you will attend a trek briefing where your guide will provide important information about the Everest Base Camp Trek, check your equipment, and answer any questions.\\n\\nThis day is mainly for preparation and relaxation before your Himalayan adventure begins. Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\\";s:23", "elev": 0, "title": "Day1: Arrived in Kathmandu(1350m/4412ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Early in the morning, we take a scenic 30-minute flight to Lukla, the gateway to the Everest region. Upon arrival, we meet our porter and begin our trek, descending to Chaurikharka and further to Thadokoshi, where you may enjoy views of the surrounding mountains. We then ascend uphill to Ghat, passing a ridge marked with painted mani stones, and after roughly an hour of trekking, reach Phakding, where we stay overnight in a cozy tea house, resting for the next stage of our journey.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: flight  to lukla &amp; trek to Padking( 4h /2610m/8695ft)\\""}, {"day": "3", "desc": "After breakfast, we begin our scenic trek following the beautiful Dudh Koshi River, enjoying the refreshing mountain air as the trail winds through pine and rhododendron forests. The sound of the rushing river accompanies us as we cross several thrilling suspension bridges decorated with colorful prayer flags and pass through small traditional Sherpa villages with stone houses, prayer wheels, and mani walls. Soon we reach Monjo, the entrance to Sagarmatha National Park, where our permits are checked before we officially enter this UNESCO World Heritage Site. The path continues with gentle ups and downs through forested terrain until we arrive at Jorsalle, the last village before Namche Bazaar, where we can take a short rest or enjoy tea while preparing for the climb ahead. From Jorsalle, the trail follows the river to the dramatic high suspension bridge at the confluence of the Dudh Koshi and Bhote Koshi rivers; standing on this bridge is an unforgettable experience, and on a clear day we may catch our first breathtaking glimpse of Mount Everest, along with surrounding Himalayan giants, a magical moment that fills us with excitement. After crossing the bridge, the trail begins a long and steady uphill ascent through dense pine forest, requiring a slow and steady pace as we gain significant altitude; along the way, the views gradually open up, revealing spectacular mountain scenery behind us. After approximately 5–6 hours of trekking, we finally reach Namche Bazaar (3,440 m), the largest Sherpa settlement and vibrant commercial hub of the Khumbu region, beautifully set in a natural amphitheater surrounded by towering peaks. Namche offers a surprising range of facilities including good restaurants, bakeries, trekking gear shops, internet cafés, ATMs, and money exchange services. In the evening, we relax and explore the lively market area before enjoying a warm meal and an overnight stay at a comfortable tea house.\\";s", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3:Phakding to Namche Bazar(7h/3450m/11290ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Today, although we remain in Namche Bazaar due to the high altitude, it is not a full rest day. After breakfast, we trek to a nearby viewpoint to enjoy breathtaking panoramic views of the surrounding mountains, including Mount Everest. We then hike up to Syangboche, home to the highest airport in the region, and visit the Everest View Hotel for some stunning vistas. After spending time here, we descend back to Namche for an overnight stay in a cozy tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4:Acclimatization day in Namche Bazaar"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "After breakfast, we begin the day with a gradual climb to Namche Top, following a trail that takes us to Kanjima via Nepali Flat. Along the way, we are treated to spectacular views of Mount Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Thamserku, Ama Dablam, and many other smaller peaks. After passing this charming Sherpa village, we descend to the Dudh Koshi River and then undertake a famous ascent through rhododendron forests to Tengboche. Upon reaching Tengboche, we visit the largest monastery in the region and soak in the breathtaking mountain views. Overnight stay is at a tea house.\\n\\nI can continue polishing your remaining trek days in the same single-paragraph, professional style, so your\\n\\";s", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5:Namche to Deboche(5:30h/3860m/12960ft)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "After breakfast, we continue trekking through pine forests, descending toward Debuche, crossing a suspension bridge before climbing past many mani stones and small stupas. We pass through a picturesque village with fields of buckwheat, potatoes, and vegetables, then continue toward Imja Village and Lobuche Khola before ascending to Dingboche. Upon arrival, we enjoy spectacular views of Ama Dablam, Lhotse, and many other surrounding peaks. Overnight stay is at a tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6:Tengboche to Dingboche(6h/4360m/14300ft)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Today is a crucial acclimatization day to help our bodies adjust to the high altitude. After a hearty breakfast, we embark on a rewarding short hike toward Nagarjun Hill, where we are treated to awe-inspiring panoramic views of some of the most iconic Himalayan peaks, including Ama Dablam, Makalu, Lhotse, Tawache, Cholatse, and numerous other majestic peaks that punctuate the skyline. The crisp mountain air, sweeping vistas, and serene landscapes make this hike an unforgettable experience, offering countless photo opportunities and moments of reflection. After soaking in these magnificent Himalayan panoramas, we gently descend back to Dingboche, where we enjoy a leisurely lunch and rest, letting our bodies recover and prepare for the adventures ahead. Overnight stay is at the same charming tea house, surrounded by the serene beauty of the mountains.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Acclimatization day in Dingboche"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "After breakfast, we continue our trek along the rocky lateral moraine of the Khumbu Glacier, walking on a rugged trail with dramatic views of the surrounding Himalayan peaks. Along the way, we pass the memorial site at Thukla, where stone monuments stand in honor of climbers who lost their lives while attempting nearby summits — a quiet and emotional place that invites reflection. From here, the trail climbs steadily uphill for some time before leveling out as we follow the glacial valley toward Lobuche. Surrounded by towering mountains and vast alpine landscapes, we finally reach Lobuche (4,910 m), a small settlement with a few tea houses serving trekkers and climbers on the Everest Base Camp route. Overnight stay at a tea house.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8:Dingboche to Lobuche(5h/4900m/16000ft)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "Finally the most Awaiting day of hour whole trip as we climb to Everest Base Camp is Today. This is a big & difficult day walk along the Khumbu glacier up to base camp. Early morning breakfast then we start our journey towards Gorakshep. The trail gradually & Rockey all the way, once we reach in Gorakshep we chick into the hotel and have some rest, we continue up the edge of the Khumbu glacier until we finally reach base camp. if you are lucky & timing is right you may see expedition team. after spending some time to enjoying, we back way down to gorakshep.over night at tea house.\\n\\"", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9:Lobuche to Everest base camp(5360m/17450ft)Back to Gorak shep(5180m/16960ft)"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "Early in the morning wake up, we begin a challenging hike to the famous viewpoint of Kala Patthar (5,545 m), the highest point of our Everest Base Camp trek. The trail climbs steeply over rocky and sandy slopes, and the thin mountain air makes the ascent slow and steady. As we gain height, breathtaking panoramic views gradually unfold, including close-up views of Mount Everest, Nuptse, Lhotse, and the stunning Pumori. Reaching the summit of Kala Patthar is a truly unforgettable moment, offering the best panoramic view of Everest and the surrounding Himalayan giants, especially during sunrise or early morning light when the peaks glow beautifully.\\n\\nAfter spending some time taking photographs and enjoying the spectacular scenery, we descend carefully back to Gorakshep for a short rest and breakfast. We then continue trekking down the valley, retracing our steps along the Khumbu Glacier toward Lobuche and further downhill to Thukla. From here, the trail gradually descends to the wide and peaceful valley of Pheriche. Compared to the previous high-altitude days, the descent feels easier as oxygen levels increase and breathing becomes more comfortable. Finally, we reach Pheriche (4,240 m), a beautiful settlement surrounded by mountains, where we enjoy a well-deserved rest and overnight stay at a tea house.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10:Early morning hike up to Kala Patthar (5550m/18192ft) Trek down to Pheriche (8h/ 4200m/14000ft)"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "we begin our descent to Namche Bazaar, enjoying an easier walk as we move toward lower altitudes. The trail follows a familiar path through beautiful rhododendron and juniper forests with scenic mountain views along the way. We gradually descend to Phunki Tenga, a small riverside settlement where we stop for lunch and a short rest. After lunch, we begin the steady uphill climb through forested trails toward Tengboche, home to the famous Tengboche Monastery, the largest monastery in the Everest region. From Tengboche, the trail continues with gentle ups and downs before descending further toward the Dudh Koshi valley. Finally, we follow the gradual trail back to Namche Bazaar, where we enjoy a relaxing evening and overnight stay at a comfortable tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Trek to Namche Bazar(7h /3450m 11290ft)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "After breakfast, we begin our final descent toward Lukla, retracing our steps along the familiar trail through beautiful pine forests and charming Sherpa villages. The path leads us down along the Dudh Koshi River, crossing several suspension bridges decorated with colorful prayer flags and enjoying the last views of the surrounding mountains. Today marks our final night in the Everest region, and as we walk, we reflect on the unforgettable journey through the Himalayas. After several hours of gradual descent and short uphill sections, we arrive in Lukla. In the afternoon, we relax and celebrate the completion of our trek with a hot shower and some free time to explore the small mountain town. In the evening, we gather with our trekking guide and porter to enjoy a few drinks, share stories, and celebrate our successful adventure together. Overnight stay at a comfortable tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12:Trek to Lukla(7h/2800m/)"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "On the final morning in the mountains, you can enjoy the last beautiful views of the snow-capped Himalayan peaks surrounding Lukla before boarding your scenic flight back to Kathmandu. The short mountain flight offers one more breathtaking aerial view of the Himalayas, bringing your unforgettable Everest adventure to a close. Upon arrival in Kathmandu, our representative will transfer you to your hotel. In the afternoon, you will have free time to relax or explore the vibrant city at your own pace — perhaps strolling through the bustling streets of Thamel for shopping, cafés, and souvenirs. Overnight stay at the hotel in Kathmandu.\\";s", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Morning flight Lukla to Kathmandu(30m flight/1300m)"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "Today is a free and relaxing day in Kathmandu after completing your Everest Base Camp trek. You may choose to rest at your hotel or explore the cultural and historical attractions of the city. Popular places to visit include Kathmandu Durbar Square, Swayambhunath (Monkey Temple), Boudhanath Stupa, and Pashupatinath Temple. You can also enjoy shopping in Thamel for souvenirs, handicrafts, and trekking gear. This day allows you to recover comfortably and enjoy the vibrant atmosphere of Kathmandu before your final departure. Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Kathmandu free day "}, {"day": "15", "desc": "Today marks the end of your unforgettable Everest Base Camp Trek. After breakfast, our representative will transfer you from your hotel to Tribhuvan International Airport for your final departure. As you leave Nepal, you will carry with you incredible memories of the Himalayan landscapes, Sherpa culture, and your successful journey to Everest Base Camp. We hope this adventure has been a truly rewarding and memorable experience. EverPeak Adventures thanks you for trekking with us and hopes to welcome you again for another Himalayan journey in the future. Safe travels.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 15: Transfer to airport for final departure"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.852	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000skbrlzngs9z4r	manaslu-circuit-trek	Manaslu Circuit Trek	<h2 data-section-id="1wwpoq2" data-start="300" data-end="339">Why Choose the Manaslu Circuit Trek?</h2>\n<p data-start="341" data-end="796">The Manaslu	<h2 data-section-id="1wwpoq2" data-start="300" data-end="339">Why Choose the Manaslu Circuit Trek?</h2>\n<p data-start="341" data-end="796">The Manaslu Circuit Trek is one of Nepal’s most rewarding off-the-beaten-path adventures. Set around Mount Manaslu (8,163 m), the world’s eighth-highest mountain, this route combines spectacular Himalayan scenery, traditional villages, and fascinating cultural experiences. Compared with the busier Everest and Annapurna trails, the region offers a quieter and more authentic experience for travelers looking to explore Nepal’s remote mountain landscapes.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="bast6b" data-start="798" data-end="835">Explore the Remote Manaslu Region</h3>\n<p data-start="837" data-end="1265">The journey begins with a scenic drive from Kathmandu to Machha Khola before following the Budhi Gandaki River through lush forests, terraced farmland, suspension bridges, and peaceful settlements. As the trail gains elevation, the landscape gradually changes from green valleys to alpine terrain. Along the way, trekkers encounter welcoming communities, traditional homes, Buddhist monasteries, and ancient cultural traditions.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="g5odpp" data-start="1267" data-end="1319">Discover Himalayan Landscapes and Mountain Views</h3>\n<p data-start="1321" data-end="1752">One of the highlights is the remarkable variety of scenery throughout the route. The trail passes through dramatic river valleys, dense forests, alpine meadows, and rugged mountain terrain. As you move higher, impressive views of Mount Manaslu, Himal Chuli, Ganesh Himal, and other snow-covered peaks create unforgettable moments. The changing landscapes also provide excellent opportunities for photography and nature exploration.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="1ofl7bg" data-start="1754" data-end="1781">Cross the Larke La Pass</h3>\n<p data-start="1783" data-end="2138">The most challenging section is the ascent to <strong data-start="1829" data-end="1856">Larke La Pass (5,160 m)</strong>. Reaching the summit requires good preparation and proper acclimatization, but the effort is rewarded with breathtaking panoramic views across the surrounding Himalayas. After crossing the pass, the trail descends toward the Marsyangdi Valley, where the scenery changes once again.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="lg5b4m" data-start="2140" data-end="2174">Culture, Nature, and Adventure</h3>\n<p data-start="2176" data-end="2590">Beyond the mountain views, this Himalayan journey offers meaningful encounters with local communities and their way of life. Trekkers can experience Buddhist traditions, visit historic monasteries, and learn about the customs that have shaped the region for generations. The combination of remote landscapes, cultural richness, and physical challenge makes this route an excellent choice for adventurous travelers.</p>\n<p data-start="2592" data-end="2773">With its peaceful trails, diverse scenery, and authentic mountain experiences, the <strong data-start="2675" data-end="2699">Manaslu Circuit Trek</strong> provides a memorable alternative to Nepal’s more crowded trekking routes.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/1000042911-1.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	14 days	1599	manaslu	Moderate		April – June	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{manaslu-region}	<p>The‌ Manaslu region is home to a mix of Gurung, Nubri, and Tibetan-influenced communities‍, each with their own traditi‌ons, dialects, and way‍ o‍f life. Ma‍ny villages,‍ especially at higher altitudes like Samagaon and Samdo, follow strong Budd‌h‌is‌t practic‌e‍s. You‌’l‌l find prayer flags, maniwa‌lls (stone carvings with Buddhist prayers),‌ and monasteries througho‌ut the trek. Life here is simp‌le and‌ revolves around farming, herding yaks, and religious rituals.</p>\n<p>As a visitor, showing respect‍ to loca‍l culture is very important. Always walk to the le‌ft side o‌f maniwalls and stupas as a sign of respect, and spin prayer⁠ whe‍el‌s clockwise. Greet locals with a smile and a simple‍ “‌Na‍maste‍” or the Tibetan‍ greeting “Tashi Delek.” Modest dress is app‌reciated in‍ villages cover shoulder‍s and avoid very short clothing, even though trek‍king gear is acce‌ptable.</p>\n<p><strong>What we can do</strong></p>\n<p>Walk left of s‌tupa‌s (clockwise).</p>\n<p>Greet locals with Namaste or‍ Tashi Delek.</p>\n<p>D‍ress modestly in villages.</p>\n<p>Carry your trash and keep the trail clean.</p>\n<p>Hike slo‌wly and acclimati‍ze pr‍operly.</p>\n<p>Support local tea houses and‍ buy from villagers.</p>\n<p>‌Ask before taking photos.</p>\n<p><strong>What we can't do</strong></p>\n<p>Don’t touch a‍ny‌one’s head or point your feet at shrines.</p>\n<p>Don’t enter monasteries withou‍t per‌mission.</p>\n<p>Don’t harm animals or w‍ildlif‌e.</p>\n<p>Don’t litter or leave plastic waste behind.</p>\n<p>Don’t rush at high altit‍udes‌-a‌void overexertion.</p>\n				[{"day": "1", "desc": "Welcome to Nepal. After arriving at Tribhuvan International Airport in Kathmandu, our representative will greet you and transfer you to your hotel. Once you check in, you can relax after your journey or take a short walk around nearby markets and cultural streets. Kathmandu is a vibrant city filled with temples, cafés, and traditional architecture. In the evening, you will meet your trekking guide for a short briefing about the trek, where your gear and final preparations will be checked.\\"", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "After an early breakfast, we leave Kathmandu and begin a scenic drive toward the Manaslu region. The road passes through hills, rivers, and traditional villages. As the journey continues, the landscape becomes more rural and mountainous. You will enjoy views of terraced farms, waterfalls, and local settlements along the route. By evening we arrive at Machha Khola, a small riverside village where we stay overnight in a local teahouse.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Drive Kathmandu to Machha Khola (930m / 3051 ft)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Today our trekking adventure begins. We follow a scenic trail along the Budhi Gandaki River, passing through small villages and lush landscapes. The trail includes suspension bridges, forest paths, and narrow river valleys. As we gradually climb higher, the environment becomes more peaceful and remote. After several hours of trekking through beautiful surroundings, we reach Jagat, a charming village known as the gateway to the Manaslu Conservation Area.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Trek Machha Khola to Jagat (1340m / 4396 ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Leaving Jagat, the trail climbs through terraced fields, forests, and traditional villages. Along the route, you will see beautiful landscapes and cultural settlements reflecting the unique lifestyle of the region. As we move deeper into the mountains, the scenery becomes more dramatic. After several hours of trekking through forests and narrow trails, we reach Lokpa, a quiet village that marks the entrance to the Tsum Valley.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Trek from Jagat to Deng (1860m / 6102 ft)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Today’s trek takes you deeper into the Manaslu region, where the scenery becomes more dramatic and the cultural atmosphere more Tibetan. The trail passes through small villages, forests, mani walls, and prayer wheels. You will cross the Budhi Gandaki River several times and climb gradually through beautiful landscapes. As you gain altitude, you may begin to see impressive mountain views and traditional stone houses. Namrung is a beautiful village with mountain views and a peaceful environment, making it a great place to rest after the day’s walk.\\";s:", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Trek from Deng to Namrung (2630m / 8629 ft)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "The walk from Namrung to Lho is one of the most scenic sections of the lower Manaslu region. The trail passes through beautiful villages such as Lihi and Sho, where you can see traditional houses, barley fields, mani walls, and prayer flags. As you move higher, the views of Manaslu and nearby peaks become more impressive. Lho is a stunning village known for its monastery and breathtaking mountain views. After reaching Lho, you can rest or visit the local monastery in the evening.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Trek from Namrung to Lho (3180m / 10433 ft)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Today’s trail offers spectacular views of Mt. Manaslu and the surrounding Himalayan peaks. You will pass through Shyala, a beautiful village surrounded by mountains and open landscapes. The route is relatively shorter but visually very rewarding. As you approach Samagaun, the valley becomes wider, and the village appears with traditional houses, monasteries, and mountain backdrops. Samagaun is one of the most important villages on the Manaslu Circuit and a key place for acclimatization before moving higher.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Trek from Lho to Samagaun (3530m / 11581 ft)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "Today is an important acclimatization day in Samagaun. You can spend the day exploring the village, visiting the monastery, or taking an optional hike to Manaslu Base Camp or Pungyen Gompa, depending on your fitness and weather conditions. The purpose of this day is to help your body adjust to the altitude before continuing towards Samdo and Larkya La Pass. Samagaun offers beautiful mountain views, peaceful cultural surroundings, and a chance to learn more about the local lifestyle of the Manaslu region.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Acclimatization Day in Samagaun"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "After proper acclimatization in Samagaun, the trek continues towards Samdo. The trail is shorter but gradually gains altitude as it follows open landscapes, yak grazing areas, and beautiful mountain scenery. The route feels more remote and peaceful as you move closer to the Tibetan border region. Samdo is a traditional village with strong Tibetan cultural influence and impressive views of surrounding peaks. After reaching Samdo, you can rest and explore the village slowly.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Trek from Samagaun to Samdo (3875m / 12713 ft)"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "Today you will trek from Samdo to Dharamsala, also known as Larkya Phedi. The trail gradually climbs through dry and rugged high-altitude landscapes. The environment becomes colder and more remote as you move closer to the base of Larkya La Pass. This is a short but important day because you need enough rest before the long and challenging pass-crossing day. After reaching Dharamsala, you will have an early dinner and prepare your gear for the next morning.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Trek from Samdo to Dharamsala / Larkya Phedi (4460m / 14632 ft)"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "This is the most challenging and rewarding day of the Manaslu Circuit Trek. You will start early in the morning and gradually climb towards Larkya La Pass, the highest point of the trek at around 5,160 meters. From the pass, you can enjoy breathtaking views of Himlung Himal, Cheo Himal, Kang Guru, Annapurna II, and other Himalayan peaks. After spending some time at the top, the trail descends steeply towards Bimthang. The long descent can be tiring, but the mountain views and sense of achievement make this day unforgettable.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Cross Larkya La Pass and Trek to Bimthang (3590m / 11778 ft)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "After crossing Larkya La Pass, today’s trail descends through beautiful forests, riverside paths, and traditional villages. The landscape changes quickly from high alpine scenery to greener valleys. You will pass through places like Yak Kharka, Gho, and Tilije before continuing towards Dharapani. This section is peaceful and scenic, with excellent views of the surrounding hills and mountains. Dharapani is connected with the Annapurna Circuit route and has better facilities compared to the higher villages.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Trek from Bimthang to Dharapani (1860m / 6102 ft)"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "Today you will drive back from Dharapani to Kathmandu. The journey usually begins with a jeep ride through rough mountain roads towards Besisahar, followed by a drive along the highway back to the capital city. The route passes through rivers, hills, villages, and scenic countryside. After many days in the mountains, returning to Kathmandu feels comfortable and refreshing. Once you arrive, you can rest at your hotel or enjoy a final evening in the city.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Drive from Dharapani to Kathmandu"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "Today we trek to Samdo, a traditional village near the Tibetan border. The trail follows a gradual climb through alpine landscapes with stunning mountain views.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Final Departure from Kathmandu"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.856	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000ukbrlionuecjh	upper-mustang-trek-16-days	Upper Mustang Trek – 16 Days (Drive Option) with 2 Nights in Lo Manthang	<h2 data-start="230" data-end="261"><strong>Upper Mustang Trek Overview</strong></h2>\n<p data-start="263" data-end="663">The 16-day <a href="https://w	<h2 data-start="230" data-end="261"><strong>Upper Mustang Trek Overview</strong></h2>\n<p data-start="263" data-end="663">The 16-day <a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=830e528a4f670b12&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnvzofO7OYVJXs-UgJ2iLxgYftxdIQ:1782007115076&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gIHbHEqXWbyThyPdUCKqTmZAKzBcRFb2qe3OBMfh6G5UU95rQ_0RWnxsY5je01K1qLprE6MJt04e2R0nugQa8ieshVwOqnImMfVyA2WhDka1Z9CIbplpiYbsLOxumutBZeEDE7TxWlqF7BJrRC0ciPoHqV_gg&amp;q=upper+mustang&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjK79LonZeVAxV82TgGHVtcIvYQtKgLegQIGhAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Upper Mustang</a> Trek begins with your arrival in Kathmandu, where our team welcomes you at the airport and transfers you to your hotel. After a trek briefing and preparation, you drive to Pokhara along the scenic Prithvi Highway. The following day, the journey continues through the Kali Gandaki Valley via Tatopani and Marpha before reaching Jomsom, the gateway to the <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/upper-mustang-jeep-tour-12-days-standard-itinerary/">Mustang</a> region.</p>\n<p data-start="665" data-end="1125">From Jomsom, the trek starts towards Kagbeni, an ancient village that marks the entrance to the restricted area of Upper Mustang. The trail then passes through traditional settlements such as Chele, Syangboche, Ghami, and Tsarang. Along the way, you walk through dramatic desert landscapes, colorful cliffs, deep valleys, and remote Tibetan-influenced villages. Ancient monasteries, prayer walls, and centuries-old traditions add cultural depth to the journey.</p>\n<p data-start="1127" data-end="1596">The trek eventually reaches Lo Manthang, the historic walled capital of the former Kingdom of Mustang. You spend two nights here to explore its rich cultural and historical attractions. Visits include ancient monasteries, traditional houses, the royal palace, and nearby Chhoser, which is famous for its mysterious cave complexes carved into the cliffs. This extra time allows for a deeper understanding of the region's Tibetan Buddhist heritage and unique way of life.</p>\n<p data-start="1598" data-end="2065">After exploring Lo Manthang, the return journey follows a scenic route through Drakmar, Ghiling, and Kagbeni. From Kagbeni, you drive back through Jomsom, Marpha, and Tatopani before reaching Pokhara. The final drive returns you to Kathmandu, completing an unforgettable adventure.</p>\n\n<h3 data-start="1598" data-end="2065">Why choose this trek?</h3>\n<p data-start="1598" data-end="2065">Combining spectacular Himalayan scenery, ancient culture, and remote desert landscapes, this trek offers one of Nepal's most rewarding and distinctive trekking experiences.</p>\n<p data-start="2832" data-end="3375"></p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/10/upper-Mustang-trek.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	16 Days	2499	mustang-region-trekking	Moderate		March–June / October–January	Hotels in Kathmandu	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{mustang-region-trekking}	<ul data-start="560" data-end="1262">\n<li data-section-id="1dfrsgr" data-start="560" data-end="686">\n<p data-start="562" data-end="686">Explore the remote Upper Mustang region, a restricted Himalayan area rich in Tibetan culture and traditional villages.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1uc4i9p" data-start="687" data-end="779">\n<p data-start="689" data-end="779">Visit Lo Manthang, the walled capital, and enjoy 2 nights in this historic town.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="jrm797" data-start="780" data-end="854">\n<p data-start="782" data-end="854">Witness stunning Himalayan desert landscapes, cliffs, and canyons.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="45w555" data-start="855" data-end="946">\n<p data-start="857" data-end="946">Trek through villages like Kagbeni, Chele, Syangboche, Ghami, Tsarang, and Drakmar.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="lls3cl" data-start="947" data-end="1057">\n<p data-start="949" data-end="1057">Experience ancient monasteries, mani walls, and prayer flags, reflecting Mustang’s spiritual heritage.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="r656wi" data-start="1058" data-end="1153">\n<p data-start="1060" data-end="1153">Remote trekking with minimal tourist crowds, offering an authentic Himalayan adventure.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="ycr51x" data-start="1154" data-end="1262">\n<p data-start="1156" data-end="1262">Opportunities for photography, cultural exploration, and unique landscapes rarely seen by outsiders.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="1oix330" data-start="161" data-end="219">\n<p data-start="163" data-end="219">Airport transfers in Kathmandu (arrival and departure)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="rmp3mt" data-start="220" data-end="295">\n<p data-start="222" data-end="295">Accommodation in Kathmandu hotels and teahouses during the trek</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="149k640" data-start="296" data-end="359">\n<p data-start="298" data-end="359">Full-board meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) during the trek</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="cpsydq" data-start="360" data-end="423">\n<p data-start="362" data-end="423">Experienced English-speaking trekking guide and porters</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1jt521w" data-start="424" data-end="494">\n<p data-start="426" data-end="494">Trekking permits and restricted area permits for Upper Mustang</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="pbhqkf" data-start="495" data-end="544">\n<p data-start="497" data-end="544">National park entry fees where applicable</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="2pu0x" data-start="545" data-end="604">\n<p data-start="547" data-end="604">First aid kit and emergency support throughout the trek</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1m2d6g0" data-start="605" data-end="685">\n<p data-start="607" data-end="685">Transportation from Pokhara to Jomsom and return drives as per itinerary</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="bir148" data-start="720" data-end="767">\n<p data-start="722" data-end="767">International airfare to and from Nepal</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="14h9bxf" data-start="768" data-end="823">\n<p data-start="770" data-end="823">Travel insurance including emergency evacuation</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="nfzoo3" data-start="824" data-end="864">\n<p data-start="826" data-end="864">Personal trekking equipment and gear</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1je8il9" data-start="865" data-end="926">\n<p data-start="867" data-end="926">Extra meals, drinks, and snacks outside the trekking plan</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1equfaq" data-start="927" data-end="958">\n<p data-start="929" data-end="958">Tips for guides and porters</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="2w89lh" data-start="959" data-end="1028">\n<p data-start="961" data-end="1028">Optional sightseeing or activities not mentioned in the itinerary</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1qw1np8" data-start="1029" data-end="1083">\n<p data-start="1031" data-end="1083">Personal expenses, laundry, phone calls, and Wi-Fi</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul data-start="283" data-end="1106">\n<li data-section-id="1j40kt8" data-start="283" data-end="387">\n<p data-start="285" data-end="387">Trekking Boots &amp; Socks: Sturdy, well-broken-in boots and moisture-wicking socks for long trails.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="uibjue" data-start="388" data-end="500">\n<p data-start="390" data-end="500">Warm Clothing: Layered clothing including down jacket, fleece, thermal wear, and windproof outer layers.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="inqd32" data-start="501" data-end="590">\n<p data-start="503" data-end="590">Rain Gear: Waterproof jacket and pants to protect against sudden weather changes.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mks26m" data-start="591" data-end="664">\n<p data-start="593" data-end="664">Trekking Poles: Helpful for stability on uneven or rocky terrain.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1u6t65g" data-start="665" data-end="756">\n<p data-start="667" data-end="756">Headwear &amp; Gloves: Hat, gloves, and sunglasses to protect from sun, wind, and cold.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="fm1zkt" data-start="757" data-end="842">\n<p data-start="759" data-end="842">Backpack: Comfortable daypack with water bottles, snacks, and personal items.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1lh2bt1" data-start="843" data-end="927">\n<p data-start="845" data-end="927">Sleeping Bag: Suitable for sub-zero temperatures at high altitude teahouses.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gkq56s" data-start="928" data-end="1028">\n<p data-start="930" data-end="1028">Personal Items: Toiletries, sunscreen, lip balm, trekking permits, and first aid essentials.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="y3jdzf" data-start="1029" data-end="1106">\n<p data-start="1031" data-end="1106">Optional Gear: Camera, binoculars, and personal trekking electronics.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Welcome to Kathmandu. After landing at Tribhuvan International Airport, our representative will transfer you to your hotel. Once settled, you can relax or explore nearby cultural streets and markets. In the evening, your trekking guide will provide a briefing, check your gear, and go over the plan for the upcoming Upper Mustang adventure. This day is mainly for rest and preparation to ensure you are ready for the journey ahead.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1,350m / 4,429 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "After breakfast, we drive from Kathmandu to Pokhara, enjoying scenic hills, terraced fields, and rivers along the way. The road passes through several towns and offers glimpses of rural Nepalese life. On arrival in Pokhara, check into your hotel and take some time to relax by Phewa Lake or explore the local bazaar. This drive allows gradual acclimatization while you enjoy picturesque landscapes and mountain views.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Drive Kathmandu to Pokhara (820m / 2,690 ft)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "We continue the journey by road toward Jomsom, crossing rivers and scenic villages. Stop at Tatopani for its hot springs and at Marpha, famous for apple orchards and local whiskey. The drive offers incredible views of Annapurna and Dhaulagiri ranges. By evening, arrive in Jomsom, the gateway to Upper Mustang, and settle in a local guesthouse for an overnight stay.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Drive Pokhara to Jomsom via Tatopani and Marpha (2,720m / 8,924 ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "The trek begins along the Kali Gandaki River, passing traditional villages and beautiful landscapes. You will cross suspension bridges, walk through arid hills, and see ancient mani walls and chortens along the way. Kagbeni, a historic village at the entrance to Upper Mustang, offers a fascinating glimpse into Tibetan-influenced culture and is a perfect first stop for acclimatization.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Trek Jomsom to Kagbeni (2,810m / 9,212 ft)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "The trail gradually ascends through dry hills and barren landscapes unique to Upper Mustang. You will pass small villages, prayer flags, and Buddhist monuments. Chele is a quiet village offering panoramic views of the surrounding Himalayan ranges and is ideal for experiencing the remote Mustang lifestyle.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Trek Kagbeni to Chele (3,050m / 10,006 ft)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "The trail passes rugged cliffs, colorful rock formations, and isolated villages. You will notice the traditional Mustang architecture and the serene environment of this arid highland region. Syangboche is a small village that provides rest and acclimatization with views of distant Himalayan peaks.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Trek Chele to Syangboche (3,290m / 10,791 ft)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Today we follow a scenic route across plateaus, valleys, and highland deserts. Ghami is a picturesque village with stone houses, prayer wheels, and traditional fields. You will pass mani walls and chortens along the way, experiencing the spiritual heritage of Upper Mustang.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Trek Syangboche to Ghami (3,520m / 11,549 ft)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "The trail gently ascends, crossing isolated fields and rugged terrain. Tsarang is an ancient village with impressive monasteries, fortifications, and beautiful Tibetan-style architecture. This is an excellent opportunity to witness the rich culture of Upper Mustang.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Trek Ghami to Tsarang (3,580m / 11,745 ft)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "Today we reach Lo Manthang, the walled capital of Upper Mustang. The trail passes arid plateaus and rocky landscapes. Lo Manthang offers stunning views of surrounding peaks and a rare insight into Mustang’s royal and spiritual heritage. Overnight stays are in guesthouses or local lodges.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Trek Tsarang to Lo Manthang (3,840m / 12,598 ft)"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "Spend the day exploring Lo Manthang’s monasteries, royal palace, and narrow streets. The village offers a unique glimpse into Mustang’s medieval architecture and Tibetan Buddhist culture. Enjoy local interactions and walk around fortified walls for scenic views.\\";s:", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Exploration in Lo Manthang (3,840m / 12,598 ft)"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "Today we visit nearby villages like Chhoser, famous for its ancient sky caves. The trail offers panoramic views of valleys and mountains. Discover unique cliffside caves once used for meditation and burial, providing insight into Mustang’s ancient culture.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Excursion around Lo Manthang (Chhoser and Sky Caves) (3,840m / 12,598 ft)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "Begin descending from Lo Manthang toward the small village of Drakmar. The trail passes through arid landscapes, cliffs, and isolated settlements. Enjoy expansive desert views and the peaceful atmosphere of this remote region.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Trek Lo Manthang to Drakmar (3,500 m / 11,482 ft)"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "Continue trekking along high desert terrain, passing small hamlets and mani walls. Ghiling offers authentic local hospitality and panoramic views of the surrounding valleys.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Trek Drakmar to Ghiling (3,420 m / 11,220 ft)"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "Descend further into the Kali Gandaki Valley toward Kagbeni. The trail passes cliffs, desert valleys, and traditional villages. Arrive in Kagbeni and enjoy a comfortable overnight stay.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Trek Ghiling to Kagbeni (2,800 m / 9,186 ft)"}, {"day": "15", "desc": "Drive back through the Kali Gandaki Valley, passing Jomsom, Marpha, and Tatopani, enjoying the dramatic valley scenery. Arrive in Pokhara and relax in a lakeside hotel after the long drive.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 15: Drive Kagbeni – Jomsom – Marpha – Tatopani – Pokhara (820 m / 2,690 ft)\\";s:11:\\""}, {"day": "16", "desc": "Drive back to Kathmandu for your onward flight. Reflect on the stunning landscapes, cultural experiences, and Himalayan adventure of the Upper Mustang Trek.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 16: Drive Pokhara to Kathmandu – Final Departure (1,400 m / 4,593 ft)\\";"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.864	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000wkbrl9z6znc54	manaslu-chum-valley-trek-19-days	Manaslu and Chum Valley 19 days	<div data-turn-id-container="6bdadc27-feff-4988-8d7a-b7443780c8e5" data-is-intersecting="true"></div>\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:e8a65c3	<div data-turn-id-container="6bdadc27-feff-4988-8d7a-b7443780c8e5" data-is-intersecting="true"></div>\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:e8a65c36-c8fc-4a60-a881-a4494a3934ab-23" data-is-intersecting="true"><section dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:e8a65c36-c8fc-4a60-a881-a4494a3934ab-23" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:e8a65c36-c8fc-4a60-a881-a4494a3934ab-23" data-testid="conversation-turn-48" data-turn="assistant">\n<div>\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div>\n<div dir="auto" tabindex="0" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="ee2c9891-649a-4918-b847-8ac37511ec09" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-6" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div>\n<div>\n<h2 data-section-id="17h2ee5" data-start="0" data-end="44">Discover the<a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=326223ae55b11ae7&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnsRILGxIye5uD6wmGGLbWiv-9hTgA:1787387595343&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gKq1sgc0zFmtILFJcehpQnp8EvsgtsNoHlk8yRnPtPFZTFppidpMf3acGusE4WvlMaqVeJ_G7aj1Gz_ymywOPYPTIOv3WGYQHHgc5nVcfWPA2jyTEUSd8triSJAXyyatewLdgwLM3BOpfnoNdQL2VYGJg25xA&amp;q=manaslu&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwju2cjV6bOWAxU8cGwGHSEKF9cQtKgLegQIIRAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25"> Manaslu</a> and Chum Valley Trek</h2>\n<p data-start="46" data-end="455">The <a href="http://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/manaslu-circuit-trek/"><strong data-start="50" data-end="78">Manaslu Chum Valley Trek</strong></a> is a remarkable 19-day journey through Nepal’s remote Himalayan landscapes. The adventure combines spectacular mountain scenery, peaceful villages, ancient Buddhist monasteries, and authentic local culture. Away from the busier Everest and Annapurna routes, this trail offers a quieter and more immersive experience for travelers seeking natural beauty and cultural discovery.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="27votb" data-start="457" data-end="490">Explore the Sacred Chum Valley</h2>\n<p data-start="492" data-end="823">Located near the Tibetan border, Chum Valley is known for its unique traditions and spiritual heritage. The trail passes through traditional villages, ancient monasteries, prayer walls, and sacred sites. Trekkers can experience the daily lifestyle of local communities while enjoying the peaceful surroundings and warm hospitality.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="dv9h8n" data-start="825" data-end="867">Experience Diverse Himalayan Landscapes</h2>\n<p data-start="869" data-end="1204">The journey moves through terraced hillsides, lush forests, rushing rivers, and remote mountain settlements. As you gain altitude, the landscape changes into alpine meadows and rugged Himalayan terrain. Along the way, you can enjoy impressive views of Mount Manaslu (8,163 m), Ganesh Himal, Himlung Himal, and other snow-covered peaks.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="1drelea" data-start="1206" data-end="1233">Cross the Larkya La Pass</h2>\n<p data-start="1235" data-end="1571">A major highlight of this adventure is crossing <strong data-start="1283" data-end="1317">Larkya La Pass at 5,106 meters</strong>. The challenging ascent rewards trekkers with breathtaking views of glaciers, towering peaks, and deep Himalayan valleys. Reaching the pass creates a memorable sense of achievement before the trail gradually descends through scenic mountain settlements.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="17594yp" data-start="1573" data-end="1616">Why Choose the Manaslu Chum Valley Trek?</h2>\n<p data-start="1618" data-end="2081">This 19-day Himalayan adventure is ideal for travelers who want a combination of challenging trails, cultural experiences, and spectacular scenery. From the sacred landscapes of Chum Valley to the dramatic crossing of Larkya La Pass, every section offers something unique. With remote villages, centuries-old traditions, and unforgettable mountain views, the <strong data-start="1977" data-end="2005">Manaslu Chum Valley Trek</strong> provides an authentic experience away from Nepal’s crowded trekking routes.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section></div>\n<h1 data-section-id="17h2ee5" data-start="22" data-end="66"><span>llenging trails, cultural discovery, and breathtaking Himalayan views, the Manaslu and Chum Valley Trek is an excellent choice for travelers seeking a quieter and more authentic Himalayan experience.</span></h1>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-28-at-15.30.00-2.jpeg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	19 days	1799	manaslu	Moderate		March -June , Oct -Dec	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{manaslu-region}	<p data-start="186" data-end="324">• Trek through the remote Manaslu region, home to the world’s 8th highest peak, <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Manaslu</span></span> (8,163 m).</p>\n<p data-start="326" data-end="450">• Explore the off-the-beaten-path Chum Valley, rich in Tibetan Buddhist culture and traditional mountain villages.</p>\n<p data-start="452" data-end="576">• Experience stunning Himalayan panoramas, including views of Manaslu, Himalchuli, Ganesh Himal, and Annapurna ranges.</p>\n<p data-start="578" data-end="685">• Cross the Larkya La Pass (5,160 m), a thrilling high-altitude pass offering spectacular landscapes.</p>\n<p data-start="687" data-end="814">• Visit ancient Buddhist monasteries, mani walls, and prayer flags, showcasing the unique local culture and spirituality.</p>\n<p data-start="816" data-end="929">• Trek through diverse terrain, including subtropical forests, alpine meadows, glaciers, and river valleys.</p>\n<p data-start="1025" data-end="1140">• Remote trekking with minimal tourist crowds, providing a true adventure and authentic Himalayan experience.</p>\n<p data-start="1142" data-end="1244">• Opportunity for photography, wildlife spotting, and witnessing rare Himalayan flora and fauna.</p>\n	<p data-start="162" data-end="213">• Airport pick-up and drop-off by private vehicle</p>\n<p data-start="215" data-end="294">• Standard hotel accommodation in Kathmandu with breakfast (as per itinerary)</p>\n<p data-start="296" data-end="440">• Tourist bus or private vehicle transportation (Kathmandu to trek starting point and trek ending point to Kathmandu/Pokhara as per itinerary)</p>\n<p data-start="442" data-end="521">• Domestic flights if required by itinerary (if applicable, optional upgrade)</p>\n<p data-start="523" data-end="588">• Accommodation in comfortable teahouses/lodges during the trek</p>\n<p data-start="590" data-end="658">• Three meals a day during the trek (Breakfast, Lunch, and Dinner)</p>\n<p data-start="660" data-end="767">• Experienced, licensed, and English-speaking trekking guide familiar with Manaslu and Chum Valley region</p>\n<p data-start="769" data-end="886">• Necessary number of porters (1 porter for 2 trekkers), including their salary, insurance, food, and accommodation</p>\n<p data-start="888" data-end="928">• Manaslu Restricted Area Permit (RAC)</p>\n<p data-start="930" data-end="1015">• Annapurna Conservation Area Permit (ACAP) if the trek passes overlapping sections</p>\n<p data-start="1017" data-end="1072">• Trekkers’ Information Management System (TIMS) card</p>\n<p data-start="1074" data-end="1127">• All government taxes and official service charges</p>\n<p data-start="1129" data-end="1167">• First aid kit carried by the guide</p>\n<p data-start="1169" data-end="1263">• Assistance for emergency rescue arrangement (rescue cost covered by your travel insurance)</p>\n	<p data-start="171" data-end="210">• International airfare to/from Nepal</p>\n<p data-start="212" data-end="230">• Nepal visa fee</p>\n<p data-start="232" data-end="300">• Travel insurance (mandatory for trek, covering emergency rescue)</p>\n<p data-start="302" data-end="387">• Personal expenses (tea/coffee, snacks, bottled water, soft drinks, alcohol, etc.)</p>\n<p data-start="389" data-end="471">• Hot showers or charging devices in teahouses (may be available for extra cost)</p>\n<p data-start="473" data-end="514">• Tips for guides, porters, and drivers</p>\n<p data-start="516" data-end="602">• Optional activities not mentioned in the itinerary (cultural tours, rafting, etc.)</p>\n<p data-start="604" data-end="657">• Sleeping bag (can be rented or bought separately)</p>\n<p data-start="659" data-end="728">• Personal trekking gear (down jacket, trekking poles, boots, etc.)</p>\n<p data-start="730" data-end="808">• Additional costs due to flight delays, landslides, or other natural events</p>\n<p data-start="810" data-end="857">• Rescue cost not covered by travel insurance</p>\n	<p data-start="244" data-end="687"><strong data-start="244" data-end="256">Clothing</strong><br data-start="256" data-end="259" />• Lightweight trekking pants and shorts<br data-start="298" data-end="301" />• Moisture-wicking t-shirts (short and long sleeves)<br data-start="353" data-end="356" />• Insulating fleece or down jacket<br data-start="390" data-end="393" />• Waterproof and windproof jacket<br data-start="426" data-end="429" />• Thermal base layers (top and bottom)<br data-start="467" data-end="470" />• Warm trekking gloves and liner gloves<br data-start="509" data-end="512" />• Hat or cap for sun protection<br data-start="543" data-end="546" data-is-only-node="" />• Warm hat/beanie for high altitudes<br data-start="582" data-end="585" />• Neck gaiter or buff<br data-start="606" data-end="609" />• Trekking socks (wool or synthetic)<br data-start="645" data-end="648" />• Gaiters (optional, for snow or mud)</p>\n<p data-start="689" data-end="809"><strong data-start="689" data-end="701">Footwear</strong><br data-start="701" data-end="704" />• Sturdy trekking boots (well broken-in, waterproof)<br data-start="756" data-end="759" />• Lightweight camp shoes or sandals for evenings</p>\n<p data-start="811" data-end="978"><strong data-start="811" data-end="837">Backpack &amp; Accessories</strong><br data-start="837" data-end="840" />• Daypack (20–30L) for daily essentials<br data-start="879" data-end="882" />• Waterproof backpack cover or dry bags<br data-start="921" data-end="924" />• Duffel bag for porters (optional, can be provided)</p>\n<p data-start="980" data-end="1138"><strong data-start="980" data-end="1007">Sleeping &amp; Camping Gear</strong><br data-start="1007" data-end="1010" />• Sleeping bag (rated -10°C to -15°C for high altitudes)<br data-start="1066" data-end="1069" />• Sleeping bag liner (optional for extra warmth)<br data-start="1117" data-end="1120" />• Trekking poles</p>\n<p data-start="1140" data-end="1436"><strong data-start="1140" data-end="1159">Health &amp; Safety</strong><br data-start="1159" data-end="1162" />• Personal first aid kit (plasters, painkillers, blister pads)<br data-start="1224" data-end="1227" />• Sunscreen (SPF 50+) and lip balm<br data-start="1261" data-end="1264" />• Sunglasses with UV protection<br data-start="1295" data-end="1298" />• Water bottles or hydration bladder<br data-start="1334" data-end="1337" />• Water purification tablets or filter<br data-start="1375" data-end="1378" />• Headlamp with spare batteries<br data-start="1409" data-end="1412" />• Personal medications</p>\n<p data-start="1438" data-end="1655"><strong data-start="1438" data-end="1455">Miscellaneous</strong><br data-start="1455" data-end="1458" />• Camera or smartphone with extra memory cards<br data-start="1504" data-end="1507" />• Power bank or solar charger<br data-start="1536" data-end="1539" />• Notebook or trekking journal (optional)<br data-start="1580" data-end="1583" />• Snacks/energy bars<br data-start="1603" data-end="1606" />• Toilet paper and wet wipes<br data-start="1634" data-end="1637" />• Hand sanitizer</p>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Welcome to Nepal. After arriving at Tribhuvan International Airport in Kathmandu, our representative will greet you and transfer you to your hotel. Once you check in, you can relax after your journey or take a short walk around nearby markets and cultural streets. Kathmandu is a vibrant city filled with temples, cafés, and traditional architecture. In the evening, you will meet your trekking guide for a short briefing about the trek, where your gear and final preparations will be checked.\\"", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "After an early breakfast, we leave Kathmandu and begin a scenic drive toward the Manaslu region. The road passes through hills, rivers, and traditional villages. As the journey continues, the landscape becomes more rural and mountainous. You will enjoy views of terraced farms, waterfalls, and local settlements along the route. By evening we arrive at Machha Khola, a small riverside village where we stay overnight in a local teahouse.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Drive Kathmandu to Machha Khola (930m / 3051 ft)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Today our trekking adventure begins. We follow a scenic trail along the Budhi Gandaki River, passing through small villages and lush landscapes. The trail includes suspension bridges, forest paths, and narrow river valleys. As we gradually climb higher, the environment becomes more peaceful and remote. After several hours of trekking through beautiful surroundings, we reach Jagat, a charming village known as the gateway to the Manaslu Conservation Area.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Trek Machha Khola to Jagat (1340m / 4396 ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Leaving Jagat, the trail climbs through terraced fields, forests, and traditional villages. Along the route, you will see beautiful landscapes and cultural settlements reflecting the unique lifestyle of the region. As we move deeper into the mountains, the scenery becomes more dramatic. After several hours of trekking through forests and narrow trails, we reach Lokpa, a quiet village that marks the entrance to the Tsum Valley.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Trek Jagat to Lokpa (2240m / 7349 ft)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Today we enter the beautiful Tsum Valley. The trail descends into forested landscapes before crossing suspension bridges over the river. Along the way, you will see traditional houses, prayer flags, and stunning mountain views. Chumling is a peaceful village surrounded by hills and farmland. It offers wonderful views of Ganesh Himal and provides a great opportunity to experience the local Tibetan-influenced culture.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Trek Lokpa to Chumling (2386m / 7828 ft)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "The trail climbs gradually through beautiful landscapes, passing ancient monasteries, mani walls, and small settlements. The scenery becomes more open with impressive mountain views. After several hours of trekking through traditional Tibetan-style villages, we reach Chhokang Paro, the largest settlement in the Tsum Valley.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Trek Chumling to Chhokang Paro (3031m / 9944 ft)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Today we trek deeper into the upper Tsum Valley. The trail passes through traditional villages, Buddhist chortens, and scenic landscapes surrounded by Himalayan peaks. The peaceful environment and cultural heritage make this section of the trek very special. After several hours of walking, we reach Nile, the last permanent settlement in the upper valley.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Trek Chhokang Paro to Nile (3361m / 11027 ft)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "Today we hike to the famous Mu Gompa, one of the most important monasteries in the Tsum Valley. Located in a peaceful mountain setting, the monastery offers incredible views and spiritual atmosphere. After exploring the monastery and surrounding landscapes, we return to Nile for the night.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Visit Mu Gompa and Trek back to Nile (3361m / 11027 ft)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "After breakfast, we retrace our route back down the valley. The descent offers beautiful views of mountains, forests, and traditional villages. Walking downhill provides a different perspective of the landscapes we previously passed. By afternoon we arrive again at Chumling where we stay overnight.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Trek Nile to Chumling (2386m / 7828 ft)"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "Leaving Chumling, we return to the main Manaslu trail and continue toward Deng. The route passes through forests, rivers, and small settlements. The scenery gradually changes as we move deeper into the Manaslu region.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Trek Chumling to Deng (1860m / 6102 ft)"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "The trail climbs gradually through forests and remote mountain landscapes. Along the way, you will notice increasing Tibetan cultural influence in the villages and monasteries. Namrung is a traditional village offering beautiful views of surrounding mountains.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Trek Deng to Namrung (2630m / 8628 ft)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "Today’s trek offers spectacular views of Manaslu and surrounding Himalayan peaks. The trail passes through alpine forests, traditional villages, and Buddhist cultural landmarks. Eventually we reach Samagaon, one of the largest villages in the region.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Trek Namrung to Samagaon (3530m / 11581 ft)"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "Today is an important acclimatization day. You may explore the village, visit monasteries, or take short hikes to nearby viewpoints. This helps your body adapt to the altitude before continuing toward higher elevations.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Acclimatization Day in Samagaon (3530m / 11581 ft)"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "Today we trek to Samdo, a traditional village near the Tibetan border. The trail follows a gradual climb through alpine landscapes with stunning mountain views.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Trek Samagaon to Samdo (3860m / 12664 ft)"}, {"day": "15", "desc": "We continue trekking toward Dharamsala, also known as Larkya Phedi. This is the base point for crossing Larkya La Pass. The trail passes through rugged alpine terrain.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 15: Trek Samdo to Dharamsala (4460m / 14632 ft)"}, {"day": "16", "desc": "Today is the most challenging and rewarding day as we cross the Larkya La Pass. From the top, enjoy spectacular panoramic views of the Himalayan peaks before descending toward Bimthang.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 16: Cross Larkya La Pass and Trek to Bimthang (3720m / 12205 ft)"}, {"day": "17", "desc": "After crossing the pass, today’s trek descends through beautiful forests and alpine landscapes. The trail offers wonderful views of surrounding peaks and valleys.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 17: Trek Bimthang to Gho (2560m / 8398 ft)"}, {"day": "18", "desc": "Today we trek to Dharapani where our trekking journey ends. From here we drive back to Kathmandu through scenic countryside landscapes.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 18: Trek Gho to Dharapani and Drive to Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}, {"day": "19", "desc": "Your unforgettable trekking adventure comes to an end today. Our team will transfer you to the airport for your international departure.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 19: Final Departure from Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.872	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000xkbrlglnxftrg	makalu-base-camp-trek	Makalu Base Camp Trek – 18 Days Himalayan Adventure	<div data-voice-floating-orb-focus-background="">\n<div>\n<div>\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:242471a9-270d-47dc-adf2-5d1b52ec924b-2" data-is	<div data-voice-floating-orb-focus-background="">\n<div>\n<div>\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:242471a9-270d-47dc-adf2-5d1b52ec924b-2" data-is-intersecting="true"><section dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:242471a9-270d-47dc-adf2-5d1b52ec924b-2" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:242471a9-270d-47dc-adf2-5d1b52ec924b-2" data-testid="conversation-turn-6" data-turn="assistant">\n<div>\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div>\n<div dir="auto" tabindex="0" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="d3217b7f-6e5d-4c07-b67f-c03e21bbe333" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div>\n<div>\n<h2>Explore the Remote Makalu Region</h2>\nThe <strong>Makalu Base Camp Trek</strong> is an 18-day Himalayan adventure through one of Nepal’s most remote and spectacular trekking regions. Far from the busy trails of Everest and Annapurna, this journey offers dramatic mountain scenery, traditional villages, rich cultural heritage, and an exceptional wilderness experience. The route leads toward the base of <strong>Mount Makalu (8,485 m)</strong>, the fifth-highest mountain in the world. The adventure begins with a scenic flight from Kathmandu to Tumlingtar, followed by a drive to Num. From here, the trail winds through traditional Rai and Sherpa villages, where you can experience local customs, welcoming communities, and the unique lifestyle of people living in the eastern Himalayas.\n<h2>Diverse Landscapes and Natural Beauty</h2>\nOne of the most remarkable features of this journey is its incredible natural diversity. The trail passes through <strong>Makalu Barun National Park</strong>, an area renowned for its rich biodiversity and pristine mountain environment. As you gain altitude, the landscape gradually changes from lush subtropical forests filled with rhododendrons and bamboo to alpine meadows, rocky valleys, glaciers, and rugged high-altitude terrain. The changing scenery makes every stage of the adventure unique. You will cross suspension bridges, walk beside cascading rivers, and follow remote mountain trails surrounded by impressive Himalayan landscapes. The peaceful environment also provides excellent opportunities for photography and wildlife observation.\n<h2>Spectacular Himalayan Mountain Views</h2>\nThroughout the route, trekkers can enjoy magnificent views of <strong>Makalu, Chamlang, Baruntse, Mera Peak</strong>, and numerous other snow-covered mountains. As the trail approaches higher elevations, the surrounding peaks become increasingly dramatic. Reaching <strong>Makalu Base Camp (4,870 m)</strong> is the major highlight of the expedition. Standing beneath the towering south face of Mount Makalu creates an unforgettable sense of achievement. The remote setting, powerful mountain scenery, and peaceful surroundings make the destination particularly rewarding for experienced trekkers.\n<h2>An Off-the-Beaten-Path Himalayan Adventure</h2>\nThis journey is ideal for experienced trekkers who want to explore a quieter and less-developed region of Nepal. Compared with more popular trekking routes, the trail offers greater solitude and a stronger connection with nature and local communities. The combination of challenging trails, diverse landscapes, traditional villages, rich biodiversity, and spectacular mountain views makes this 18-day adventure an excellent choice for travelers seeking something beyond the usual Himalayan routes. From the lower forests to the high alpine wilderness, every section reveals a different side of eastern Nepal and creates lasting memories of an extraordinary mountain expedition.\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section></div>\n</div>\n<div aria-hidden="true"></div>\n<div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div></div>\n</div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div></div>\n<div>\n<div data-prompt-textarea-header="">\n<div>\n<div><aside>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div>\n<div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</aside></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/3-makalu-moun.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	18 Days	2150	makalu-region-trekking	Moderate		Spring (March–May) and Autumn (September–November)	Hotel in Kathmandu and Local Tea Houses during the trek	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{makalu-region-trekking}	<ul data-start="1064" data-end="1537">\n<li data-section-id="1mpbaci" data-start="1064" data-end="1127">\n<p data-start="1066" data-end="1127">Trek to the remote and beautiful Makalu Base Camp (4,870 m)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="y6ytmt" data-start="1128" data-end="1213">\n<p data-start="1130" data-end="1213">Stunning views of Mount Makalu (8,485 m), the fifth highest mountain in the world</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="xmjk16" data-start="1214" data-end="1281">\n<p data-start="1216" data-end="1281">Explore Makalu Barun National Park with diverse flora and fauna</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="m5i18e" data-start="1282" data-end="1348">\n<p data-start="1284" data-end="1348">Experience traditional Sherpa and Rai villages along the trail</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="x7uhnk" data-start="1349" data-end="1416">\n<p data-start="1351" data-end="1416">Scenic flight to Tumlingtar and dramatic Arun Valley landscapes</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="t6hzmg" data-start="1417" data-end="1469">\n<p data-start="1419" data-end="1469">Crossing high mountain passes and alpine valleys</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="yddfj" data-start="1470" data-end="1537">\n<p data-start="1472" data-end="1537">One of Nepal’s least crowded and most adventurous trekking routes</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="1qfirtf" data-start="1589" data-end="1642">\n<p data-start="1591" data-end="1642">Airport pickup and drop-off services in Kathmandu</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="r2iaeg" data-start="1643" data-end="1703">\n<p data-start="1645" data-end="1703">2 nights hotel accommodation in Kathmandu with breakfast</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="xcakmx" data-start="1704" data-end="1758">\n<p data-start="1706" data-end="1758">Domestic flight Kathmandu – Tumlingtar – Kathmandu</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="ps9h0g" data-start="1759" data-end="1804">\n<p data-start="1761" data-end="1804">All ground transportation during the trek</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="cb4le0" data-start="1805" data-end="1848">\n<p data-start="1807" data-end="1848">Makalu Barun National Park entry permit</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="lmr6dl" data-start="1849" data-end="1891">\n<p data-start="1851" data-end="1891">Makalu Restricted Area trekking permit</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1ke4459" data-start="1892" data-end="1936">\n<p data-start="1894" data-end="1936">Licensed English-speaking trekking guide</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="128rc7l" data-start="1937" data-end="1993">\n<p data-start="1939" data-end="1993">Experienced porter service (1 porter for 2 trekkers)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="gwwyph" data-start="1994" data-end="2050">\n<p data-start="1996" data-end="2050">3 meals during the trek (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="13hfn3f" data-start="2051" data-end="2099">\n<p data-start="2053" data-end="2099">Tea house accommodation during trekking days</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="dz816h" data-start="2100" data-end="2140">\n<p data-start="2102" data-end="2140">Basic first aid kit carried by guide</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="14xdbp5" data-start="2141" data-end="2179">\n<p data-start="2143" data-end="2179">Government taxes and service charges</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="16utmg9" data-start="2231" data-end="2274">\n<p data-start="2233" data-end="2274">International flights to and from Nepal</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="jtoq12" data-start="2275" data-end="2294">\n<p data-start="2277" data-end="2294">Nepal visa fees</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1jffxyy" data-start="2295" data-end="2354">\n<p data-start="2297" data-end="2354">Travel insurance (mandatory for high altitude trekking)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="nfzoo3" data-start="2355" data-end="2395">\n<p data-start="2357" data-end="2395">Personal trekking equipment and gear</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1nj9z1i" data-start="2396" data-end="2424">\n<p data-start="2398" data-end="2424">Extra meals in Kathmandu</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="gyivbq" data-start="2425" data-end="2470">\n<p data-start="2427" data-end="2470">Alcoholic and soft drinks during the trek</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="xf26bs" data-start="2471" data-end="2535">\n<p data-start="2473" data-end="2535">Personal expenses such as laundry, phone calls, and internet</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1v18ca9" data-start="2536" data-end="2574">\n<p data-start="2538" data-end="2574">Tips for trekking guide and porter</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="70q9ph" data-start="2575" data-end="2643">\n<p data-start="2577" data-end="2643">Any additional costs caused by weather delays or unforeseen ev</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<p data-start="2719" data-end="2731"><strong data-start="2719" data-end="2731">Clothing</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="2733" data-end="2926">\n<li data-section-id="1hy5b6f" data-start="2733" data-end="2773">\n<p data-start="2735" data-end="2773">Down jacket or warm insulated jacket</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1kk2e3" data-start="2774" data-end="2814">\n<p data-start="2776" data-end="2814">Waterproof trekking jacket and pants</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="6nruzq" data-start="2815" data-end="2838">\n<p data-start="2817" data-end="2838">Thermal base layers</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1sxewht" data-start="2839" data-end="2880">\n<p data-start="2841" data-end="2880">Trekking shirts and lightweight pants</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="rl6zpk" data-start="2881" data-end="2909">\n<p data-start="2883" data-end="2909">Warm gloves and wool hat</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="jrjqh8" data-start="2910" data-end="2926">\n<p data-start="2912" data-end="2926">Trekking socks</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start="2928" data-end="2940"><strong data-start="2928" data-end="2940">Footwear</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="2942" data-end="3019">\n<li data-section-id="1yt62qy" data-start="2942" data-end="2972">\n<p data-start="2944" data-end="2972">Comfortable trekking boots</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1lf9koe" data-start="2973" data-end="2998">\n<p data-start="2975" data-end="2998">Camp shoes or sandals</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1iln5tk" data-start="2999" data-end="3019">\n<p data-start="3001" data-end="3019">Gaiters (optional)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start="3021" data-end="3038"><strong data-start="3021" data-end="3038">Trekking Gear</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="3040" data-end="3191">\n<li data-section-id="1f6cq7a" data-start="3040" data-end="3062">\n<p data-start="3042" data-end="3062">Backpack (40–60 L)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="eipj5x" data-start="3063" data-end="3102">\n<p data-start="3065" data-end="3102">Sleeping bag (rated -10°C or lower)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="bhpv4e" data-start="3103" data-end="3121">\n<p data-start="3105" data-end="3121">Trekking poles</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1d64pdv" data-start="3122" data-end="3155">\n<p data-start="3124" data-end="3155">Headlamp with extra batteries</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="irypc8" data-start="3156" data-end="3191">\n<p data-start="3158" data-end="3191">Water bottles or hydration system</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start="3193" data-end="3211"><strong data-start="3193" data-end="3211">Personal Items</strong></p>\n<ul data-start="3213" data-end="3327">\n<li data-section-id="8bg4ri" data-start="3213" data-end="3246">\n<p data-start="3215" data-end="3246">Sunglasses with UV protection</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="2one1c" data-start="3247" data-end="3273">\n<p data-start="3249" data-end="3273">Sunscreen and lip balm</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="6dl1ug" data-start="3274" data-end="3298">\n<p data-start="3276" data-end="3298">Personal medications</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="6b4xuc" data-start="3299" data-end="3327">\n<p data-start="3301" data-end="3327">Camera or phone for photos</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Upon arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport, our representative will welcome you and transfer you to your hotel in Kathmandu. After checking in, you can relax or explore the nearby streets of the city. Kathmandu is rich in culture, ancient temples, and vibrant markets. In the evening, your trekking guide will meet you for a detailed briefing about the Makalu Base Camp Trek and check your trekking equipment for the journey ahead.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1400m / 4593 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Today we take a scenic domestic flight from Kathmandu to Tumlingtar in eastern Nepal. During the flight you may enjoy views of hills and Himalayan peaks. After landing, we continue with a beautiful drive through rural villages, terraced fields, and forested hills toward Num. The village sits on a ridge overlooking the Arun River valley and serves as the starting point of the trekking journey.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Fly Kathmandu to Tumlingtar and Drive to Num (1560m / 5118 ft)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "The trek begins with a steep descent from Num toward the Arun River. After crossing a suspension bridge, the trail gradually climbs through forests and small villages until reaching Seduwa. This village lies within the Makalu Barun National Park area and offers a peaceful environment surrounded by green hills and farmland.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Trek Num to Seduwa (1500m / 4921 ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Today’s trek continues through beautiful forest trails and traditional villages. The path gradually climbs higher, offering scenic views of hills and farmland. After several hours of trekking through peaceful surroundings, we arrive at Tashigaon, the last major settlement before entering the higher alpine region of the Makalu area.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Trek Seduwa to Tashigaon (2100m / 6890 ft)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Today is a challenging day as the trail climbs steeply through dense forests and mountain terrain. As you gain altitude, the landscape becomes more alpine with beautiful views of surrounding peaks. After a long ascent, we reach Khongma Danda, a high ridge that provides impressive mountain scenery.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Trek Tashigaon to Khongma Danda (3500m / 11482 ft)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Today is an important rest and acclimatization day. You may take short hikes around the ridge to help your body adjust to the altitude while enjoying beautiful views of surrounding mountains. Proper acclimatization helps reduce the risk of altitude sickness during the higher sections of the trek.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Acclimatization Day at Khongma Danda (3500m / 11482 ft)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "The trail today crosses several high passes including Shipton La before descending through alpine landscapes toward Dobate. Along the route you may enjoy spectacular views of Himalayan peaks and rugged mountain terrain. After descending through rocky trails and forest areas, we arrive at Dobate for the night.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Trek Khongma Danda to Dobate (3650m / 11975 ft)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "Today the trail descends gradually through rhododendron forests and scenic valleys. The route follows the Barun River valley with beautiful views of surrounding mountains and waterfalls. After a pleasant day of trekking, we reach the open grazing fields of Yangri Kharka.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Trek Dobate to Yangri Kharka (3600m / 11811 ft)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "Today we continue along the Barun Valley as the scenery becomes more dramatic and alpine. The trail gradually climbs through open valleys surrounded by towering peaks and glaciers. After several hours of trekking through breathtaking Himalayan landscapes, we reach Langmale Kharka.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Trek Yangri Kharka to Langmale Kharka (4410m / 14469 ft)"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "Today we reach the highlight of the trek. The trail leads across wide glacial valleys toward Makalu Base Camp. From here you can enjoy spectacular views of Mount Makalu, the fifth-highest mountain in the world, along with other Himalayan peaks.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Trek Langmale Kharka to Makalu Base Camp (4870m / 15977 ft)"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "Today you can explore the surroundings of Makalu Base Camp. The area offers breathtaking views of Mount Makalu (8,485 m), glaciers, and dramatic mountain landscapes. It is a perfect opportunity for photography and enjoying the beauty of the Himalayas.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Exploration Day at Makalu Base Camp (4870m / 15977 ft)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "After enjoying the spectacular views at Makalu Base Camp, the journey begins back down the Barun Valley. The trail gradually descends through wide alpine landscapes with impressive views of surrounding peaks and glaciers. Walking downhill makes the trek more comfortable as you return toward greener valleys and yak grazing fields. By afternoon you will reach Yangri Kharka, where you will stay overnight in a peaceful mountain setting.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Trek Makalu Base Camp → Yangri Kharka (3600m / 11811 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "Today the trail continues through scenic valleys and rhododendron forests as you retrace your route toward Dobate. The path includes gentle climbs and descents while offering beautiful views of rivers, waterfalls, and surrounding hills. The peaceful environment and fresh mountain air make this section very enjoyable for trekkers returning from higher altitudes.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Trek Yangri Kharka → Dobate (3650m / 11975 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "The trail climbs back toward Khongma Danda, passing through beautiful alpine landscapes and high mountain ridges. Along the way you may again cross the scenic passes that connect the valleys of the Makalu region. The panoramic mountain views from the ridge make this day particularly rewarding.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Trek Dobate → Khongma Danda (3500m / 11482 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "15", "desc": "Today you descend from the high alpine zone into greener landscapes filled with forests and traditional villages. The trail leads through beautiful rhododendron and pine forests before reaching Tashigaon. This welcoming village offers a comfortable resting place after the long descent.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 15: Trek Khongma Danda → Tashigaon (2100m / 6890 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "16", "desc": "The trek continues through beautiful farmland, forest paths, and small villages. You will cross suspension bridges and follow the trail back toward the ridge-top village of Num. As the trek approaches its end, you can enjoy the peaceful rural scenery and friendly local communities along the way.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 16: Trek Tashigaon → Num (1560m / 5118 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "17", "desc": "Today you leave the trekking trail and travel by vehicle from Num to Tumlingtar through scenic hills and rural villages. After reaching the airport, you will take a short domestic flight back to Kathmandu. Upon arrival, transfer to your hotel and enjoy a relaxing evening in the city after completing the Makalu Base Camp adventure.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 17: Drive Num → Tumlingtar and Fly to Kathmandu (1400m / 4593 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "18", "desc": "Today marks the end of your Makalu Base Camp Trek adventure in Nepal. According to your international flight schedule, our team will transfer you from your hotel to Tribhuvan International Airport. You may spend the remaining time relaxing at the hotel or exploring nearby markets for last-minute souvenirs. We hope you leave Nepal with wonderful memories of the Himalayas, beautiful landscapes, and warm local hospitality.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 18: Final Departure from Kathmandu (1400m / 4593 ft)"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.877	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000ykbrllmba0dk9	lower-dolpo-phoksundo-lake-trek	Lower Dolpo & Phoksundo Lake Trek–16 Days	<h2>Explore the Remote Dolpo Region</h2>\nThe <strong>Lower Dolpo &amp; Phoksundo Lake Trek</strong> is a spectacular 16-day wilderness adventure throu	<h2>Explore the Remote Dolpo Region</h2>\nThe <strong>Lower Dolpo &amp; Phoksundo Lake Trek</strong> is a spectacular 16-day wilderness adventure through one of Nepal’s most remote and culturally fascinating regions. The journey takes you through untouched valleys, rugged mountain landscapes, traditional villages, and areas strongly influenced by Tibetan culture. Far from Nepal’s busier trekking routes, the region offers a peaceful experience surrounded by dramatic scenery and pristine nature.\n\nThe adventure begins in Kathmandu with a flight to Nepalgunj, followed by a flight to Juphal, the gateway to the Dolpo region. From here, the trail passes through traditional settlements, terraced fields, deep river valleys, and rugged mountain terrain. Along the way, you will encounter local communities whose customs and lifestyles have been preserved for generations.\n<h2>Journey Through the Himalayan Wilderness</h2>\nThe route passes through places such as Dunai, Tarakot, Laini, and Nawarpani before reaching higher and more remote landscapes. As the trail climbs, green valleys gradually give way to dramatic cliffs, rocky slopes, and high mountain scenery.\n\nA major highlight is <strong>Dho Tarap</strong>, one of Nepal’s highest permanent settlements. This remote Himalayan village provides an excellent opportunity to experience local culture while acclimatizing to the increasing altitude. Surrounded by impressive mountains and traditional homes, the settlement offers a fascinating glimpse into life in the Dolpo region.\n\nThe trail then crosses remote valleys and challenging mountain passes before continuing toward Numa La Base Camp and Pelung Tang. The changing landscapes, colorful rock formations, deep valleys, and panoramic Himalayan views make this section particularly rewarding for adventurous trekkers.\n<h2>Discover the Beauty of Phoksundo Lake</h2>\nThe spectacular <strong>Phoksundo Lake</strong> is the crown jewel of the journey. Famous for its brilliant turquoise waters, the lake is surrounded by dramatic cliffs, forests, and cascading waterfalls, creating one of Nepal’s most remarkable natural landscapes.\n\nReaching the lake provides a memorable opportunity to appreciate the peaceful beauty of the region and explore its surrounding trails. The area is also known for its unique cultural heritage, traditional villages, and connection to the ancient Bon and Tibetan Buddhist traditions.\n<h2>An Unforgettable Himalayan Adventure</h2>\nThis journey is ideal for experienced trekkers seeking solitude, cultural immersion, and extraordinary natural scenery. The combination of remote mountain trails, traditional communities, high-altitude landscapes, and the magnificent Phoksundo Lake creates an unforgettable Himalayan experience.\n\nWith its untouched wilderness and distinctive cultural character, the Dolpo region offers a rewarding alternative to Nepal’s more crowded trekking destinations. From remote villages and rugged passes to the turquoise waters of Phoksundo Lake, every stage of the adventure reveals a different side of Nepal’s spectacular western Himalayas.	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Upper-Dolpa.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	16 Days	2400	dolpo-region-trekking	Moderate		March–May &amp; September–November	Teahouses / Lodges along the route	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{dolpo-region-trekking}	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="al6r87" data-start="163" data-end="249">\n<p data-start="165" data-end="249">Explore the ancient walled city of Lo Manthang, the former kingdom of Mustang.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="usz0sk" data-start="250" data-end="314">\n<p data-start="252" data-end="314">Visit Tibetan Buddhist monasteries and the royal palace.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="jlxgap" data-start="315" data-end="391">\n<p data-start="317" data-end="391">Discover the sky caves of Chhoser, carved into cliffs centuries ago.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1lzy06x" data-start="392" data-end="475">\n<p data-start="394" data-end="475">Experience the unique desert landscapes and barren cliffs of Upper Mustang.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="ithahp" data-start="476" data-end="550">\n<p data-start="478" data-end="550">Interact with the local Tibetan-influenced culture and traditions.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1h8ehzu" data-start="551" data-end="640">\n<p data-start="553" data-end="640">Walk through remote villages like Kagbeni, Chele, Syangboche, Ghami, and Tsarang.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="orc0kh" data-start="641" data-end="729">\n<p data-start="643" data-end="729">Witness breathtaking high-altitude desert scenery and panoramic Himalayan views.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="l23420" data-start="730" data-end="792">\n<p data-start="732" data-end="792">Enjoy two nights of cultural immersion in Lo Manthang.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="ka6n9s" data-start="1155" data-end="1200">\n<p data-start="1157" data-end="1200">Airport pick-up and drop-off in Kathmandu</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="v1yrtp" data-start="1201" data-end="1277">\n<p data-start="1203" data-end="1277">All internal transportation (Kathmandu–Pokhara–Jomsom and return drives)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="evrin9" data-start="1278" data-end="1324">\n<p data-start="1280" data-end="1324">Lodge / teahouse accommodation during trek</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="4reren" data-start="1325" data-end="1358">\n<p data-start="1327" data-end="1358">All meals (B.L.D) during trek</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1q1eaf1" data-start="1359" data-end="1401">\n<p data-start="1361" data-end="1401">Experienced trekking guide and porters</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1i6jhv0" data-start="1402" data-end="1463">\n<p data-start="1404" data-end="1463">Trekking permits and Upper Mustang restricted area permit</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="ztvqzo" data-start="1464" data-end="1505">\n<p data-start="1466" data-end="1505">First aid kit and insurance for staff</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul data-start="1562" data-end="1768">\n<li data-section-id="1u00mml" data-start="1562" data-end="1601">\n<p data-start="1564" data-end="1601">International flights to/from Nepal</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1g03ghl" data-start="1602" data-end="1636">\n<p data-start="1604" data-end="1636">Meals in Kathmandu and Pokhara</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="oqc9g9" data-start="1637" data-end="1668">\n<p data-start="1639" data-end="1668">Personal trekking equipment</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="apccc2" data-start="1669" data-end="1712">\n<p data-start="1671" data-end="1712">Travel / medical insurance for trekkers</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1wm8q8b" data-start="1713" data-end="1768">\n<p data-start="1715" data-end="1768">Extra personal expenses (hot showers, drinks, tips)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="1xy921b" data-start="1849" data-end="1886">\n<p data-start="1851" data-end="1886">Daypack and duffel bag for porter</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="11kpn0j" data-start="1887" data-end="1927">\n<p data-start="1889" data-end="1927">Trekking boots and comfortable shoes</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1csvoxv" data-start="1928" data-end="1975">\n<p data-start="1930" data-end="1975">Warm clothing, down jacket, gloves, and hat</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="qh8m02" data-start="1976" data-end="2019">\n<p data-start="1978" data-end="2019">Sunglasses, sunscreen, and water bottle</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="nqv3b8" data-start="2020" data-end="2070">\n<p data-start="2022" data-end="2070">Sleeping bag (if preferred over lodge bedding)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="ej4cmv" data-start="2071" data-end="2116">\n<p data-start="2073" data-end="2116">Trekking poles (optional but recommended)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-section-id="1vag7xt" data-start="2117" data-end="2156">\n<p data-start="2119" data-end="2156">Personal medications and toiletries</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Upon arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport, you will be transferred to your hotel in Kathmandu. The rest of the day is free to relax or explore the city. In the evening, the trekking guide will meet you for a detailed briefing, including trek preparation, equipment check, and Nepal travel guidelines.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1,350 m / 4,429 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Today we take a short domestic flight from Kathmandu to Nepalgunj in western Nepal. Upon arrival, you will be transferred to your hotel. Nepalgunj is a gateway for western and far-western Nepal treks and provides a glimpse of Terai culture and plains life.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Kathmandu → Nepalgunj (150 m / 492 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Early morning, we fly from Nepalgunj to Jhupal. From Jhupal, the trek begins toward Dunai along forested trails and small villages. The path gradually climbs through hills and farmland before reaching the district headquarters of Dolpo. Overnight stay in a lodge or tea house in Dunai.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Nepalgunj → Jhupal → Dunai (2,850 m / 9,350 ft)\\";s:"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "The trail descends slightly from Dunai into the valley before gently ascending toward Tarakot. This day passes through forests, traditional villages, and terraced farmland. Tarakot is a small village providing overnight accommodation in tea houses.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Dunai → Tarakot (2,543 m / 8,343 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "The trail today climbs steadily through alpine valleys and mixed forest. Laini is a small Dolpo settlement with stone houses and guesthouses. Trekkers will enjoy the scenic views of the surrounding mountains and glimpse traditional Dolpo life along the trail.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Tarakot → Laini (3,160 m / 10,367 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "The trail ascends through alpine terrain with views of rugged hills and distant peaks. Nawar Pani is a small cluster of tea houses located near high pastures. The village is ideal for a night stop before entering higher alpine zones.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Laini → Nawar Pani (3,545 m / 11,627 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Today is a steep climb into the high Dolpo region. The trail passes through open alpine valleys and yak grazing areas. Dho Tarap is one of the largest Dolpo villages, featuring traditional stone houses and Buddhist monasteries. Overnight stay in local guesthouses.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Nawar Pani → Dho Tarap (4,090 m / 13,419 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "A full rest and acclimatization day in Dho Tarap. You may take short hikes around the village or visit local monasteries. Proper acclimatization today ensures a safe ascent to the Numa La Base Camp in the coming days.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Acclimatization Day at Dho Tarap (4,090 m / 13,419 ft)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "The trek continues through high alpine valleys toward Numa La Base Camp. You will experience rugged mountain landscapes, glacial moraines, and dramatic cliffside trails. Numa La Base Camp provides a perfect viewpoint of the surrounding peaks.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Dho Tarap → Numa La Base Camp (4,440 m / 14,567 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "The trail continues along glacial valleys and high ridges. Pelung Tang is a small campsite area near high pastures. Trekkers enjoy panoramic views of surrounding peaks and glaciers along this relatively short but steep trek.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Numa La Base Camp → Pelung Tang (4,465 m / 14,649 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "Today we descend slightly toward Dajok Tang, a remote campsite area surrounded by alpine scenery. The trail passes yak pastures, small streams, and rocky paths. Overnight stay in tents or local tea houses if available.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Pelung Tang → Dajok Tang (4,080 m / 13,386 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "The trail descends gradually into the picturesque Phoksundo Lake area. Ringmo village lies on the shore of the turquoise lake, surrounded by forests and cliffs. The village provides tea house accommodation and offers views of the lake, which is sacred in the local culture.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Dajok Tang → Ringmo / Phoksundo Lake (3,600 m / 11,811 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "A rest day to explore Phoksundo Lake and Ringmo village. Optional short hikes around the lake, village, and nearby cliffs. Enjoy photography and interaction with the local Dolpo culture.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Acclimatization Day at Phoksundo Lake (3,612 m / 11,847 ft)"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "The trail descends through forested valleys, cliffs, and terraced farmland. Shyanta is a small settlement offering overnight accommodation and the chance to experience rural Dolpo life.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Phoksundo Lake → Shyanta (2,520 m / 8,268 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "15", "desc": "The trail continues descending through scenic valleys, villages, and forests back to Jhupal. This village provides a comfortable resting place before the flight back to Nepalgunj.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 15: Shyanta → Jhupal (2,320 m / 7,612 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "16", "desc": "Morning flight from Jhupal to Nepalgunj, then connecting flight back to Kathmandu. Upon arrival, transfer to your hotel in Kathmandu. The rest of the day is free for relaxation or shopping in the capital city.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 16: Jhupal → Nepalgunj → Kathmandu (1,350 m / 4,429 ft)\\";s:"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.883	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u0010kbrlugv92zl8	upper-mustang-jeep-tour-12-days	Upper Mustang Jeep Tour – 12 Days Standard Itinerary	<p data-start="193" data-end="569">The Upper Mustang Jeep Tour is one of Nepal's most unique overland adventures. It takes travelers deep into the hid	<p data-start="193" data-end="569">The Upper Mustang Jeep Tour is one of Nepal's most unique overland adventures. It takes travelers deep into the hidden Himalayan kingdom of Mustang. Once an independent Tibetan kingdom, Upper Mustang has preserved its culture and traditions for centuries. Today, it is known for its ancient monasteries, cave settlements, medieval villages, and dramatic desert landscapes.</p>\n<p data-start="571" data-end="896">This 12-day journey begins in Kathmandu and continues to Pokhara. From there, travelers enter the Kali Gandaki Valley by private 4WD jeep. The route passes through Kagbeni, Chhusang, Samar, Ghami, Tsarang, and Lo Manthang. Along the way, visitors enjoy breathtaking Himalayan scenery and authentic Tibetan-influenced culture. The tour offers a unique opportunity to explore one of Nepal's most remote regions. Travelers can visit traditional villages, historic monasteries, and sacred Buddhist sites. Additionally, the route features spectacular cliffs, deep canyons, and colorful rock formations. These landscapes create a truly unforgettable travel experience.</p>\n<p data-start="1301" data-end="1625">Lo Manthang is the cultural heart of Upper Mustang. This historic walled city served as the capital of the former Kingdom of Mustang. Visitors can walk through narrow streets, explore ancient palaces, and observe local traditions. Furthermore, the city provides excellent insight into the region's rich history and heritage. The itinerary also includes an excursion to the famous Chhoser Cave area. These ancient caves were carved into cliffs centuries ago and remain one of Mustang's most fascinating attractions. Upper Mustang is deeply connected to Tibetan Buddhism. Throughout the journey, travelers encounter prayer flags, chortens, monasteries, and sacred sites. Moreover, local communities continue to practice traditions that have been preserved for generations.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="1tsmsob" data-start="2113" data-end="2155">Why Choose the Upper Mustang Jeep Tour?</h2>\n<p data-start="2157" data-end="2505">The Upper Mustang Jeep Tour is ideal for travelers who prefer comfort while exploring remote destinations. Unlike trekking, a jeep tour allows visitors to cover greater distances in less time. Finally, the return journey includes a visit to the sacred Muktinath Temple, making this adventure both culturally enriching and spiritually rewarding.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/ChatGPT-Image-Jun-5-2026-08_40_16-PM.png	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	12 Days	2800	mustang-region-trekking	Moderate		March-June/ Oct-Dec	Hotels &amp; Guesthouses/Lodges	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{mustang-region-trekking}	<ul>\n<li>Explore the ancient walled city of Lo Manthang</li>\n<li>Travel through Nepal's restricted Upper Mustang region</li>\n<li>Experience authentic Tibetan Buddhist culture</li>\n<li>Visit ancient monasteries, palaces, and cave settlements</li>\n<li>Explore Chhoser Cave and Jhong Cave area</li>\n<li>Drive through dramatic desert landscapes and colorful cliffs</li>\n<li>Visit the sacred Muktinath Temple</li>\n<li>Scenic journey through the Kali Gandaki Valley</li>\n<li>Comfortable travel by private 4WD jeep</li>\n<li>Beautiful mountain views of Nilgiri, Dhaulagiri, Annapurna, and Mustang Himal</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Airport pick-up and drop-off services</li>\n<li>Two nights hotel accommodation in Kathmandu with breakfast</li>\n<li>Two nights hotel accommodation in Pokhara with breakfast</li>\n<li>Private 4WD Jeep transportation throughout the tour</li>\n<li>Experienced English-speaking guide</li>\n<li>Upper Mustang Restricted Area Permit</li>\n<li>Annapurna Conservation Area Permit (ACAP)</li>\n<li>All required government taxes and service charges</li>\n<li>Accommodation in local lodges/guesthouses during the Mustang tour</li>\n<li>Driver salary, food, accommodation, fuel, and vehicle expenses</li>\n<li>First aid medical kit</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>International airfare</li>\n<li>Nepal entry visa fees</li>\n<li>Travel insurance</li>\n<li>Kathmandu and Pokhara sightseeing entrance fees</li>\n<li>Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu and Pokhara</li>\n<li>Domestic flights (Kathmandu–Pokhara–Kathmandu or Jomsom–Pokhara if chosen)</li>\n<li>Personal expenses such as drinks, laundry, internet, charging, and telephone calls</li>\n<li>Tips for guide and driver</li>\n<li>Additional accommodation due to weather delays, road blockages, or personal reasons</li>\n<li>Emergency rescue or medical expenses</li>\n<li>Any services not specifically mentioned in the Package Includes section</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Warm jacket, t-shirt, pants</li>\n<li>Trekking shoes and socks</li>\n<li>Sunglasses and sunscreen</li>\n<li>Day backpack and water bottle</li>\n<li>Personal medicines</li>\n<li>Power bank and phone</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Kathmandu Sightseeing and Permit Preparation"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Drive or Fly from Kathmandu to Pokhara"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Drive from Pokhara to Tatopani / Kalopani"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Drive from Tatopani / Kalopani to Kagbeni"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Drive from Kagbeni to Ghami / Tsarang"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Drive from Ghami / Tsarang to Lo Manthang"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Explore Lo Manthang and Chhoser Cave Area"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Drive from Lo Manthang to Muktinath / Jomsom"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Drive or Fly from Jomsom to Pokhara"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Drive or Fly from Pokhara to Kathmandu"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Final Departure from Kathmandu"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.891	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u0012kbrlq3pacxx4	everest-luxury-trek-helicopter-return	Everest Luxury Trek with Heli Return	<h2 data-section-id="31twoa" data-start="344" data-end="390"><strong>Experience the Ultimate Everest Luxury Trek</strong></h2>\n<p data-start="392" dat	<h2 data-section-id="31twoa" data-start="344" data-end="390"><strong>Experience the Ultimate Everest Luxury Trek</strong></h2>\n<p data-start="392" data-end="730">The Everest Luxury Trek with Helicopter Return is the perfect choice for travelers who want to experience the Everest region in comfort. It combines scenic trekking, luxury mountain lodges, and a breathtaking helicopter flight back to Kathmandu. As a result, you can enjoy the beauty of the Himalayas without retracing the same trail.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="1d8293t" data-start="732" data-end="778"><strong>A Scenic Journey Through the Everest Region</strong></h2>\n<p data-start="780" data-end="1193">Your adventure begins with a spectacular flight to Lukla. From there, you trek through the heart of Sagarmatha National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Along the way, you pass traditional Sherpa villages, ancient monasteries, colorful prayer flags, and suspension bridges. In addition, every day offers magnificent views of Mount Everest, Lhotse, Ama Dablam, Thamserku, and many other Himalayan peaks.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="grektz" data-start="1195" data-end="1237"><strong>Luxury Accommodation and Better Comfort</strong></h2>\n<p data-start="1239" data-end="1663">Unlike the standard Everest Base Camp Trek, this luxury trek includes the best available accommodation along the route. Whenever possible, you stay in comfortable mountain lodges with private rooms and modern facilities. Moreover, you enjoy warm hospitality, delicious meals, and personalized service throughout the journey. The itinerary also includes proper acclimatization days, making your trek safer and more enjoyable.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="kgbex4" data-start="1665" data-end="1698"><strong>Helicopter Return from Everest</strong></h2>\n<p data-start="1700" data-end="2125">One of the highlights of this adventure is the scenic helicopter flight back from Gorak Shep after visiting Kala Patthar. Instead of trekking back to Lukla, you fly over glaciers, deep valleys, and snow-covered Himalayan peaks. Consequently, you save several days of walking while enjoying spectacular aerial views of the Everest region. This unforgettable flight adds a unique and luxurious finish to your adventure.</p>\n\n<h2><strong>Why Choose the Everest Luxury Trek with Helicopter Return?</strong></h2>\nWhether you are celebrating a special occasion, planning a honeymoon, or simply seeking a premium Himalayan adventure, this trek is an excellent choice. It offers the perfect balance of adventure, comfort, culture, and breathtaking scenery. Furthermore, our experienced guides, carefully selected accommodations, and professional service ensure a smooth and memorable experience from start to finish.	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/everest-luxury.png	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	12 Days	2899	everest	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Dec	4 Star Hotel/ Tea house	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{everest-region}	<ul>\n<li>Experience a premium Everest trekking adventure with luxury lodges and personalized service</li>\n<li>Enjoy a thrilling helicopter flight from the Everest region back to Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Witness spectacular views of Mount Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Ama Dablam, Thamserku, and other Himalayan giants</li>\n<li>Trek through the legendary Sherpa villages of Lukla, Phakding, Namche Bazaar, Tengboche, Dingboche, and Lobuche</li>\n<li>Visit the famous Tengboche Monastery, the spiritual heart of the Khumbu region</li>\n<li>Reach Everest Base Camp (5,364m), the world's most iconic trekking destination</li>\n<li>Hike to Kala Patthar (5,545m) for the best sunrise and panoramic views of Mount Everest</li>\n<li>Explore the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Sagarmatha National Park, home to diverse wildlife and alpine landscapes</li>\n<li>Cross exciting suspension bridges, walk beneath colorful prayer flags, and admire ancient mani walls and monasteries</li>\n<li>Enjoy comfortable mountain accommodations, delicious meals, and warm Sherpa hospitality throughout the journey</li>\n<li>Save several days of trekking with a scenic helicopter return while enjoying breathtaking aerial views of glaciers, valleys, and snow-capped peaks</li>\n<li>Experience the perfect combination of adventure, luxury, culture, and unforgettable Himalayan scenery</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Airport pick-up and drop-off by private tourist vehicle</li>\n<li>2 nights' accommodation in a <strong>4-star hotel in Kathmandu</strong> with breakfast (before and after the trek)</li>\n<li>Round-trip domestic flights between Kathmandu, Lukla  and  Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Scenic helicopter flight from the Everest region back to Lukla</li>\n<li>Accommodation in the best available luxury lodges and comfortable teahouses during the trek</li>\n<li>Three meals a day (breakfast, lunch, and dinner) during the trekking period</li>\n<li>Experienced, government-licensed English-speaking trekking guide</li>\n<li>Porter service (1 porter for every 2 trekkers, carrying up to 20 kg)</li>\n<li>Sagarmatha National Park Entry Permit</li>\n<li>Khumbu Pasang Lhamu Rural Municipality Entrance Permit</li>\n<li>All guide and porter salaries, insurance, meals, accommodation, and equipment</li>\n<li>Comprehensive first aid kit carried by the guide</li>\n<li>Sleeping bag and down jacket (available on request, to be returned after the trek)</li>\n<li>All government taxes and official service charges</li>\n<li>Farewell dinner at a traditional Nepali restaurant in Kathmandu</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>International airfare to and from Nepal</li>\n<li>Nepal entry visa fees</li>\n<li>Travel and rescue insurance (mandatory)</li>\n<li>Personal trekking equipment and clothing</li>\n<li>Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Hot and cold beverages, bottled water, alcoholic drinks, and personal snacks</li>\n<li>Personal expenses such as laundry, telephone, Wi-Fi, battery charging, and hot showers where applicable</li>\n<li>Tips for trekking guides, porters, and  crew (highly appreciated)</li>\n<li>Personal medical expenses and emergency evacuation costs if not covered by insurance</li>\n<li>Extra accommodation and meals due to flight delays, weather conditions, natural disasters, or unforeseen circumstances</li>\n<li>Costs arising from itinerary changes beyond the company's control</li>\n<li>Any services not specifically mentioned in the "Package Includes" section</li>\n</ul>\n	<h3>Clothing</h3>\n<ul data-spread="false">\n<li>Moisture-wicking base layers (top and bottom)</li>\n<li>Fleece or insulated mid-layer jacket</li>\n<li>Waterproof and windproof outer jacket</li>\n<li>Waterproof trekking pants</li>\n<li>Lightweight trekking pants and T-shirts</li>\n<li>Warm down jacket</li>\n<li>Thermal underwear</li>\n<li>Comfortable underwear and extra socks</li>\n<li>Warm hat, sun hat, and neck gaiter or buff</li>\n<li>Waterproof gloves and warm inner gloves</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Footwear</h3>\n<ul data-spread="false">\n<li>Waterproof trekking boots with good ankle support</li>\n<li>Lightweight camp shoes or sandals</li>\n<li>Gaiters (optional, depending on the season)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Trekking Gear</h3>\n<ul data-spread="false">\n<li>Daypack (25–35L) with rain cover</li>\n<li>Duffel bag (provided or personal)</li>\n<li>Trekking poles</li>\n<li>Sleeping bag (rated to at least -10°C, available on request)</li>\n<li>Headlamp with extra batteries</li>\n<li>Reusable water bottles or hydration bladder (2–3 liters)</li>\n<li>Water purification tablets or filter</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Personal Items</h3>\n<ul data-spread="false">\n<li>Sunglasses with UV protection</li>\n<li>Sunscreen (SPF 50+) and lip balm</li>\n<li>Quick-dry towel</li>\n<li>Toiletries and personal hygiene items</li>\n<li>Wet wipes and hand sanitizer</li>\n<li>Camera or smartphone with charger and power bank</li>\n<li>Passport, permits, passport-size photos, and travel insurance copy</li>\n<li>Cash for personal expenses and tips</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>First Aid &amp; Medication</h3>\n<ul data-spread="false">\n<li>Personal prescription medications</li>\n<li>Basic first aid kit</li>\n<li>Blister treatment</li>\n<li>Pain relief medication</li>\n<li>Diamox (Acetazolamide) for altitude sickness (consult your doctor before use)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Optional Items</h3>\n<ul data-spread="false">\n<li>Binoculars</li>\n<li>Energy bars or snacks</li>\n<li>Travel pillow</li>\n<li>Notebook and pen</li>\n<li>Lightweight crampons or microspikes (recommended during</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Welcome to Nepal. Upon your arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport in Kathmandu, our representative will warmly greet you and transfer you to your hotel. After check-in, you can take some time to rest and recover from your journey.\\n\\nKathmandu is a vibrant city rich in culture, history, and tradition. Depending on your arrival time, you may explore the nearby streets, local markets, and experience the unique atmosphere of Nepal’s capital. In the evening, you will attend a trek briefing where your guide will provide important information about the Everest Base Camp Trek, check your equipment, and answer any questions.\\n\\nThis day is mainly for preparation and relaxation before your Himalayan adventure begins. Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\\";s:23", "elev": 0, "title": "Day1: Arrived in Kathmandu(1350m/4412ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Early in the morning, we take a scenic 30-minute flight to Lukla, the gateway to the Everest region. Upon arrival, we meet our porter and begin our trek, descending to Chaurikharka and further to Thadokoshi, where you may enjoy views of the surrounding mountains. We then ascend uphill to Ghat, passing a ridge marked with painted mani stones, and after roughly an hour of trekking, reach Phakding, where we stay overnight in a cozy tea house, resting for the next stage of our journey.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: flight  to lukla &amp; trek to Padking( 4h /2610m/8695ft)\\""}, {"day": "3", "desc": "After breakfast, we begin our scenic trek following the beautiful Dudh Koshi River, enjoying the refreshing mountain air as the trail winds through pine and rhododendron forests. The sound of the rushing river accompanies us as we cross several thrilling suspension bridges decorated with colorful prayer flags and pass through small traditional Sherpa villages with stone houses, prayer wheels, and mani walls. Soon we reach Monjo, the entrance to Sagarmatha National Park, where our permits are checked before we officially enter this UNESCO World Heritage Site. The path continues with gentle ups and downs through forested terrain until we arrive at Jorsalle, the last village before Namche Bazaar, where we can take a short rest or enjoy tea while preparing for the climb ahead. From Jorsalle, the trail follows the river to the dramatic high suspension bridge at the confluence of the Dudh Koshi and Bhote Koshi rivers; standing on this bridge is an unforgettable experience, and on a clear day we may catch our first breathtaking glimpse of Mount Everest, along with surrounding Himalayan giants, a magical moment that fills us with excitement. After crossing the bridge, the trail begins a long and steady uphill ascent through dense pine forest, requiring a slow and steady pace as we gain significant altitude; along the way, the views gradually open up, revealing spectacular mountain scenery behind us. After approximately 5–6 hours of trekking, we finally reach Namche Bazaar (3,440 m), the largest Sherpa settlement and vibrant commercial hub of the Khumbu region, beautifully set in a natural amphitheater surrounded by towering peaks. Namche offers a surprising range of facilities including good restaurants, bakeries, trekking gear shops, internet cafés, ATMs, and money exchange services. In the evening, we relax and explore the lively market area before enjoying a warm meal and an overnight stay at a comfortable tea house.\\";s", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3:Phakding to Namche Bazar(7h/3450m/11290ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Today, although we remain in Namche Bazaar due to the high altitude, it is not a full rest day. After breakfast, we trek to a nearby viewpoint to enjoy breathtaking panoramic views of the surrounding mountains, including Mount Everest. We then hike up to Syangboche, home to the highest airport in the region, and visit the Everest View Hotel for some stunning vistas. After spending time here, we descend back to Namche for an overnight stay in a cozy tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4:Acclimatization day in Namche Bazaar"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "After breakfast, we begin the day with a gradual climb to Namche Top, following a trail that takes us to Kanjima via Nepali Flat. Along the way, we are treated to spectacular views of Mount Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Thamserku, Ama Dablam, and many other smaller peaks. After passing this charming Sherpa village, we descend to the Dudh Koshi River and then undertake a famous ascent through rhododendron forests to Tengboche. Upon reaching Tengboche, we visit the largest monastery in the region and soak in the breathtaking mountain views. Overnight stay is at a tea house.\\n\\nI can continue polishing your remaining trek days in the same single-paragraph, professional style, so your\\n\\";s", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5:Namche to Deboche(5:30h/3860m/12960ft)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "After breakfast, we continue trekking through pine forests, descending toward Debuche, crossing a suspension bridge before climbing past many mani stones and small stupas. We pass through a picturesque village with fields of buckwheat, potatoes, and vegetables, then continue toward Imja Village and Lobuche Khola before ascending to Dingboche. Upon arrival, we enjoy spectacular views of Ama Dablam, Lhotse, and many other surrounding peaks. Overnight stay is at a tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6:Tengboche to Dingboche(6h/4360m/14300ft)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Today is a crucial acclimatization day to help our bodies adjust to the high altitude. After a hearty breakfast, we embark on a rewarding short hike toward Nagarjun Hill, where we are treated to awe-inspiring panoramic views of some of the most iconic Himalayan peaks, including Ama Dablam, Makalu, Lhotse, Tawache, Cholatse, and numerous other majestic peaks that punctuate the skyline. The crisp mountain air, sweeping vistas, and serene landscapes make this hike an unforgettable experience, offering countless photo opportunities and moments of reflection. After soaking in these magnificent Himalayan panoramas, we gently descend back to Dingboche, where we enjoy a leisurely lunch and rest, letting our bodies recover and prepare for the adventures ahead. Overnight stay is at the same charming tea house, surrounded by the serene beauty of the mountains.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Acclimatization day in Dingboche"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "After breakfast, we continue our trek along the rocky lateral moraine of the Khumbu Glacier, walking on a rugged trail with dramatic views of the surrounding Himalayan peaks. Along the way, we pass the memorial site at Thukla, where stone monuments stand in honor of climbers who lost their lives while attempting nearby summits — a quiet and emotional place that invites reflection. From here, the trail climbs steadily uphill for some time before leveling out as we follow the glacial valley toward Lobuche. Surrounded by towering mountains and vast alpine landscapes, we finally reach Lobuche (4,910 m), a small settlement with a few tea houses serving trekkers and climbers on the Everest Base Camp route. Overnight stay at a tea house.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Dingboche to Lobuche(5h/4900m/16000ft)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "Finally the most Awaiting day of hour whole trip as we climb to Everest Base Camp is Today. This is a big & difficult day walk along the Khumbu glacier up to base camp. Early morning breakfast then we start our journey towards Gorakshep. The trail gradually & Rockey all the way, once we reach in Gorakshep we chick into the hotel and have some rest, we continue up the edge of the Khumbu glacier until we finally reach base camp. if you are lucky & timing is right you may see expedition team. after spending some time to enjoying, we back way down to gorakshep.over night at tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9:Lobuche to Everest base camp(5360m/17450ft)Back to Gorak shep(5180m/16960ft)"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "Today, we hike to Kala Patthar, the highest point of the Everest Base Camp Trek. We start early in the morning to enjoy a spectacular sunrise over the majestic Himalayan peaks. From Kala Patthar, you can admire breathtaking views of Mount Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Pumori, and the surrounding mountains. After enjoying the panoramic views, we descend to Gorak Shep for breakfast. From there, we take a shared helicopter flight to Lukla. Please note that the helicopter flight is shared, not a private charter. If you prefer a private helicopter flight, please contact us for the additional cost.\\n\\nDue to aviation limitations at high altitudes above 4,500 meters, helicopters can land at Gorak Shep but can take off with a maximum of three passengers at a time. If there are more than three passengers, the helicopter will first take three passengers from Gorak Shep and drop them at a designated location below 4,500 meters, usually Pheriche. The helicopter will then return to Gorak Shep to pick up the remaining passengers. After collecting the first group from the designated location, it will continue to Lukla with everyone together. The helicopter flight from Gorak Shep to Lukla takes approximately 15–20 minutes, depending on weather conditions and the number of passengers.\\";s:", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Morning Hike to Kala Patthar, Descent to Gorak Shep &amp; Shared Helicopter Flight to Lukla"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "Lukla to Manthali Flight (March, April, May, September, October & November)\\n\\nDuring the peak trekking seasons, flights from Lukla usually operate to Manthali (Ramechhap) Airport. The flight takes approximately 20 minutes, followed by a 5–6 hour drive to Kathmandu. Driving time may vary depending on road and traffic conditions. Upon arrival in Kathmandu, you will be transferred to your hotel by a shared tourist vehicle.\\n\\nLukla to Kathmandu Flight (January, February, June, July, August & December)\\n\\nDuring the remaining months, flights generally operate directly from Lukla to Kathmandu and take approximately 35 minutes. After landing in Kathmandu, you will be transferred to your hotel by a shared tourist vehicle. Please note that flight schedules and destinations are determined by the airlines and aviation authorities and may change depending on weather conditions and seasonal air traffic.\\n\\n🚁 Helicopter Upgrade (Optional)\\n\\nFor added comfort and convenience, you can upgrade to a direct shared helicopter flight from Lukla to Kathmandu for an additional USD 450 per person (based on a minimum of 5 passengers sharing). This is the best option to avoid the long drive from Manthali to Kathmandu during the peak trekking seasons (March, April, May, September, October, and November).\\n\\nIf you have extra time in Nepal, we also offer exciting tours to Pokhara, Chitwan National Park, Kathmandu Valley, and many other destinations. We also organize outbound tours to Tibet, India, and Bhutan. In the evening, enjoy a farewell dinner at a traditional Nepali restaurant to celebrate the successful completion of your Everest adventure.\\";s:23:\\"day_wise", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Flight from Lukla to Kathmandu or Manthali (Ramechhap) and Transfer to Kathmandu"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "Your unforgettable Everest Base Camp Trek with Helicopter Return comes to an end today. After breakfast, one of our airport representatives will transfer you to Tribhuvan International Airport for your onward flight.\\n\\nWe sincerely thank you for choosing Ever Peak Adventures and hope you leave Nepal with unforgettable memories. We look forward to welcoming you back for another Himalayan adventure in the future.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Transfer to the International Airport for Your Final Departure"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.896	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u0013kbrlx1ph9ibw	everest-base-camp-with-island-peak-climb	Everest Base Camp with Island Peak	<div>\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:567b6668-eb95-4592-8bae-a6b0fe483c19-0" data-is-intersecting="true"><section dir="auto" data-turn-id="r	<div>\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:567b6668-eb95-4592-8bae-a6b0fe483c19-0" data-is-intersecting="true"><section dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:567b6668-eb95-4592-8bae-a6b0fe483c19-0" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:567b6668-eb95-4592-8bae-a6b0fe483c19-0" data-testid="conversation-turn-2" data-turn="assistant">\n<div>\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div>\n<div dir="auto" tabindex="0" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="660ea219-771e-4864-b8f1-fabcdc6479f3" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-6" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div>\n<div>\n<div data-writing-block-fullscreen-fallback-target="inline">\n<div data-oai-writing-block-surface="" data-writing-block="true" data-testid="writing-block-container">\n<div data-writing-block-fullscreen-shell-border="true" aria-hidden="true">\n<div>\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:567b6668-eb95-4592-8bae-a6b0fe483c19-0" data-is-intersecting="true"><section dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:567b6668-eb95-4592-8bae-a6b0fe483c19-0" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:567b6668-eb95-4592-8bae-a6b0fe483c19-0" data-testid="conversation-turn-2" data-turn="assistant">\n<div>\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div>\n<div dir="auto" tabindex="0" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="660ea219-771e-4864-b8f1-fabcdc6479f3" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-6" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div>\n<div>\n<div data-writing-block-fullscreen-fallback-target="inline">\n<div data-oai-writing-block-surface="" data-writing-block="true" data-testid="writing-block-container">\n<div data-writing-block-fullscreen-shell-border="true" aria-hidden="true">\n<h2><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=c26270ef90080d49&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnuK4w3GM4SQDLoqyaBqkfTBcVbVLA:1787384299475&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gIHbHEqXWbyThyPdUCKqTmZAKzBcRFb2qe3OBMfh6G5URtuzGpQgwyLjG0HlVfwOhBKT-_MjHW6JAI50fK8ctSDBzYN4QFmM5h2f-J2LGaBBmSbliULKp1HwnGA8zByXKCw81aKc7LO2xjbgBVfvicOu9VOvA&amp;q=everest&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwj7oPyx3bOWAxXYjOEIHYJ-FR4QtKgLegQIIxAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Everest</a> Base Camp with Island Peak Adventure</h2>\nThe <strong><a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/everest-luxury-trek-helicopter-return/">Everest Base Camp</a> with Island Peak</strong> adventure combines the iconic Everest Base Camp trek with the exciting challenge of climbing Island Peak (6,189 m/20,305 ft). This unforgettable Himalayan journey takes you through the beautiful Khumbu Valley, offering breathtaking mountain views, authentic Sherpa culture, ancient monasteries, and traditional mountain villages surrounded by some of the world’s highest peaks.\n\nYour adventure begins with a scenic flight to Lukla, followed by a classic trek through Phakding, Namche Bazaar, Tengboche, Dingboche, and Lobuche toward Everest Base Camp. Carefully planned acclimatization stops help your body adjust to the increasing altitude while you enjoy spectacular views of <strong>Mount Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Ama Dablam, Thamserku, and Kongde</strong>.\n\nAfter reaching <strong>Everest Base Camp</strong>, the journey continues to <strong>Kala Patthar (5,545 m)</strong>, one of the best viewpoints in the region for sunrise and panoramic views of Mount Everest and the surrounding Himalayan peaks. The trek then heads toward Island Peak, where you will receive professional guidance and practical training in essential mountaineering skills before attempting the summit.\n<h3>Island Peak Climbing and Summit Experience</h3>\nThe <strong>Everest Island Peak</strong> journey includes adequate acclimatization and preparation for the Island Peak summit. You will learn essential climbing techniques and use mountaineering equipment such as crampons, harnesses, ropes, and an ice axe under the guidance of experienced climbing professionals.\n\nReaching the summit of <strong>Island Peak (6,189 m)</strong> is a rewarding achievement, with spectacular views of Mount Everest, Lhotse, Nuptse, Ama Dablam, Makalu, and Baruntse. Standing above the Khumbu Valley and surrounded by towering Himalayan peaks makes the summit experience an unforgettable highlight for adventurous trekkers and aspiring mountaineers.\n\nWith an experienced local trekking and climbing team, carefully planned acclimatization, quality equipment, and personalized support, this trek is designed to provide a safe, professional, and memorable Himalayan adventure. It is an ideal choice for physically fit trekkers who want to experience the legendary Everest Base Camp trek while taking on the rewarding challenge of climbing a high-altitude Himalayan peak.\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:567b6668-eb95-4592-8bae-a6b0fe483c19-0" data-is-intersecting="true"><section dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:567b6668-eb95-4592-8bae-a6b0fe483c19-0" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:567b6668-eb95-4592-8bae-a6b0fe483c19-0" data-testid="conversation-turn-2" data-turn="assistant">\n<div>\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div>\n<div dir="auto" tabindex="0" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="660ea219-771e-4864-b8f1-fabcdc6479f3" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-6" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div>\n<div>\n<div data-writing-block-fullscreen-fallback-target="inline">\n<div data-oai-writing-block-surface="" data-writing-block="true" data-testid="writing-block-container">\n<div>\n<div></div>\n</div>\n<div data-writing-block-fullscreen-shell-border="true" aria-hidden="true"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section></div>\n</div>\n<div aria-hidden="true"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section></div>\n</div>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/ChatGPT-Image-Jul-31-2026-09_33_21-PM.png	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	19 days	2975	everest	Moderate		March/May  , Sep/Nov	Hotel, Teahouse, Camping	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{everest-region}	<div class="qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot">\n<div class="" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:74fd0317-29a5-4b14-a405-f6bf213ab47b-0" data-is-intersecting="true">\n<section class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:74fd0317-29a5-4b14-a405-f6bf213ab47b-0" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:74fd0317-29a5-4b14-a405-f6bf213ab47b-0" data-testid="conversation-turn-2" data-turn="assistant">\n<div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-8 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)">\n<div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow">\n<div class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" dir="auto" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="4edc24ec-758a-4920-b823-b7748f1d8d09" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden">\n<div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling">\n<ul data-start="128" data-end="1292" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">\n<li data-section-id="1cggj5h" data-start="128" data-end="207">Summit <strong data-start="137" data-end="162">Island Peak (6,189 m)</strong>, one of Nepal's most popular trekking peaks.</li>\n<li data-section-id="lirka7" data-start="208" data-end="264">Trek to the legendary <strong data-start="232" data-end="263">Everest Base Camp (5,364 m)</strong>.</li>\n<li data-section-id="6kwii9" data-start="265" data-end="359">Witness a breathtaking sunrise from <strong data-start="303" data-end="329">Kala Patthar (5,545 m)</strong> with panoramic Everest views.</li>\n<li data-section-id="7rms84" data-start="360" data-end="455">Experience the thrill of glacier travel and basic mountaineering with expert climbing guides.</li>\n<li data-section-id="13138gr" data-start="456" data-end="520">Enjoy scenic mountain flights between <strong data-start="496" data-end="519">Kathmandu and Lukla</strong>.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1kdwc5f" data-start="521" data-end="579">Explore the vibrant Sherpa capital of <strong data-start="561" data-end="578">Namche Bazaar</strong>.</li>\n<li data-section-id="19tkcoc" data-start="580" data-end="658">Visit the famous <strong data-start="599" data-end="622">Tengboche Monastery</strong>, the spiritual heart of the Khumbu.</li>\n<li data-section-id="rloeeh" data-start="659" data-end="749">Walk through the spectacular <strong data-start="690" data-end="718">Sagarmatha National Park</strong>, a UNESCO World Heritage Site.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1wwu6q2" data-start="750" data-end="851">Cross iconic Himalayan suspension bridges and trek through beautiful rhododendron and pine forests.</li>\n<li data-section-id="b0u6jx" data-start="852" data-end="1111">Admire magnificent views of **<span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Mount Everest</span></span>, <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Lhotse</span></span>, <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Nuptse</span></span>, <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Ama Dablam</span></span>, <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Makalu</span></span>, and many other Himalayan giants.</li>\n<li data-section-id="p2k8tf" data-start="1112" data-end="1191">Stay in authentic Sherpa teahouses and experience warm Himalayan hospitality.</li>\n<li data-section-id="18dfsu8" data-start="1192" data-end="1292" data-is-last-node="">Celebrate your successful <strong data-start="1220" data-end="1242">Island Peak summit</strong> with unforgettable views over the Everest region.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"></div>\n</div>\n<div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1" data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="pointer-events-none -mt-px h-px translate-y-(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom)" aria-hidden="true"></div>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="1w0xhiq" data-start="19" data-end="69">Airport pick-up and drop-off by private vehicle.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1imqj9i" data-start="70" data-end="129">2 nights hotel accommodation in Kathmandu with breakfast.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1nza2mu" data-start="130" data-end="191">Round-trip domestic flights: Kathmandu – Lukla – Kathmandu.</li>\n<li data-section-id="kh6dfm" data-start="192" data-end="237">All airport transfers for domestic flights.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1p79eo3" data-start="238" data-end="288">Standard teahouse accommodation during the trek.</li>\n<li data-section-id="cyl1lu" data-start="289" data-end="356">Three meals a day (breakfast, lunch, and dinner) during the trek.</li>\n<li data-section-id="qpe0sn" data-start="357" data-end="410">Seasonal fresh fruits after dinner during the trek.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1jaj531" data-start="411" data-end="478">Experienced, government-licensed English-speaking trekking guide.</li>\n<li data-section-id="rkvyak" data-start="479" data-end="536">Professional Island Peak climbing guide (Summit Guide).</li>\n<li data-section-id="agdyy6" data-start="537" data-end="607">Porter service (1 porter for every 2 trekkers; carries up to 20 kg).</li>\n<li data-section-id="17xxlcq" data-start="608" data-end="638">Island Peak climbing permit.</li>\n<li data-section-id="9w0tqw" data-start="639" data-end="692"><span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Sagarmatha National Park</span></span> entry permit.</li>\n<li data-section-id="ksjr16" data-start="693" data-end="750">Khumbu Pasang Lhamu Rural Municipality entrance permit.</li>\n<li data-section-id="uoz9mr" data-start="751" data-end="800">TIMS card (if required by current regulations).</li>\n<li data-section-id="1xrkv0t" data-start="801" data-end="871">Group climbing equipment (fixed ropes, ice screws, snow bars, etc.).</li>\n<li data-section-id="w6mnpa" data-start="872" data-end="1000">Climbing gear support (rope, harness, helmet, crampons, ice axe, ascender, descender, carabiners) if included in your package.</li>\n<li data-section-id="2dab5b" data-start="1001" data-end="1063">One night accommodation at Island Peak Base Camp with meals.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1ny1le5" data-start="1064" data-end="1153">Sleeping tent, dining tent, kitchen tent, mattress, and camping equipment at Base Camp.</li>\n<li data-section-id="16unycn" data-start="1154" data-end="1209">Experienced cook and kitchen staff for the Base Camp.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1a61yt9" data-start="1210" data-end="1259">Boiled drinking water at Island Peak Base Camp.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1w5gaoo" data-start="1260" data-end="1311">Comprehensive first aid kit carried by the guide.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1xmqkc3" data-start="1312" data-end="1417">Guide, climbing guide, porter, and staff salaries, insurance, meals, accommodation, and transportation.</li>\n<li data-section-id="rs8e9c" data-start="1418" data-end="1465">Government taxes and company service charges.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1jip3c" data-start="1466" data-end="1541" data-is-last-node=""></li>\n</ul>\n	<div class="qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot">\n<div class="" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:74fd0317-29a5-4b14-a405-f6bf213ab47b-2" data-is-intersecting="true">\n<section class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:74fd0317-29a5-4b14-a405-f6bf213ab47b-2" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:74fd0317-29a5-4b14-a405-f6bf213ab47b-2" data-testid="conversation-turn-6" data-turn="assistant">\n<div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-8 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)">\n<div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow">\n<div class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" dir="auto" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="07a4b5a7-3245-4261-ae0c-bcc42b275cb4" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden">\n<div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling">\n<ul data-start="22" data-end="1090" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">\n<li data-section-id="jfvbaa" data-start="22" data-end="60">International airfare to/from Nepal.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1o2ewr3" data-start="61" data-end="84">Nepal entry visa fee.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1u5ag7x" data-start="85" data-end="141">Travel and high-altitude rescue insurance (mandatory).</li>\n<li data-section-id="129s1vm" data-start="142" data-end="319">Personal climbing equipment rental (boots, down jacket, sleeping bag, crampons, ice axe, harness, helmet, ascender, descender, trekking poles, etc.) unless stated as included.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1x03vwb" data-start="320" data-end="358">Personal trekking gear and clothing.</li>\n<li data-section-id="8dqayx" data-start="359" data-end="391">Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu.</li>\n<li data-section-id="xucc2y" data-start="392" data-end="487">Personal expenses (laundry, Wi-Fi, hot shower, charging devices, snacks, drinks, tips, etc.).</li>\n<li data-section-id="ltk7ft" data-start="488" data-end="559">Bottled water, soft drinks, alcoholic beverages, and extra beverages.</li>\n<li data-section-id="6vpnnn" data-start="560" data-end="625">Porter for personal extra luggage beyond the package allowance.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mgosxn" data-start="626" data-end="714">Emergency evacuation, helicopter rescue, or medical expenses not covered by insurance.</li>\n<li data-section-id="f7zhzo" data-start="715" data-end="818">Extra hotel nights in Kathmandu due to early arrival, late departure, or flight delays/cancellations.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1wfns5n" data-start="819" data-end="932">Costs arising from itinerary changes caused by weather, natural disasters, strikes, or other unforeseen events.</li>\n<li data-section-id="bcc4x7" data-start="933" data-end="1020">Tips for guides, climbing guides, porters, and support staff (expected but optional).</li>\n<li data-section-id="1q7v48l" data-start="1021" data-end="1090" data-is-last-node="">Any services not specifically mentioned under <strong data-start="1069" data-end="1089">Package Includes</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"></div>\n</div>\n<div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1" data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="pointer-events-none -mt-px h-px translate-y-(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom)" aria-hidden="true"></div>\n	<ul>\n<li><b data-path-to-node="1,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">Peak Season Flight Note:</b> <span class="citation-31 citation-end-31">During high season (March–May &amp; October–November), fixed-wing flights to Lukla operate out of Manthali Airport in Ramechhap.</span> <span class="citation-30 citation-end-30">If flying during these months, you will leave Kathmandu by road around 1:30 AM (a 4–5 hour drive) to catch an early morning flight from Ramechhap to Lukla.</span> <span class="citation-29 citation-end-29">Outside peak months, flights depart directly from Kathmandu.</span></li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Welcome to Nepal! Upon arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport, our representative will warmly welcome you and transfer you to your hotel in Kathmandu. After check-in, you can relax or explore the vibrant streets of Thamel, famous for its trekking shops, restaurants, and cultural atmosphere.\\n\\nIn the evening, you will meet your trekking and climbing guide for a detailed briefing about the Everest Base Camp with Island Peak Climbing adventure. Equipment will be checked, permits verified, and final preparations completed to ensure you are fully ready for the expedition.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1,400 m / 4,593 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "An early morning scenic flight takes you to Lukla, offering breathtaking aerial views of the Himalayan range. After meeting the porters and organizing trekking gear, the journey begins with a gentle descent through beautiful Sherpa villages, prayer wheels, suspension bridges, and pine forests.\\n\\nFollowing the Dudh Koshi River, you reach the peaceful village of Phakding, where you can relax and enjoy your first night in the Everest region.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Fly to Lukla (2,840 m / 9,317 ft) &amp; Trek to Phakding (2,610 m / 8,562 ft)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Walk through pine forests and cross high suspension bridges spanning the Dudh Koshi River, including the famous Hillary Suspension Bridge. Enter Sagarmatha National Park at Monjo. Take on a steady, steep uphill climb that rewards you with your first views of Mt. Everest before reaching the vibrant hub of Namche Bazaar.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Trek from Phakding to Namche Bazaar (3,440 m / 11,286 ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Essential rest day to adapt to the higher altitude. Take an acclimatization hike up to the Everest View Hotel (3,880 m / 12,729 ft) for panoramic vistas of Mt. Everest, Ama Dablam, Lhotse, and Thamserku. Afterwards, explore the Sherpa Culture Museum or stroll through the local cafes and shops in town.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Acclimatization Day in Namche Bazaar (3,440 m / 11,286 ft)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Follow a trail with panoramic views of the Everest range before descending to Phunki Tenga near the river for lunch. The afternoon involves a climb through rhododendron and pine forests up to Tengboche, home to the largest Buddhist monastery in the Khumbu region.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Trek from Namche Bazaar to Tengboche (3,860 m / 12,664 ft)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Descend through birch and rhododendron forests to Deboche, crossing the Imja River via a suspension bridge. Pass ancient mani walls and ascend gradually past Pangboche village, taking in up-close views of Ama Dablam while continuing into the Imja Valley to reach Dingboche.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Trek from Tengboche to Dingboche (4,410 m / 14,468 ft)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "econd scheduled acclimatization day. Hike up to Nagarjun Hill (5,100 m / 16,732 ft) or Chhukung Valley for high-altitude training. Enjoy expansive views of Makalu, Lhotse, Chaloche, and the impressive north face of Ama Dablam.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Acclimatization Day in Dingboche (4,410 m / 14,468 ft)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "Trek along the lateral moraine of the Khumbu Glacier. Ascend Thokla Pass (Dughla Pass), home to stone memorials dedicated to climbers who lost their lives in the Everest region. Continue across rough glacial terrain to reach the small settlement of Lobuche.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Trek from Dingboche to Lobuche (4,940 m / 16,207 ft)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "Walk along the rugged moraine of the Khumbu Glacier to Gorakshep. After a brief stop, push onward to Everest Base Camp. Stand beneath the Khumbu Icefall, surrounded by high Himalayan peaks, before returning to Gorakshep for the night.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Trek from Lobuche to Gorakshep (5,170 m / 16,961 ft) &amp; Visit Everest Base Camp (5,364 m / 17,598 ft)"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "Begin an early pre-dawn climb up Kala Patthar for sunrise views of Mt. Everest, Nuptse, Changtse, and Pumori. Descend to Gorakshep for breakfast, pack up, and retrace your steps back down the valley past Lobuche and Thokla. Continue descending to the lower, oxygen-rich village of Dingboche to rest and recover before starting the Island Peak leg.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Hike to Kala Patthar (5,550 m / 18,208 ft) &amp; Descend to Dingboche (4,410 m / 14,468 ft)"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "Take a gentle, easy morning trek gradually ascending east through the Imja Valley. Walk along the riverbed beneath the towering south face of Lhotse and Ama Dablam to reach Chhukung. After arriving, check into the lodge, rest, and organize your technical climbing gear (harness, boots, crampons, ice axe, helmet) with your Sherpa climbing guide.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Trek from Dingboche to Chhukung (4,730 m / 15,518 ft)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "Trek along the south flank of the Imja Valley, following the moraine trail past Imja Tsho glacier lake to reach Island Peak Base Camp (Pareshaya Gyab). Set up camp in tents. In the afternoon, your climbing Sherpa guide will conduct a mandatory practical session on fixed ropes, jumars/ascenders, crampons, ice axes, and rappelling technique.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Trek from Chhukung to Island Peak Base Camp (5,200 m / 17,060 ft) &amp; Pre-Climb Training"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "Wake up around 12:30 AM for breakfast and begin the summit push by 1:00 AM. Scramble up a rocky gully to High Camp / Crampon Point (5,600m). Put on crampons and rope up to navigate the crevassed glacier. Clip into fixed ropes to climb the steep 40–45° snow headwall up to the narrow summit ridge. Reach the summit of Island Peak (6,189m) for panoramic vistas of Lhotse, Makalu, and Ama Dablam. Abseil down to Base Camp, rest, pack up camp, and return to Chhukung.\\";s", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Summit Day: Base Camp to Island Peak Summit (6,189 m / 20,305 ft) &amp; Return to Chhukung (4,730 m / 15,518 ft)"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "Extra safety buffer day built into the schedule in case bad weather, high ridge winds, or individual acclimatization issues prevent a summit attempt on Day 13.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Reserve / Contingency Day for Summit (6,189 m / 20,305 ft)"}, {"day": "15", "desc": "Begin the downward trek out of the high alpine valley. Pass Dingboche and descend along the Imja Khola river valley through lower alpine pastures to the village of Pangboche or Tengboche. Noticeably denser oxygen levels and warmer temperatures greet you as you drop elevation.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 15: Trek from Chhukung to Tengboche / Pangboche (3,860 m / 12,664 ft)"}, {"day": "16", "desc": " Descend through rhododendron and pine forests down to Phunki Tenga near the river. Climb up the opposite ridge trail past Kyangjuma and contour around the mountain slopes back into Namche Bazaar. Celebrate your successful summit climb in local bakeries, cafes, or pubs.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 16: Trek from Tengboche/Pangboche to Namche Bazaar (3,440 m / 11,286 ft)"}, {"day": "17", "desc": " Final day on the trekking trail. Descend steeply down Namche hill, cross the Hillary Suspension Bridge, and exit Sagarmatha National Park at Monjo. Continue along the Dudh Koshi River through Phakding and Ghat, finishing with a final gentle uphill climb into Lukla.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 17: Trek from Namche Bazaar to Lukla (2,840 m / 9,317 ft)"}, {"day": "18", "desc": "Board an early morning flight from Lukla back to Kathmandu (or Ramechhap/Manthali with drive to Kathmandu). Transfer to your hotel upon arrival. Spend the rest of the afternoon relaxing, shopping for souvenirs in Thamel, or getting a massage. Enjoy a farewell celebration dinner hosted by the team in the evening.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 18: Fly from Lukla to Kathmandu (1,400 m / 4,593 ft)"}, {"day": "19", "desc": "Enjoy breakfast at your hotel. Depending on your flight schedule, an airport representative will pick you up from your hotel and transfer you to Tribhuvan International Airport for your final flight home.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 19: Final Departure from Kathmandu (1,400 m / 4,593 ft)"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.899	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u0007kbrlodztkn7k	kanchenjunga-complete-circuit-trek	Kanchenjunga Complete Circuit Trek – North & South Base Camp (21 Days)	<h2 data-section-id="1p1mup2" data-start="494" data-end="571"></h2>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-w	<h2 data-section-id="1p1mup2" data-start="494" data-end="571"></h2>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=htEk6d_2c/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Kanchenjunga Complete Circuit Trek – Nepal's Ultimate Remote Adventure<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIDRAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">The <strong data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Kanchenjunga Complete Circuit Trek<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></strong> is one of Nepal's most spectacular and least-explored trekking adventures. Located in eastern Nepal, this remarkable journey combines both the North and South Base Camps of Mount Kanchenjunga, the world's third-highest mountain at 8,586 meters. Unlike Nepal's busier trekking routes, this expedition offers peaceful trails, untouched wilderness, and authentic mountain culture. As a result, it is perfect for trekkers seeking a true Himalayan adventure.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=htEk6d_2g/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Explore Remote Villages and Diverse Landscapes<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIDhAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">The scenic route passes through lush forests, rhododendron hills, alpine meadows, glacier valleys, and high mountain passes. Along the way, you visit traditional Rai, Limbu, and Sherpa villages where local customs and warm hospitality remain unchanged. Furthermore, every day reveals breathtaking views of Kanchenjunga, Makalu, Jannu, and numerous snow-covered Himalayan peaks. In addition, the surrounding Conservation Area is home to rare wildlife, including the snow leopard, Himalayan black bear, red panda, blue sheep, and musk deer.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=htEk6d_2j/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Visit Both North and South Base Camps<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIDxAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">One of the greatest highlights of the itinerary is visiting both North Base Camp at Pangpema and South Base Camp near Oktang. Meanwhile, trekkers enjoy dramatic glaciers, towering ice walls, and unforgettable mountain panoramas. Afterward, crossing the scenic Sele La Pass connects the two valleys and adds even more adventure to the journey. Consequently, the trek becomes one of Nepal's most rewarding high-altitude expeditions.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=htEk6d_2m/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Why Choose this Legendary Wilderness Route?<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIEBAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" aria-owns="action-menu-parent-container" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">This epic path offers the perfect balance of challenging adventure, pristine nature, and deep cultural immersion. Not only does it offer incredible mountain scenery, but it also provides rich local culture, diverse landscapes, abundant wildlife, and peaceful trails. Ultimately, this unforgettable adventure delivers an authentic Himalayan experience that few trekkers ever have the opportunity to enjoy.</div>\n<h2 data-section-id="1p1mup2" data-start="494" data-end="571"><span role="text"><strong data-start="497" data-end="571"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=11b7b2325caaf8c6&amp;sxsrf=APpeQntihPW-19gyFqd3ozc0fEPE8kuBHA:1782911166825&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gIHbHEqXWbyThyPdUCKqTmZAKzBcRFb2qe3OBMfh6G5URtuzGpQgwyLjG0HlVfwOhBKT-_MjHW6JAI50fK8ctSDBzYN4QFmM5h2f-J2LGaBBmSbliULKp1HwnGA8zByXKCw81aKc7LO2xjbgBVfvicOu9VOvA&amp;q=kanchenjunga&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjhy47WxbGVAxUqV3ADHes5F44QtKgLegQIFBAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">anchenjunga</a> Complete Circuit Trek – Nepal's Ultimate Remote Adventure</strong></span></h2>\n<p data-start="573" data-end="1077">The <strong data-start="577" data-end="615"><a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking-types/kanchenjunga-region/">Kanchenjunga</a> Complete Circuit Trek</strong> is one of Nepal's most spectacular and least-explored trekking adventures. Located in eastern Nepal, this remarkable journey combines both the North and South Base Camps of Mount Kanchenjunga, the world's third-highest mountain at 8,586 meters. <strong data-start="861" data-end="871">Unlike</strong> Nepal's busier trekking routes, this expedition offers peaceful trails, untouched wilderness, and authentic mountain culture. <strong data-start="998" data-end="1013">As a result</strong>, it is perfect for trekkers seeking a true Himalayan adventure.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="15znfpy" data-start="1079" data-end="1132"><span role="text"><strong data-start="1082" data-end="1132">Explore Remote Villages and Diverse Landscapes</strong></span></h2>\n<p data-start="1134" data-end="1711">The <strong data-start="1138" data-end="1176">Kanchenjunga Complete Circuit Trek</strong> passes through lush forests, rhododendron hills, alpine meadows, glacier valleys, and high mountain passes. <strong data-start="1285" data-end="1302">Along the way</strong>, you visit traditional Rai, Limbu, and Sherpa villages where local customs and warm hospitality remain unchanged. <strong data-start="1417" data-end="1432">Furthermore</strong>, every day reveals breathtaking views of Kanchenjunga, Makalu, Jannu, and numerous snow-covered Himalayan peaks. <strong data-start="1546" data-end="1561">In addition</strong>, the Kanchenjunga Conservation Area is home to rare wildlife, including the snow leopard, Himalayan black bear, red panda, blue sheep, and musk deer.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="kzg3cd" data-start="1713" data-end="1757"><span role="text"><strong data-start="1716" data-end="1757">Visit Both North and South Base Camps</strong></span></h2>\n<p data-start="1759" data-end="2230">One of the greatest highlights of the <strong data-start="1797" data-end="1835">Kanchenjunga Complete Circuit Trek</strong> is visiting both North Base Camp at Pangpema and South Base Camp near Oktang. <strong data-start="1914" data-end="1927">Meanwhile</strong>, trekkers enjoy dramatic glaciers, towering ice walls, and unforgettable mountain panoramas. <strong data-start="2021" data-end="2034">Afterward</strong>, crossing the scenic Sele La Pass connects the two valleys and adds even more adventure to the journey. <strong data-start="2139" data-end="2155">Consequently</strong>, the trek becomes one of Nepal's most rewarding high-altitude expeditions.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="kky509" data-start="2232" data-end="2289"><span role="text"><strong data-start="2235" data-end="2289">Why Choose the Kanchenjunga Complete Circuit Trek?</strong></span></h2>\n<p data-start="2291" data-end="2741">The <strong data-start="2295" data-end="2333">Kanchenjunga Complete Circuit Trek</strong> is ideal for experienced trekkers who want to explore one of Nepal's last truly remote trekking regions. <strong data-start="2439" data-end="2451">Not only</strong> does it offer incredible mountain scenery, <strong data-start="2495" data-end="2510">but it also</strong> provides rich local culture, diverse landscapes, abundant wildlife, and peaceful trails. <strong data-start="2600" data-end="2614">Ultimately</strong>, this unforgettable adventure delivers an authentic Himalayan experience that few trekkers ever have the opportunity to enjoy.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Kanchenjunga-Trekking-2.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	21	2999	kanchenjunga-region-trekking	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Dec	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{kanchenjunga-region-trekking}	<p><strong>The Trail Conditions: </strong></p>\n<p>Straight, Uphill, Downhill, Jig Jag with small rocky, pebbles, somewhere flat man made stone steps, through the rhododendron, moss covered forests, suspensions metal bridges</p>\n<p><strong>Medication </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bandage for sprains</li>\n<li>Plasters/Band-aids</li>\n<li>Iodine or water filter (optional)</li>\n<li>Moleskin/Second skin - for blisters</li>\n<li>Antiseptic ointment for cuts</li>\n<li>Anti-bacterial throat lozenges (with antiseptic)</li>\n<li>Aspirin/paracetamol - general painkiller</li>\n<li>Oral dehydration salts</li>\n<li>Broad-spectrum antibiotic (norfloxacin or ciprofloxin)</li>\n<li>Anti-diarrhea medication (antibiotic)</li>\n<li>Diarrhea stopper (Imodium - optional)</li>\n<li>Antibiotic for Giardia or similar microbe or bacteria</li>\n<li>Diamox (altitude sickness - can be bought in Kathmandu)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong> </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Clothing / Equipment List </strong></p>\n<p><em>Kindly bring the following list of clothing / equipment for our trek to Kanchenjunga<br />\n</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pair trekking boots and waterproofing agent</li>\n<li>Pair lightweight trekking sandals</li>\n<li>Pairs thin walking socks</li>\n<li>Pairs lightweight wind – water proof pants</li>\n<li>T-shirts</li>\n<li>Fleece Jacket</li>\n<li>Set lightweight thermals</li>\n<li>North Face down Jacket (Preferably)</li>\n<li>Small thin towel (sports towel best)</li>\n<li>Soap</li>\n<li>Shampoo</li>\n<li>Sunscreen</li>\n<li>Extra lightweight shirt for daypacks - for stops along the way</li>\n<li>Hat</li>\n<li>Cotton or silk bag liner – optional</li>\n<li>Neck warmer</li>\n<li>Pairs 'thinners' gloves</li>\n<li>Rucksack</li>\n<li>Pack tissues</li>\n<li>Pair sunglasses</li>\n<li>Water filter / Iodine (you could buy boiled water in hotels/ lodges which is safe to drink.</li>\n<li>Camera and films</li>\n<li>Head torch and spare batteries</li>\n<li>Sleeping bag (rated -15(above) deg C during our trek)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Above things are required for Kanchenjunga Trek. However if you do not have clothing you can either buy or rent in Nepal. In this case we have equipment cheaper than your country.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n	<h3>✅ Package Includes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Airport pick-up and drop-off by private vehicle</li>\n<li>Domestic flights: Kathmandu – Bhadrapur – Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Private jeep transportation as per itinerary</li>\n<li>Kanchenjunga Restricted Area Permit (RAP)</li>\n<li>Kanchenjunga Conservation Area Permit (KCAP)</li>\n<li>All required government taxes and permit fees</li>\n<li>Experienced English-speaking licensed trekking guide</li>\n<li>Porter service (1 porter for every 2 trekkers)</li>\n<li>Guide and porter salary, meals, accommodation, insurance, and equipment</li>\n<li>Teahouse/lodge accommodation during the trek</li>\n<li>Three meals a day during the trek (Breakfast, Lunch, and Dinner)</li>\n<li>Seasonal fresh fruits during the trek</li>\n<li>Three nights hotel accommodation in Kathmandu with breakfast</li>\n<li>Comprehensive first-aid medical kit carried by the guide</li>\n<li>Sleeping bag and duffel bag (upon request)</li>\n<li>Welcome and farewell dinner in Kathmandu</li>\n<li>24/7 emergency support from the company</li>\n<li style="list-style-type: none"></li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Nepal entry visa fees</li>\n<li>International airfare to and from Nepal</li>\n<li>Travel and rescue insurance</li>\n<li>Personal trekking equipment and clothing</li>\n<li>Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu</li>\n<li>Hot showers, Wi-Fi, battery charging, and personal expenses during the trek</li>\n<li>Alcoholic, soft, and bottled drinks</li>\n<li>Snacks, desserts, and extra food outside the set menu</li>\n<li>Tips for guide, porter, and driver (recommended)</li>\n<li>Personal medical expenses</li>\n<li>Extra hotel nights in Kathmandu due to early arrival, late departure, or itinerary changes</li>\n<li>Costs arising from flight delays, natural disasters, strikes, weather conditions, or circumstances beyond our control</li>\n<li>Any services not specifically mentioned in the "Package Includes" section</li>\n</ul>\n	<div class="qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot">\n<div class="" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:09004f46-8f67-45b2-ae2a-fe3ef4911786-8" data-is-intersecting="true">\n<section class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:09004f46-8f67-45b2-ae2a-fe3ef4911786-8" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:09004f46-8f67-45b2-ae2a-fe3ef4911786-8" data-testid="conversation-turn-18" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant">\n<div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)">\n<div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn">\n<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow">\n<div class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" dir="auto" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="38c41d11-1681-4078-bc14-ac4543c788d5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden">\n<div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling">\n<h4 data-start="74" data-end="97">🎒 Backpack &amp; Bags</h4>\n<ul data-start="98" data-end="183">\n<li data-section-id="7dkx1g" data-start="98" data-end="119">Duffel bag (70–90L)</li>\n<li data-section-id="hmvzas" data-start="120" data-end="138">Daypack (30–40L)</li>\n<li data-section-id="15d4y9d" data-start="139" data-end="151">Rain cover</li>\n<li data-section-id="oapnsj" data-start="152" data-end="183">Dry bags or waterproof liners</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="185" data-end="201">👕 Clothing</h4>\n<ul data-start="202" data-end="368">\n<li data-section-id="18ki1uo" data-start="202" data-end="227">Trekking T-shirts (3–4)</li>\n<li data-section-id="ximcft" data-start="228" data-end="256">Trekking pants (2–3 pairs)</li>\n<li data-section-id="ht9c86" data-start="257" data-end="278">Thermal base layers</li>\n<li data-section-id="4ccdyu" data-start="279" data-end="294">Fleece jacket</li>\n<li data-section-id="108ul6w" data-start="295" data-end="308">Down jacket</li>\n<li data-section-id="x46bqt" data-start="309" data-end="336">Waterproof jacket &amp; pants</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gmos76" data-start="337" data-end="359">Warm hat and sun hat</li>\n<li data-section-id="1xfofe4" data-start="360" data-end="368">Gloves</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="370" data-end="386">👞 Footwear</h4>\n<ul data-start="387" data-end="482">\n<li data-section-id="1lca0sf" data-start="387" data-end="414">Waterproof trekking boots</li>\n<li data-section-id="1jhchx8" data-start="415" data-end="435">Camp shoes/sandals</li>\n<li data-section-id="1r9e18k" data-start="436" data-end="464">Trekking socks (5–6 pairs)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mfsepp" data-start="465" data-end="482">Warm wool socks</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="484" data-end="510">🥾 Trekking Equipment</h4>\n<ul data-start="511" data-end="645">\n<li data-section-id="129l9l6" data-start="511" data-end="554">Sleeping bag (-15°C to -20°C recommended)</li>\n<li data-section-id="jpijbi" data-start="555" data-end="571">Trekking poles</li>\n<li data-section-id="1s6undc" data-start="572" data-end="582">Headlamp</li>\n<li data-section-id="5c7vo5" data-start="583" data-end="619">Water bottles or hydration bladder</li>\n<li data-section-id="11rfapo" data-start="620" data-end="632">Sunglasses</li>\n<li data-section-id="dluokx" data-start="633" data-end="645">Power bank</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="647" data-end="669">🧴 Personal Items</h4>\n<ul data-start="670" data-end="781">\n<li data-section-id="10pl9xo" data-start="670" data-end="681">Sunscreen</li>\n<li data-section-id="1voh31b" data-start="682" data-end="692">Lip balm</li>\n<li data-section-id="l5061k" data-start="693" data-end="715">Personal medications</li>\n<li data-section-id="1h5dihr" data-start="716" data-end="737">Basic first-aid kit</li>\n<li data-section-id="8yarze" data-start="738" data-end="750">Toiletries</li>\n<li data-section-id="k8zdnf" data-start="751" data-end="781">Wet wipes and hand sanitizer</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start="783" data-end="1058" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node=""><strong data-start="783" data-end="795">❄️ Note:</strong> Kanchenjunga is one of Nepal's most remote trekking regions. Expect long trekking days, limited facilities, and cold temperatures at higher elevations. Warm clothing, sturdy boots, and a high-quality sleeping bag are essential for a safe and comfortable journey.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"></div>\n<div class="mt-3 w-full empty:hidden">\n<div class="text-center"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="pointer-events-none -mt-px h-px translate-y-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom)-14*var(--spacing))]" aria-hidden="true"></div>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Welcome to Nepal. After arriving at Tribhuvan International Airport in Kathmandu, our representative will greet you and transfer you to your hotel. After check-in, you can relax and recover from your journey or explore nearby markets and cultural sites in the city. Kathmandu offers a unique mix of ancient temples, lively streets, and traditional architecture. In the evening, your trekking guide will meet you for a short briefing about the Kanchenjunga Base Camp trek and review the final preparations for the adventure ahead.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1400m / 4593 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Today we take a scenic flight from Kathmandu to Bhadrapur in eastern Nepal. During the flight, you may enjoy beautiful aerial views of the Himalayan range. After landing, we continue our journey with a drive through tea gardens, hills, and traditional villages toward Taplejung. The drive introduces you to the rural lifestyle and landscapes of eastern Nepal. By evening, we reach Taplejung where we prepare for the trek.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Fly to Bhadrapur and Drive to Taplejung (1820m / 5971 ft)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "After breakfast, we continue the journey by road deeper into the Kanchenjunga region. The drive passes through remote villages, forests, and river valleys. The scenery becomes increasingly mountainous as we move closer to the trekking route. Eventually we arrive at Sekathum, a small settlement located near the river where the trekking trail begins.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Drive to Sekathum (1650m / 5413 ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Today the trekking adventure officially begins. We follow a trail through forests and narrow river valleys while walking along the Ghunsa Khola. The route includes suspension bridges and scenic paths surrounded by lush greenery. After several hours of trekking through peaceful natural surroundings, we arrive at the small settlement of Amjilosa.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Trek to Amjilosa (2510m / 8234 ft)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Today’s trail climbs steadily through dense forests of bamboo, rhododendron, and pine. The path offers beautiful natural scenery and occasional glimpses of snow-covered peaks. After several hours of trekking through forest landscapes, we reach the small village of Gyabla, which sits in a peaceful alpine setting.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Trek to Gyabla (2730m / 8957 ft)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "The trail gradually climbs through beautiful alpine landscapes and traditional Tibetan-influenced villages. Along the way, you will see prayer flags, chortens, and monasteries that reflect the region’s cultural heritage. Ghunsa is one of the largest villages in the region and offers impressive views of surrounding mountains.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Trek to Ghunsa (3595m / 11795 ft)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Today is an important acclimatization day. You may explore the village, visit nearby monasteries, or take short hikes to viewpoints around Ghunsa. These activities help your body adapt to the altitude and prepare for the higher elevations ahead.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Acclimatization Day at Ghunsa (3595m / 11795 ft)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "Leaving Ghunsa, the trail follows the river valley through rocky terrain and alpine landscapes. The scenery becomes more dramatic with towering peaks and glaciers visible in the distance. After several hours of trekking through high mountain terrain, we arrive at Kambachen.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Trek to Kambachen (4050m / 13287 ft)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "Today we trek through remote alpine landscapes toward Lhonak. The trail passes glaciers, rocky valleys, and dramatic mountain scenery. As we gain elevation, the environment becomes more rugged and spectacular. Lhonak is a small high-altitude settlement located near the Kanchenjunga glacier.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Trek to Lhonak (4780m / 15682 ft)"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "Today we hike to the spectacular Kanchenjunga North Base Camp. The trail offers incredible views of glaciers and towering Himalayan peaks. Standing at the base of the world’s third-highest mountain is a truly unforgettable experience. After enjoying the breathtaking scenery, we return to Lhonak for the night.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Trek to Kanchenjunga North Base Camp and Return to Lhonak (5143m / 16873 ft)"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "After an early breakfast in Lhonak, we begin the return journey toward Ghunsa. The trail follows the same valley route with magnificent views of glaciers, rocky landscapes, and surrounding Himalayan peaks. Walking downhill through alpine terrain makes the trek more comfortable compared to the ascent. Along the way, you may see yak pastures and small stone shelters used by herders. After several hours of trekking, we arrive back at the peaceful village of Ghunsa where we spend the night.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Trek back to Ghunsa (3595m / 11795 ft)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "Today we leave the main valley and climb toward the Sele La region. The trail ascends gradually through alpine landscapes with fewer settlements along the way. The route offers impressive mountain scenery and quiet trekking paths surrounded by rugged Himalayan terrain. After several hours of steady climbing, we reach the Sele La area where we stay overnight in a basic mountain lodge.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Trek to Sele La (4290m / 14075 ft)"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "Today we cross scenic high passes before descending toward Tseram. The trail offers breathtaking views of surrounding snow-covered peaks and wide alpine valleys. As we descend gradually, the landscape becomes greener with alpine meadows and small streams. After several hours of trekking through peaceful mountain scenery, we reach the settlement of Tseram.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Trek to Tseram (3870m / 12697 ft)"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "The trek continues toward Ramche, passing through beautiful alpine landscapes and open valleys. The trail gradually climbs higher with excellent views of glaciers and surrounding Himalayan peaks. Ramche is a small high-altitude settlement located close to Kanchenjunga South Base Camp. The environment here feels truly remote and peaceful.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Trek to Ramche (4580m / 15026 ft)"}, {"day": "15", "desc": "Today we hike toward the stunning Kanchenjunga South Base Camp area. The trail leads through dramatic alpine scenery with breathtaking views of Kanchenjunga and nearby peaks. After enjoying the spectacular surroundings and taking photographs, we return along the same trail back to Tseram for the night.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 15: Explore Kanchenjunga South Base Camp and Return to Tseram (3870m / 12697 ft)"}, {"day": "16", "desc": "Leaving the high alpine region, we begin descending toward Tortong. The trail passes through forests, waterfalls, and scenic mountain valleys. As the altitude decreases, the environment becomes greener and the air feels warmer. After a pleasant trekking day through natural landscapes, we reach Tortong.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 16: Trek to Tortong (2995m / 9826 ft)"}, {"day": "17", "desc": "Today’s trail continues through beautiful forests, terraced fields, and small traditional villages. As we descend further, the climate becomes milder and the landscapes more vibrant. Yamphudin is a charming village where trekkers can experience local culture and hospitality.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 17: Trek to Yamphudin (2080m / 6824 ft)"}, {"day": "18", "desc": "The trail today passes through hillsides, forests, and farmland as we continue our descent. The route offers pleasant walking with scenic views of rural eastern Nepal. Eventually we arrive at Khebang, a peaceful village surrounded by natural landscapes.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 18: Trek to Khebang (1900m / 6233 ft)"}, {"day": "19", "desc": "After breakfast, we begin the long drive from the hills toward the plains of eastern Nepal. The journey passes through scenic landscapes, villages, and tea plantations. By evening we arrive in Bhadrapur where we stay overnight before the flight back to Kathmandu.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 19: Drive to Bhadrapur (91m / 299 ft)"}, {"day": "20", "desc": "Today we take a domestic flight from Bhadrapur back to Kathmandu. During the flight you may once again enjoy aerial views of Nepal’s hills and mountains. After arriving in Kathmandu, you will be transferred to your hotel. The rest of the day is free to relax, explore the city, or shop for souvenirs.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 20: Fly to Kathmandu (1400m / 4593 ft)"}, {"day": "21", "desc": "Your incredible Kanchenjunga Base Camp adventure comes to an end today. According to your flight schedule, our team will transfer you to Tribhuvan International Airport. We hope you leave Nepal with wonderful memories of the mountains, culture, and people you encountered during this remarkable journey.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 21: Final Departure from Kathmandu (1400m / 4593 ft)"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.799	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000bkbrl98fnkjg7	tamang-heritage-trek	6 days Tamang heritage trek	<h2 data-section-id="ytu71i" data-start="307" data-end="346">6 Days <a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=23c6f1fa80babc08&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnvB	<h2 data-section-id="ytu71i" data-start="307" data-end="346">6 Days <a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=23c6f1fa80babc08&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnvBrDCcAwyOgIKUOu8jhn_GDXAd6Q:1783130784924&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832cSpkWkfSwsmpNIrD_OQ-UdFAe4qAwsQWVbrtprjzBSpqcpRIjrWvpllIY_DcnbWIK5czq4gtgqB7WOzZs6JddYdDo_t0V6s0JMLK64pDRnGkYNIGfztWBVfYbsIzzUIcs9CR7Z2AOyYobj57MCgOyoSG2bQDFqNm1HZuramKgM8oiC2zA&amp;q=langtang+tamang+heritage+trek&amp;sa=X&amp;sqi=2&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjQzJfo97eVAxXKbGwGHasCH9kQtKgLegQIFBAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Tamang Heritage Trek</a> Overview</h2>\n<p data-start="348" data-end="773">The <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/6-day-langtang-valley-treks/"><strong data-start="352" data-end="383">6 Days Tamang Heritage Trek</strong></a> is a short and rewarding adventure in Nepal's beautiful Langtang region. This cultural trek takes you through traditional Tamang villages, scenic hills, and peaceful forests. Moreover, it offers a wonderful chance to experience authentic Himalayan culture without trekking to extreme altitudes. Therefore, it is an excellent choice for beginners, families, and travelers with limited time.</p>\n<p data-start="775" data-end="1201">The journey begins with a scenic drive from Kathmandu to Syabrubesi, the starting point of the trek. From there, you walk through charming villages such as Gatlang, Tatopani, Thuman, and Briddim. Along the way, you enjoy breathtaking mountain views, terraced farms, and lush rhododendron forests. In addition, the friendly Tamang people warmly welcome visitors and proudly share their traditions, culture, and daily lifestyle.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="1xq9yjo" data-start="1203" data-end="1252">Experience Tamang Culture and Himalayan Beauty</h2>\n<p data-start="1254" data-end="1582">One of the highlights of the trek is the opportunity to discover the rich heritage of the Tamang community. You can visit ancient monasteries, spin colorful prayer wheels, and explore villages influenced by Tibetan Buddhism. Furthermore, staying in local tea houses allows you to enjoy traditional meals and genuine hospitality.</p>\n<p data-start="1584" data-end="1912">Another memorable stop is Tatopani, where you can relax in natural hot springs after a rewarding day of hiking. Meanwhile, the surrounding landscapes provide stunning views of Langtang Lirung, Ganesh Himal, and other snow-covered peaks. Although the trek is relatively short, every day offers something unique and unforgettable.</p>\n<p data-start="1914" data-end="2199">The best seasons for the <strong data-start="1939" data-end="1970">6 Days Tamang Heritage Trek</strong> are spring (March to May) and autumn (September to November). During these months, the weather is usually clear, and the mountain views are spectacular. However, the trek can also be enjoyed in winter by well-prepared travelers.</p>\n<p data-start="2201" data-end="2502">Overall, the <strong data-start="2214" data-end="2245">6 Days Tamang Heritage Trek</strong> combines natural beauty, local culture, and comfortable trekking into one unforgettable journey. Whether you are looking for cultural discovery, peaceful trails, or amazing Himalayan scenery, this trek promises a memorable experience in the heart of Nepal.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/1114.jpeg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	6 Days	599	langtang	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Jan	Hotels in Kathmandu and teahouses during the trek	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{langtang-region}	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="u9n4oz" data-start="48" data-end="119">🏔️ Stunning views of the Langtang Himal range throughout the trek</li>\n<li data-section-id="14a9d7i" data-start="120" data-end="208">🏘️ Authentic Tamang village experiences in Ghatlang, Tatopani, Thuman, and Briddim</li>\n<li data-section-id="4foxg0" data-start="209" data-end="309">🚗 Scenic drive from <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Kathmandu</span></span> to Syabrubesi, gateway of the region</li>\n<li data-section-id="uoj512" data-start="310" data-end="379">♨️ Natural hot springs at Tatopani for relaxation after trekking</li>\n<li data-section-id="1g8glsp" data-start="380" data-end="446">🏡 Traditional Tamang homestay experience with local families</li>\n<li data-section-id="t70opw" data-start="447" data-end="533">🧭 Rich Tibetan-influenced culture, monasteries, and prayer flags along the trail</li>\n<li data-section-id="1c79ia1" data-start="534" data-end="609">🌲 Peaceful trails through rhododendron forests and terraced hillsides</li>\n<li data-section-id="8rpseh" data-start="610" data-end="700">📸 Excellent photography opportunities of landscapes, culture, and daily village life</li>\n<li data-section-id="18thwtc" data-start="701" data-end="783">🥾 Moderate trekking difficulty, suitable for beginners and cultural trekkers</li>\n<li data-section-id="s4ayn0" data-start="784" data-end="857">🤝 Warm hospitality and cultural exchange with the Tamang community</li>\n</ul>\n				[{"day": "1", "desc": "Early morning departure from Kathmandu with a scenic drive towards Syabrubesi, the gateway to the Tamang Heritage and Langtang region. The road follows winding mountain highways, river valleys, terraced fields, and small rural settlements, offering beautiful views of hills and distant Himalayan peaks.\\n\\nYou will pass through Trishuli River valley and several small towns along the route. The journey gradually becomes more rugged as you approach Syabrubesi, giving you your first real taste of Himalayan road travel and mountain lifestyle.\\";", "elev": 1400, "title": "Day 1: Kathmandu to Syabrubesi (1,400m)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "After breakfast in Syabrubesi, the trek begins with a gradual ascent through lush forests, suspension bridges, and traditional Tamang settlements. The trail offers peaceful surroundings with views of rolling hills, terraced fields, and distant Himalayan peaks.\\n\\nYou will pass through small rural villages and local farmlands, experiencing authentic mountain life along the way. As you climb higher towards Ghatlang, the landscape becomes more scenic and culturally rich, with strong Tibetan-influenced traditions.\\";", "elev": 2200, "title": "Day 2: Syabrubesi to Ghatlang (2,200m)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "The trek continues after breakfast in Ghatlang with a steady uphill walk through dense forests, small Tamang villages, and beautiful terraced landscapes. The trail gradually opens up to wider mountain views, giving a peaceful and refreshing trekking experience.\\n\\nYou will pass through remote settlements and local farmlands, where you can observe traditional mountain lifestyles and warm hospitality. As you approach Tatopani, the environment becomes more serene and culturally rich, surrounded by natural beauty.\\";", "elev": 2600, "title": "Day 3: Ghatlang to Tatopani (2,600m)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "fter a refreshing stay in Tatopani, the trek continues through beautiful forest trails and gentle uphill paths towards Thuman. The route offers peaceful surroundings, traditional Tamang settlements, and wide views of rolling hills and distant Himalayan peaks.\\n\\nAs you approach Thuman, the cultural atmosphere becomes more prominent with prayer flags, monasteries, and strong Tibetan-influenced traditions. The village is known for its warm hospitality and scenic hillside location.\\";", "elev": 2400, "title": "Day 4: Tatopani to Thuman (2,400m)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "From Thuman, the trail descends gradually through peaceful forests, traditional villages, and terraced fields towards Briddim. The route is culturally rich, offering deep insight into the daily lifestyle of the Tamang community along the border region.\\n\\nAs you reach Briddim, you are welcomed into one of the most preserved Tamang villages, known for its authentic homestay experience and strong Buddhist traditions. The village offers a calm atmosphere with beautiful views of surrounding hills.\\";", "elev": 2200, "title": "Day 5: Thuman to Briddim (2,200m)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "After breakfast in Briddim, you begin your return journey with a scenic drive back to Kathmandu. The route follows mountain roads, river valleys, and rural settlements, giving you one last chance to enjoy the Himalayan landscape.\\n\\nThe drive gradually descends from the hills to the bustling capital city, marking the end of your Tamang Heritage Trek. It is a relaxing journey where you can reflect on the cultural experiences and natural beauty you encountered during the trek.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Briddim to Kathmandu"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.809	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000gkbrl0yfe7uqh	ghandruk-trekking	Ghandruk Trekking	<h1 data-section-id="bq4omm" data-start="274" data-end="302"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=23c6f1fa80babc08&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnutuY_XbKp	<h1 data-section-id="bq4omm" data-start="274" data-end="302"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=23c6f1fa80babc08&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnutuY_XbKpPm-7OLtItq_0WKc3CbA:1783131415827&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832cK-OlyrFp0q_lDSVqWSWpDEzO_-mUx3hdbQlSvWRAm3a3D3y0P_3kyEtVBac4Ukyhuw8w7LpgH4P8gabJmURZOPQ4a3gZGUodu7xwLfDZxZfAGRVNeHZa4rjqOzxW8vGjvSV0TkFaCxKU3opgvz93ZBmZmPf2FlC1JNr8eE-UUKshOmBQ&amp;q=ghandruk&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwid54KV-reVAxW9zDgGHdVfCdQQtKgLegQIFhAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Ghandruk</a> Trekking Overview</h1>\n<p data-start="304" data-end="668"><a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/ghorepani-ghandruk-trek/"><strong data-start="304" data-end="325">Ghandruk Trekking</strong> </a>is one of the most popular short treks in Nepal. It takes you to the beautiful Gurung village of Ghandruk at 1,940 meters in the Annapurna region. Moreover, the trek offers breathtaking mountain views, rich local culture, and peaceful walking trails. Therefore, it is an excellent choice for beginners, families, and anyone with limited time.</p>\n<p data-start="670" data-end="1019">The journey starts with a scenic drive from Pokhara to Nayapul or Kimche. From there, you follow easy trails through terraced fields, rhododendron forests, and traditional villages. Along the way, you cross suspension bridges and enjoy fresh mountain air. In addition, friendly tea houses provide comfortable accommodation and delicious local meals.</p>\n<p data-start="1021" data-end="1214">Furthermore, every day rewards you with spectacular views of Annapurna South, Machhapuchhre (Fishtail), Hiunchuli, and Gangapurna. As a result, the trek remains enjoyable from beginning to end.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="aegfu3" data-start="1216" data-end="1244">Experience Gurung Culture</h2>\n<p data-start="1246" data-end="1509">One of the highlights of <strong data-start="1271" data-end="1292">Ghandruk Trekking</strong> is visiting the traditional Gurung village. Here, you can explore stone-paved streets, traditional houses, and ancient monasteries. Moreover, you can visit the Gurung Museum and learn about local history and customs.</p>\n<p data-start="1511" data-end="1756">Meanwhile, local families warmly welcome visitors into their community. Consequently, you experience authentic Himalayan hospitality throughout the trek. Likewise, the peaceful surroundings create a relaxing atmosphere after each day of walking.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="xdlb5" data-start="1758" data-end="1782">Scenic Mountain Views</h2>\n<p data-start="1784" data-end="2105">Besides its rich culture, <strong data-start="1810" data-end="1831">Ghandruk Trekking</strong> is famous for its outstanding scenery. During spring, colorful rhododendron forests bloom across the hillsides. Similarly, autumn brings crystal-clear skies and excellent mountain visibility. However, winter also offers beautiful snow-covered landscapes and quieter trails.</p>\n<p data-start="2107" data-end="2269">In addition, photographers enjoy countless opportunities to capture sunrise and sunset over the Annapurna range. Therefore, every season has its own unique charm.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="11jzbxc" data-start="2271" data-end="2305">Best Time for Ghandruk Trekking</h2>\n<p data-start="2307" data-end="2586">Spring (March to May) and autumn (September to November) are the best seasons for <strong data-start="2389" data-end="2410">Ghandruk Trekking</strong>. During these months, the weather is usually stable and comfortable. Furthermore, mountain views are at their best. However, proper trekking gear is important in every season.</p>\n<p data-start="2588" data-end="2877">Finally, <strong data-start="2597" data-end="2618">Ghandruk Trekking</strong> combines stunning Himalayan scenery, authentic Gurung culture, comfortable tea houses, and peaceful trails into one unforgettable adventure. Overall, it is one of the finest short treks in Nepal and an excellent choice for travelers of all experience levels.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Ghandruk-Trekkingss.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	7 Days	1100	annapurna	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Feb		B.B.		\N	Trekking	{annapurna-region}	<p><strong>The Trail Conditions: </strong></p>\n<p>Straight, Uphill, Downhill, Jig Jag with small rocky, pebbles, somewhere flat man made stone steps, through the rhododendron, moss covered forests, suspensions metal bridges</p>\n<p><strong>Medication </strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Bandage for sprains</li>\n<li>Plasters/Band-aids</li>\n<li>Iodine or water filter (optional)</li>\n<li>Moleskin/Second skin - for blisters</li>\n<li>Antiseptic ointment for cuts</li>\n<li>Anti-bacterial throat lozenges (with antiseptic)</li>\n<li>Aspirin/paracetamol - general painkiller</li>\n<li>Oral dehydration salts</li>\n<li>Broad-spectrum antibiotic (norfloxacin or ciprofloxin)</li>\n<li>Anti-diarrhea medication (antibiotic)</li>\n<li>Diarrhea stopper (Imodium - optional)</li>\n<li>Antibiotic for Giardia or similar microbe or bacteria</li>\n<li>Diamox (altitude sickness - can be bought in Kathmandu)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong> </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Clothing / Equipment List </strong></p>\n<p><em>Kindly bring the following list of clothing / equipment for our trek to Ghandruk Trek </em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pair trekking boots and waterproofing agent</li>\n<li>Pair lightweight trekking sandals</li>\n<li>Pairs thin walking socks</li>\n<li>Pairs lightweight wind – water proof pants</li>\n<li>T-shirts</li>\n<li>Fleece Jacket</li>\n<li>Set lightweight thermals</li>\n<li>North Face down Jacket (Preferably)</li>\n<li>Small thin towel (sports towel best)</li>\n<li>Soap</li>\n<li>Shampoo</li>\n<li>Sunscreen</li>\n<li>Extra lightweight shirt for daypacks - for stops along the way</li>\n<li>Hat</li>\n<li>Cotton or silk bag liner – optional</li>\n<li>Neck warmer</li>\n<li>Pairs 'thinners' gloves</li>\n<li>Rucksack</li>\n<li>Pack tissues</li>\n<li>Pair sunglasses</li>\n<li>Water filter / Iodine (you could buy boiled water in hotels/ lodges which is safe to drink.</li>\n<li>Camera and films</li>\n<li>Head torch and spare batteries</li>\n<li>Sleeping bag (rated -15(above) deg C during our trek)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Above things are required for Upper Ghandruk Trek. However if you do not have clothing you can either buy or rent in Nepal. In this case we have equipment cheaper than your country.</p>\n				[]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.822	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
