ta-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-xid="Gd7Hsc" data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-wiz-uids="NGsbLc_2e" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">\n<div data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">\n\n<span data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[[1,1,1]]--></span>\n<div data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px 0px 0px -8px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">\n<div data-sfc-root="ep" data-wiz-uids="NGsbLc_3s,NGsbLc_3t,NGsbLc_3u" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">\n<div data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=VBjomf_34/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Annapurna Base Camp Trek – 12 Days Itinerary<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIDhAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">The <strong data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Annapurna Base Camp Trek<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></strong> is one of Nepal's most legendary and popular classic walking adventures. This stunning route brings you deep into the spectacular Annapurna Sanctuary, offering an immersive journey surrounded by giant Himalayan peaks. Because of its incredible variety of terrains, this classic multi-day expedition remains an absolute favorite for travelers worldwide who dream of standing at the foot of massive mountains.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=VBjomf_3d/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">What to Expect on the Annapurna Base Camp Trek<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIDxAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Your expedition begins with a scenic drive from Pokhara to the trailhead, quickly leading into beautiful rhododendron forests and traditional Gurung villages. As you ascend toward the base camp, the lush green hills slowly transform into a rugged alpine landscape. Along the way, staying in cozy local teahouses allows you to experience warm Nepalese hospitality firsthand while enjoying spectacular daily mountain views.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=VBjomf_3l/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Reaching the Spectacular Annapurna Sanctuary<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIEBAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Arriving at the final destination provides an unparalleled 360-degree panorama of majestic peaks, including Annapurna I, Annapurna South, Machapuchare (Fishtail), and Hiunchuli. Watching the morning sun rise over these ice-capped walls is an unforgettable highlight of the adventure. Additionally, the itinerary allows for safe acclimatization, making the high-altitude route accessible and enjoyable for average hikers.<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sfc-inited="2" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);"><!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div role="heading" aria-level="3" data-animation-nesting="" data-sfc-cp="" data-wiz-attrbind="aria-level=VBjomf_3t/fLk2Md" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-sae="" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 24px 0px 12px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Why Choose This Iconic 12-Day Journey?<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></div>\n<div data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-hveid="CAAIERAA" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" aria-owns="action-menu-parent-container" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">The <strong data-sfc-cp="" data-sfc-root="ep" data-complete="true" data-processed="true" data-copy-service-computed-style="font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(230, 232, 240);">Annapurna Base Camp Trek<!--TgQPHd|||[]--></strong> offers the perfect mix of dramatic high-mountain landscapes, deep cultural immersion, and accessible trails. Not only do you walk through diverse ecological zones, but you also challenge yourself in a safe, guided setting. Ultimately, this unforgettable Himalayan holiday delivers incredible memories, stunning photography opportunities, and a deep appreciation for mountain life.</div>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/IMG_20260220_225001.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	12 Days	1099	annapurna	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Jan	Hotel / Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{annapurna-region}	<div class="">\n<p class="" data-start="725" data-end="1204">✅ <strong data-start="727" data-end="811">Panoramic views of Annapurna I, Machhapuchhre (Fishtail), Dhaulagiri &amp; Hiunchuli</strong><br data-start="811" data-end="814" />✅ <strong data-start="816" data-end="863">Explore traditional Gurung &amp; Magar villages</strong> like Ghandruk &amp; Chhomrong<br data-start="889" data-end="892" />✅ <strong data-start="894" data-end="941">Relax in natural hot springs at Jhinu Danda</strong> after trekking<br data-start="956" data-end="959" />✅ <strong data-start="961" data-end="994">Experience diverse landscapes</strong> – from rhododendron forests to glacial valleys<br data-start="1041" data-end="1044" />✅ <strong data-start="1046" data-end="1127">Reach Annapurna Base Camp (4,130m) &amp; enjoy a 360-degree view of the Himalayas</strong><br data-start="1127" data-end="1130" />✅ <strong data-start="1132" data-end="1159">Moderate trekking route</strong> – suitable for beginners with good fitness</p>\n</div>\n	<p class="" data-start="4474" data-end="4823">✔️ <strong data-start="4477" data-end="4518">Airport transfers &amp; private transport</strong>.<br data-start="4519" data-end="4522" />✔️ <strong data-start="4525" data-end="4573">Accommodation in Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara (Hotel)</strong>.<br data-start="4574" data-end="4577" />✔️ <strong data-start="4580" data-end="4620">Tea house accommodations during trek</strong>.<br data-start="4621" data-end="4624" />✔️ <strong data-start="4627" data-end="4683">All meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) during the trek</strong>.<br data-start="4684" data-end="4687" />✔️ <strong data-start="4690" data-end="4729">Trekking permits (ACAP &amp; TIMS Card)</strong>.<br data-start="4730" data-end="4733" />✔️ <strong data-start="4736" data-end="4781">English-speaking trekking guide &amp; porters</strong>.<br data-start="4782" data-end="4785" />✔️ <strong data-start="4788" data-end="4820">First aid &amp; safety equipment</strong>.</p>\n	<p>❌ <strong data-start="4854" data-end="4879">International airfare</strong>.<br data-start="4880" data-end="4883" />❌ <strong data-start="4885" data-end="4944">Travel insurance (mandatory for high-altitude trekking)</strong>.<br data-start="4945" data-end="4948" />❌ <strong data-start="4950" data-end="5014">Personal expenses (hot showers, Wi-Fi, charging, tips, etc.)</strong>.<br data-start="5015" data-end="5018" />❌ <strong data-start="5020" data-end="5065">Extra meals &amp; drinks in Kathmandu/Pokhara</strong>.<br data-start="5066" data-end="5069" />❌ <strong data-start="5071" data-end="5130">Optional activities (paragliding, bungee jumping, etc.)</strong>.</p>\n		[{"day": "1", "desc": "We will meet you outside of Tribhuvan International Airport (TIA), waiting with a warm greeting and take you towards your hotel. In the evening, our team will explain overall pre - tour plan in brief.\\n\\n\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day - 1: Arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport (TIA) Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Our remarkable journey begins with bus ride from Kathmandu to Pokhara passing through the mesmerizing scenery of beautiful landscape. For much of the journey, the road runs parallel to the Trishuli and later Marsyangdi river, offering scenic views of terraced farmlands, valleys, and rolling green hills. Finally the busy capital city connects to the peaceful lake city of Pokhara. After refreshment at the hotel, we will take you around the beautiful tourist hub of lakeside.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day - 2: Drive to Pokhara (820m / 2690 ft) 6-7 hours drive"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "The journey from Pokhara to Ulleri begins with a scenic drive along winding mountain roads, passing through terraced fields, rivers, and charming hillside villages. The road gradually climbs higher, offering glimpses of Annapurna peaks before reaching the Gurung village of Ulleri. From here, the trek towards Banthanti initiates with stone-paved steps and lush forests. The trail is surrounded by rhododendron and oak trees along with fresh mountain air. As you walk deeper into the forest leaving the roads behind, and after a few hours of steady trekking, you arrive at Banthanti, which is perfect for rest and Himalayan views. Overnight at tea house.\\n\\n\\";", "elev": 0, "title": " Day – 3: Drive from Pokhara to Ulleri and trek to Banthanti (2210m / 7250 ft) 3 hrs drive and 2 hrs trek\\";"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "The trek from Banthanti to Ghorepani is a refreshing walk through enchanting section of Annapurna region. The trail winds gently uphill, shaded by dense rhododendron and oak trees. The path allows you to soak in the natural beauty and serenity of the forest. After few hours of trekking, the traditional houses of Ghorepani  covered with Magar community can be seen. From the cozy tea houses of Ghorepani, we can see stunning views of Mt. Annapurna, Mt. Dhaulagiri and Mt. Nilgiri. Overnight at tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 4: Trek from Banthanti to Ghorepani (2780m / 9121 ft) 3-4 hrs hike\\";"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Early in the morning, we hike up to Poon Hill (3210m) observing the breathtaking sunrise over the Mt. Annapurna and Mt. Dhaulagiri ranges, where golden rays light up the snowcapped peaks in an unforgettable panorama. After returning to hotel for breakfast, we continue our hike towards another beautiful hilltop Tadapani through enchanting forests having fresh mountain air. Then the path leads to a peaceful, small village Tadapani, surrounded by forest. From here, we can enjoy the closer, dramatic views of the Himalayas such as Annapurna South, himchuli, and Mt. Fishtail in a serene setting.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 5: Trek form Ghorepani/Poon Hill to Tadapani (2680m/8727ft) 5 hrs hike\\";"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "The trek from Tadapani to Chomrong is a beautiful journey that takes you deeper into the heart of the Annapurna region. Leaving Tadapani, the trail descends through lush rhododendron and pine trees with the sound of streams accompanying the walk. The path winds down to the charming Gurung village of Chuile and continues through terraced farmlands and small settlements. After crossing a suspension bridge over the Kimrong Khola, the trail climbs uphill, eventually leading to Chomrong, a welcoming village perched on the hillside. The views of Annapurna south and fishtail feel close and majestic, making Chomrong a perfect gateway to the higher Annapurna sanctuary.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day –   6: Trek from Tadapani to Chomrong (2060m/6759ft) 5 hrs hike\\";"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Our hike from Chomrong to Dovan takes you closer to the Annapurna sanctuary, with mix of steep descents and ascents through charming villages and lush forests. The trails first, drops down a long stone staircase to suspension bridge crossing the river. After the crossing, a steady climb begins through terraced fields and forest reaching the small settlement of Sinuwa. From here, the landscape become quieter and more secluded as the trails enters dense bamboo and rhododendron forest passing through Bamboo    village and enjoying the cool shade of forest. The walk is peaceful with the sound of rushing rivers and glimpses of towering cliffs. Finally, we reach Dovan, a tranquil stop surrounded by forested hills, offering a restful atmosphere before climb towards Deurali and the Annapurna base camp. Overnight at tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 7: Trek from Chomrong to Dovan (2600m/8580ft) 5-6 hrs hike\\";"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "Leaving the quite forested village Dovan, the trail follows Modhi khola valley with the sound of river enhoing below. The path winds through dense forests of bamboo and rhododendron, often shaded and cool, with occasional clearings that reveal dramatic cliffs and waterfalls cascading down the hillside. Passing through the small settlement of Himalaya the climb continue  gradually and the air feels fresher as you gain altitude. The vegetation begins to thin, giving way to more open landscapes with sweeping views. Finally, after several hours of hiking you reach Deurali, a serene stop nestled at foot of towering peaks, offering breathtaking views and a sense of being close to the heart of the Himalayas. Overnight at tea house. ", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 8: Trek from Dovan to Deurali (3200m/10545ft) 4 hrs hike\\";"}, {"day": "9", "desc": " The most awaiting day Finally today, the hike from Deurali to Annapurna Base Camp (ABC) is one of the most dramatic and rewarding section of the journey. The trail gradually ascends along the Modhi khola, with the landscape opening wider as dense forests give way to alpine meadows and rugged cliffs. Soon you reach Machhapuchhre Base Camp(3700m), a stunning viewpoint surrounded by snowcapped peaks, where Machhapuchhre (fishtail) rises sharply above. From MBC, the trail continues gently uphill across a high alpine plateau and with each step the panorama expands. Finally, after a few hours of steady hikes, you arrive at Annapurna Base Camp (4130M) a breathtaking amphitheater of mountains known as the Annapurna Sanctuary. Here, the peaks stand so closer and towering that you feel completely immersed in the heart of the Himalaya, making it the highlight and ultimate reward of the trek. Overnight at tea house.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 9: Trek from Deurali to Annapurna Base Camp (4130m/13590ft) 4-5 hrs hike \\";"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "The hike from Annapurna Base Camp to Bamboo marks the beginning of the return journey offering a different perspective of the mountain you just conquered. Leaving   the high alpine plateau of ABC, the trail gradually descends through the same valley we hiked up. Passing Machhapuchhre Base Camp once again, the path winds through open meadows, rocky ridges, and patches of rhododendron forest, with the snowcap peaks slowly fading into the distance. As you descend further, the air grow warmer and the vegetation denser, returning to bamboo groves and pine forests. The trails passess small settlements and teahouses, where trekkers can rest and enjoy the serene surroundings.  After several hours descent you arrive at Bamboo, a peaceful village. Overnight couple of hours of descent you arrive at teahouse. ", "elev": 0, "title": "  Day - 10:  Annapurna Base Camp to Bamboo ( 2310m/ 7580ft) 5-6 hrs hike"}, {"day": "11", "desc": " The hike back from Bamboo to Jhinu Danda is a beautiful and refreshing descent. Leaving bamboo, the trail gently up and downhill through dense rhododendron, oak and bamboo forests, with the sound of birds and nearby streams accompanying your walk. Along the way, we pass traditional Gurung settlement offering glimpses of local life in the mountains. The path eventually leads to Jhinu Danda, a charming village known for its neutral hot springs. Here, trekkers can relax and soak in the warm waters, soothing tired muscles after days of trekking, overnight at teahouse.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 11: Bamboo to Jhinu Danda (1780m/5800ft) 5-6 hrs hike\\";"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "After a refreshing morning in Jhinu Danda, where many trekkers enjoy a relaxing dip in the natural hot springs by the Modi Khola, the journey back toward civilization begins. A short walk down to the jeep station connects you to the road.  The drive gradually transitions from mountain tracks to smoother highways as you approach Pokhara within couple of hours, we arrive in the beautiful lakeside city. After the arrival, in the afternoon we explore Pokhara. Overnight at hotel.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 12: Jhinu to Pokhara (820m / 2690 ft) 3 hrs\\";"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "After completing the incredible days in Himalaya, today marks the return to Kathmandu. In the morning, we take a scenic drive form Pokhara back to the capital.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 13: Pokhara to Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "14", "desc": " Today we explore the Kathmandu, a living museum home to seven World Heritage Sites that showcase Nepal’s rich history, culture, and spirituality. A day tour of these sites offers an unforgettable journey through ancient temples, royal palaces, and sacred monuments that reflect art and tradition of Nepal.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 14: Kathmandu city tour/free time\\";"}, {"day": "15", "desc": " After breakfast, as your time, our representative from Nepal Dream Adventure  will drop you off at the Airport before your flight departs.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day – 15: Departure\\";"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.827	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000mkbrljku2fnid	6-day-langtang-valley-treks	6-Day Langtang valley Treks	<h3 data-section-id="1duvf1a" data-start="297" data-end="337">Discover a Short Himalayan Adventure</h3>\n<p data-start="339" data-end="699">The 6-Day L	<h3 data-section-id="1duvf1a" data-start="297" data-end="337">Discover a Short Himalayan Adventure</h3>\n<p data-start="339" data-end="699">The 6-Day Langtang Valley Trek is a rewarding journey through one of Nepal’s most beautiful mountain regions. Located north of Kathmandu, this route combines dramatic Himalayan scenery, peaceful forests, traditional villages, and welcoming teahouses. It is an excellent choice for travelers who want an authentic mountain experience within a limited timeframe.</p>\n<p data-start="701" data-end="1055">The adventure begins with a scenic drive from Kathmandu to Syabrubesi, the gateway to the valley. From there, the trail follows the Langtang River through dense rhododendron and bamboo forests. Along the way, trekkers cross suspension bridges, pass waterfalls, and walk through traditional Tamang settlements surrounded by impressive mountain landscapes.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="1g80td" data-start="1057" data-end="1084">Stunning Mountain Views</h3>\n<p data-start="1086" data-end="1390">A major highlight is reaching <strong data-start="1116" data-end="1133">Kyanjin Gompa</strong>, a peaceful settlement surrounded by spectacular Himalayan peaks. From here, trekkers can hike toward <strong data-start="1236" data-end="1266">Kyanjin Ri at 4,773 meters</strong> for panoramic views of Langtang Lirung, Dorje Lakpa, Gangchempo, Yala Peak, Langshisa Ri, and other snow-covered mountains.</p>\n<p data-start="1392" data-end="1599">The early morning scenery is particularly impressive, with sunlight illuminating the surrounding peaks. The viewpoint also provides excellent opportunities for photography and quiet moments in the mountains.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="18cffhg" data-start="1601" data-end="1630">Experience Tamang Culture</h3>\n<p data-start="1632" data-end="1986">The journey offers more than beautiful landscapes. Travelers can experience the traditions and hospitality of local Tamang communities while staying in family-run teahouses and enjoying traditional Nepalese meals. The route passes through villages that reflect the resilience of local communities and their strong connection to the Himalayan environment.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="1o3s71b" data-start="1988" data-end="2021">A Perfect Short Trek in Nepal</h3>\n<p data-start="2023" data-end="2298">With manageable walking days and well-established trails, this adventure is suitable for both beginners and experienced hikers with a reasonable level of fitness. The gradual change in altitude also allows trekkers to enjoy the scenery and cultural experiences along the way.</p>\n<p data-start="2300" data-end="2493">For travelers seeking spectacular mountain views, peaceful trails, local culture, and an authentic Himalayan experience, this <strong data-start="2426" data-end="2450">Langtang Valley trek</strong> offers an unforgettable six-day adventure.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/IMG_20260220_124757.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	6 Days	599	langtang	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Feb	Hotels in Kathmandu and teahouses during the trek	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{langtang-region}	<ul>\n<li><strong>Weather Conditions:</strong> Be prepared for rapidly changing weather. Dress in layers, as the temperature can vary significantly between day and night. Also put waterproof gear for unexpected rain.</li>\n<li><strong>Road Conditions:</strong> The roads can be rough and dusty, so ensure your Scorpio Jeep is in good condition.</li>\n<li><strong>Difficulty Levels:</strong> Our trips include challenging ascents and descents. Ensure you're in good physical condition.</li>\n<li><strong>Altitude Awareness:</strong> Gradual acclimatization is crucial. Follow our guides’ advice to avoid altitude sickness.</li>\n<li><strong>Proper Gear:</strong> Wear sturdy, comfortable boots or shoes and bring essentials like a hat, sunscreen, and a first-aid kit. Tips for the Trip:</li>\n<li><strong>Local Culture:</strong> Respect local customs and communities. Your journey will take you through diverse cultural regions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n	<ul>\n<li>Authorized English-speaking/local Expert Trekking Guide x1 during trek  Hotel pickup and drop-off</li>\n<li>Road permits, all necessary paperwork, and Trekkers' Information Management System fee(s)</li>\n<li>All applicable government tax</li>\n<li>Accommodation x6 nights during the trek</li>\n<li>All meals (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner) during the trek</li>\n<li>Shared Transportation by bus from Kathmandu to Syafrubesi and Syafrubesi to Kathmandu as per the itinerary.</li>\n<li>All expenses for the guide; meals, accommodation, salary, equipment, insurance, and transportation.</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Soft and hard drinks</li>\n<li>Travel and rescue insurance</li>\n<li>International flights; Nepalese visa fee</li>\n<li>Tips for guide(s), porter(s) and driver(s)</li>\n<li>Personal expenses (phone calls, laundry, bar bills, battery recharge, extra porters, bottle or boiled water,<br />\nshower, etc.)</li>\n<li>Extra night accommodation in Kathmandu or else because of early arrival, late departure, or early return<br />\nfrom the trip due to any reason other than the scheduled itinerary</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Sunscreen</li>\n<li>Cash</li>\n<li>Pairs of socks</li>\n<li>Trousers (x3+)</li>\n<li>Backpack for yourself</li>\n<li>Water bottle</li>\n<li>Headlamp</li>\n<li>Jacket(down)</li>\n<li>T-shirts(x3+)</li>\n<li>Hat</li>\n<li>Underwear</li>\n<li>Some Snacks</li>\n<li>Normal jacket</li>\n<li>Sunglass</li>\n</ul>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Leaving Kathmandu early in the morning, you’ll set off on a scenic drive to Syabrubesi, the gateway to the beautiful Langtang Valley. The road winds along hillsides and riverbanks, passing terraced farms, small roadside villages, and dramatic mountain scenery that gradually feels more remote and untouched. After reaching Syabrubesi, you’ll begin a gentle two-hour walk through peaceful forests, following the soothing sound of the Langtang River as it flows beside the trail. The path is relatively easy, making it a pleasant introduction to the trek, with fresh mountain air and glimpses of local life along the way. By late afternoon, you’ll arrive in the quiet settlement of Pahiro, where you can relax, enjoy a warm meal, and settle in for the night surrounded by nature.\\";s:23", "elev": 1750, "title": "Day 1: Kathmandu to Syabrubesi to Pairo (1,750m)(6 hrs drive, 2 hrs trek)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Leaving Pahiro after breakfast, you’ll continue your trek toward Ghoda Tabela, following the well-marked trail alongside the rushing Langtang River. The path winds through thick forests of bamboo and rhododendron, gradually gaining elevation as you move deeper into the valley. Along the way, you’ll pass through the small settlement of Bamboo, a peaceful stop surrounded by greenery, and continue toward Rimche, where the scenery begins to feel more alpine and open. Waterfalls cascade down the rocky cliffs, suspension bridges cross the river below, and the mountain air grows cooler and fresher with every step. By the time you reach Ghoda Tabela, the valley widens into open pastureland, offering a calm and scenic setting for your overnight stay.\\";s:", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Pahiro to Ghoda Tabela (2,900m/9,514 ft)(6 hrs trek)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "You’ll continue your trek from Ghoda Tabela to Kyanjin Gompa, following a scenic trail that takes you through the charming villages of Langtang Village and Thangsyap. Along the way, you’ll get a glimpse of daily life in the mountains, meet the warm and welcoming Tamang people, and experience their unique culture and traditions. The trek offers spectacular views of the surrounding Himalayan peaks, and once you reach Kyanjin Gompa, you can explore the quiet village streets, visit the local cheese factory, and wander through peaceful monasteries. You’ll spend the night in Kyanjin Gompa, surrounded by the serene beauty of the mountains.\\";s:23", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Ghoda Tabela to Kyanjin Gompa (3,870m/12,696 ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "Early in the morning, we hike up to Kyanjin Ri, one of the most famous viewpoints in the Langtang region, offering stunning sunrise views over Langtang Lirung, glaciers, and surrounding Himalayan peaks. After spending time at the top and enjoying the panoramic scenery, we descend back to Kyanjin Gompa and continue our trek down the valley. Following the same trail, we gradually walk back through alpine landscapes and settlements, finally reaching Thyangshyap, a peaceful village surrounded by mountains.", "elev": 3140, "title": "Day 4: Hike to Kyanjin Ri &amp; Trek Back to Thyangshyap (3,140m)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "After breakfast at Thyangshyap, we begin our final descent of the trek. The trail passes through beautiful forests, traditional villages, suspension bridges, and river valleys as we gradually lose altitude. Walking alongside the Langtang River, we retrace our steps through familiar landscapes until we finally reach Syabrubesi, marking the completion of our trekking journey in the Langtang region.", "elev": 1460, "title": "Day 5:  Trek from Thyangshyap to Syabrubesi (1,460m)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "After breakfast, we bid farewell to the beautiful Langtang region and begin our scenic drive back to Kathmandu. The journey follows the Trishuli River, passing through winding mountain roads, green hills, villages, and terraced fields. As we descend towards the city, the landscapes gradually change from peaceful mountain scenery to the busy streets of Kathmandu, marking the end of our Langtang adventure.", "elev": 1400, "title": " Day 6: Drive from Syabrubesi to Kathmandu (1,400m)"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.837	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000okbrl1wyv1zef	trekking-mardi-himal-trek	Mardi Himal Trek	<h2>Discover the Hidden Gem of the Annapurna Region</h2>\n<p data-start="81" data-end="519">The <strong data-start="85" data-end="105"><a href="https:/	<h2>Discover the Hidden Gem of the Annapurna Region</h2>\n<p data-start="81" data-end="519">The <strong data-start="85" data-end="105"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=adb3d433e634a8e1&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnssG9LEKLkxZaPmemOgoBdgwTn47A:1782908668596&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gIHbHEqXWbyThyPdUCKqTmZAKzBcRFb2qe3OBMfh6G5UU95rQ_0RWnxsY5je01K1qLprE6MJt04e2R0nugQa8ieshVwOqnImMfVyA2WhDka1Z9CIbplpiYbsLOxumutBZeEDE7TxWlqF7BJrRC0ciPoHqV_gg&amp;q=Mardi+himal&amp;sa=X&amp;sqi=2&amp;ved=2ahUKEwi78u6uvLGVAxUtSGcHHeepK1IQtKgLegQIGRAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Mardi Himal</a> Trek</strong> is one of the best short trekking adventures in Nepal. Located in the famous Annapurna region, this peaceful trail offers stunning mountain views, beautiful forests, and authentic village life. Opened to trekkers in 2012, the route is still less crowded than the popular Annapurna Base Camp Trek. It is an excellent choice for travelers who want a quieter Himalayan experience without missing spectacular scenery.</p>\n<p data-start="521" data-end="877">The journey begins with a scenic drive from Kathmandu to Pokhara, followed by a short drive to Kande. From there, the trail climbs through lush rhododendron forests, peaceful oak woods, and charming Gurung and Magar villages. As you gain altitude, the landscape changes into open alpine meadows and narrow ridges with breathtaking views in every direction.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="1gipd5g" data-start="879" data-end="909">Spectacular Himalayan Views</h3>\n<p data-start="911" data-end="1310">One of the biggest highlights of the <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/annapurna-circuit-trek/"><strong data-start="948" data-end="968">Mardi Himal Trek</strong> </a>is the incredible mountain scenery. Throughout the trek, you will enjoy close-up views of Machhapuchhre (Fishtail), Annapurna South, Hiunchuli, Mardi Himal, and several other snow-covered peaks. The hike to Mardi Himal Base Camp, at approximately 4,500 meters, rewards you with one of the finest panoramic viewpoints in the Annapurna region.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="18h1qye" data-start="1312" data-end="1361">Perfect for Beginners and Experienced Trekkers</h3>\n<p data-start="1363" data-end="1727">The <strong data-start="1367" data-end="1387">Mardi Himal Trek</strong> is suitable for both beginners and experienced hikers. The trail is well marked and does not require technical climbing skills. Although you will reach a high altitude, the itinerary allows enough time for proper acclimatization. Comfortable teahouses along the route provide warm meals, cozy accommodation, and genuine Nepali hospitality.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="1f0avqp" data-start="1729" data-end="1766">A Short Trek with Lasting Memories</h3>\n<p data-start="1768" data-end="2176">Whether you are visiting Nepal for the first time or returning for another adventure, the <strong data-start="1858" data-end="1878">Mardi Himal Trek</strong> offers an unforgettable Himalayan experience. It combines breathtaking mountain landscapes, rich local culture, peaceful trails, and rewarding viewpoints in just a few days. If you are looking for an adventure that is both accessible and unforgettable, the Mardi Himal Trek is an excellent choice.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Mardi-4.jpeg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	7 Days	699	annapurna	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Jan	Hotel/ Teahouse	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{annapurna-region}	<p>• Scenic mountain flight and breathtaking Himalayan views<br data-start="283" data-end="286" />• Explore traditional Sherpa villages and local mountain culture<br data-start="350" data-end="353" />• Spectacular views of Mount Everest, Annapurna, Machhapuchhre, and surrounding peaks<br data-start="438" data-end="441" />• Walk through beautiful rhododendron forests and alpine landscapes<br data-start="508" data-end="511" />• Experience stunning sunrise views from high Himalayan viewpoints<br data-start="577" data-end="580" />• Visit remote mountain settlements and traditional teahouses<br data-start="641" data-end="644" />• Enjoy panoramic views of glaciers, valleys, and snow-covered peaks<br data-start="712" data-end="715" />• Adventure trekking experience in one of the world’s most famous trekking regions<br data-start="797" data-end="800" />• Discover peaceful trails away from crowded trekking routes<br data-start="860" data-end="863" />• Memorable Himalayan adventure with experienced local guides</p>\n	<p data-start="228" data-end="930">• Airport pickup and drop-off by private vehicle<br data-start="276" data-end="279" />• All ground transportation as mentioned in the itinerary<br data-start="336" data-end="339" />• Domestic flights (if included in the itinerary)<br data-start="388" data-end="391" />• Tourist standard hotel accommodation in Kathmandu / Pokhara with breakfast<br data-start="467" data-end="470" />• Teahouse or lodge accommodation during the trek<br data-start="519" data-end="522" />• All meals during the trek (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner)<br data-start="576" data-end="579" />• Experienced English-speaking trekking guide<br data-start="624" data-end="627" />• Required number of porters (1 porter for 2 trekkers)<br data-start="681" data-end="684" />• Trekking permits<br />\n• TIMS (Trekkers Information Management System) card<br data-start="786" data-end="789" />• Guide and porter insurance during the trek<br data-start="833" data-end="836" />• Government taxes and official service charges<br data-start="883" data-end="886" />• Basic first aid kit carried by the guide</p>\n	<p>• International airfare to and from Nepal<br data-start="998" data-end="1001" />• Nepal entry visa fee<br data-start="1023" data-end="1026" />• Personal travel insurance (must cover trekking and evacuation)<br data-start="1090" data-end="1093" />• Personal trekking equipment and gear<br data-start="1131" data-end="1134" />• Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu / Pokhara (unless specified)<br data-start="1194" data-end="1197" />• Extra accommodation due to early arrival, late departure, or flight delays<br data-start="1273" data-end="1276" data-is-only-node="" />• Hot showers, WiFi, and charging fees in mountain lodges<br data-start="1333" data-end="1336" />• Personal expenses such as drinks, snacks, laundry, and phone calls<br data-start="1404" data-end="1407" />• Tips for guide and porter</p>\n	<h2 data-section-id="owr3tl" data-start="507" data-end="518">Clothing</h2>\n<p data-start="520" data-end="849">• Warm down jacket<br data-start="538" data-end="541" />• Waterproof jacket or rain jacket<br data-start="575" data-end="578" />• Lightweight trekking shirts (quick-dry)<br data-start="619" data-end="622" />• Thermal base layers<br data-start="643" data-end="646" />• Warm fleece jacket or sweater<br data-start="677" data-end="680" />• Comfortable trekking pants<br data-start="708" data-end="711" />• Warm hat or woolen cap<br data-start="735" data-end="738" />• Sun hat or cap<br data-start="754" data-end="757" />• Gloves (warm and waterproof)<br data-start="787" data-end="790" />• Several pairs of trekking socks<br data-start="823" data-end="826" />• Comfortable underwear</p>\n<h2 data-section-id="12cy4za" data-start="851" data-end="862">Footwear</h2>\n<p data-start="864" data-end="996">• Trekking boots with good ankle support<br data-start="904" data-end="907" />• Lightweight camp shoes or sandals<br data-start="942" data-end="945" />• Gaiters (optional, useful during snow conditions)</p>\n<h2 data-section-id="19ngyfg" data-start="998" data-end="1019">Trekking Equipment</h2>\n<p data-start="1021" data-end="1294">• Backpack or daypack (30–40L recommended)<br data-start="1063" data-end="1066" />• Duffel bag for porter (if applicable)<br data-start="1105" data-end="1108" />• Trekking poles<br data-start="1124" data-end="1127" />• Headlamp or flashlight with extra batteries<br data-start="1172" data-end="1175" />• Water bottles or hydration system<br data-start="1210" data-end="1213" />• Sunglasses with UV protection<br data-start="1244" data-end="1247" />• Sleeping bag (suitable for cold temperatures)</p>\n<h2 data-section-id="7o5mjf" data-start="1296" data-end="1313">Personal Items</h2>\n<p data-start="1315" data-end="1533">• Personal first aid kit<br data-start="1339" data-end="1342" />• Sunscreen and lip balm<br data-start="1366" data-end="1369" />• Toiletries and personal hygiene items<br data-start="1408" data-end="1411" />• Quick-dry towel<br data-start="1428" data-end="1431" />• Hand sanitizer and wet wipes<br data-start="1461" data-end="1464" />• Energy snacks or chocolate bars<br data-start="1497" data-end="1500" />• Camera or smartphone for photos</p>\n<h2 data-section-id="eymysy" data-start="1535" data-end="1563">Optional but Useful Items</h2>\n<p data-start="1565" data-end="1659">• Power bank<br data-start="1577" data-end="1580" />• Travel pillow<br data-start="1595" data-end="1598" />• Earplugs<br data-start="1608" data-end="1611" />• Trekking map or guidebook<br data-start="1638" data-end="1641" />• Notebook and pen</p>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Upon arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport in Kathmandu, our team will welcome you and transfer you to your hotel. After check-in, you can relax after your journey or explore nearby streets of the city. Kathmandu is rich in culture, temples, and historic sites. In the evening, your guide will provide a short briefing about the Mardi Himal trek and help you prepare for the adventure ahead.", "elev": 1345, "title": "Day 1 : Arrival in Kathmandu Airport (1345m)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "The day begi⁠ns with a‌n ear‌ly morning scenic d​r​ive along th‍e Prithvi H‌ighway. The ro‍ad winds alongside‍ the Trishuli Riv​er, known fo⁠r​ w‍hite-water ra‍fting, and‍ pa‌sses through green hills, terraced‍ fields, and smal​l roadside‍ towns. After 6–7 hour‍s, you’ll reach Po‌khara, a l⁠aid-back lake​sid‍e city. In the even​ing,‍ you can take a peaceful wa​lk alon⁠g Phe​wa L⁠ake,‌ with reflections of Machhap⁠uch​hre and Anna‍pu​rna in‍ the water.\\nHighligh‍ts: Sceni⁠c‌ driv⁠e, Phewa Lake s‍unset view,‌ Pokhara’s r⁠e​laxing⁠ atmo⁠s​ph⁠ere.\\nOvernigh‌t:‍ Hot‌el in Pokha‌ra.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:17:\\"Kathmandu (1345m)\\";s:21:\\"day_wise_e", "elev": 820, "title": "Day 2: Drive from Kathm⁠a‌n​du⁠ to‌ Pokhara (820m)\\";s:11:\\"de"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "After breakfast​, a sh​ort driv‌e takes yo⁠u to Kande, the​ s‌tarting⁠ point of the trek. The trail first cl‌imbs steadily to Australian Camp, a famous viewp‍oin‍t of​fering wi‍de panoramas of Annapurna S‍outh, Hiu⁠nchuli, Mac​hhap‍uchhr​e, and Lamj⁠ung H⁠imal. Continu‌ing th‌roug​h P‍othana vil​lage, you’ll pass st⁠on‍e-pave⁠d p‍at​hs and terrace‌d fields‍ be⁠fo‍re‌ reaching Deur‍a‌li, situated on⁠ a ridg⁠e with stunning v‍iews of the vall⁠ey below. The evening her​e is pe‌aceful, surrounded by forests an‌d cool mountain air.\\nT‍rekking Dur‌ation: 4–5 hours.\\nHig‌hl‍i‍ghts⁠: Australian Camp views, Gurung v⁠illage l‌ife, pea‌ceful ridge-top setting.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:14:\\"Pokhara (820m)\\";s:21:\\"day_wise_en", "elev": 0, "title": "D‍a⁠y‌ 3: Drive to Kande &amp; T‌rek to Deura‍li (2,125‍m)\\";s:11:\\"desc"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "‌Today’s trail le‌av‍es‌ the village​s behind and enters a dense forest of⁠ r‌h⁠odode​ndron, oak⁠, and maple trees. The fo‌rest f⁠eels mystical, with the sound of bir‌ds a⁠nd occasional glimpses of snow-capped peaks through the trees.​ Few settlements are found alon‍g th​is route, mak⁠ing it one of the qu‍i​eter pa‍rts of the trek.⁠ After 5–6 h‍ours, you a‍r‍rive at Forest Camp, a s​mall cluste⁠r of te​ahouses surround⁠ed by ta⁠ll trees‍. The night here is‍ c‌older, and the sky is often filled with‍ s‌tars.\\nTrek‌king Dur‌ation⁠: 5–‍6 hours.\\nHi⁠ghlig‍hts: Rhododendron forests, peacef‍ul trekking environm‍en⁠t, starry night sky.\\nOvernight: Teahouse in Forest⁠ C‍amp.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:16:\\"Deurali (2,125m)\\";s:21:\\"", "elev": 2600, "title": "​Day 4: Trek from D⁠eura​li to Forest Ca‌mp (2,600m)\\";s:11:\\""}, {"day": "5", "desc": "The trail ascends steadily, pass‌ing Low Camp (3​,050m) where th‌e tr‌ees thin out and open vi⁠stas be‌gin. You wi​ll walk alon⁠g a ridg⁠e⁠ above the clouds, wit‍h magni‌fic​ent view​s of Machhapuc⁠hhre’s sh‍arp‍ peak directly ahead and A‍nn‌apurna South to‍ the wes​t. The higher you clim⁠b, the mo‍re dr‍amati​c the⁠ landscapes become, with wide meadows and al​pine s⁠hru​bs replacin​g‍ for‍ests‌. Arriving at High Camp,‌ you’ll b⁠e reward‍ed with sweeping views and cozy teahouses perched on the ridge.\\nTrekking Du⁠ration: 6–7 hours‌.\\nHighlights:‌ First clear​ views of Annapurna a​nd M​ach‍hap⁠uchhre, ridge-t​o​p trekking, alpine meado‍ws.\\nOve‌rnigh⁠t: T⁠eahouse in High Camp‌.⁠\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:20:\\"Forest Camp (2,600m)\\";s:21:\\"day_wise", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5‍: Trek fr‍om Forest⁠ Camp​ to High Ca⁠mp (3⁠,580m)\\";s:11:\\"desc"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Thi‍s i​s the most​ e‍xciting⁠ and challe​ng​ing​ da‍y o​f the trek. A‍n‌ ea‌rly m⁠ornin⁠g start all⁠ows you⁠ to reach Mardi Himal Base‍ Camp in time for sunrise. The tra‌il is s‍tee​p an‍d rocky‍, but as you climb hi⁠gher, th​e m‌ou⁠ntains appear clos⁠er with every step. From the top, yo‍u’‌ll sta⁠nd‌ be⁠neath the to​wering Annapurna South (7,‌219m) and face-‍to-f⁠a​ce with Machh​apuchh‌re (6,9⁠93m). The golden morning light shinin‍g on snow peak‌s cre‌ates​ an unforge⁠tta​ble sight. After s⁠pending time at‍ the base ca‍mp,⁠ yo‌u retu​rn to Hig​h Camp fo‍r a warm m‌eal a‌nd rest.\\nTrekk​ing Duration: 6–7 hours rou‌nd tri⁠p.\\nHighlig‌hts: Su⁠nrise over​ A‍nnapurna Massif, standing at (4,500m), breat​hta‍king panoramas.\\nOvernight: Teahouse in High Camp.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:18:\\"High Camp (3,580m)\\";s:21:\\"day_wise_ending_point\\";s:18:\\"High Ca", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6:‌ Hi‌ke⁠ to Mardi Hima⁠l Base Camp‍ (​4,500m) &amp; Return to High Camp\\";s:11:\\"desc"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "Tod‍ay is mostly downhill, de​scending throug⁠h⁠ forests and traditional Gurung villag‍es.‍ Un‍like t‌he upwar‌d route, the desc​e‍nt to​ Si‍d​ing village follows a different pat‍h, offer‌in​g a fre‍sh perspec​tiv‍e of local life, terra‍ced‍ fields,‌ and ri⁠vers. Siding is a charming vi⁠llage wh⁠ere trekk‌ers can‌ experien‍ce auth‍entic Nepali culture and hospitali⁠ty.​ From h​ere, a je⁠ep drive takes you⁠ back to P‌okhara b⁠y evening.\\nTrekking Dura​tion: 5–6 hours t⁠rek + 3–​4‍ hour​s drive.⁠\\nHighlight⁠s:​ Cu‌ltural immersion in Si​ding, scenic countrysi‍de‍, return to Pokhara comforts.​\\nOv‌ernight: Hotel in Pokhara\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:18:\\"High Camp (3,580m)\\";s:21:\\"day_w", "elev": 1750, "title": "Da‌y 7: Trek from High Camp to Siding Village (1,750m) &amp; Drive t​o Pokhara \\";s:"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "After breakfast‍, you r‌eturn to⁠ Kathmandu e​ither​ by t​o⁠urist bus (6–7 hour⁠s). The roa‌d jo‌urney offers one‌ last chance to⁠ admire Nepal‍’s rivers, h‌ills, a‍nd countryside. Upon r⁠each⁠in‍g Kathmand‌u, you can ex‌plor​e its markets for souvenirs or enjoy a farewell di‌n⁠n‍er. If de⁠partin⁠g the s‌a​me day, transfer to the​ airpo‍rt for⁠ you⁠r onward j⁠ourney.\\nHig​hl‍igh‍ts: Scenic return​ jo‌urney, shopping/sight​s​eeing in K​at⁠h‍mandu.\\n‍Overni⁠ght: Hotel i‍n Kat​h​man‌d‍u or dep‍arture.\\n\\";s:23:\\"day_wise_gallery_images\\";s:0:\\"\\";s:24:\\"days_wise_starting_point\\";s:14:\\"Pokhara (820m)\\";s:21:\\"day_wise_", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Drive/Fly Bac⁠k to K⁠athmand‍u (1,350‌m)\\";s:11:\\""}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.843	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000tkbrlvqggn6kw	langtang-valley-yala-peak	Langtang valley Yala peak	<div>\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:f9709b1d-1066-4bab-a69d-da9a46644ce0-1" data-is-intersecting="true"><section dir="auto" data-turn-id="r	<div>\n<div data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:f9709b1d-1066-4bab-a69d-da9a46644ce0-1" data-is-intersecting="true"><section dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:f9709b1d-1066-4bab-a69d-da9a46644ce0-1" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:f9709b1d-1066-4bab-a69d-da9a46644ce0-1" data-testid="conversation-turn-4" data-turn="assistant">\n<div>\n<div data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div>\n<div dir="auto" tabindex="0" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="897073a9-20d0-4137-8ffe-0803a1d359d9" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div>\n<h2 data-section-id="o4nj61" data-start="197" data-end="246">Why Choose the <a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=326223ae55b11ae7&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnvkp6t8f87maj89y5Gv75cGA6X_4A:1787388360591&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832TwKwURgSKi78Lao9SQTWQTCCDIMoePJrL1a7owHukug_NBBwdYjIxudvb2ZgPb0lzkZ0BeL5Q7raKVXdG25pUI116X-Og33oqKjsL7aNZNikucBZQN2ptn0rhC81q-r7fM7cuSNikFpyhiuJ1bxodTxU5wubygSaacWM1v01LJNPYV38A&amp;q=langtang&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwj-2rvC7LOWAxUc1jgGHbv2HssQtKgLegQIJRAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Langtang Valley</a> Yala Peak Trek?</h2>\n<p data-start="248" data-end="703">The <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/langtang-valley-comfort-trek-9-days/">Langtang Valley</a> Yala <strong data-start="344" data-end="378">Trek</strong> combines scenic Himalayan trekking with an exciting peak-climbing experience in Nepal. The journey takes you through lush forests, traditional Tamang villages, peaceful mountain valleys, and impressive high-altitude landscapes.</p>\n<p data-start="608" data-end="949">The adventure begins with a scenic drive from Kathmandu to the trailhead before following the Langtang Valley toward Kyanjin Gompa. Along the way, trekkers pass through rhododendron forests, suspension bridges, rivers, and welcoming mountain communities. The changing scenery provides a wonderful mix of nature, culture, and Himalayan views.</p>\n<p data-start="951" data-end="1262">After reaching Kyanjin Gompa, you have time to acclimatize and explore the surrounding area. The route then leads toward Yala Peak, which stands at approximately 5,520 meters. The climb offers an exciting challenge and rewarding views of Langtang Lirung, Dorje Lakpa, Ganesh Himal, and other snow-covered peaks.</p>\n<p data-start="1264" data-end="1557">Beyond the climb, the journey provides opportunities to experience local culture and enjoy the peaceful atmosphere of the Langtang region. Experienced guides, comfortable teahouse accommodation, and gradual acclimatization make the adventure suitable for trekkers with a good level of fitness.</p>\n<p data-start="1559" data-end="1842">Overall, this journey is an excellent choice for travelers who want to combine a Himalayan trek with a manageable peak-climbing experience. It offers beautiful scenery, cultural encounters, and memorable mountain views without the crowds found on some of Nepal’s more popular routes.</p>\n\n<h3 data-section-id="gculsm" data-start="1844" data-end="1855"></h3>\n</div>\n<div>\n<div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section></div>\n</div>\n<div aria-hidden="true"></div>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/IMG_20260220_221909.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	12 Days	1499	langtang	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Dec	Hotels in Kathmandu and teahouses during the trek	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{langtang-region}	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="1r7qkmc" data-start="171" data-end="262">Trek through the beautiful Langtang Valley, one of Nepal's most scenic Himalayan regions.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1wtev5a" data-start="263" data-end="357">Summit <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Yala Peak</span></span> (5,500m), a perfect introductory trekking peak.</li>\n<li data-section-id="hf0elx" data-start="358" data-end="464">Enjoy breathtaking views of Langtang Lirung, Dorje Lakpa, Shishapangma, and surrounding Himalayan peaks.</li>\n<li data-section-id="feh911" data-start="465" data-end="543">Visit the traditional Tamang villages and experience local mountain culture.</li>\n<li data-section-id="irnxri" data-start="544" data-end="619">Explore the historic settlement of <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Kyanjin Gompa</span></span>.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1q42b38" data-start="620" data-end="694">Hike to Kyanjin Ri for spectacular sunrise and panoramic mountain views.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1byyoqm" data-start="695" data-end="757">Walk through lush forests of rhododendron, pine, and bamboo.</li>\n<li data-section-id="rioxuz" data-start="758" data-end="832">Encounter diverse wildlife within <span class="hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline"><span class="whitespace-normal">Langtang National Park</span></span>.</li>\n<li data-section-id="yt9mpg" data-start="833" data-end="901">Experience comfortable teahouse accommodation throughout the trek.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1he98uu" data-start="902" data-end="985">Ideal combination of cultural trekking and non-technical peak climbing adventure.</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="17j6fbl" data-start="61" data-end="114">Airport pick-up and drop-off service in Kathmandu.</li>\n<li data-section-id="w536af" data-start="115" data-end="175">2 nights hotel accommodation in Kathmandu with breakfast.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1p6q0zx" data-start="176" data-end="266">Transportation from Kathmandu to Syabrubesi and Kathmandu</li>\n<li data-section-id="q0xgu1" data-start="267" data-end="313">Teahouse accommodation throughout the trek.</li>\n<li data-section-id="8hrggg" data-start="314" data-end="382">Three meals daily during the trek (breakfast, lunch, and dinner).</li>\n<li data-section-id="1oruw2" data-start="439" data-end="486">Experienced English-speaking trekking guide.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1dnqnho" data-start="487" data-end="538">Assistant guide for larger groups (if required).</li>\n<li data-section-id="15pwufm" data-start="539" data-end="595">Professional Yala Peak climbing guide for summit day.</li>\n<li data-section-id="3mpukp" data-start="596" data-end="636">Langtang National Park Entry Permit.</li>\n<li data-section-id="6rofvt" data-start="637" data-end="693">TIMS (Trekkers' Information Management System) Card.</li>\n<li data-section-id="ufadu" data-start="694" data-end="724">Yala Peak Climbing Permit.</li>\n<li data-section-id="gumhg" data-start="725" data-end="797">Group climbing equipment, including ropes and necessary safety gear.</li>\n<li data-section-id="g9me49" data-start="798" data-end="871">Porter service (1 porter for every 2 trekkers, carrying up to 20 kg).</li>\n<li data-section-id="k1dizw" data-start="872" data-end="956">Guide, climbing guide, and porter salaries, meals, accommodation, and insurance.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1b6850c" data-start="957" data-end="1010">Comprehensive first aid kit carried by the guide.</li>\n<li data-section-id="10mu2lv" data-start="1011" data-end="1061">Government taxes and official service charges.</li>\n</ul>\n	<div class="qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot">\n<div class="" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:49c232bf-1391-4892-9434-2367b7b5f0e0-0" data-is-intersecting="true">\n<section class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:49c232bf-1391-4892-9434-2367b7b5f0e0-0" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:49c232bf-1391-4892-9434-2367b7b5f0e0-0" data-testid="conversation-turn-2" data-turn="assistant">\n<div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)">\n<div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" data-conversation-screenshot-content="">\n<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow">\n<div class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" dir="auto" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="1767ad6e-93c0-4b1b-855b-52e861a5bdb6" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden">\n<div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling">\n<ol data-start="1085" data-end="1761" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">\n<li data-section-id="12f473o" data-start="1085" data-end="1128">International airfare to and from Nepal.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1lb85ot" data-start="1129" data-end="1154">Nepal entry visa fees.</li>\n<li data-section-id="79zs88" data-start="1155" data-end="1186">Travel and rescue insurance.</li>\n<li data-section-id="g91vaw" data-start="1187" data-end="1282">Personal climbing equipment (boots, crampons, harness, helmet, ice axe, sleeping bag, etc.).</li>\n<li data-section-id="w6z0cm" data-start="1283" data-end="1375">Personal expenses such as drinks, snacks, hot showers, Wi-Fi, charging fees, and laundry.</li>\n<li data-section-id="chee7w" data-start="1376" data-end="1409">Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu.</li>\n<li data-section-id="tgtyp6" data-start="1410" data-end="1505">Extra accommodation in Kathmandu due to early arrival, late departure, or itinerary changes.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1lboqgd" data-start="1506" data-end="1632">Costs arising from flight cancellations, natural disasters, weather conditions, strikes, or other unforeseen circumstances.</li>\n<li data-section-id="10491ly" data-start="1633" data-end="1682">Tips for guides, climbing guides, and porters.</li>\n<li data-section-id="1wvs64o" data-start="1683" data-end="1761" data-is-last-node="">Any services not specifically mentioned in the "Package Includes" section.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"></div>\n<div class="mt-3 w-full empty:hidden">\n<div class="text-center"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="pointer-events-none -mt-px h-px translate-y-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom)-14*var(--spacing))]" aria-hidden="true"></div>\n	<h3 data-section-id="u9i6vf" data-start="62" data-end="84">🎒 Backpack &amp; Bags</h3>\n<p data-start="85" data-end="156">• Daypack (30–40L)<br data-start="103" data-end="106" />• Duffel bag or trekking backpack<br data-start="139" data-end="142" />• Rain cover</p>\n<h3 data-section-id="sbghua" data-start="158" data-end="173">👕 Clothing</h3>\n<p data-start="174" data-end="336">• Trekking shirts and pants<br data-start="201" data-end="204" />• Fleece jacket<br data-start="219" data-end="222" />• Down jacket<br data-start="235" data-end="238" />• Waterproof jacket and pants<br data-start="267" data-end="270" />• Thermal base layers<br data-start="291" data-end="294" />• Warm hat, gloves, socks, and underwear</p>\n<h3 data-section-id="1yr0x85" data-start="338" data-end="353">🥾 Footwear</h3>\n<p data-start="354" data-end="450">• Waterproof trekking boots<br data-start="381" data-end="384" />• Mountaineering boots (for Yala Peak)<br data-start="422" data-end="425" />• Camp shoes or sandals</p>\n<h3 data-section-id="vn607r" data-start="452" data-end="472">🧗 Climbing Gear</h3>\n<p data-start="473" data-end="539">• Helmet<br data-start="481" data-end="484" />• Harness<br data-start="493" data-end="496" />• Crampons<br data-start="506" data-end="509" />• Ice axe<br data-start="518" data-end="521" />• Trekking poles</p>\n<h3 data-section-id="b09e8h" data-start="541" data-end="561">😴 Sleeping Gear</h3>\n<p data-start="562" data-end="598">• Sleeping bag (-15°C recommended)</p>\n<h3 data-section-id="1b0sdcs" data-start="600" data-end="622">🕶️ Personal Items</h3>\n<p data-start="623" data-end="735">• Sunglasses<br data-start="635" data-end="638" />• Headlamp<br data-start="648" data-end="651" />• Water bottles<br data-start="666" data-end="669" />• Sunscreen and lip balm<br data-start="693" data-end="696" />• Personal toiletries and medications</p>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "We meet you outside of Tribhuvan International Airport (TIA). We will be waiting with a warm greeting & take you to your hotel. An evening will have a tour briefing about hole trip. over in hotel.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrived in Kathmandu(1350m/4429ft0)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Today you will start trek with a scenic drive from Kathmandu to syabrubesi the gateway to Langtang and enjoy the Picturesque landscapes along the way and get ready for the adventure ahead.\\n\\n\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Kathmandu drive to syabrubesi (1550m/5085ft/6h)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "After breakfast you will start trek from Syabrubesi to lama hotel, immersing yourself in the peaceful atmosphere of the Langtang region.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Syabrubesi to Lama hotel(2380m/7880ft/6h)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "We continue walking from lama hotel to Langtang where you will be surrounded by stunning mountain vista and luse green forest you will explore the charming Langtang village and Soka in the nature beauty of the reason.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Lama hotel to Langtang(3430m/11253ft/7h)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "We continue trek from Langtang to Kyanjing Gompa a renowned monastery in the area, enjoy the breathtaking views of the snowcapped peaks and immerses yourself in the spiritual atmosphere of the monastery.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Langtang to Kyanjin Gompa (3870m/12697ft/4h)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "We take one more day at kyanjin Gompa to explore the beauty of Langtang and acclimatize ourselves to the increasing altitude before heading for the Yala peak. the highlight to visit today Kyanjin ri, cheese factory and monastery.\\n\\"", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Acclimatization day at Kyanjin Gompa "}, {"day": "7", "desc": "We leave the final human settlement in the highland and head towards the rocky glacier route with a fantastic view of the pristine glacier and Himalaya peaks, we walk towards the Yala base camp. upon arrival our team set up camp in appropriate spot, and we start preparing some warm food. Then time for basic climbing skills training for peak. Overnight in tent. ", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Kyanjin Gompa to Yala peak Base camp(4800m/15748ft/5h)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "The most waiting & exciting day of your trip (Are you ready) today. We leave our camp early in the morning & climb to yala peak. We plan to summit before noon if everything fine. The final 40 meters will be more challenging please listen your body and guide carefully. Once we get top the views are just wow wow such as Shishapangma, Nayak ang, Dorje Lakpa, Langtang Lirung, Ganchenop and many more. Then we slowly desecent to the base camp. About 2 hours we reach back base camp we collecting bag take a rest for while we continue walk back to Kyanjin Gompa for the night. Now it is time to celebrate the victory.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Summit Yala peak (5732m/18802ft) &amp; back to Kyanjin Gompa"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "After breakfast you will trek back from Kyanjin Gompa to lama hotel, retracing your steps and taking in the familiar sights of the region and enjoy the peacefull surroundings the sense of accomplishment as you make your way back.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Kyanjin Gompa to Lama hotel(2380m/7808ft/6-7h)"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "We continue our hike back to Syabrubesi via rimche bamboo a small Sherpa or tamang camp.by lunch time we reach town and enjoy the rest time with the crew. evening enjoy your dinner with strong team.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Trek back from lama to Syabrubesi(1503m/4931ft/5h)"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "Today we will drive back to Kathmandu, bringing an end to your Langtang and Yala peak trek. You will reflect on the incredible experience, beautiful landscapes and the sense of accomplishment you have gained throughout the journey.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Drive back to Kathmandu(1350m/6h)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "Today you enjoy your last moment in Kathmandu. We will drop you airport for your final departure 3 hours before your flight namaste.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Fly back home"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.86	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000vkbrlh2eqvli4	chum-valley-trek-16-days	Chum Valley Trek | Remote Manaslu Cultural Trek Nepal	<h2 data-section-id="fi34s6" data-start="399" data-end="427"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sa=X&amp;sca_esv=326223ae55b11ae7&amp;sxsrf=APpeQn	<h2 data-section-id="fi34s6" data-start="399" data-end="427"><a href="https://www.google.com/search?sa=X&amp;sca_esv=326223ae55b11ae7&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnvEvzKRGeF6z42LVdhsZArGP7iO7Q:1787387832047&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gLBqm8s-GD1U00Y35xg2IBZBhWxEYXfaDQIFbVcjhhGSy7WaSBQHpqE8IzTtbP5PaQYw_LhmcQl-1k6AdIfhJcZo5f41YteImmkQfUxYVSsjFRJeUpJr7xI8TG7bkhSNbCW-9CUcvN5jhP2GVaLUYN3TVnGsQ&amp;q=chum+valley&amp;ved=2ahUKEwiu97fG6rOWAxVmyjgGHQO9OTIQtKgLegQIDxAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Chum Valley</a> Trek Overview</h2>\n<p data-start="429" data-end="842">The <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/manaslu-chum-valley-trek-19-days/"><strong data-start="433" data-end="453">Chum Valley Trek</strong> </a>is a rewarding 16-day journey into one of Nepal’s most remote Himalayan regions. Located in the Manaslu area, this peaceful valley is known for its Tibetan-influenced culture, ancient monasteries, traditional villages, and spectacular mountain scenery. Away from busy trekking routes, the journey offers an authentic experience surrounded by pristine landscapes and welcoming communities.</p>\n<p data-start="844" data-end="1207">The adventure begins with a scenic drive from Kathmandu to Machha Khola. From there, the trail follows the Budhi Gandaki River through forests, terraced fields, suspension bridges, and traditional settlements. Along the way, trekkers pass through Jagat, Lokpa, Chumling, Chhokang Paro, and Nile while experiencing the region’s unique culture and warm hospitality.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="27votb" data-start="1209" data-end="1242">Explore the Sacred Chum Valley</h2>\n<p data-start="1244" data-end="1601">One of the major highlights is a visit to <strong data-start="1286" data-end="1298">Mu Gompa</strong>, an important spiritual center in the region. Trekkers can explore ancient Buddhist sites, prayer walls, and traditional settlements while learning about the customs preserved by local communities. The route also provides beautiful views of Ganesh Himal, Himalchuli, and surrounding snow-covered peaks.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="1yo4q3d" data-start="1603" data-end="1644">Experience Remote Himalayan Landscapes</h2>\n<p data-start="1646" data-end="1951">The trail features deep valleys, alpine meadows, forests, rivers, and rugged mountain terrain. As the elevation increases, gradual acclimatization allows trekkers to adjust comfortably while enjoying changing landscapes. The highest point of the journey reaches approximately 5,160 meters above sea level.</p>\n\n<h2 data-section-id="1usd6mg" data-start="1953" data-end="1988">Why Choose the Chum Valley Trek?</h2>\n<p data-start="1990" data-end="2402">This adventure is ideal for travelers looking for a combination of cultural discovery, peaceful trails, and impressive Himalayan scenery. From ancient monasteries and remote villages to dramatic mountain landscapes, every section offers a memorable experience. The <strong data-start="2255" data-end="2275">Chum Valley Trek</strong> provides an excellent opportunity to explore a hidden Himalayan destination while connecting with local traditions and nature.</p>	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/WhatsApp-Image-2026-01-28-at-15.30.00-1.jpeg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	16 Days	1499	manaslu	Moderate		March -June , Oct -Dec	Hotels in Kathmandu and teahouses during the trek	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{manaslu-region}	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="1537a9" data-start="51" data-end="148">Explore the remote and sacred Tsum Valley, often called the “Hidden Valley of Happiness”</li>\n<li data-section-id="1hme9re" data-start="149" data-end="223">Visit ancient Buddhist monasteries like Mu Gompa and Rachen Gompa</li>\n<li data-section-id="lq09ds" data-start="224" data-end="305">Experience authentic Tibetan-influenced culture and traditional village life</li>\n<li data-section-id="1r98312" data-start="306" data-end="389">Scenic drive from Kathmandu to Machha Khola through rivers, hills, and valleys</li>\n<li data-section-id="o0bmrl" data-start="390" data-end="465">Trek through untouched landscapes of the Manaslu Conservation Area</li>\n<li data-section-id="zu57ha" data-start="466" data-end="551">Walk along beautiful Budhi Gandaki River with suspension bridges and deep gorges</li>\n<li data-section-id="1d4aq27" data-start="552" data-end="621">Spot diverse Himalayan flora, fauna, and peaceful alpine scenery</li>\n<li data-section-id="in0li2" data-start="622" data-end="701">Reach high viewpoints with dramatic views of Manaslu and surrounding peaks</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="1oshnab" data-start="131" data-end="181">All airport pick-up and drop-off in Kathmandu</li>\n<li data-section-id="w2xdko" data-start="182" data-end="243">3 nights hotel accommodation in Kathmandu with breakfast</li>\n<li data-section-id="17z8n8t" data-start="244" data-end="308">Full board meals (breakfast, lunch, dinner) during the trek</li>\n<li data-section-id="autvey" data-start="309" data-end="354">Licensed English-speaking trekking guide</li>\n<li data-section-id="o7fcr7" data-start="355" data-end="432">Required permits (Manaslu Conservation Area Permit &amp; Tsum Valley Permit)</li>\n<li data-section-id="19mfdtz" data-start="433" data-end="499">Private jeep transport (Kathmandu – Machha Khola – Kathmandu)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1jlftl4" data-start="500" data-end="549">Teahouse/lodge accommodation during the trek</li>\n<li data-section-id="1byfnix" data-start="550" data-end="609">First aid kit and necessary trekking support equipment</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li data-section-id="t4muf2" data-start="638" data-end="678">International airfare to/from Nepal</li>\n<li data-section-id="1ve9p26" data-start="679" data-end="720">Nepal visa fees and travel insurance</li>\n<li data-section-id="18qi10l" data-start="721" data-end="776">Personal expenses (snacks, drinks, phone, laundry)</li>\n<li data-section-id="nofryz" data-start="777" data-end="831">Hot showers, WiFi, and charging fees in teahouses</li>\n<li data-section-id="hgk9kq" data-start="832" data-end="871">Tips for guide, porter, and driver</li>\n<li data-section-id="115102q" data-start="872" data-end="928">Porter service (available on request at extra cost)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mq5mr8" data-start="929" data-end="997">Extra accommodation or meals due to early return/late departure</li>\n<li data-section-id="9cwe0m" data-start="998" data-end="1053">Emergency evacuation or rescue costs (if required)</li>\n<li data-section-id="9cwe0m" data-start="998" data-end="1053">City sightseeing entrance fee</li>\n</ul>\n	<p data-start="244" data-end="687"><strong data-start="244" data-end="256">Clothing</strong><br data-start="256" data-end="259" />• Lightweight trekking pants and shorts<br data-start="298" data-end="301" />• Moisture-wicking t-shirts (short and long sleeves)<br data-start="353" data-end="356" />• Insulating fleece or down jacket<br data-start="390" data-end="393" />• Waterproof and windproof jacket<br data-start="426" data-end="429" />• Thermal base layers (top and bottom)<br data-start="467" data-end="470" />• Warm trekking gloves and liner gloves<br data-start="509" data-end="512" />• Hat or cap for sun protection<br data-start="543" data-end="546" data-is-only-node="" />• Warm hat/beanie for high altitudes<br data-start="582" data-end="585" />• Neck gaiter or buff<br data-start="606" data-end="609" />• Trekking socks (wool or synthetic)<br data-start="645" data-end="648" />• Gaiters (optional, for snow or mud)</p>\n<p data-start="689" data-end="809"><strong data-start="689" data-end="701">Footwear</strong><br data-start="701" data-end="704" />• Sturdy trekking boots (well broken-in, waterproof)<br data-start="756" data-end="759" />• Lightweight camp shoes or sandals for evenings</p>\n<p data-start="811" data-end="978"><strong data-start="811" data-end="837">Backpack &amp; Accessories</strong><br data-start="837" data-end="840" />• Daypack (20–30L) for daily essentials<br data-start="879" data-end="882" />• Waterproof backpack cover or dry bags<br data-start="921" data-end="924" />• Duffel bag for porters (optional, can be provided)</p>\n<p data-start="980" data-end="1138"><strong data-start="980" data-end="1007">Sleeping &amp; Camping Gear</strong><br data-start="1007" data-end="1010" />• Sleeping bag (rated -10°C to -15°C for high altitudes)<br data-start="1066" data-end="1069" />• Sleeping bag liner (optional for extra warmth)<br data-start="1117" data-end="1120" />• Trekking poles</p>\n<p data-start="1140" data-end="1436"><strong data-start="1140" data-end="1159">Health &amp; Safety</strong><br data-start="1159" data-end="1162" />• Personal first aid kit (plasters, painkillers, blister pads)<br data-start="1224" data-end="1227" />• Sunscreen (SPF 50+) and lip balm<br data-start="1261" data-end="1264" />• Sunglasses with UV protection<br data-start="1295" data-end="1298" />• Water bottles or hydration bladder<br data-start="1334" data-end="1337" />• Water purification tablets or filter<br data-start="1375" data-end="1378" />• Headlamp with spare batteries<br data-start="1409" data-end="1412" />• Personal medications</p>\n<p data-start="1438" data-end="1655"><strong data-start="1438" data-end="1455">Miscellaneous</strong><br data-start="1455" data-end="1458" />• Camera or smartphone with extra memory cards<br data-start="1504" data-end="1507" />• Power bank or solar charger<br data-start="1536" data-end="1539" />• Notebook or trekking journal (optional)<br data-start="1580" data-end="1583" />• Snacks/energy bars<br data-start="1603" data-end="1606" />• Toilet paper and wet wipes<br data-start="1634" data-end="1637" />• Hand sanitizer</p>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Upon arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport, you will be greeted by our representative and transferred to your hotel. After check-in, you can relax or take a short walk around nearby streets and markets. In the evening, meet your trekking guide for a briefing on the Manaslu trek, final gear checks, and preparation tips for the journey ahead.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1,400 m / 4,593 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Today you will explore Kathmandu’s rich cultural heritage. Visit major sites including Pashupatinath Temple, Boudhanath Stupa, and Kathmandu Durbar Square. Experience local markets, traditional architecture, and vibrant streets. The day provides a gentle introduction to Nepalese culture while allowing you to adjust to the city’s altitude before trekking begins.\\";s:", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Full day sightseeing in Kathmandu (1,400 m / 4,593 ft)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "After breakfast, we drive toward Machha Khola, passing through picturesque hills, terraced farms, rivers, and traditional villages. The road gradually becomes more mountainous as we approach the Manaslu region. Upon arrival in Machha Khola, check into a local teahouse and relax before starting the trek tomorrow.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Drive Kathmandu to Machha Khola (870 m / 2,854 ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "The trek begins along the Budhi Gandaki River, passing forests, small settlements, and suspension bridges. Enjoy views of terraced fields and traditional villages as the trail gradually climbs. Jagat is a charming village marking the start of the Manaslu Conservation Area and offers a peaceful overnight stay in local lodges.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Trek Machha Khola to Jagat (1,340 m / 4,396 ft)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Leaving Jagat, the trail climbs through terraced fields and forested valleys. You will pass small villages with traditional homes, prayer flags, and friendly locals. Lokpa is a quiet settlement at the entrance of the Tsum Valley, offering beautiful views and an authentic cultural experience.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Trek Jagat to Lokpa (2,240 m / 7,349 ft)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "Today you enter the scenic Tsum Valley. The trail winds through forests, rivers, and traditional villages. Chumling is surrounded by farmland and offers wonderful views of Ganesh Himal. Experience local Tibetan-influenced culture and enjoy a peaceful night in this remote village.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Trek Lokpa to Chumling (2,386 m / 7,828 ft)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "The trail climbs gradually past ancient monasteries, mani walls, and small settlements. The scenery opens up to spectacular mountain views. Chhokang Paro is the largest village in Tsum Valley, offering overnight accommodations and cultural experiences.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Trek Chumling to Chhokang Paro (3,010 m / 9,875 ft)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "We continue deeper into the upper Tsum Valley. The trail passes villages, Buddhist chortens, and serene landscapes surrounded by Himalayan peaks. Nile is the last permanent settlement in the upper valley and provides a peaceful overnight stop.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Trek Chhokang Paro to Nile (3,361 m / 11,027 ft)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "Today we hike to Mu Gompa, one of the most important monasteries in Tsum Valley. Enjoy the peaceful mountain setting and spiritual atmosphere. After visiting the monastery and surrounding viewpoints, return to Nile for the night.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Exploration day – visit Mu Gompa and return to Nile (3,361 m / 11,027 ft)\\";"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "We begin the descent back toward Chhokang Paro. Enjoy a different perspective of the valley, passing through traditional villages and serene landscapes. Overnight stays are in local lodges, providing rest after the exploration day.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Trek Nile to Chhokang Paro (3,010 m / 9,875 ft)"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "The descent continues through forests and open landscapes. Enjoy scenic views of rivers, mountains, and traditional villages. Arrive in Chumling for a restful overnight stay.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Trek Chhokang Paro to Chumling (2,386 m / 7,828 ft)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "Today we begin the descent from Chumling, passing through forests, terraced fields, and traditional villages. The trail follows gentle slopes along the Budhi Gandaki River, offering beautiful valley and mountain views. Lokpa provides a quiet stop with comfortable lodges for overnight rest.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Trek Chumling to Lokpa (2,240 m / 7,349 ft)"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "The trail continues downhill through forests, small villages, and terraced farms. Trekking today offers new perspectives of the valley and distant mountain views. Jagat, the gateway village to the Manaslu Conservation Area, is where trekkers usually rest before the final day of trekking.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Trek Lokpa to Jagat (1,340 m / 4,396 ft)"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "The last day of trekking follows the Budhi Gandaki River valley through forests and riverside paths. Enjoy scenic views of villages, suspension bridges, and terraced fields along the way. Arrive in Machha Khola in the afternoon to relax and celebrate completing the trek.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Trek Jagat to Machha Khola (870 m / 2,854 ft)"}, {"day": "15", "desc": "After breakfast, we drive from Machha Khola back to Kathmandu. The route passes through rivers, forests, and traditional villages. On arrival, check into your hotel and relax, or explore Kathmandu’s markets and cultural streets one last time.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 15: Drive Machha Khola to Kathmandu (1,400 m / 4,593 ft)"}, {"day": "16", "desc": "Today marks the end of your Manaslu Trek adventure. After breakfast, you will be transferred to Tribhuvan International Airport for your onward flight. Take memories of stunning Himalayan landscapes, Tsum Valley culture, and the unique experience of the Manaslu Circuit with you.", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 16: Final Departure from Tribhuvan International Airport (1,400 m / 4,593 ft)"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.868	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u000zkbrlniwhk1d9	gokyo-valley-trek-14-days	Gokyo Valley Trek – 14 Days	<h2>Explore the <a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=c26270ef90080d49&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnuDtxGPltiFsY23gAfAsvKzHq6nwQ:1787386273234&amp;udm=2&a	<h2>Explore the <a href="https://www.google.com/search?sca_esv=c26270ef90080d49&amp;sxsrf=APpeQnuDtxGPltiFsY23gAfAsvKzHq6nwQ:1787386273234&amp;udm=2&amp;fbs=ABfTbFVyMZGZf1hfvX9uKjN_-G8c4u0nXx4bEIpwm1lnNH832VTJOOCxW_fyN-Q_ezyf8gIPCeKHBvvzkIIwjmkYPTVw8EGq5ehdsmr_mla81VLtj_jQ7FVpQ3YmTSkyUUEXuTUuhNrtnzoGZLER8nBQtuZPtUDAsiXrQf1kz9sHgVILMEmwf9HCscNW86dnbOS1fipG_FB9OWFgc5C2AP1sWOOd4wxEtw&amp;q=gokyo&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=2ahUKEwjDhZHf5LOWAxUPxTgGHZPfMWkQtKgLegQIGBAB&amp;biw=1536&amp;bih=730&amp;dpr=1.25">Gokyo Valley</a></h2>\nThe <a href="https://everpeakadventures.com/trekking/gokyo-lake-trekking/"><strong>Gokyo Valley Trek</strong></a> is a spectacular 14-day journey through Nepal’s Everest region, combining peaceful mountain landscapes, traditional Sherpa villages, turquoise alpine lakes, and breathtaking Himalayan views. It offers a quieter alternative to the busier Everest Base Camp route while providing an unforgettable high-altitude experience.\n\nThe adventure begins with a scenic flight from Kathmandu to Lukla. From there, the trail follows the Dudh Koshi River through lush forests, suspension bridges, and charming mountain settlements before reaching Namche Bazaar. This vibrant Sherpa town is an important acclimatization stop and provides an opportunity to experience local culture while enjoying views of the surrounding peaks.\n\nAfter Namche, the route leaves the main Everest trail and heads toward Dole and Machhermo. As you climb higher, the landscape gradually changes from green forests to alpine valleys surrounded by impressive Himalayan peaks. The trail eventually reaches Gokyo, a beautiful lakeside settlement surrounded by mountains and glaciers.\n<h2>Gokyo Ri and Himalayan Panoramas</h2>\nOne of the major highlights is the early morning ascent of <strong>Gokyo Ri (5,360 m)</strong>. From the summit, trekkers can enjoy panoramic views of Mount Everest, Lhotse, Makalu, Cho Oyu, and the enormous Ngozumpa Glacier. The sunrise over the Himalayan peaks creates a memorable experience and offers excellent opportunities for photography.\n\nThe <strong>Gokyo Lakes</strong> are another remarkable attraction along the route. Their clear turquoise waters, surrounded by rugged mountains and glaciers, create one of the most beautiful landscapes in the Everest region. The journey also provides opportunities to experience authentic Sherpa traditions and observe the unique lifestyle of communities living in the high Himalayas.\n<h2>A Peaceful Himalayan Adventure</h2>\nCarefully planned acclimatization helps you adjust gradually to the increasing altitude. The combination of scenic trails, mountain villages, alpine landscapes, and spectacular viewpoints makes this journey ideal for travelers looking for adventure, natural beauty, and cultural experiences.\n\nAfter exploring the Gokyo region, the trail descends toward Lukla. A scenic flight then returns you to Kathmandu, where you can relax, explore the city, or prepare for your onward journey. With its stunning scenery, peaceful trails, and unforgettable mountain views, this 14-day Himalayan adventure is an excellent way to experience the beauty of Nepal’s Everest region.	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Gokyo-Lake-Trekking-2.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	14 days	1599	everest	Moderate		Spring (March–Jun) &amp; Autumn (September–December)	Hotel in Kathmandu &amp; Teahouses During Trek	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{everest-region}	<ul>\n<li>Scenic mountain flight between Kathmandu and Lukla</li>\n<li>Explore the vibrant Sherpa town of Namche Bazaar</li>\n<li>Acclimatization hike with stunning Himalayan views</li>\n<li>Trek through peaceful and less-crowded Gokyo Valley</li>\n<li>Visit the magnificent Gokyo Lakes</li>\n<li>Sunrise hike to Gokyo Ri (5,360 m)</li>\n<li>Panoramic views of Everest, Lhotse, Makalu, and Cho Oyu</li>\n<li>Experience authentic Sherpa culture and hospitality</li>\n<li>Walk alongside the massive Ngozumpa Glacier</li>\n<li>Comfortable airport-to-airport service in Nepal</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>Airport pick-up and drop-off services in Kathmandu.</li>\n<li>All ground transportation as per the itinerary.</li>\n<li>Two nights hotel accommodation in Kathmandu on a twin-sharing basis with breakfast.</li>\n<li>Domestic flight ticket from Kathmandu to Lukla and Lukla to Kathmandu.</li>\n<li>Sagarmatha National Park Entry Permit.</li>\n<li>Khumbu Pasang Lhamu Rural Municipality Permit.</li>\n<li>Experienced, government-licensed English-speaking trekking guide.</li>\n<li>Porter service (one porter for every two trekkers).</li>\n<li>All guide and porter expenses, including meals, accommodation, salary, insurance, and transportation.</li>\n<li>Teahouse accommodation during the trek on a twin-sharing basis.</li>\n<li>Three meals a day (breakfast, lunch, and dinner) during the trek.</li>\n<li>First aid medical kit carried by the guide.</li>\n<li>All applicable government taxes and service charges.</li>\n</ul>\n	<ul>\n<li>International airfare to and from Nepal.</li>\n<li>Nepal entry visa fees.</li>\n<li>Travel and rescue insurance.</li>\n<li>Personal trekking equipment and gear.</li>\n<li>Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu.</li>\n<li>Additional hotel nights in Kathmandu due to early arrival, late departure, or flight delays.</li>\n<li>Personal expenses such as laundry, telephone calls, internet, hot showers, charging devices, and drinks.</li>\n<li>Bottled water, soft drinks, alcoholic beverages, and snacks.</li>\n<li>Tips for guides, porters, and support staff.</li>\n<li>Emergency evacuation and rescue expenses.</li>\n<li>Costs arising from flight delays, cancellations, natural disasters, political disturbances, or unforeseen circumstances beyond our control.</li>\n<li>Any services not specifically mentioned in the "Package Includes" section.</li>\n</ul>\n	<div class="qMYqUG_convSearchResultHighlightRoot">\n<div class="" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:09004f46-8f67-45b2-ae2a-fe3ef4911786-2" data-is-intersecting="true">\n<section class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto R6Vx5W_threadScrollVars scroll-mb-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom,0px)+var(--thread-response-height))] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:09004f46-8f67-45b2-ae2a-fe3ef4911786-2" data-turn-id-container="request-WEB:09004f46-8f67-45b2-ae2a-fe3ef4911786-2" data-testid="conversation-turn-6" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant">\n<div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)">\n<div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn">\n<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow">\n<div class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" dir="auto" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="acfffa9d-e9e4-48ec-ac6d-1ba2d90e3bc2" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-5" data-turn-start-message="true">\n<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden">\n<div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert wrap-break-word w-full dark markdown-new-styling">\n<h4 data-start="57" data-end="80">🎒 Backpack &amp; Bags</h4>\n<ul data-start="81" data-end="134">\n<li data-section-id="1guau1w" data-start="81" data-end="102">Duffel bag (60–80L)</li>\n<li data-section-id="66vgdu" data-start="103" data-end="121">Daypack (25–35L)</li>\n<li data-section-id="15d4y9d" data-start="122" data-end="134">Rain cover</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="136" data-end="152">👕 Clothing</h4>\n<ul data-start="153" data-end="317">\n<li data-section-id="18kis2u" data-start="153" data-end="178">Trekking T-shirts (2–3)</li>\n<li data-section-id="17x2whl" data-start="179" data-end="205">Trekking pants (2 pairs)</li>\n<li data-section-id="ht9c86" data-start="206" data-end="227">Thermal base layers</li>\n<li data-section-id="4ccdyu" data-start="228" data-end="243">Fleece jacket</li>\n<li data-section-id="108ul6w" data-start="244" data-end="257">Down jacket</li>\n<li data-section-id="x46bqt" data-start="258" data-end="285">Waterproof jacket &amp; pants</li>\n<li data-section-id="1gmos76" data-start="286" data-end="308">Warm hat and sun hat</li>\n<li data-section-id="1xfofe4" data-start="309" data-end="317">Gloves</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="319" data-end="335">👞 Footwear</h4>\n<ul data-start="336" data-end="431">\n<li data-section-id="1lca0sf" data-start="336" data-end="363">Waterproof trekking boots</li>\n<li data-section-id="1jhchx8" data-start="364" data-end="384">Camp shoes/sandals</li>\n<li data-section-id="1brc45i" data-start="385" data-end="413">Trekking socks (4–5 pairs)</li>\n<li data-section-id="1mfsepp" data-start="414" data-end="431">Warm wool socks</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="433" data-end="459">🥾 Trekking Equipment</h4>\n<ul data-start="460" data-end="582">\n<li data-section-id="bvyvto" data-start="460" data-end="491">Sleeping bag (-10°C to -15°C)</li>\n<li data-section-id="jpijbi" data-start="492" data-end="508">Trekking poles</li>\n<li data-section-id="1s6undc" data-start="509" data-end="519">Headlamp</li>\n<li data-section-id="5c7vo5" data-start="520" data-end="556">Water bottles or hydration bladder</li>\n<li data-section-id="11rfapo" data-start="557" data-end="569">Sunglasses</li>\n<li data-section-id="dluokx" data-start="570" data-end="582">Power bank</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 data-start="584" data-end="606">🧴 Personal Items</h4>\n<ul data-start="607" data-end="718">\n<li data-section-id="10pl9xo" data-start="607" data-end="618">Sunscreen</li>\n<li data-section-id="1voh31b" data-start="619" data-end="629">Lip balm</li>\n<li data-section-id="l5061k" data-start="630" data-end="652">Personal medications</li>\n<li data-section-id="1h5dihr" data-start="653" data-end="674">Basic first-aid kit</li>\n<li data-section-id="8yarze" data-start="675" data-end="687">Toiletries</li>\n<li data-section-id="k8zdnf" data-start="688" data-end="718">Wet wipes and hand sanitizer</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start="720" data-end="855" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node=""><strong data-start="720" data-end="732">❄️ Note:</strong> Temperatures at Gokyo and Gokyo Ri can drop below freezing, so warm layers and a good sleeping bag are highly recommended.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"></div>\n<div class="mt-3 w-full empty:hidden">\n<div class="text-center"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="pointer-events-none -mt-px h-px translate-y-[calc(var(--scroll-root-safe-area-inset-bottom)-14*var(--spacing))]" aria-hidden="true"></div>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Fly from Kathmandu to Lukla and Trek to Phakding (2610m / 8563 ft)"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Trek from Phakding to Namche Bazaar (3440m / 11286 ft)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 4: Acclimatization Day in Namche Bazaar"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 5: Trek from Namche Bazaar to Dole (4038m / 13248 ft)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Trek from Dole to Machhermo (4470m / 14665 ft)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Trek from Machhermo to Gokyo (4790m / 15715 ft)"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Hike to Gokyo Ri and Explore Gokyo Lakes (5360m / 17585 ft)"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Trek from Gokyo to Dole (4038m / 13248 ft)"}, {"day": "10", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 10: Trek from Dole to Namche Bazaar (3440m / 11286 ft)"}, {"day": "11", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 11: Trek from Namche Bazaar to Lukla (2860m / 9383 ft)"}, {"day": "12", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 12: Fly from Lukla to Kathmandu (1350m / 4412 ft)"}, {"day": "13", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 13: Free Day in Kathmandu"}, {"day": "14", "desc": "", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 14: Final Departure from Kathmandu"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.887	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
cmt563w1u0011kbrli40glee5	langtang-valley-comfort-trek-9-days	Langtang Valley Comfort Trek – 9 Days	<h2>Why Choose the Langtang Valley Comfort Trek?</h2>\nThe <strong>Langtang Valley Comfort Trek</strong> is a carefully designed 9-day Himalayan advent	<h2>Why Choose the Langtang Valley Comfort Trek?</h2>\nThe <strong>Langtang Valley Comfort Trek</strong> is a carefully designed 9-day Himalayan adventure combining breathtaking mountain scenery, authentic Tamang culture, and comfortable lodge accommodation. It offers an excellent balance of adventure and relaxation, making it ideal for travelers who want to explore the Himalayas without sacrificing comfort.\n\nYour journey begins with a scenic drive from Kathmandu to Syabrubesi, the gateway to the Langtang region. From here, the trail passes through lush rhododendron and bamboo forests, crosses suspension bridges, and follows peaceful mountain rivers. Along the way, you will encounter traditional Tamang villages and experience the warm hospitality and unique culture of local communities.\n<h2>Discover the Beauty of Langtang Valley</h2>\nAs you continue higher, the landscape gradually changes from dense forests to beautiful alpine meadows and dramatic Himalayan terrain. The trail provides spectacular views of Langtang Lirung, Dorje Lakpa, Langshisa Ri, and other surrounding peaks.\n\nOne of the major highlights is reaching <strong>Kyanjin Gompa</strong>, a peaceful mountain settlement surrounded by impressive peaks. You can explore the historic monastery, enjoy the mountain scenery, and experience the unique atmosphere of this remote Himalayan village. An early morning hike toward Kyanjin Ri provides panoramic views and unforgettable sunrise scenery.\n<h2>A Comfortable Himalayan Adventure</h2>\nThis 9-day journey is perfect for travelers seeking a comfortable way to experience the natural and cultural beauty of Nepal. Comfortable lodges, delicious local meals, and carefully planned walking distances make each day more enjoyable while allowing sufficient time to appreciate the surrounding environment.\n\nThe route is also less crowded than some of Nepal’s more popular trekking areas, offering a peaceful experience through forests, villages, and high mountain landscapes. Whether you are visiting Nepal for the first time or returning for another Himalayan adventure, this <strong>Langtang trek</strong> offers a memorable combination of nature, culture, comfort, and mountain scenery.\n\nFor travelers interested in exploring other regions of Nepal, you can also visit our <strong>Gokyo Valley Trek</strong> or explore our other Himalayan trekking packages for additional adventure options.	https://everpeakadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/Langtang-1.jpg	{}	\N	\N	\N	f	9 days	1099	langtang	Moderate		March-Jun / Oct-Feb	Hotels in Kathmandu and teahouses during the trek	B.B.		\N	Trekking	{langtang-region}	<ul>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Explore the spectacular Langtang Valley, one of Nepal's most beautiful trekking regions</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Enjoy stunning mountain views of Langtang Lirung, Dorje Lakpa, Gangchempo, and surrounding peaks</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Hike to Kyanjin Ri (4,773m) for breathtaking panoramic Himalayan vistas</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Visit the historic Kyanjin Gompa and traditional yak cheese factory</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Trek through lush rhododendron and bamboo forests rich in wildlife</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Experience authentic Tamang and Tibetan-influenced culture and hospitality</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Stay in comfortable mountain lodges throughout the journey</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Discover charming villages including Langtang Village, Ghodatabela, and Sherpa Gaun</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Follow scenic trails alongside rivers, waterfalls, and alpine meadows</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Enjoy a well-paced itinerary combining adventure, comfort, culture, and unforgettable Himalayan scenery</li>\n</ul>\n	<p class="isSelectedEnd">• Airport pick-up and drop-off by private vehicle</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">• 2 nights hotel accommodation in Kathmandu with breakfast</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">• Private transportation from Kathmandu to Syabru and return from Syabrubesi to Kathmandu</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">• Comfortable lodge accommodation during the trek</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">• Three meals a day (breakfast, lunch, and dinner) during the trek</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">• Experienced English-speaking trekking guide</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">• Necessary porter service (1 porter for every 2 trekkers)</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">• Langtang National Park Entry Permit</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">• TIMS (Trekkers' Information Management System) card</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">• Guide and porter salary, insurance, meals, accommodation, and transportation</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">• First aid kit carried by the guide</p>\n<p>• Government taxes and service charges</p>\n	<ul>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd"> International airfare to and from Nepal</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Nepal entry visa fees</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Travel and personal insurance</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Lunch and dinner in Kathmandu</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Personal expenses such as drinks, snacks, laundry, phone calls, and internet</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Hot showers and charging fees at teahouses where applicable</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Personal trekking equipment and clothing</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Tips for guides, porters, and drivers</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Any expenses arising from unforeseen circumstances such as flight delays, natural disasters, illness, or changes to the itinerary</li>\n<li class="isSelectedEnd">Any services not specifically mentioned in the "Package Includes" section</li>\n</ul>\n	<p class="isSelectedEnd">🎒 <strong>Backpack &amp; Bags</strong><br />\n• Daypack (20–35L)<br />\n• Duffel bag or trekking backpack<br />\n• Rain cover</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">👕 <strong>Clothing</strong><br />\n• Moisture-wicking trekking shirts<br />\n• Lightweight trekking pants<br />\n• Fleece or warm jacket<br />\n• Down jacket<br />\n• Waterproof jacket and pants<br />\n• Thermal base layers<br />\n• Undergarments and trekking socks</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">🥾 <strong>Footwear</strong><br />\n• Comfortable trekking boots<br />\n• Camp shoes or sandals</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">🧢 <strong>Accessories</strong><br />\n• Sun hat or cap<br />\n• Warm hat/beanie<br />\n• Sunglasses with UV protection<br />\n• Gloves</p>\n<p class="isSelectedEnd">💧 <strong>Essentials</strong><br />\n• Reusable water bottles or hydration bladder<br />\n• Water purification tablets or filter<br />\n• Sunscreen and lip balm<br />\n• Personal toiletries<br />\n• Personal medications</p>\n<p>🔦 <strong>Other Items</strong><br />\n• Trekking poles<br />\n• Headlamp with spare batteries<br />\n• Camera or smartphone<br />\n• Power bank<br />\n• Snacks and energy bars</p>\n	[{"day": "1", "desc": "Upon arrival at Tribhuvan International Airport, you will be greeted by our representative and transferred to your hotel in Kathmandu. After check-in, you can relax or take a short walk around the vibrant Thamel area, known for its trekking shops, cafés, and cultural atmosphere.\\n\\nIn the evening, a brief trek orientation will be conducted where your guide will explain the route, safety guidelines, altitude awareness, and overall plan for the Langtang Valley Comfort Trek. This helps you prepare properly for the journey ahead.\\";s", "elev": 1400, "title": "Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu (1,400m)"}, {"day": "2", "desc": "Early morning departure from Kathmandu with a scenic drive towards Syabrubesi, the gateway to the Langtang region. The road follows winding mountain highways alongside rivers, terraced fields, and small rural settlements, offering beautiful views of hills and distant snow-capped peaks.\\n\\nYou will pass through several local towns and may experience rough road sections, especially near the Pahiro area, which is known for landslide-prone terrain. Despite the challenging road conditions, the journey is highly scenic and gives your first real glimpse of rural Himalayan life. By late afternoon, you reach the Pahiro/Syabrubesi area for an overnight stay.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 2: Kathmandu to Syabrubesi via Pahiro (1,200–1,400m)\\";"}, {"day": "3", "desc": "Today marks your first trekking day in the Langtang Valley. After breakfast, you begin your hike from Pahiro, following a scenic trail that gradually ascends through dense forests, suspension bridges, and riverside paths. The sound of flowing rivers and waterfalls accompanies you as you move deeper into the Langtang region.\\n\\nAlong the way, you may spot wildlife, yak caravans, and small resting points used by trekkers. The trail becomes more peaceful and surrounded by alpine forest as you approach Ghodatabela. This area is known for its wide open valley views and fresh mountain air, making it a perfect place to end the day’s trek.\\";s:", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 3: Pahiro to Ghodatabela (3,000m approx.)"}, {"day": "4", "desc": "After breakfast, you continue your trek deeper into the Langtang Valley, gradually leaving the forest zone behind and entering wide alpine landscapes. The trail opens up with spectacular views of snow-covered peaks, yak pastures, and traditional Tamang settlements along the way.\\n\\nAs you ascend steadily, you will pass through small villages like Langtang area remnants and open valley sections shaped by the 2015 earthquake, now beautifully rebuilt. The scenery becomes more dramatic as Langtang Lirung and surrounding peaks dominate the horizon. By afternoon, you reach Kyanjin Gompa, the spiritual heart of the valley, surrounded by mountains and glaciers.\\";", "elev": 3870, "title": "Day 4: Ghodatabela to Kyanjin Gompa (3,870m)"}, {"day": "5", "desc": "Today is a rest and exploration day in the beautiful Kyanjin Valley. Early in the morning, you can hike up to Kyanjin Ri, one of the best viewpoints in the Langtang region, offering panoramic views of Langtang Lirung, glaciers, icefalls, and surrounding Himalayan peaks. The climb is steep but highly rewarding with unforgettable scenery.\\n\\nAfter returning, you can explore Kyanjin Gompa village, visit the ancient monastery, and optionally tour the local cheese factory to experience traditional yak cheese production. The rest of the day is free to relax, enjoy the mountain atmosphere, and acclimatize properly before descending.\\";", "elev": 3870, "title": "Day 5: Acclimatization &amp; Exploration at Kyanjin Gompa (3,870m)"}, {"day": "6", "desc": "After breakfast, you begin your descent from Kyanjin Gompa, retracing your steps back through the beautiful Langtang Valley. The trail offers a completely different perspective of the landscapes you climbed earlier, with wide alpine valleys, yak pastures, and distant snow peaks gradually giving way to forested sections.\\n\\nThe downhill walk is long but comfortable, passing through scenic viewpoints, small settlements, and river crossings. As you lose altitude, the air becomes warmer and the vegetation gradually turns dense again. By late afternoon, you arrive at Ghodatabela, where you will rest for the night surrounded by peaceful mountain scenery.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 6: Trek from Kyanjin Gompa to Ghodatabela (3,000m approx.)"}, {"day": "7", "desc": "After breakfast, you continue your descent from Ghodatabela through lush forests, river valleys, and small traditional settlements. The trail is peaceful and less crowded, offering a relaxing walking experience compared to the higher alpine sections. Along the way, you will pass suspension bridges, waterfalls, and local Tamang villages that reflect the culture of the Langtang region.\\n\\nBy afternoon, you reach Sherpa Gaun, a quiet and beautiful village known for its authentic mountain lifestyle and warm hospitality. It is a perfect place to rest and experience local culture after several days of trekking in higher altitudes.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 7: Trek from Ghodatabela to Sherpa Gaun (2,500–2,600m)\\";"}, {"day": "8", "desc": "After breakfast, you begin your return journey from Sherpa Gaun (via Syabrubesi road point) back to Kathmandu. The drive follows the same scenic mountain highway, passing through rivers, green hills, waterfalls, and rural settlements. Along the way, you can enjoy the final views of the Langtang region before descending fully into the Kathmandu Valley.\\n\\nThis is a long but comfortable drive that gives you time to relax and reflect on the completed trek. Upon arrival in Kathmandu, you will be transferred to your hotel where you can rest, shop, or explore the city one last time.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 8: Drive from Sherpa Gaun / Syabrubesi to Kathmandu"}, {"day": "9", "desc": "After breakfast, you will be transferred from your hotel to Tribhuvan International Airport for your onward journey. Depending on your flight schedule, you may have some free time for last-minute shopping or short exploration around Kathmandu.\\n\\nThis marks the end of your 9 Days Langtang Valley Comfort Trek, filled with beautiful mountain landscapes, cultural villages, and unforgettable Himalayan experiences. Safe travels and hope to see you again for another adventure in Nepal.\\";", "elev": 0, "title": "Day 9: Final Departure from Kathmandu"}]	\N	f	0	2026-08-23 02:08:07.938	2026-08-23 02:13:42.893	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	Kathmandu	\N	\N	Kathmandu
\.
